    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a027b678-b20d-11e8-b7b7-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a027b678-b20d-11e8-b7b7-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2017-02-08T11:34:30</review:date>
        <review:description>I got this game for 4€ on sale on the PS4. Therefore, the &amp;lt;2h length did not bother me.

Virginia is a story, very much so like film. It controls the pace through frequent cuts, harking back to Thrity Flights of Loving, which it is as much based on as actual TV influences like Twin Peaks.

The story and how you read it is the real &quot;fun&quot; of this game. It follows two women of color, and touches on some themes this brings, without being blunt about them. I found watching it as enjoyable as working out the plot and how the visual metaphors fit into the rest of it all.

Exploration is limited, but there. By not looking at everything and checking every door, even if most don&apos;t open, minor details can be missed. I recommend letting yourself be guided by the game the first time, enjoying it as it is clear it wants to be played, and at consecutive playthroughs to break the flow and try to look at everything.

This also makes clear that the main audience is not &apos;hardcore&apos; gamers. This might even be a good game to introduce people to the medium.

If you are open to what games can be and do, this is an interesting experiment. And, in my opinion, it paid off.
If you feel cautious, perhaps wait until it is on sale.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">28</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>a027b678-b20d-11e8-b7b7-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Strong Storytelling</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">21</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a03050ac-a032-11ea-95d9-fa163e93294d -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a03050ac-a032-11ea-95d9-fa163e93294d">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-05-27T18:56:28</review:date>
        <review:description>Polecam takie nowe The Setllers w pięknej grafice. Jedyne co mogli by zmienić do każdy klan mógłby nie otrzymywać kar do szczęścia za nieulepszone domy. Cieszę się że w końcu na Gogu mogłem kupić tę grę na Steama jej nie kupowałem nie można posiadać kopii gry to nie kupuje na Steama. Ale mam też na konsoli bo chciałem zobaczyć jak to wygląda jest rewelacja. </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>a03050ac-a032-11ea-95d9-fa163e93294d</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Świetna gra Game is cool</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a053d9e4-1c75-11ec-9806-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a053d9e4-1c75-11ec-9806-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-09-23T16:53:26</review:date>
        <review:description>The main point of this DLC is an addition of one more puppet. It consists of one small area where you start a quest, then backtrack to previously visited locations to kill a couple of new quest monsters that drop a quest item, bring the items back to the DLC area, use them, fight a boss and add him to your (by that point) already overcrowded roster. That&apos;s pretty much it.

The associated quest also has pretty much no context or story to it. Just a random small dungeon you get to enter like 2/3rds into the game.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>a053d9e4-1c75-11ec-9806-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>Short, random, meh....</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a0cc8d4a-a519-11eb-9a93-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a0cc8d4a-a519-11eb-9a93-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-04-24T19:25:05</review:date>
        <review:description>More simple Darkest Dungeon I finished and enjoyed more.

The art direction was stunning, the environments and map of the  city, designs of the characters and animations. Can&apos;t believe it is work of pretty must one person. 

Interesting remix of more western fantasy races and Korean fox folk.

The sound and the music are really nice, engrossing you in a setting. 

Getting outfits alongside doing side-quests was nice.. and a bit addicting for me, (like in newer Tomb Raiders) and could affect characters and narrative. 

I liked the combat, and that bosses were challenging for me on normal, and you had to thread more carefully your actions, and you will not loose your comrades.
 
Would love to have manual saves.. or more ways of saving especially during the dungeon parts.

I would like your party to be more customizable and different within classes, but I understand that if you loose one, you can pick up any other form the same class and it only be different by one skill max, so no that big of a deal, . Also because of my companions not dying on normal, I had soo much resources and money in the end, no need to spend it on anything. </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>a0cc8d4a-a519-11eb-9a93-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Awesome setting and enjoyable characters</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">7</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a0ec494a-9488-11e8-b6c0-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a0ec494a-9488-11e8-b6c0-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2011-11-01T15:22:38</review:date>
        <review:description>As a long time space shooter player I can truly say, wow. Starting on X-wing and then its sequels, moving through wing commander and of course its privateer follow on and picking up the odd bits and pieces there after. I can honestly say that nothing compares to this, gaming industry take note, this is a game that even over 10 years after it was released has a vibrant modding community that shows no signs of slowing down, and they certainly helped it along with such things as a amazing built in mission editor.

A note on the fanbase: This is the kind of community that treats the game seriously, discussions on the best ways to attack specific capital ships, blind spots and the like or simply the ease of landing all shots on a moving target with a specific fighters gun placement are commonplace.

But don&apos;t be intimidated by all that, the game is incredible and you would be doing yourself a incredible favour in playing it, and for this price, who wouldn&apos;t? I picked it up on 3 discs originally, simply for the ease of not messing about with those I am tempted to buy the GOG version.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>a0ec494a-9488-11e8-b6c0-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Awesome</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a10a14e4-316c-11e9-be39-00163e4e60cc -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a10a14e4-316c-11e9-be39-00163e4e60cc">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-02-15T23:57:03</review:date>
        <review:description>This game is infuryatingly impossible to play. Even on the easiest setting opponents speed off at the speed of light never to be seen again, the drift mechanic is fun when it triggers - but rarely does -, and the tracks are repetitive and uninspired. Worst of all, the tutorial is actually broken - during the slipstream session I cannot catch up to the car I&apos;m supposed to tailgate, and I kinda doubt I&apos;m too stupid to press down RT on my friggen controller.

Do yourself a favour and play &quot;80s Overdrive&quot; on a 3DS instead. Much more fun, better handling, and best of all: portable.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">20</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>a10a14e4-316c-11e9-be39-00163e4e60cc</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:rating>
        <review:title>Disappointing waste of money</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">11</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a10f3c3e-cfa9-11eb-982e-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a10f3c3e-cfa9-11eb-982e-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-06-17T23:21:42</review:date>
        <review:description>I hear the story is nice and but I will never get to enjoy it. Since I absolutely hate the chaotic combat.  There are no tactics. Your characters do nothing other than a standard attack unless you explicitely tell them what to do. As a combat round is less than 2 seconds, get used to pressing pause issuing commands and immediately pressing pause again. All the while watching in shock as your chars run through enemies to attack the enemy right in front of them. It takes a quarter second to fill what is displayed in the combat log (so better get used to scrolling up all the time). 
Such a shame since I quite like the system and levelling my characters. However, I simply can&apos;t bring myself to continue playing this game....</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">19</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>a10f3c3e-cfa9-11eb-982e-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>Hidden gem that stays hidden</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">11</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a128a528-d9f8-11e9-b792-d2b5edd577c7 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a128a528-d9f8-11e9-b792-d2b5edd577c7">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-09-18T09:42:29</review:date>
        <review:description>Return of the Obra Dinn is the best detective game to date. It has a great story and narrative, an intriguing art-style and minimalistic but very rewarding gameplay. Nothing is unnecessary. 

Don&apos;t worry if all the different characters, plots and scenes are a bit too much to handle. You will sort it all out eventually, even I did, though it took me quite some time. 
Once you get into the flow of solving one fate after another through deduction, elimination and sometimes a bit of clever guessing, no other game is as rewarding as Obra Dinn.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>a128a528-d9f8-11e9-b792-d2b5edd577c7</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Murder Sudoku</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a19db360-957d-11e8-81d0-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a19db360-957d-11e8-81d0-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2015-03-20T02:33:11</review:date>
        <review:description>Buy the pack with freespace 2 as well. Then look for FS2Open. They ported the greatwar campaing and totally updated FS2... well worth the download and replay.

With FS2Open the graphics are modernized and well worth the play :-)</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>a19db360-957d-11e8-81d0-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
