        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">45</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a26d7a24-2f2b-11eb-b8f3-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a26d7a24-2f2b-11eb-b8f3-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-11-25T16:36:42</review:date>
        <review:description>The most long awaited game for me personaly ever since I discovered GOG back in 2012. 

I played the game when it first released back in 2009. It reminded me of Baldur&apos;s gate with its complex and solid RPG system and beautiful story.

I bought it again on steam and now D.R.M. free on G.O.G.

It was simply a naturl choice.

If you love old school C.R.P.G.s like Baldur&apos;s gate 1 &amp;amp; 2 and aren&apos;t discouraged by slightly complex RPG mechanics this is the game for you.

I hope that G.O.G. adds the sequel (actually prequel) and it&apos;s expansion to it&apos;s catalogue.

It will be a certain purchase for me and a natural fit for this store.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">8</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>a26d7a24-2f2b-11eb-b8f3-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>A long awaited addition to the GOG!!!</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">77</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a2a37bf0-5e10-11ec-b470-fa163e9aa6fa -->

