    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a51d16d0-9efc-11eb-a1ca-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a51d16d0-9efc-11eb-a1ca-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-04-17T00:42:30</review:date>
        <review:description>First I thought &quot;well looks like another HD Retro Shooter to play&quot;

then I thought &quot;well i really like the mechanics already, this seems like it stands out to its predecessors just by having abilities of movement by nature.

At last I realized, this is hard, this is relentlessly skillbased, and to finish my short review for such an already great game - it feels highly rewarding for actually pulling of some fast paced moves. Switching between different weapon variations mid air to get that last enemy off your back that was just too close to hit you. Damn this feels good!

I will certainly prefer this highly skill based shooter over any visuality-based splatterfest.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>a51d16d0-9efc-11eb-a1ca-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Truely Surprised of its Originiality</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a527b17e-e1aa-11e8-bcc6-00163e4e60cc -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a527b17e-e1aa-11e8-bcc6-00163e4e60cc">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2018-11-06T11:59:26</review:date>
        <review:description>Your brain will boil. Your eyes will bleed. Your hands will pull your hair out of your head. but in the end you will know what satifaction means.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>a527b17e-e1aa-11e8-bcc6-00163e4e60cc</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>A must have</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a528d9ce-93fc-11e8-a6ff-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a528d9ce-93fc-11e8-a6ff-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2009-02-15T00:19:27</review:date>
        <review:description>Old-school gameplay; which is to say, unrefined and frustrating to a modern gamer.  Also, the designers were desperate to make a game for adults, and like children erroneously concluded that you market a game to adults by filling it with titillation and gore.  I&apos;m all for titillation and gore, but here it just comes across as immature.

Potentially of interest to historians, or game programmers interested an the early dynamic tessellation system for models.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">24</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>a528d9ce-93fc-11e8-a6ff-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:rating>
        <review:title>Immature and clunky</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">8</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a52f768c-20d0-11ea-b237-00163e4e60cc -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a52f768c-20d0-11ea-b237-00163e4e60cc">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-12-17T15:25:08</review:date>
        <review:description>Un clasico divertido de hace 22 años que puede jugar en Hardware moderno</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>a52f768c-20d0-11ea-b237-00163e4e60cc</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Un clasico de PC</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a560e4ae-93fc-11e8-9ca1-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a560e4ae-93fc-11e8-9ca1-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2009-02-15T07:53:05</review:date>
        <review:description>This FPS is much different than Quake 2, where its engine is modded for this game.
You can still go-out-and-blast on Novice or Easy, but at Normal or higher difficulty, you have to think about stealthy approach, talking around, or get your henchmen and gang on enemies.

AI are decent for both your henchmen and enemies.
They try to follow you through vents and ladders(think of the fact that it&apos;s released one year after Half-Life), ask you to stop for healing(they regenerate slowly, somehow).
Though you can&apos;t bring them between chapters and you can have only two henchmen at once.
If you don&apos;t need those henchmen anymore, you can just shoot them in the head and grab their guns dropped. 
During combat, some cowards(NPCs) try to run if you have guns better than theirs(like, you point shotgun at a guy with lead pipe) or they&apos;re hurt too much(They usually leave blood trails), and not-so-wimpy NPCs will strafe and crouch frequently, making your aim much harder.

The singleplayer is hard, as there&apos;s some parts where you can get stuck(like, Chapter 2 have a bad ending scene), or hard to find things and ways out(easier than Xatrix&apos;s previous game, Redneck Rampage though).

Overall I liked its difficulty, and its DEMO(contained an Chapter 1, without the scrapyard map and Flamethrower was hidden in the last map) was the FIRST FPS I HAVE EVER PLAYED.

Note : this game contains LOADS OF F-words. I&apos;ve seen no games with more F-words than Kingpin.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>a560e4ae-93fc-11e8-9ca1-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Dark, Violent and Intelligent.</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">11</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a562583e-d859-11ec-96f8-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a562583e-d859-11ec-96f8-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-05-20T19:26:48</review:date>
        <review:description>I wanna say i didn&apos;t play the crap outta this while at a contracted security post, but i put in about 150 hours. Theres easily 3 different endings with an &apos;ansestory&apos; gimic. In a play through you can seal away 5 items for your next of kin. So as you may figure, thers some pretty powerful stuff, and while you can aquire it all, it takes like 5 or 6 playthroughs to get it all. Even then, you&apos;re not a god, you just have good stats. 

Overall, if you want to be spoon fed information, your battles easy, and liniar one playstyle wins all type of game, this is not for you. I played through as a different &apos;entity&apos; every time and felt it was rewarding to some degree, if at least, out of curiosity. Also, split screen. 

Combat is a bit slow and clunky but your character isn&apos;t a hero or decended from a hero line. Just a guy who gets thrown in a really crappy position and has to turn to adventuring to survive. Also, you get to work around this. So if you want Jedi jumping all over, super ninja Goku crap, well...were human down here. Please pass this planet up.

Definatly more fun with a friend. so grab a controller, or buddy up on the keyboard and have fun! Oh, and the 150 hours was in the base game, no DLC. Planning on getting those, just ... in time. The best way i can describe it to the modern gamer is, a solo experience MMO. Large enough world, a few options to skills and combat, and things want to kill you dead if only for you are crunchy and taste good with ketchup. </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>a562583e-d859-11ec-96f8-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Old schoolers will like this</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a579df6a-93ff-11e8-b0d0-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a579df6a-93ff-11e8-b0d0-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2009-10-03T21:01:11</review:date>
        <review:description>Hands down one of the best space sims of all time.  This right here is a console seller!  Fantastic graphics for even today, captivating story line, and full control of your destiny.  All action!  Replay value high!</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>a579df6a-93ff-11e8-b0d0-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>One of the best Space Sims of all time!</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a57c9a72-0a13-11e9-979a-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a57c9a72-0a13-11e9-979a-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2018-12-27T22:11:50</review:date>
        <review:description>This game is the only game I have ever played that is a true mystery. You are required to use a significant amount of critical thinking in order to determine the identities of the poor souls lost aboard the Obra Dinn. As a long time fan of authors like Patrick O Brian and CS Forester I really enjoyed the attention to detail when it came to nautical knowledge, but a handy glossary would provide more than enough information to even a complete layman. The low quality graphics loop right back around to being charming and unique, and the story that is slowly told is excellent. I highly recommend this game and hope that Lucas Pope will continue to release stellar work like this.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>a57c9a72-0a13-11e9-979a-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Excellent Mystery Game</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a58df204-9549-11eb-a310-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a58df204-9549-11eb-a310-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-04-04T16:28:30</review:date>
        <review:description>Просто замечательная игра, но подойдет не всем, герой здесь настолько медленно движется, что нужно находиться в таком расслабленном настроении, некуда не спешить, что бы получать удовольствие от постепенного исследования пещер.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>a58df204-9549-11eb-a310-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Прекрасная игра</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a5c99890-e1fe-11e9-9a05-e6c21c8a18f9 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a5c99890-e1fe-11e9-9a05-e6c21c8a18f9">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-09-28T14:45:43</review:date>
        <review:description>I got this on Switch, which comes with New Powers. I&apos;ll not talk about UI, nor will I review the new aspects New Powers brings.

While lacking a lot of features one would expect from the veteran grand strategies out there, 
Realpolitiks does offer a taste of grand strategy in a simplified edition that everyone can try.

The core problem of Realpolitiks is neither in the balance (or lack thereof) nor in its simplicity (it&apos;s actually pretty good all things considered), but in the incredible lack of information presented. It&apos;s no secret that the complexity of grand strategies necessitates a wiki of some sort, but Realpolitiks shows you less information than Final Fantasy Tactics does, which is incredible considering that Final Fantasy Tactics was made 2 decades ago

While the tutorial tells you a thing or two about the game, ultimately you&apos;ll be left wondering &quot;what does this do again?&quot; or &quot;why is this happening?&quot; pretty much all the time. You&apos;re given no information in practically everything: why am I losing a battle? What does the province stats do? why is the world economy plummeting? and so on and so forth

All things considered, it&apos;s something you can try if you wanted to try a grand strategy but is not willing to jump straight into the behemoths that are Paradox games</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>a5c99890-e1fe-11e9-9a05-e6c21c8a18f9</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:rating>
        <review:title>Has potential, good for newcomers</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a60dc634-1b26-11eb-acd0-fa163e7e880a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a60dc634-1b26-11eb-acd0-fa163e7e880a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-10-31T05:10:37</review:date>
        <review:description>For a game like this, the pacing is brilliant. There is a constant pressure to move forward. Constant goals to work toward. The need to survive can push you to the edge and force you to make some tough decisions. All the gameplay systems are tightly interwoven to create a game that sneaks up on you and sinks it&apos;s fangs in without you even knowing it. I found it hard to put down once I started. 

I wouldn&apos;t call it a scary per se, so if you are someone who shys away from horror games and hates jumpscares, there really isn&apos;t any of that here but the subject matter is indeed very dark and there are some surreal/haunting visuals that startled me at times. I strongly recommend it. It starts a bit slow and might even come off as confusing but things will start to make sense soon.  </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>a60dc634-1b26-11eb-acd0-fa163e7e880a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Really something special</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a63818f8-946e-11e8-a0be-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a63818f8-946e-11e8-a0be-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2011-06-25T08:43:36</review:date>
        <review:description>I thought it might just be nostalgia, the memories of when space sims were the genre to be.  Its been how many years since more than one or two were released in a year? Even more since any of them were worthy of praise.
A few hours in and its most definitely not nostalgia. This game (save for the graphics) has lost nothing.  Were it released today with a graphics update and nothing more, it would probably be hailed as the rebirth of the space sim.
You really fall into this game, feel the ship around you, feel the combat, the scope and size of the vastness of space.
The don&apos;t make games as complete as this too often these days. Developers these days makes games and call them art, but back then, developers were making art and calling them games.  This is a gem.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>a63818f8-946e-11e8-a0be-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>A game from a different age.</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">29</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a63e051a-94d7-11e8-a16c-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a63e051a-94d7-11e8-a16c-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2012-12-16T08:50:26</review:date>
        <review:description>My brother urged me to get this. So glad I did. It&apos;s been a long time since I last experienced a space battle game like this. It&apos;&apos;s really enjoyable and I highly recommend it. We are yet to try out the multi-player option in the game.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>a63e051a-94d7-11e8-a16c-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>No need to think twice.</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a648a49a-80d3-11ea-ab1a-fa163e62c76a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a648a49a-80d3-11ea-ab1a-fa163e62c76a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-04-17T20:48:30</review:date>
        <review:description>Отточили механику, но после 1/3 игры наскучило. Уход в сторону от оригинала не пошел на пользу атмосфере и общему восприятию сюжета.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>a648a49a-80d3-11ea-ab1a-fa163e62c76a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:rating>
        <review:title>Не влезетело</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a64a860c-780a-11e9-b0f2-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a64a860c-780a-11e9-b0f2-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-05-16T21:44:34</review:date>
        <review:description>The game is very pleasing to see, the graphism is good quality, and the animations are fluid and complete with no trace of clumsiness or heaviness. The story is straightforward and simple, wet the atmosphere of the different scenery and the personnality of the characters are well transmitted. 

The game has a fairly good potential for a second playthrought, as a pacifist, to uncover all the secrets and curious easter-egg or simply with a higher difficulty. The challenge is present (but please note that i am not used to platforme game), and the ulgrades are fun and useful to get and use.

I get the game while it had a smaller price (for 5euros, i think), and mainly because i was curious. I beat the game in 7 hours, and it was a good surprise.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>a64a860c-780a-11e9-b0f2-00163e97122a</review:id>
