    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a666c08c-d46e-11e8-83c6-00163e4e60cc -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a666c08c-d46e-11e8-83c6-00163e4e60cc">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2018-10-20T16:47:13</review:date>
        <review:description>Wow, everything is a surprise in this game, from the look with CGA-like (not even, only 2 colors!) graphics, the set (inquirery on a boat), the navigation (reality, past, book). This is really a unique experience, I haved only played about one hour so far but I am impatient to see what will come next.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">10</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>a666c08c-d46e-11e8-83c6-00163e4e60cc</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Original and fascinating</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">45</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a6b49752-63fd-11e9-a169-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a6b49752-63fd-11e9-a169-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-04-21T09:21:08</review:date>
        <review:description>I absolutely loved this game. Hopping aboard the Obra Dinn and slowly unraveling the mysterious tragedy of its voyage was so much fun and made me feel like an absolute genius when I correctly guessed the fates of some of the crew. It did get a little frustrating near the end because there was just so much information to gleam and navigating between memories for a particular person became a little tedious. I wish there was a way to just jump to certain memories and to simply play those vignettes from the book once you had already seen them, but still, it was fine. It also did feel like, at times, I was just making educated guesses and occasionally the details of a vignette weren&apos;t super clear so it was hard to actually see what had happened. Other than a few nitpicks, this was one of my favourite mystery games I&apos;ve played because it felt like I was really a detective. The music was great, the overall aesthetic of the game was beautiful and it all came together to make one hell of a game.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>a6b49752-63fd-11e9-a169-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Atmospheric and Engaging Murder Mystery!</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


