    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a82d7afa-93fa-11e8-b94c-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a82d7afa-93fa-11e8-b94c-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2008-11-27T08:24:22</review:date>
        <review:description>I played through this game brand new. Interesting idea: Take control of characters by possessing them. This was useful when the characters were tough brutish guards and soldiers... but most of the time they were scientists or night shift security.

But the game fell flat on it&apos;s soft pink face when crash after crash made it near impossible to complete a level. Soon I was fighting the game rather than the characters in the game in order to win it.

Even at this price, pass.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>a82d7afa-93fa-11e8-b94c-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>Great idea, poor game</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">10</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a842a614-93fa-11e8-b54c-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a842a614-93fa-11e8-b54c-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2008-11-27T10:36:17</review:date>
        <review:description>Just a quick note, but this game is a must buy for anyone that hasn&apos;t played it.  I still remember beating it when it first came out, and look forward to again... I dug the install disc&apos;s out a few months ago, and reinstalled and played through on a new tablet I&apos;d purchased. Was still impressed, and then I found it on here.  I&apos;m sure I&apos;ll eventually pick it up here as well just to have a digital copy, it&apos;s that good.

I don&apos;t remember it being that hard, so not positive where that knock is coming from, but a great game regardless! Just be aware of the profanity, as this isn&apos;t one I&apos;d play at work with the volume cranked up....</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>a842a614-93fa-11e8-b54c-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Love it!</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">11</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a86eb696-92f8-11eb-9a98-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a86eb696-92f8-11eb-9a98-fa163e9aa6fa">
