    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a8fdc9f2-a916-11ea-b2d2-fa163e62c76a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a8fdc9f2-a916-11ea-b2d2-fa163e62c76a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-06-08T02:28:57</review:date>
        <review:description>Весёлое лёгкое приключение

Понравилось:
- Переработанные способности и механики. Танцы работают иначе.
- Возрос темп игры по сравнению с предыдущей частью. Мгновенно переключающиеся облики.
- Красивые арты персонажей в диалогах.
- Впервые из коробки завезли русский язык. Хороший перевод.
- Лёгкий ненавящевый юмор.
- Ввели коллектаблз значки монстров с пассивными умениями. Жаль, смысла в них нет, на геймплей особого влияние не имеют.
- Очень удобный и красивый интерфейс.
- Музыка с уклоном в ретро-псевдо-16-битную музыку. У кузнеца музыка топчик.

Не понравилось:
- Скучные персонажи: броневой барон не сравнится с оружейным бароном. Кальмарный барон стал плоским. У Скай пара реплик. Дяда уже не тот, да и Боло тоже. Введено очень много новых персонажей, в итоге очень мало времени каждому, раскрыться они не успевают.
- Не было традиционной битвы с кальмарным бароном.
- Долгие и скучные боссы. 
- Сильно упавшая сложность. Боссы проходятся на раз. Риски бутс не представляет никакой угрозы. На аренах есть сейф зоны, в которых можно сидеть не получая урона. Локации можно просто пробегать не убивая мобов, серьёзного урона они нанести не могут. Отовсюду сыпятся аптечки.
- Слабый левелдизайн. Уровни очень однообразные по механикам, при этом визуал отличный.
- Малая продолжительность игры. 

Прочее, то что не понравилось, но вкусовщина:
- По сравнению с Half Genie Hero шаг назад: 
   - обратно от тридешных уровней к плоским
   - маленькие, часто одноэкранные арены с чистым метроидванским строением мира.
   - нет таких классных уровней как гонки на коврах самолётах и уровень с похищенными принцессами.
   - нет таких боссов как ультимативный кальмарный борон плюс Риски бутс. 
- В Steam версии ачивки есть. В версии для GOG ачивки не поддерживаются. Это указано в описании игры перед покупкой, поэтому претензий нет. 

Итог: считаю Half Genie Hero вершиной серии, но и в эту часть обязательно стоит поиграть.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>a8fdc9f2-a916-11ea-b2d2-fa163e62c76a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Продолжение серии, верность традициям</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">8</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a90780d2-3052-11eb-9033-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a90780d2-3052-11eb-9033-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-11-27T03:48:34</review:date>
        <review:description>On paper, this is the ultimate &quot;heartbreaker&quot; rpg game. 
Based on the &quot;Dark eye&quot; tabletop roleplaying game (Germany&apos;s answer to Ad&amp;amp;d) the whole thing seems as generic as it gets.
Yet, somehow it clicks.
I think the respect the devs show the source material makes this one a pretty unique experience.
The Dark eye is your typical oldschool, heroic rpg. On one hand it means almost incomprehensable rulesets, but also a lot of freedom to do whatever you wish to do in this well realised, lore-rich fantasy wolrd. And the world is really endearing in it&apos;s oldschool ways. It has zero pretentions, zero edge, not a spec of cynicism. The whole thing is shamelessly, lovingly nerdy. 
It&apos;s not perfect unfortunately.
As I wrote above, the rules are rather messy. If you&apos;re not familiar with the mechanics of the Dark eye games, you&apos;ll be scratching your head a lot. The interface also doesn&apos;t help much, as it is quite convoluted. The inventory and skill pages are super easy to get lost in, and leveling up can be very confusing. Also there&apos;s practically no fast travel and the maps can be a little vague.
 Also, the story is a little impersonal this time around.
All in all, it is a little rough around the edges but if you&apos;re looking for a lovingly made, old fashioned stat-heavy heroic rpg, definitely give this one a try
 - or wait a little until GOG releases the sequel: The River of time. Which is very similar to this one, only better in every way.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>a90780d2-3052-11eb-9033-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Good, but surpassed by it&apos;s sequel.</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">25</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a925f558-8643-11ea-93e7-fa163e62c76a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a925f558-8643-11ea-93e7-fa163e62c76a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-04-24T18:52:54</review:date>
        <review:description>4 out of 5 because it´s mostly a too harshly unbalanced fight against bars and stats, fetchquesting and generally if you go pacifistic, which you will unless you use the custom difficulty sliders, you will realise it´s a pure walking sim most of the time. 

The Original was just that. Mostly walking and trading. PLG2 is just that too MOST of the time, but with reduced walking times and with sprinting and more way more combat. PLG2 is a reIMAGINING of pathologic 1. 

EXTREMELY atmopsheric story, world and philosophies, intriguing characters and a still beautiful hobo with a shotgun style hobo economy. Item spawns are smart as in, the game at certain days helps you give you enough water flasks/bottles when you need them, other items you still have to scavenge. this game, in it´s own terms without referencing pathologic 1 from now on, does many things better than most games, but also poorer than some others. 

Combat, is way improved but still janky and too stamina based. the thing about decisions decisions, decisions is a bit of a fluke in the endgame, but it does have many branches within the days from 2 to 11. Pathologic 2 plays within 12 days, each day 2 real life hrs. It is generally built with a starting point, many paths towards two/&quot;three&quot; endings. What this game does best is the world building, the mystery, the art, the sound (except weapon soundmixing), the general feeling of dread as you grow a personal attachment of these transcendental decisionmaking processes, and some characters. 

The economy is unforgiving and brutal, combat still does too. You will probably save often. You will walk alot, you will read a lot, you will hate your decisions alot . This game does one thing perfect, letting you feel like a microbe in a cosmos of fate. Immersive Sim? 100% in my book. It´s tedious, it´s beautiful, entrancing, torturous. So is framepacing, performance sometimes and the ressource grind. Exploration isn´t as rewarding as you´d expect either.

Unique!</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>a925f558-8643-11ea-93e7-fa163e62c76a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Ascension isn´t a Deus Ex Monopoly</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a93a24c8-93fc-11e8-9f57-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/a93a24c8-93fc-11e8-9f57-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2009-02-17T22:33:00</review:date>
        <review:description>Freespace 2 , it&apos;s space-combat as it best.
Sequel to the aclaimed Freespace, it take everything that made the first one a great game and make it better. With graphics that&apos;s still take comparison to younger title like Darkstar one  the game deliver an experience that few (If none) other game have been able to.
Im talking about fast spaced combat with an overall management of your ship and something more than aim-shoot-repeat style of gameplay, coupled with large scale battle that will make you shiver with excitement . And adding to the experience is the well balanced sounds effect and music.
With a solid story with interesting twist and the fact your accomplishement and failure weight on the future missions.
It&apos;s worthy of your bucks, and a must buy if you like a game that take advantage of your Joystick.

And with a moding communitty still on the go and updating new content every month, You are gonna still be able to enjoy : Multiplayer, High-def graphics and new mission.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>a93a24c8-93fc-11e8-9f57-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>A milestones in Space-sim.</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


