    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/ac837c26-4afe-11ec-ab6c-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/ac837c26-4afe-11ec-ab6c-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-11-21T21:10:21</review:date>
        <review:description>I just want to keep this as brief as possible and as simple as i can be. During the tutorial moment, i cannot figure out how to turn my ship then i found out that i can only turn using the numpad which it is not even exist on my laptop. I cannot contain my anger because i realized that all of the ships in the game are mostly blocks of cube that somehow got duct taped together. Lastly, even though it&apos;s a 1999 game, it cannot even compare with the game from 1994 which is a huge disappointment in my opinion.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">12</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>ac837c26-4afe-11ec-ab6c-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:rating>
        <review:title>Outdated cannot go with Modern</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/ac861b5e-2938-11eb-bc43-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/ac861b5e-2938-11eb-bc43-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-11-18T02:54:55</review:date>
        <review:description>I don&apos;t own it as of now, but I used to play it on many various occasions. Once, I even managed to finish it. ( It was kind of a paladin build, where I focused melee, but had tons of healing, and shielding magic.). To describe how much this game became a thorn in my side, the music from this game plays in my head when something disappointing happens in my life. This is by far my most hated piece of digital garbage; I&apos;ve ever had the discomfort of playing.

On the surface, seems okay, but the longer you play you notice glaring problems. Like, why does mage, or archer focused abilities even exist, if you won’t ever, and I&apos;m being absolutely honest. YOU WILL NEVER have a pure wizard, or pure archer build that actually works in this game. The enemies come at you in massive swarms. You cannot by design, be a pure anything, but a fighter. Fighter can do anything he wants. 

The music is a drowning, boring loop of shit. At first you might actually enjoy it, for the first few seconds, but then it gets mad boring real fast. Its cool there&apos;s a lot of skills, but you won’t be using most of them. Basically 80% of the skills are not viable, especially the summoning skills. Oh my god, it&apos;s horrible. You summon a thing, and it drains your mana endlessly until you banish it or it drains your mana completely. So, if you wanted a summoner build tough luck. 

Charisma is only useful at the start, later on it’s pointless. It&apos;s basically the illusion of choice, you get all this cool stuff, but the game only wants you to be a dumb warrior. That&apos;s about it. Also, don&apos;t bother power game, and train yourself, monsters level up with you. So, chances are, the game will be EVEN HARDER, if you try and level yourself up too fast.
</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>ac861b5e-2938-11eb-bc43-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:rating>
        <review:title>It&apos;s a torture device not a game.</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/aca79868-e8d3-11ec-89d3-42010a340c25 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/aca79868-e8d3-11ec-89d3-42010a340c25">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
