    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/af645d0a-9401-11e8-afe7-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/af645d0a-9401-11e8-afe7-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2010-01-06T14:11:24</review:date>
        <review:description>I remember when I was young, at the time when PC&apos;s were just some huge greys machines on your desk, with a big awful screen, my father had MDK on his computer. And when I played it, I was completeley terrified. The robot&apos;s screams were so......so.......they gave me so much thrills !!!! I never finished the first level &amp;gt;&amp;lt; An some years later, I played again, and I just finished this god dam first level with these god dam robots (which show their asses ^^) in 5 minutes and I discovered......that it was not the game but just a demo..........I was so disapointed. That was about 10 years ago.
 And now, thanks to GOG.com, I re-discovered this amazing action game !!! Really, I didn&apos;t realise that but MDK was sooooo funny !! And so cool !!! Don&apos;t hesitate and buy the pack, it&apos;s really worth it !!</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>af645d0a-9401-11e8-afe7-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Awesome !!</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/af6516fc-c802-11e8-9daa-00163e4e60cc -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/af6516fc-c802-11e8-9daa-00163e4e60cc">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2018-10-04T21:24:09</review:date>
        <review:description>For many years I&apos;ve waited for this game to be available for newer computers and finally it&apos;s come at last! While this game has aged a bit, it is still a solid adventure game with a good atmosphere. </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>af6516fc-c802-11e8-9daa-00163e4e60cc</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>At Last!</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">13</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/af6f6a4e-2b4d-11ea-ae48-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/af6f6a4e-2b4d-11ea-ae48-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-12-30T23:45:24</review:date>
        <review:description>Non-existent story and childish attempts at being mature aside, it&apos;s a genuinely solid retro shooter that introduced some interesting ideas for the time.

The sidekick A.I. isn&apos;t perfect and gets stuck sometimes, which may be annoying but for the most part, it works fine and these guys are actually helpful in combat. Optional objectives and ability to interact with NPCs is also pretty cool but I thought it was under-utilized. Probably the first optional mission is the most intricate way this whole system was implemented but as soon as you acquire some useful guns, side activities become very rare and you&apos;ll be spending most of your time squeezing gats till the clip is empty.

Regardless, it&apos;s an entertaining Quake 2-era FPS which deserves its place among the classics of the genre. The very same studio was later renamed to Gray Matter and went on to make an excellent Return To Castle Wolfenstein and you can feel some of this game in Kingpin.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>af6f6a4e-2b4d-11ea-ae48-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>This is the first time I played this</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/af806710-37b5-11ec-a555-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/af806710-37b5-11ec-a555-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-10-28T09:10:01</review:date>
        <review:description>Ich habe habe 15 Jahre drauf gewartet, dass des Spiel DRM frei wird. Danke an GOG.
Aber ich habe auch Kritik.

Folgende Punkte hat der Entwickler nicht hinbekommen.
 
 - Auflösung auf max 1920x1080
 - Fenstermodus, man sollte zwischen Vollbild und Fenstermodus wechseln, weil sonst des halb Bild den Bilschirm verdeckt.
 - Die eher schwammige Steuerung, sollte überarbeitet werden,
 
Jetzt sind mir folgende Bugs immer noch aufgefallen.

 - Wenn man ein Auto klaut, dann fliegt immer die Tür ab.
 - des Bild ist 4:3 mit 2 schwarzen Balken links rechts, das kann man auch nicht ändern.

Wenn man diese Bugs als auch Fehler behebt, dann bekommt des Spiel bei gog 2 Sterne mehr.

Sonst wäre es ein super Spiel, da es jetzt DRM frei ist, kann ich es endlich mal durch spielen .... Sollte aber von gog noch verbesser werden.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>af806710-37b5-11ec-a555-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>Spiel ist gut aber verbesserungswürdig</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/afcb6692-b2e4-11e8-85f8-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/afcb6692-b2e4-11e8-85f8-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2018-07-07T04:46:25</review:date>
        <review:description>Realmente um filme interativo. Não espere fazer escolhas ou explorar o cenário, pois as interações disponiveis não permitem isso, basicamnete a única jogabilidade é andar e apontar para os objetos que o personagem precisa interagir. O visual é incrível e a ambientação ajuda muito, existem alguns momentos de suspense e até terror, porém nada tão impressionante.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>afcb6692-b2e4-11e8-85f8-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:rating>
        <review:title>Filme interativo</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/afe8030e-8667-11e9-87e6-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/afe8030e-8667-11e9-87e6-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-06-04T04:25:50</review:date>
        <review:description>This game is a testament to lackluster indie Metroidvania.  While I give it 9/10 for graphics and sound, and I love the character design (beautiful and inspired) the gameplay is quite simply broken.  The level layouts are poorly designed, enemies early in the game aren&apos;t simply hard, but in fact cheap and punishing.  Playing this game is an exercise in frustration and while I repeatedly tried to enjoy it (and originally blamed my skills) I eventually began to see that this is just a case of bad game design.  The developers did not spend enough time studying the gameplay mechanics of SOTN or any other Castelvania game to understand what makes those titles great.  Enemy placement is terrible, hit detection is off, and the game is just cheap as hell in its mechanics.

 the default control setup is agony to use.  And even though it&apos;s listed in the options, there is NO USB CONTROLLER SUPPORT.  wth.  I had to look up on the forums here to see that the game was lying about this.  No scanline option, either.  

and the main character can&apos;t dash.  This might be a minor quibble, but I think all modern Metroidvania titles should have this option.

I thought it was worth a try at five dollars, but now I want a refund.   #regrets.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">9</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>afe8030e-8667-11e9-87e6-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>broken gameplay and no controller support</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


