    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/b46662ea-d5b6-11eb-8694-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/b46662ea-d5b6-11eb-8694-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-06-25T16:10:25</review:date>
        <review:description>========== 2 звезды (3 с натяжкой) ==========
________________________________________________

Задумка интересна с переключением во времени. На этом интересное заканчивается. 
Игровой процесс немного скучноват. Ботаникула намного интереснее в плане прохождения и вызванных эмоций.
Порой игра немного раздражала из-за повторения прохождения одно и того же в случае смерти героя (чувствовался коридорный сценарий). Местами чувствуется заторможенность игрового процесса с переключением фонаря времени.
Тот же &quot;FAR: Lone Sails&quot; тоже коридорный, но наличие атмосферы игры включая и музыкальную составляющую - на голову выше и интереснее.
Без большой скидки это брать смысла нет.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>b46662ea-d5b6-11eb-8694-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>Игра коридорная и так себе :\</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/b472bed4-93fe-11e8-b069-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/b472bed4-93fe-11e8-b069-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2009-08-13T01:34:09</review:date>
        <review:description>This is a great space sim. I remember when I first played the demo on cd that came with a gaming magazine years ago. This game stand the test of time and is just enjoyable now as it was then. The graphics and environment are great as is the storyline. If you like space genre or science fiction this is a must have.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>b472bed4-93fe-11e8-b069-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Freespace 2</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/b497f40a-84c6-11ea-9740-fa163e62c76a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/b497f40a-84c6-11ea-9740-fa163e62c76a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-04-22T21:25:55</review:date>
        <review:description>The Evil Within 1 received mixed reviews, and I was one of them who rated it as rather not that good. The horror aspect was terrifying from the start, but the gameplay itself lacked in too many ways to excite me.

So here we are with part two of the series and to state the most important: the sequel is better in almost any aspect than its predecessor. The horror remains well placed, the visuals are a pleasure to look at, &apos;Union&apos; is well-designed, and the story is well-presented. You have various gameplay mechanics, like stealth, crafting, weapon upgrades, and of course, shooting.

But why do I rate with only three stars out of five when all of this is so impressive? Because sometimes the whole is more than the sum of its parts. And sometimes the whole is less than the sum of its parts. Unfortunately, for The Evil Within 2 applies the latter. It just doesn&apos;t do for me.

But this is only my conclusion, and I&apos;m sure the game does very well for others. So don&apos;t hesitate to give it a try.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>b497f40a-84c6-11ea-9740-fa163e62c76a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:rating>
        <review:title>Way more enjoyable than the first one</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


