    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/bb957d20-c728-11e8-9c60-00163e4e60cc -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/bb957d20-c728-11e8-9c60-00163e4e60cc">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2018-10-03T19:23:59</review:date>
        <review:description>Only the English version is included in this release, so this is my rating for the quality of this launch. The Spanish version had cinema quality voiceover from the guy who dubs Harrison Ford in the Star Wars movies, and that&apos;s missing here. And suspect players from other territories are not happy either.

Localized versions exist. But GOG, as usual, doesn&apos;t care that much about non-English releases.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">34</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>bb957d20-c728-11e8-9c60-00163e4e60cc</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:rating>
        <review:title>English only</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">31</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/bbb32c06-b21a-11ea-a672-fa163e62c76a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/bbb32c06-b21a-11ea-a672-fa163e62c76a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-06-19T13:50:47</review:date>
        <review:description>I&apos;m only a few hours in the Soroborean DLC, and I can tell that it looks like content that should have been there since launch and completes the game. It seems like they put a lot of work into it.
The new area is fantastic and feels bigger/fuller than the rest, although 99% of the time it seems to be winter and snow.
The new mechanics are great. There are new enemies, potions, weapons, equipment, recipes, etc. The music is also great.
The new dungeon is huge, labyrinthine, and has tougher enemies. This DLC is worth it only for this dungeon.
It also has its flaws that need to be polished. Recommended if you like the base game.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>bbb32c06-b21a-11ea-a672-fa163e62c76a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Great DLC</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">54</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/bbc51a68-3dda-11ec-8fcd-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/bbc51a68-3dda-11ec-8fcd-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-11-05T03:50:20</review:date>
        <review:description>The best way to imagine playing this game is like you&apos;ve discovered a lost version of MediEvil on the PS2, given an HD treatment. It has the melee combat, the environmental puzzles and navigation and the cartoonish spooky atmosphere you&apos;d imagine it to have.

It has a solid art style and direction that feels like something you&apos;ve seen before, but it does enough to distinguish it as its own, like Overlord (2009) or Subcon Forest from A Hat in Time, the music is &quot;spookified&quot; versions of classical music that sounds like would&apos;ve fit in, again, like Subcon Forest.

Everything feels familiar, but it doesn&apos;t feel like it&apos;s rip off another game. Everything fits well, has variety and intentional direction. There&apos;s clear passion and effort woven into it, and it&apos;s difficult to deny or ignore it. I wasn&apos;t blown away, because I&apos;ve experienced way too many games of a similar type, but that&apos;s fine. It can feel unrefined at times, but that&apos;s to be expected. I do wish it would figure out its target audience, as that&apos;s the one part that feels directionless. And the barriers in some levels need to be more obvious, or at least use unique models; some fencing was used interchangeably as an invisible barrier, and some was just level dressing.

I was able to get it on a sale, and for myself, I felt like the price I got it for was more than fair. GOG didn&apos;t properly track total playtime, and while I missed 3 collectible items, after getting 100% of the game done, it totaled to roughly 4 hours. Everything is straight forward with little in the way of branching out. It was enjoyable though, and I couldn&apos;t ask for much more.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>bbc51a68-3dda-11ec-8fcd-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Short yet Enjoyable Action Platformer</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/bc05dc5e-aef8-11eb-9912-fa163e3a9b6e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/bc05dc5e-aef8-11eb-9912-fa163e3a9b6e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-05-07T08:54:49</review:date>
        <review:description>The message of the game is simple: workers are squeezed out day after day, no paycheck raise, nothing. It’s time for someone to take matters into his own hands. And this someone happens to be the game player :)

The game has simple pixel graphics, yet enough for what it is.
It has an arcade vibe, simple to control, what do you want more? It is playable with mouse + keyboard or controller/gamepad.

Didn&apos;t encounter any bugs.

I liked it and fully recommend it.

Played on: Ryzen 1600AF, 32 GB RAM, Geforce 1650, Windows 10 64-bit Home, SATA SSD</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">15</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>bc05dc5e-aef8-11eb-9912-fa163e3a9b6e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Action game with some strategy elements</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">12</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/bc3b2440-7def-11e9-bfdc-00163e4e60cc -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/bc3b2440-7def-11e9-bfdc-00163e4e60cc">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-05-24T09:47:02</review:date>
        <review:description>This is a story-driven-survival-arthouse with a lot of dialogues and decision-making. It&apos;s really one of a kind.

Art style is both dark and beautiful.
Lore is incredibly deep and complex.
Dialogues are very elaborate and constantly mock and manipulate you.

Gameplay mostly consists of walking from place to place, talking to people and trying to survive.
Unlike in other &quot;survival&quot; games, here survival mechanics make sense and affect everything you do instead of just wasting your time. 
By the way, time will never be on your side. Each ingame day you got multiple tasks you will have to complete in order to save people, but you will also have to stay alive, and each day is more difficult than the other. 
Decisions are also tough and getting tougher with time. You have to be very careful with what you say and do.
The game does a good job at keeping you under pressure all the time. You can&apos;t relax even for  a minute.

This is a unique experience I really recommend trying.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">11</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>bc3b2440-7def-11e9-bfdc-00163e4e60cc</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Deep, beautiful and terrifying</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">189</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/bc4c0b58-f7b9-11ea-9164-fa163e62c76a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/bc4c0b58-f7b9-11ea-9164-fa163e62c76a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-09-16T04:12:48</review:date>
        <review:description>Fun, I got the hang of it really quickly. Worth about £10-15 for the short duration, has replayability with the characters and challenges which I&apos;ll probably play. My only gripe is that I was expecting a bunch of different tracks at least one per level and while they are different it&apos;s still kinda the same.

The items are kinda unbalanced as well as one item can just make you invincible or demolish all enemies and make any gun type pointless. However this doesn&apos;t detract from the game very much.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>bc4c0b58-f7b9-11ea-9164-fa163e62c76a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Decent</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">28</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/bc5b53f2-aa41-11eb-b385-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/bc5b53f2-aa41-11eb-b385-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-05-01T08:54:47</review:date>
        <review:description>Well, I don&apos;t know why people get offended by this game, surely was a controversial giveaway but a giveaway non the less!
Well I haven&apos;t finish it yet, but it&apos;s a really fun game, the combat is fast and the levels are short, there are different types of enemies that add a component of variety and strategic to the game cause you have to know how to react to reach the end of the level with most of your workers safe. 
In the game you can also play as the policeman an try to stop the riots. 
The game has a political message that brainwashes you and try to make you a communist? Nah, that&apos;s BS. Well now I have to sleep, tomorrow I will take the factory with my comrades and we will destroy the demonic capitalism!!!!</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">48</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>bc5b53f2-aa41-11eb-b385-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>It&apos;s a fun game!!!!</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">40</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/bc80f206-5669-11ea-9925-fa163e62c76a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/bc80f206-5669-11ea-9925-fa163e62c76a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-02-23T20:24:32</review:date>
        <review:description>The &quot;sewer&quot; environment eventually introduces moving platforms and levers, turning the game into a puzzle platformer with some enemies. The situation greatly worsens when reaching &quot;the internet&quot; with the aforementioned elements and its signature features (seams of electricity, mines and shields you have to deactivate). When you&apos;re first given an assault rifle, dual-wielding (only possible with the pistols and uzis) becomes increasingly nonviable and the ramped up damage levels permanently change the game.

My Friend Pedro is consistently enjoyable through the first two worlds and pure platforming elements first appear in the chapter &quot;Pedro&apos;s World&quot;, which plays without combat for a while as do two levels of the Internet. Issues related to the platforming elements are mainly the obscure animation quality and unusual behavior on slopes (Pedro gains close to no height). Functional at best.

There are two extremely cliched boss fights (of four in total?), one with glowing weak spots and heavily repeating optimal strategy, the other is nothing but an occasionally-evading bullet sponge in essence.

Additionally, the soundtrack consists of repeating, very similar pulsating rhythms and has absolutely no appeal to me in or outside the game. One of the rare instancew outside of the licensed &quot;playlist&quot; OSTs in gaming I considered disabling music entirely.

When judged within context, the puzzle and platforming sections are universally god-awful. The shooting mechanics provide an occasional highlight, but the early levels support the gunplay with essentially no real roadblocks and endorse my theory that this game was artificially extended to reach the playtime of around four hours.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>bc80f206-5669-11ea-9925-fa163e62c76a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:rating>
        <review:title>Greatly degrades from the sewers onwards</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">20</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/bc895b7a-fa06-11eb-94b7-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/bc895b7a-fa06-11eb-94b7-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-08-10T21:14:00</review:date>
        <review:description>Most ppl. write about the single player mode, which is decent for a 2009 game. Voice acting and music gets the game setting right and makes the game memerable and almost a classic. But actually the LAN mode of the game is the real beauty for me. The maps are very well constructed and balanced in terms of weapon drops and tactics. The player creator is very versatile.  And the different gamemodes eg. bagman is alot of fun. It all bodes for high adreanaline action. 

Highly recomedable.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>bc895b7a-fa06-11eb-94b7-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Most rewarding multiplayer games</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/bca9002e-f6ab-11ea-be48-fa163edf6d96 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/bca9002e-f6ab-11ea-be48-fa163edf6d96">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-09-14T20:00:05</review:date>
        <review:description>i have this game on steam, after playing for 20 hours or so the enemies start to disappear if you dont loot every item the enemies drop, something to do with limit of the loot bags? you fave to go back to the old areas to pick up the old loot , but even after that i kept getting the same bug  after a while

apart from the bug i would rate this 3/5 , very entertaining and fluid combat, but the level of difficulty is VERY low, classes are pretty broken and somewhat boring to the end, and the crafting is crazy OP, lot of quests in the game which are pretty good and different , but again in the and start to feel like a drag because of useless rewards. if you have played this 8 years ago its pretty much the same game , so i wouldnt recommend this to those , hope there will be modding added , i see this having a lot of potential this way</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>bca9002e-f6ab-11ea-be48-fa163edf6d96</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:rating>
        <review:title>game breaking bugs</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">11</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/bcb6bfd4-9a3c-11e8-becc-00163e97122a -->

