    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/bf6a2914-b1b1-11e8-9afb-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/bf6a2914-b1b1-11e8-9afb-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2016-05-17T01:39:18</review:date>
        <review:description>A few thoughts:

This game is advertised as &quot;RPG RTS hybrid&quot; but, like, a lot of games that have tried to run under that it is more akin to a tactical game. Really in line with the Geneforge series except just remove ALL of the RPG leveling mechanics. So . . . You know, a tactical game only.

There&apos;s also issues with representation. Pretty much our story is littered with white males. So, just imagine a world where about 9/10ths of the population is male and there is no variation in skin tone, except for the random minor character. Yes, it breaks immersion. Yes, there is no f***ing good reason for it devs.

I may write a longer review, but for now . . . Go back and play Geneforge if you haven&apos;t for awhile.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">80</review:downvotes>
