    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/bfaac9fa-dec3-11eb-ae56-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/bfaac9fa-dec3-11eb-ae56-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-07-07T04:36:28</review:date>
        <review:description>poor performance. I&apos;m well above min specs, as I&apos;m sure most people are, but the game had dipped under 60 FPS multiple times. Not really cool.

mundane and simplistic mechanics devoid of strategy or intelligent design. You literally just spam attack button over and over while holding a directional key. It&apos;s not interesting 

story is whack. It starts with &quot;capitalism bad&quot; and then apparently you just committ mass violence and that somehow solves all problems. Leftism in a nutshell I guess.

I resorted to trying to speed run and seeing how much combat I can skip to go straight to the end of a level, but I got soft locked and was forced to just exit back to the main menu to start over. Not sure if it&apos;s a bug or something. I think the game gets confused if you stop killing people. not cool!

pros: the art is great.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">28</review:downvotes>
