    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/bfd09094-da28-11eb-b6c0-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/bfd09094-da28-11eb-b6c0-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-07-01T07:56:51</review:date>
        <review:description>This game makes the mechanics of the other game more interesting. Also, has new additions.
Now the story develops ins a small open world where you have many possibilities. Go to point A to Point B in a non-linear way. Enjoy what the world has to offer such as new weapons, recolection of green goo to upgrade Sebastian abilities and even some side quest which you need to find in your exploration.
The story, despite being kinda cliche, is still pretty good and entertaining.
If you played the first The Evil Within, you will definitely like this one, and so much more.</review:description>
