    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/c0004430-946f-11e8-9cf5-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/c0004430-946f-11e8-9cf5-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2011-06-30T13:26:08</review:date>
        <review:description>I haven&apos;t played it all that much yet but so far this is what I&apos;ve been looking for.  I grew up playing X-Wing Alliance (I never played X-wing or Tie fighter) and I loved it.  I&apos;ve been looking for a game similar to that and this is it.  I like how it is complicated with energy management and subsystem targeting and wing management.  I was very pleasantly surprised at how similar this game was to my beloved x-wing game. 
The modding community for this game is also quite insane.  There are graphics packs and total conversions for almost every sci-fi show out there. 
While I don&apos;t always play space sim games, whenever I get the urge this one will be at the top of my list.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>c0004430-946f-11e8-9cf5-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Where has this game been my whole life?</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/c0120468-9451-11e8-a63a-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/c0120468-9451-11e8-a63a-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2010-12-01T19:11:26</review:date>
        <review:description>This game is unlike others.  It&apos;s easy to get into.  And hard to leave.

The plot is railroaded and linear, but the pacing is perfection.  The story is great - reading the FreeSpace bible shows the developers really managed to get most of what they planned into the game (a rare feat).

I know some people dislike a railroaded plot, but I loved it here - it was like being the protagonist in a well-written novelette.  I can&apos;t change the story, but I wouldn&apos;t want to; I could only make it worse.  The story captures the emotions, and leads the player along a journey which, surprisingly for a game, contains a moral lesson.

The early game ends feeling on the defensive against what could only be described as a god.  But, slowly, as humanity understands their technology, the god is deconstructed, until we feel we are their equal.  And then, the game enters the final act - our hubris at believing ourselves equal to god destroys us, and shatters our foolish &quot;myth of humanity everlasting&quot; (a great quote from the opening of FreeSpace 2).

Though technologically inferior to FreeSpace 2, the lesson on the folly of pride, and the perfect pacing places this game, in my opinion, well above the sequel.  This game captured my fantasy and emotions like few other - placing it in the same class as Half Life, Deus Ex, and Baldur&apos;s Gate.  A great game - buy it.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>c0120468-9451-11e8-a63a-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Fantastic FreeSpace</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/c01ad20a-b2f6-11e8-bbdc-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/c01ad20a-b2f6-11e8-bbdc-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2018-08-25T15:53:44</review:date>
        <review:description>kinda weird since you get classic BG soundtrack by buying BG EE and those few new tracks are not worthy that much</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">11</review:downvotes>
