        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">9</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/c137fb3e-dde2-11ec-8115-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/c137fb3e-dde2-11ec-8115-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-05-27T20:30:51</review:date>
        <review:description>But you know what sells better instead of this perverted shistfest? Yea, you guessed it right. Good Old Games, not Bad Perverted Games for Degen.

Stop selling trash, look at your goodam wishes for once and fulfill them, the big ones; bring Halo, Elden Ring, Dark Souls, rED dEAD, CoD, GTA, Diablo... and Skyrim, Those will sell x10 or even more than this things. Bring them already and stop bringing this degenerative shite for pervs. 

You want money? You can get it by making the right deals and bringing the right stuff people have been rooting for for years, not porn sims. That I can assure you. Good old Games is your name, right? Or now it has changed to Depraved Immoral Games? W.T.F.

Put your shit together. Still waiting for Prototype, a game old as hell that should have been here months/years ago, i bet Activ doesn&apos;t have any issue giving you the license to sell it, and  as far as I am aware you are doing fine economically. So what&apos;s the hold up? 

Cyberpunk sold like cupcakes, the debuckle you pulled gave you free marketing over it at the cost of your reputation, makng more moeny for you but loosing all the trust earned from your past and the creative director of the Witcher 3 among other creative leads. Which means for you, new stuff, less money to pay, more advertising of your products and a new study to go against. And probably better. 

GoG sells well, The Witcher 3 even better, your debuckle has given you free advertising for years. where is the good stuff, what the hell are you doing CD/GoG? </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">26</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>c137fb3e-dde2-11ec-8115-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:rating>
        <review:title>BIG TITS SELL. </review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/c18ed918-df3b-11ec-bfef-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/c18ed918-df3b-11ec-bfef-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-05-29T13:40:28</review:date>
        <review:description>A delightful building game and well worth getting, the ablity to customise your character as well as a building game to have combat, although not the main focus and the gather of resources is wonderful.

Even though I&apos;m not finished with the story it&apos;s a delight to play and see where it&apos;s going.

Well worth your time, even though patches seem to had been stunted from other platforms.
I can&apos;t wait unti.

My Time At Sandrock joins this on my playlist collection</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
