    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/c1ac3b88-0a62-11ec-9438-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/c1ac3b88-0a62-11ec-9438-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-08-31T16:53:01</review:date>
        <review:description>Regardless of graphics and some issues (all is forgiven - early dev stage) I don&apos;t see much in this game that would convince me to choose this one instead of cities skylines. 

The mechanics and what you can build is simmilar to those it CS yet less intuitive. 
From what is being said to be implemented into the game it also sounds like features alredy present in other games.

What I am trying to say is that this game looks like a few people project - both on graphics and variety of options in the game. If you want to compete with popular city building games you need to have something that is interesting to the player or maybe rethink the concept. Best of luck!

 </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>c1ac3b88-0a62-11ec-9438-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>what does it have to offer?</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/c1d32538-bbc3-11eb-9a71-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/c1d32538-bbc3-11eb-9a71-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-05-23T15:38:20</review:date>
        <review:description>I&apos;ve just finished this amazing game/VN and my answer would be &quot;no&quot;. Each location, each poster, the story, the characters, the dialogues, the soundtrack and of course the rain ... if you are even remotely a fan of the film noir genre you won&apos;t be disappointed. Of course this still is a VN at heart but unlike the usual VN it does not feel this way. It offers a few mini games and puzzles, gives you the opportunity to chose which hotspots you want to click on first or which dialogue you want to hear next ... last but not least there are the interrogation and conclusion scenes and the very few action scenes in which you have to shoot (don&apos;t worry - you can always retry if you fail). Then there is the fact that depending on the dialogues you chose you might unlock additional codex entrys (background of the universe the game plays in) and you can also collect some collectibles more or less hidden inside the scenes. However, even if this would just be the usual VN it would still be great because of the unusual artwork, the great characters and most of all the voice over they must have stripped right out of some noir movie since it is so spot on. Along with the atmosphere the mystery itself also unfolds nicely and the solution might surprise some. If the devs should decide to do a sequel I will definitely buy it on release. Highly recommended for every fan of the genre. </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>c1d32538-bbc3-11eb-9a71-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Could it be even more &quot;Noir&quot;?</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/c1f6cfe8-1c89-11ec-9234-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/c1f6cfe8-1c89-11ec-9234-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-09-23T19:17:33</review:date>
        <review:description>Bear in mind that this game was released in 1999... it was and may still be a truly awesome game. Right off the bat, let&apos;s get it out of the way, gog has done it dirty bacause Freespace 2 has been freeware for many years now (try fsoinstaller dot com). That said, this version deserves 0 stars because not only does it NOT WORK it actually wrecked my gog galaxy installation somehow. Compatibility modes, turn this on, that off, yell at it - nope. No work. And then Galaxy stopped working so bad not even a fresh install got it functional so &apos;Dear GOG, you&apos;ve really screwed this up in every way possible&apos;.    (eventually got galaxy to work again, can&apos;t remember how though.) 2 stars just for keeping awareness of this legendary title alive though.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">12</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>c1f6cfe8-1c89-11ec-9234-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>Horrible port</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/c1f9edec-b29f-11e8-83b2-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/c1f9edec-b29f-11e8-83b2-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2018-01-25T00:32:02</review:date>
        <review:description>any developer that puts out a free demo of their game gets my vote, and while there are mechanics in the game that are missing from the demo, what i played was enough to convince me to buy it. i do recommend giving it a thorough playthrough, as initially i was so-so about the game, but after spending time messing about i appreciated it more.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>c1f9edec-b29f-11e8-83b2-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>One for the sneak and steal lovers</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">14</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/c20ea452-5d76-11ea-beb8-fa163e62c76a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/c20ea452-5d76-11ea-beb8-fa163e62c76a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-03-03T19:45:23</review:date>
        <review:description>Rimworld — это больше 460 часов игры. А это топ-5 в моём списке игр, по количеству проведенного за игрой времени.

Лучшая реиграбельность — партии никогда не будут похожи (по крайней мере у меня).

Каждая номерная версия даже альфы привносила многое в игру.

После релиза игра стала ещё лучше.

Этот обзор не в  моей стандартной манере, т.к. я всегда пишу минусы игры. Тут их нету. Даже простая графика, это плюс этой игры.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>c20ea452-5d76-11ea-beb8-fa163e62c76a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>топ-4 любимых игр</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">14</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/c2135e32-cdf2-11eb-b784-fa163ed508dc -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/c2135e32-cdf2-11eb-b784-fa163ed508dc">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
