    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/c9f2f4b2-18b4-11eb-9a24-fa163e7e880a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/c9f2f4b2-18b4-11eb-9a24-fa163e7e880a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-10-28T02:30:32</review:date>
        <review:description>I just entered the last level. And I can&apos;t wait to finish the game. First I want to acknowledge the many references to Archer/Marvel/StarWars(Level 5 Cantina Band?) and so many more. Really cool. The dev and I seem to share the same sense of humour. The game itself is a really cool 3D platformer that feels like the games from the early 2000s and also makes me feel like I am ten years old again (good times, good times). Really reminds me of Medievil, Spyro, Crash Bandicoot, Sly Cooper...you name it. Could be the nostalgia writing this, but let&apos;s get to the the details:
The gameplay is just awesome. Minor flaws that will be patched probably. But controls and gameplay loop are easy to pick up but the game is still challenging in a way. Didn&apos;t have that much fun in a long time.
Story is cool. Not too deep and not to shallow. Just right for a game like this.
Soundtrack is also pretty awesome. Many classic themes ported into an interesting halloween version. Of course the game is too short to have a big array of different tracks. But it is more than enough here.
Graphics are stylized and really fit perfectly for the game. The dev really uses light and shadow to create a Halloween worthy atmosphere.
Speaking of atmosphere: I can&apos;t describe how he pulled it off, but the halloween-spooky thing is nailed here.
There are very few bugs. The game runs really well (a few FPS drops here and there, but most the time 60FPS+) on an i5 from 2013 and an RX570 4GB (no not my main rig). Apart from that I did not have any sort of problems.

Respect to the dev! I really wish the game was much longer and I hope there will be more content (DLCs/Episodes/Addons/Successor -&amp;gt; give me an open world like in the Sly Cooper games). There is so much that could be done here. Right now if you&apos;re not a die hard platformer fan, Pumpkin Jack could be a bit pricey for the current content (depending on your region) but I think it is totally worth it. If you do not buy it now, definitely get it on sale.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>c9f2f4b2-18b4-11eb-9a24-fa163e7e880a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>A surprise to be sure, but a welcome one</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/ca2a8a32-f9e0-11ea-99b6-fa163e7ab9c9 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/ca2a8a32-f9e0-11ea-99b6-fa163e7ab9c9">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-09-18T21:57:24</review:date>
        <review:description>I love this game. My only complaint is that there aren&apos;t more stages. I&apos;m a sucker for metal, and shooting baddies to the beat of brutal, headbanging metal is just a great experience. The soundtrack is amazing, every song is very well composed. The performance on the guitar is amazing. The game is as much about the gameplay as it is about the music. If you&apos;re not into metal, you probably won&apos;t like the music and therefore you won&apos;t like the game. And about the complaints that the music is all the same, it&apos;s really not, you just need to have an ear for metal. Also, it&apos;s like an album, and if you&apos;ve ever listened to any album by a single artist, the songs usually use similar keys, instruments, tunings, and composition styles. Normally, if an album has songs that sound very different from each other, it&apos;s because they were composed by different people. The soundtrack was composed and performed by the same 2 people.

Difficulty:
I would say that, this is probably one of the most forgiving rogue-likes I&apos;ve ever played. Sure, I struggled when I first played on Easy mode, but eventually you get used to the gameplay and shooting+dodgeing becomes pretty easy to manage. Even Hard mode is not that much more difficult, there are more rooms, more enemies, and the AI seems to be smarter, but they have the same HP as in Easy. As long as you can dodge and shoot, it&apos;s easy. There are no I-frames from taking damage as far as I can tell.

RNG:
The game uses a luck mechanic, so you can influence drops by increasing your luck stat. It may not be necessary though, as there are only so many items in the game, you will quickly learn what&apos;s good and what isn&apos;t. Enemies attacks don&apos;t seem to be beholden to RNG either.

Wepons:
So, I won&apos;t spoil what weapons are in the game, but just expect Doom-like weapons. There isn&apos;t a very large selection to choose from, so I recommend experimenting early on and trying out different weapons rather than just B-lining to the final stage.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>ca2a8a32-f9e0-11ea-99b6-fa163e7ab9c9</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Amazing Rhythm-FPS-Rogue-like</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/ca409570-d0b2-11ec-aa3e-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/ca409570-d0b2-11ec-aa3e-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-05-11T01:44:45</review:date>
        <review:description>С огромным удовольствием начал играть, но насладиться не могу. Игра вылетает каждые минут 5.

Если работает интернет, то игра при запуске обращается к странице 404. А после второго обращения к этой странице (минут через 4-5) вылетает.
Если играть без WIFI и интернета, то игра вылетает сразу же при запуске! Играть невозможно.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">13</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>ca409570-d0b2-11ec-aa3e-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>Игра постоянно вылетает на mac.</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/ca474f16-b269-11e8-b911-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/ca474f16-b269-11e8-b911-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2017-10-02T13:40:07</review:date>
        <review:description>Pour commencer, il vous faudra environ 15 heures pour boucler complètement l&apos;extension.
C&apos;est un contenu qui n&apos;a pas pour ambition de corriger le jeu de base, c&apos;est avant tout un add-on là pour que la nouvelle équipe de Reality Pump se fasse les crocs. Et si effectivement on y retrouve beaucoup d&apos;éléments et d&apos;assets issus du jeu de base et son excellent add-on, force est de constater que le travail est très correct, avec une histoire assez longue et intéressante à suivre avec un très bon travail sur les quêtes secondaires notamment.

Désormais mieux fini, on ne peut plus vraiment se plaindre des bugs, reste un équilibrage qui rend l&apos;expérience globalement trop facile et le fait que c&apos;est juste du &quot;more of the same&quot; mais n&apos;est-ce pas ce qu&apos;on demande à un add-on à l&apos;origine ?

En tout cas pour son petit prix, Call of the Tenebrae est vraiment un contenu intéressant, mais il faut avoir aimé le jeu de base, évidemment.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">19</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>ca474f16-b269-11e8-b911-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:rating>
        <review:title>Add-on solide</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">9</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


