    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/cd35cf88-3a33-11ea-8ba4-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/cd35cf88-3a33-11ea-8ba4-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-01-18T22:47:54</review:date>
        <review:description>A very short (2,5h if you do absolutely everything) story where you play as the Bachelor. I recommend playing it only after finishing the main game. It has some interesting story tidbits, but nothing major and it&apos;s not as good as the main Haruspex storyline. You can safely skip it or pick it up on sale.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>cd35cf88-3a33-11ea-8ba4-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Good, but nowhere near the full game</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/cd377234-b24e-11e8-801e-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/cd377234-b24e-11e8-801e-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2017-07-12T22:32:42</review:date>
        <review:description>First of all: This is quite a good and entertaining DLC and I am glad that the developers keep this game alive and not only made Call of the Tenebrae but also plan to release one mode DLC for called Shattered Embrace.
And they also have plans for Two Worlds III which I am already looking forward to.

Now, for the &quot;gory bits&quot;:
For all the players who verbally abused and humiliated the developers on Steam and elsewhere: You should be ashamed of yourself!
The in-game shop is nothing but a convenience store for players who are just too damn lazy to play the game and collect loot. To be very clear about this: You do not need to buy *anything* from the in-game store because any single item there can be found inside the game. So just ignore it, for Christ&apos;s sake!
Also, the command console, though missing for just two days, is back in the game.

So, now, fellow gamers: Please give the devs a break! Two Worlds II is a really nice game, and these guys are really doing fine. After all, they gave us really nice gaming experiences with Two Worlds and Two Worlds II, and, after all, they are doing it with passion and they are trying to make a living. So please show some decency, for the love of God!</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">64</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>cd377234-b24e-11e8-801e-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>A Good DLC</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">117</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/cd436da4-6864-11eb-b474-fa163e9aa6fa -->

