    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/d9ff0fbc-d7b7-11ec-b1f8-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/d9ff0fbc-d7b7-11ec-b1f8-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-05-20T00:08:37</review:date>
        <review:description>A great experience - great world, great music, the voice acting in particular is stellar. Some jank and some tedium with some of the click-clicking. A linear experience - plot had some good twists and turns but I would have loved to see an even deeper and more convoluted plot for this well-realized world. Can&apos;t wait to see more from this team!</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>d9ff0fbc-d7b7-11ec-b1f8-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Beautiful World</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/da038358-93ff-11e8-8109-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/da038358-93ff-11e8-8109-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2009-10-10T17:57:43</review:date>
        <review:description>Kingpin is one of those games I&apos;ve known about for a long time but, for some reason, never played. So it was nice to be able to give it a try, and at first, I was plesantly surprised. It looked good, had a good atmosphere and the shooting was fun. Then, I realised that the game had very little or not direction and storyline. You are given no clues of where to go and what to do, and going back and forth between areas trying to find a door or passage that would lead you somewhere new gets old pretty fast. If you are patient enough this might be the game for you, personally, I just got too frustrated with it.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>da038358-93ff-11e8-8109-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>A frustrating mess</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">12</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/da07b7a4-ee1a-11e9-92ed-00163e4e60cc -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/da07b7a4-ee1a-11e9-92ed-00163e4e60cc">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-10-14T03:37:50</review:date>
        <review:description>Infelizmente Devil&apos;s Hunt é um jogo que tinha tudo pra ser bom e acaba sendo apenas problemático, diversos bugs e problemas de performance atrapalham a experiencia do Gameplay que é completamente sem graça. O combate do jogo é bem triste e quebrado, você não sente que está acertando os inimigos no combate muito menos que está recebendo dano, você só percebe que está morrendo quando olha a barra de vida.  

Não recomendo o jogo, a história tem tudo pra ser interessante mas as expressões faciais dos personagens é bem ruim praticamente inexistente que atrapalham na imersão. </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>da07b7a4-ee1a-11e9-92ed-00163e4e60cc</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:rating>
        <review:title>Jogo Bugado e Problemático. </review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/da274810-1904-11eb-9bfc-fa163e41fb2f -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/da274810-1904-11eb-9bfc-fa163e41fb2f">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-10-28T12:03:39</review:date>
        <review:description> Sinceramente, eu paguei o valor do jogo não esperando que iria encontrar algo tão bom. 
 Pumpkin Jack é um plataformer bem divertido e colorido, com a temática de Halloween bem executada, assim como a sua atmosfera, e uma gameplay gostosa e simples que te estimula a jogar até o final.
 Muito bem otimizado e bonito, confesso que não esperava que minha máquina tankaria o jogo no ultra (sem RTX ligado, óbvio), e o jogo mostrou uma performance perfeita, atingindo os 60fps capados.
 Sabe qual a parte mais sinistra? Esse jogo foi feito praticamente, POR UMA PESSOA APENAS, então sinceramente? Valoriza o jogo do cara, é um jogo feito com muito carinho para aqueles que sentem falta de plataformers gostosos...
P.S: a trilha sonora desse jogo é MUITO boa.
P.S²: fiz a review em português, porque aparentemente o pessoal BR é bem oculto nessa plataforma, espero ver mais de vocês usando esse local, que por mim, está provando ter tanta qualidade quanto a Steam.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>da274810-1904-11eb-9bfc-fa163e41fb2f</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Experiência divertida e bem executada.</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/da41edaa-6347-11ea-b28c-fa163e62c76a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/da41edaa-6347-11ea-b28c-fa163e62c76a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-03-11T05:24:44</review:date>
        <review:description>Time flies when you&apos;re having fun. Or relaxed. Or cozy. 400 days doesn&apos;t have to FEEL like 400 days. I wonder what things one could find or do to pass the time more quickly. 

I&apos;ve longed for a game where the comfort or happiness of my character could directly influence the game, and I&apos;m happy to have found one in such a lovely package. </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>da41edaa-6347-11ea-b28c-fa163e62c76a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Beautiful and Charming</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">17</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/da454a7a-63f1-11ec-9b60-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/da454a7a-63f1-11ec-9b60-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-12-23T15:11:34</review:date>
        <review:description>I bought the first game mostly for the coop experience and in this game you can&apos;t play that type of coop where one player does the cooking and the other the expediting. Both of you HAVE to be cooks, which is fine for those who wanted that, but for me, that means less casual fun and less co-operation between players required. 

It&apos;s like two people playing CSD2 on two computers at the same time, instead of working together to win. All the while the actual expediting has gotten more complex and interesting with holding stations, so the lack of the original coop experience is just sad. If the dev ever makes a 4th game in the series, please bring back the original coop.

The settings are oddly frustrating. For example you can&apos;t choose to play with key+mouse as player1 while p2 uses the gamepad, while in the previous game you could and the button prompt settings are less conveniently placed in the options when they used to be in the co-op menu.
The selection for what your cook looks like is made worse, instead of seeing all the options in one window you have to slowly scroll through every option.

During gameplay if a key corresponding to a ingredient is pressed it only activates if it is currently visible, while in the previous game you could memorize what the keybinding was and press it without opening the extended ingredients menu. This is very annoying.

In general I feel more lost with the interface design and feels like there are more unnecessary clicks involved. Hard to find things I&apos;m looking for and inconsistent menu design, in one menu you can go forwards and backwards in your selection while in another menu you can only go forwards.

There is a lot to like in this game, but all of these negative changes just make me want to play the first game instead.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>da454a7a-63f1-11ec-9b60-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:rating>
        <review:title>Better but also a bit worse</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/da5767c2-fa7a-11eb-a99b-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/da5767c2-fa7a-11eb-a99b-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-08-11T11:05:12</review:date>
        <review:description>The Encyclopaedia Comédica is a funny and entertaining book. It is well written and fun to read.

But the best part is the strategy guide. With it you can find all the hidden items, quests and secrets. I follow the step-by-step guide in my playthrough and don&apos;t miss a thing.

The skills and new weapons are of course also a nice gimmick.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>da5767c2-fa7a-11eb-a99b-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Helpful deluxe content</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


