    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/db56d8c2-5387-11ec-828d-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/db56d8c2-5387-11ec-828d-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-12-02T17:52:30</review:date>
        <review:description>Maybe the experience is colored by some nostalgia, but the writing in this game is great. 

I get approximately the same vibe from the writing in this game that I got from Beneath a Steel Sky: wacky with a dash of somber truth. 

The graphics were about average for the time, But they still do a fine job of conveying the feeling of being somewhere strange. If you like a game that makes you feel a little bit out of your element, if you like feeling a little bit off-kilter, this game does it. </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>db56d8c2-5387-11ec-828d-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Fun characters and otherworldly feel</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">11</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/db7f6d4c-b21c-11e8-8683-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/db7f6d4c-b21c-11e8-8683-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2017-03-23T17:51:51</review:date>
        <review:description>My first Novalogic game was F-22 Lightning 2 and since then, i started to enjoy their games. When I got a Demo of Delta Force 1 and later the Full release, It was awsome. Yeah, there are many features missing but for it&apos;s time, it&apos;s ok. Enemies patrol the terrain but detect you easly, making some missions hard to beat in stealth mode. You can choose any kind of weapons every mission (besides the game suggest some), so, you can play with Barret Sniper in every single mission. You have many missions to beat and at the time, you could easly play online using Novaworld, which I managed to play few times. It is indeed a very fun game to play. You can choose easy mode or realistc mode, where you die very offen. It&apos;s not a game for players that are new to the franchise and only played modern FPS games.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>db7f6d4c-b21c-11e8-8683-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Fun at his time</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">17</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/dbaab17e-5475-11ec-8ed6-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/dbaab17e-5475-11ec-8ed6-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-12-03T22:16:11</review:date>
        <review:description>Wow, Chronomaster. Let me tell you about about this game, because you probably haven’t heard of it. This is one of the final works of famed novelist Roger Zelazny, winner of many literary prizes and famous for “The Chronicles of Amber” series. The story revolves around agents that deal with time-related problems in the universe, and the dialogue is really good. The world is conceptualized really well and feels rather fresh. In terms of gameplay, it’s not very good, attempting to mix classic point-and-click with some action elements, but it’s playable enough. If you like to discover hidden gems of gaming, make sure to have a look at this one!</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>dbaab17e-5475-11ec-8ed6-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Hidden gem</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">12</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/dbc9fc1a-aac9-11eb-8e7a-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/dbc9fc1a-aac9-11eb-8e7a-fa163e99870e">
