    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/dd446a6a-4d66-11ea-851c-fa163e93294d -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/dd446a6a-4d66-11ea-851c-fa163e93294d">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-02-12T09:11:18</review:date>
        <review:description>:: Tip for the new DLC :: So after fighting with the game for a while and trying to get the update installed... it just wasn&apos;t showing in the game and kept telling me to go to the store and buy it, of which I already did. So it turns out you need to uninstall the game, but don&apos;t check the box to remove your settings and saves. Then after it&apos;s uninstalled, re-install the game and it will get the latest version. And if you still don&apos;t have it, make sure the 6 MB Bad Seed file has been installed too. it should bring you back to your most recent progress and keep you in your custom mode.

So the game... I love it, and this just adds so much more to it. The teams are killing it (pun intended) with this game! Keep up the great work Motion Twin and Evil Empire! The levels are fun and difficult at the same time, even on zero cell mode... cause who farms for new equipment on anything else. They have also polished out other bugs too. Like when your custom build is WAY too powerful and crashes the game... not anymore. I was able to beat the new boss super fast with Ice Shard (unlimited ammo), Hoakto&apos;s Bow, and 2 eagles (one with &quot;spreads oil&quot;). Normally the game would crash with this build when I got to the Giant, but nope... knocked him out in like 15 seconds. it was so much fun flying through the game and gathering the new stuff... all while exploring these awesome levels!</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>dd446a6a-4d66-11ea-851c-fa163e93294d</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Great addition; frustrating to update</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">45</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/dd638176-e127-11e9-a720-1e8caab536f7 -->

