    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/dd67e68a-1b84-11e9-b01b-00163e4e60cc -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/dd67e68a-1b84-11e9-b01b-00163e4e60cc">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-01-19T02:55:07</review:date>
        <review:description>I&apos;ve bought and played this game on Steam when it was on Early Access, and it&apos;s actually a fun and addictive game! The game is like Stardew Valley, but set in a 3D world, and instead of a farmer (although this game has the ability to raise animals and grow crops), you play the role of a builder. Sure, it&apos;s not perfect, as there are some things that needs improvement (including the voice acting, as not every line that the citizens of Portia says has voice acting, among a few other things), but the final game had just launched three days ago.

If you love games like Harvest Moon and Stardew Valley, you&apos;ll love My Time at Portia!</review:description>
