    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e1e08282-86c8-11ec-adbf-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e1e08282-86c8-11ec-adbf-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-02-05T23:16:28</review:date>
        <review:description>What a nice game !
You own a shop specialized in plant. All the gameplay is about finding, identifying and sell those plants. Each one of them have a specific effect, a unique appearance, smell, etc.. You have a book, basically your bible with a list of plants to identify, by their description. You can label the one you found and you have a mapto explore the small world. The gameplay is well made, challenging, and if you&apos;re stuck you can ask for help.

The story is good, but a little hard to follow.She is given throught interactions with people visiting the shop and needing your help . They will ask for a plant, or give you puzzles, enigmas, clues to follows leading to more plants or entry to your book. Therefore, you will have bits of story, and between lots of thinking to solve those riddles.  So it&apos;s difficult to follow the plot. The music and sound design are perfect, chilly and mysterious.

Some blackspot : there is only english, deutsh, russian or chinese. If your motherthong isn&apos;t one of them you may struggle to understood some parts and specific vocabulary.

Took me 10 hours to finish, and i have only one ending. There are 8 possibles ending. I will gladly play it again some times later to found the others. Plus you can pet the cat. </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>e1e08282-86c8-11ec-adbf-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Chill and challenging </review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e1ec83c0-591f-11eb-bb58-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e1ec83c0-591f-11eb-bb58-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-01-18T01:58:23</review:date>
        <review:description>Balance stimmt.
Viele verschiedene Aufgaben.
Aufgabenstellung verändert sich je weiter man kommt.
Zeiten für Aufträge lassen bequem einhalten.
Menüführung gut durchdacht, wie z.B. das die Produkte für angenommene Aufträge separat aufscheinen damit man da nicht ewig herumsuchen muss.
Die meiste Zeit sind eigene Entscheidungen möglich wie man vorgehen will.
Nette Grafik im Comicstyle.

Fehler scheint man inzwischen alle behoben zu haben
</review:description>
