    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e2661194-67cb-11eb-b015-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e2661194-67cb-11eb-b015-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-02-05T18:04:53</review:date>
        <review:description>Bit like rollercoaster tycoon and sid meier&apos;s simgolf. Pleasant, not too difficult to pick up, relaxing. It does require some planning with your volunteers which would take a game or two to get the hang of, but it seems to be worth the effort.

Judging from the demo, this would be a good game for casual gamers like myself. </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>e2661194-67cb-11eb-b015-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Pleasant</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e270764a-eefc-11ea-bc17-fa163e62c76a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e270764a-eefc-11ea-bc17-fa163e62c76a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-09-05T01:20:48</review:date>
        <review:description>Hi fellow gamers, I would like to begin by stating that the only real time strategy games I&apos;ve played are Age of Empires and Warcraft 3 (two of the greatest games of its genre according to some people), and I really didn&apos;t enjoyed them that much. That being said I felt like the genre wasn&apos;t for me, until I played Rimworld.

This game&apos;s crude take on survival, resource management, and injury system seems unfair at times, but when you prepare and manage to hold off a great treat it&apos;s so satisfying.

THIS GAME IS NOT FOR EVERYBODY!!

The game demands a great sink of time to build up your colonist&apos;s skills, research (what you can build), and colony.

I highly recommend to DOWNLOAD quality of life MODS and AI improvement. The game is still being updated because it hasn&apos;t reached its final state. Some mods even get integrated to the base game when they are deemed important to improve the player experience.

Overall a great game and unique game (at least to me is unique), but you really need to download mods if you don&apos;t want to micro management every action of your 5-13 colonists every 10 seconds.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>e270764a-eefc-11ea-bc17-fa163e62c76a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Unexpected gameplay and funness.</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e2712226-a25a-11ec-98aa-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e2712226-a25a-11ec-98aa-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-03-13T01:19:37</review:date>
        <review:description>Sadly, the game is really painful to play. It has cool graphics, nice sounds, well designed world that really puts you in a peacefull state of mind. So you should relax and enjoy the game, right?

Unfortunately, even on easy difficulty, it is so hard to understand and accomplish missions that it just makes you nervous and angry when you fail the mission after 2-3h struggle. 

Mission briefing, managing your buildings and units needs major improvements. And since this game is few years old, it seems that devs no longer care so no fixes are coming. 

Gave up after like 5th mission. Cannot recommend this game to anyone.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">7</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>e2712226-a25a-11ec-98aa-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:rating>
        <review:title>Terrible User Experience</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e28862c2-cfbc-11eb-93b1-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e28862c2-cfbc-11eb-93b1-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-06-18T01:39:32</review:date>
        <review:description>It is the first time i ever put a 1 star on a game... but i&apos;m afraid it reflects the general interest of this one !
Lets be clear: the only quality value in this game are in the close up combat screens (drawn background + animated pixel arts characters) and the hand drawn character designs in the team select screen, and... and that&apos;s it !
Gameplay is simplistic, shallow, and lacks of any depth... Hear me, i&apos;m not even comparing this game to other modern indies, i simply put it in competition with retro old games it claim to be inspired and to be the heir to ! There were more smart ideas, varieties in battle, and solid mechanics, compelling story in Shining Force 1, and i said 1 ! On Sega Genesis/Megadrive... It&apos;s as if this game disregarded each and any evolution, progress, improvement ever made in the turn based tactical genre in the last 3 decades to serve a product inferior to the titles of the 80ies :
You cannot propose a game like that in 2021 after other devs managed to pull of an excellent &quot;tribute&quot; to same inspirations like Fell Seal: Arbiter&apos;s Mark (clearly inspired by the Ogre serie)
It&apos;s so blatantly poor that i wonder if i could treat the store page&apos;s words as a blatant scam, tbh !
If you have 15 bucks to spare, dont waste them on this game for your own good; hell, you could rather purchase the sega classics collection that is on steam and that has first Shining Force inside, instead, and yet have better time and fun !
I know, developping a game is hard and so on, and i feel sorry for the devs but... what did you have in mind exactly ? i really would like to know what kind of game you had in your minds and dreams, and how it could devolve from that into this final form instead ? For i won&apos;t quesiton the sincerity of the intents and passion behind the project, but as a end-customer, the product lacks in every department !</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>e28862c2-cfbc-11eb-93b1-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:rating>
        <review:title>Shallow, uninspired</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">13</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e29c7900-b29c-11e8-ba5a-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e29c7900-b29c-11e8-ba5a-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2018-01-16T06:47:21</review:date>
        <review:description>It seems like almost every game on GOG is given a low rating by the community.  This one is sitting at three stars, currently, which I assumed I could ignore.  However, now that I&apos;ve played it, yes, it is a 3-star game, a confusing mix of great and poor storytelling, giving an overall &quot;average&quot; impression.  However, I don&apos;t think the average rating gives a sense of how much a roller coaster this game is.

Okay, first of all, there&apos;s the literal motion sickness.  Sometimes you are walking, teetering around, bobbing and swaying, which is bad.  Sometimes you are in a moving car and expected to look outside, which is worse.  But the worst thing is all the YANKING of the camera.  Ugh...I barely made it through the game.  I&apos;m still not sure if I&apos;m going to be sick.

The story...?  Despite the stripping away of nearly every narrative convention, this game does manage to somewhat tell a story, which is an impressive feat.  But the narrative is tattered and thin.  It&apos;s under two hours long, but twice during the story, the protagonist gets drunk/high, and all sense goes flying out the window.  And sleeps six times and has weird dreams.  That does not leave much time for stuff that definitely happened.  The story has a beginning--&quot;there was this FBI agent&quot;--but after that, you are on your own.  The game basically says, &quot;Here&apos;s some nonsense to sort through.  Good luck!&quot;  The story really earns those averaged 3 stars.

If you like weirdness to think about and don&apos;t mind the camera movement, you may like this game?  I...do not, so it&apos;s hard to know how to recommend it.  If it appeals, I suggest you pull up a let&apos;s play video in full screen and make sure you don&apos;t get sick before buying.

Bonus nitpick section:  game forces you the protagonist to throw away a new tube of lipstick; that hurt me deep in my miserly soul.  That stuff is expensive!</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>e29c7900-b29c-11e8-ba5a-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:rating>
        <review:title>CAUTION:  Caused Motion-Sickness!</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e2d83966-944e-11e8-a25f-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e2d83966-944e-11e8-a25f-00163e97122a">
