    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e2e0a990-6ebc-11e9-a44a-00163e4e60cc -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e2e0a990-6ebc-11e9-a44a-00163e4e60cc">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-05-05T01:35:15</review:date>
        <review:description>MDK jest jedną z pierwszych gier akcji z widokiem zza pleców bohatera. A przynajmniej jedną z pierwszych tak dobrze dopracowanych. Dzięki niezwykle dynamicznemu gameplayowi i niesamowitemu designowi poziomów w MDK gra się świetnie nawet dziś. Do tego dochodzi GENIALNA muzyka oraz lekko doprawiony humor. Kupa radochy.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>e2e0a990-6ebc-11e9-a44a-00163e4e60cc</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Legendarna gra akcji</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e2eb05ec-69cb-11ea-8285-fa163e62c76a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e2eb05ec-69cb-11ea-8285-fa163e62c76a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-03-19T12:24:59</review:date>
        <review:description>Ich hab das Spiel schon als Alpha gekauft - und man bekommt seit dem fortwährend Weiterentwicklungen und es ist mein Geheimtipp schlechthin. 
Klar, die 2D-Grafik ist nicht High End - aber mit dem Effekten und einem ganz eigenen Charme sehr hübsch.

Letztlich mach das Spiel mit der unglaublichen Spieltiefe und einer - am Anfang sicher frustrierenden - steilen Lernkurve locker weg, was an Grafik fehlt. Für mich heist das - 600 h + an Spielzeit und durch das Sandkastenprinzip mit wechselnden Startbedingungen ergeben sich auch nach Monaten immer wieder neue Aspekte und Entwicklungen. 

In Summe ist es eine Mischung von Anno und Sims auf einem kruden Planeten.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>e2eb05ec-69cb-11ea-8285-fa163e62c76a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Das uneheliche Kind von Anno und Sims.</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e2f897a0-94df-11e9-90e3-fa18e6945d7c -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e2f897a0-94df-11e9-90e3-fa18e6945d7c">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-06-22T11:21:31</review:date>
        <review:description>My Friend Pedro is a very addicting action game. A side scroller with unique action inspired by franchises like The Matrix and Max Payne. It begs for experimentation with it&apos;s combat and I recommend this game to any gamer. It is a little short though but at it&apos;s price it is more fun than most 40 to 60 dollar video games . Definetely buy it ( from GOG)</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>e2f897a0-94df-11e9-90e3-fa18e6945d7c</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Great Game with High Replayability</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">7</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e3075ff8-053b-11e9-a73f-fa163ecdd5fb -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e3075ff8-053b-11e9-a73f-fa163ecdd5fb">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2018-12-21T18:17:18</review:date>
        <review:description>I love puzzle games. This is the first puzzle game that in a while where I had to break out  pen and paper and actually take notes. I got about 15 fates in and I was like, &quot;Well, I guess that&apos;s all this game is going to give me&quot;. Then I looked closer and slowly started to solve the rest of the fates, and a majority of the fates took some serious mental straining. To ding the game a little, I wasn&apos;t exactly sure how to solve some of the fates, but through a process of elimination, but even that felt rewarding. 

This game was refreshing to me, especially after I just got through with playing one of the Myst games, which, no offense, the world doesn&apos;t make much sense and the puzzles suffer because of it. This game, even though there were obvious fantasy elements, felt like close to reality. Loved it. I&apos;d like more games with a similar game mechanic.   </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>e3075ff8-053b-11e9-a73f-fa163ecdd5fb</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>I feel smart after playing this game.</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e3170170-f20a-11ea-9235-fa163e62c76a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e3170170-f20a-11ea-9235-fa163e62c76a">
