    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e34d646e-9441-11e8-95e5-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e34d646e-9441-11e8-95e5-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2010-04-30T10:38:07</review:date>
        <review:description>Freespace 2 plays like a great sci-fi novel. It has mystery, adventure and great action against insurmountable odds. You have to play to believe it.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>e34d646e-9441-11e8-95e5-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>An awesome space sim</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e354a830-9489-11e8-afb0-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e354a830-9489-11e8-afb0-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2011-11-09T12:19:37</review:date>
        <review:description>An epic RPG. It has its flaws, it&apos;s not the best RPG in the world, but surely deserves 5 stars - epic gameplay.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>e354a830-9489-11e8-afb0-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Great RPG</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e366f984-1d91-11eb-9c0e-fa163e41fb2f -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e366f984-1d91-11eb-9c0e-fa163e41fb2f">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-11-03T07:03:18</review:date>
        <review:description>After deeply analyzing the ending that I ended up choosing in Pathologic, I realized that this gaming experience represented for me one of those instances in life where your way of thinking is altered, perhaps not drastically, but even to such a point that I believe that now I see life with a clarity that previously eluded me.

Pathologic has an enviable rhythm, which catches and forces you to play for just one more hour; it has a script that, as a writer, I can only dream of achieving, and that gives depth and charisma to its characters, because no one is purely bad or purely good in this story, and every decision is important, drastic, and has bittersweet consequences.

It is a difficult game, so much that it becomes overwhelming, but the game explicitly tells you this has a purpose, so you trust it and accept it, waiting for a life lesson ath the end. So, ¿does it pay off? It does; I won&apos;t spoil anything, but the feelings of triumphalism and satisfaction once you reach the end while never turned the difficulty down, become rewards that you want to talk about to everyone. The game truly transforms this experience into your own, hard-earned story.

The soundtrack stays with you for days after it&apos;s finished, and the art direction is beautiful and immersive.

I have nothing negative to say about this game. I treasure the 35 hours it gave me, and although I am dying to experience a second round to explore closed avenues and better understand some details of the story, I am proud of every decision I made on my first journey.

On the other hand, if one is a playwright, novelist, or screenwriter, Pathologic plays like a Brechtian play, and as such is a wonderful, intellectually powerful example, which has a lot to teach.

Ultimately, I think it is a masterpiece.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>e366f984-1d91-11eb-9c0e-fa163e41fb2f</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>The Dream of a Writer</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">12</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e37f2fb0-fb61-11ea-8647-fa163e7ab9c9 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e37f2fb0-fb61-11ea-8647-fa163e7ab9c9">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-09-20T19:54:03</review:date>
        <review:description>В отличие от Стим-версии здесь, как это обычно бывает полностью отсутствуют достижения. Разработчик не письма не отвечает, так-же он не отвечает на вопрос о том, почемму версия игры для GOG - единственная без достижений?</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">18</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>e37f2fb0-fb61-11ea-8647-fa163e7ab9c9</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:rating>
        <review:title>No achievments here.</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e3a4b576-b593-11ec-83fd-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e3a4b576-b593-11ec-83fd-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-04-06T13:25:32</review:date>
        <review:description>The game is accessible, if dated. The missions are hard enough to be challenging, but are winnable even for a new player within a few tries. This is a fun game!

The downside:

The controls are wonky, failing to make adequate use of the mouse.

Make sure you study the controls on the main screen, since you can&apos;t access them while in a mission.

Sometimes missions spring surprises on you that cause you to fail the mission, as you could not have anticipated them. Likewise, sometimes the game glitches, and the non-player ships fail to take a required action. This can cause you to fail through no fault of your own. This is the chief flaw in the game.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>e3a4b576-b593-11ec-83fd-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Really cool but glitchy</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e3a823d6-d3c8-11ea-9024-fa163e62c76a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e3a823d6-d3c8-11ea-9024-fa163e62c76a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-08-01T10:30:35</review:date>
        <review:description>As someone who never played Darkest Dungeon but 2 of the other games it is inspired by i enjoyed my time pretty much. 

COMBAT is a little bit monotone after a while after you settle with one combination of followers but that&apos;s what i could honestly say about most games to be honest. 

I enjoyed the STORY and liked the main character for beeing a relatable humble person and not a &apos;super human, the chosen one&apos;. Have more than one ending is a nice feature i appreciate. 

The SAVE SYSTEM was alright and i guess makes sense for this kind of game since it makes you think about getting prepared well enaugh to be able to make it. 
I understand though that it takes a moment to prepare a strategy for this mild inconvinience. 

I played the game in GERMAN version 1.09 on another plattform on NORMAL DIFFICULTY. 
There were a few translation issues here and there but i haven&apos;t encountered any bugs. 

Game was UPDATED afterwards which i applaude Devespresso games since they were working on other projects in the meantime. 
The fact they seem to have updated the GOG version shortly after the Steam version makes me like this Dev even more. 

All in all a solid game, story and mechanic wise with a suitable soundtrack. 

Will buy this and the soundtrack on GOG again if i see a good (bundle) discount on both so that i can have it on here aswell - and give a little more support to the Devs and GOG. </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>e3a823d6-d3c8-11ea-9024-fa163e62c76a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Pretty Good for newbies in this genre..</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">7</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e3b5a930-2f2a-11eb-a2bc-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e3b5a930-2f2a-11eb-a2bc-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-11-25T16:31:22</review:date>
        <review:description>[Retailversion] So, finally! The devs were big fans of the sourcematerial (The Black Eye, a german Tabletop-Classic from the 80s, kinda like D&amp;amp;D) and crafted a beautiful game here. Its a great old-school RPG that will be worth your time and money. The game can be rough and hard at times, so keep an eye on skills, talents and classes. But if you start to figure it out, it feels rewarding. Kinda like the first Dragon Age if you will. A modern german classic.
The game is set in the world of THE BLACK EYE on the continent Aventuria. Your adventure revolves around the city of Ferdok. The world is fully fleshed out, with a lot of history and lore behind it. You move via a map, so its not open world, but it does not need to be.
I replayed it like 2 years ago on Win10 and it worked like a charme and i had a lot of fun. Srsly! The look maybe a bit stiff nowadays, but still charming. Sound, music, story, world... Just perfect. Still sad about the fact, that this game was so underlooked back then. 
Make sure to check out the sequel &quot;The river of time&quot;. 


</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>e3b5a930-2f2a-11eb-a2bc-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Hidden gem</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">99</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e4056d72-93fe-11e8-853a-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e4056d72-93fe-11e8-853a-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2009-08-25T07:32:58</review:date>
        <review:description>After all the games I have played, this one along with Freespace 2, are the only ones I keep coming back to. The campiagn is so compelling that even after finishing the game I was absolutely obsessed in finding out more about the Freespace universe. HIGHLY RECOMMENDED for anyone!!!! :)</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>e4056d72-93fe-11e8-853a-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Best space game ever!!!</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e40c77e8-eb51-11e8-ba98-fa163ecdd5fb -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e40c77e8-eb51-11e8-ba98-fa163ecdd5fb">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2018-11-18T18:49:18</review:date>
        <review:description>All of the murder mystery games that I&apos;ve played and seen focused on some far-fetched series of puzzles that you should solve to move the story. You should complete one puzzle after another in exact order to progress. Some times these games will hold you by the hand and scream some clues at you like: &quot; MISSIS SOANDSO HAS BLOOD ON HER BOOTS!!! HER HANDS HAVE BRUISES LIKE SHE WAS KILLING THAT MAN LAST NIGHT WINK-WINK NUDGE-NUDGE!!!!!&quot;
Sometimes these games will have some puzzle that you just don&apos;t understand or maybe you can&apos;t spot something which ultimately resolves with pixel hunting and other silliness.
The point is that this &quot;genre&quot; of games pretty much was defined and it was (IMHO) stupid.

And Lucas Pope did it again...
The author of this magnificent game may have been known to you by his previous game &quot;Papers, please&quot; which was a genre-bending or even genre defining experience in game design. Return to the Obra Dinn made by exactly this habit of the author - to ignore conventions and barriers of genres. It almost seems like he was mad as me by this void of proper games that will make you feel like Sherlock Holmes or some other great detective. And he made this game as if to fix and revitalize this dreadful and un-dead genre.

PROS:
- The game will show you the whole story (except for one chapter) of what happened regardless of how good you are as a detective. No stream of stupid pixelhunting puzzles that lock your progress.
- No stupid hand holding and screaming clues at you. There are some clues that are blunt, some are very subtle, but nothing is in-your-face press-e-to-sherlock
- You have one and only one thing to worry about. The main game mechanic is simple to understand and the game builds on it effortlessly. No new out of the blue and far-fetched puzzles!
- Music is superb!
- Sound design, voice work and the direction is godlike.

CONS:
- The opening of every new scene may drag a tiny-bit at times :(</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>e40c77e8-eb51-11e8-ba98-fa163ecdd5fb</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Lucas Pope did it again!</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e42a6be4-597e-11ea-9284-fa163e62c76a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e42a6be4-597e-11ea-9284-fa163e62c76a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-02-27T18:33:31</review:date>
        <review:description>I have played MDK2 first before this prequel and I don&apos;t understand why this game is so praised. It might have been impressive back then, but nowadays it has it&apos;s flaws, and many of them. 

Because the default keybard layout is messy, it took a long time for me to adjust the controls so I could get along with it. The game has ZERO information of saving system with F2 which is not acceptable at all. There are some platforming scenes which requires Kurt to reach platforms too far away from each other. It&apos;s just impossible to reach those platforms by gliding because Kurt lose altitude way too fast with his parachute. 

Yes, with the sniper scope you can shoot distant enemies, but you cannot tell do you actually hit your targets, do you cause any damage and how much. There&apos;s a health bar for enemies which is not displayed while in sniper mode for some reason? Besides, all enemies look pretty much the same having nothing personality or such.

But the worst thing is there is NO story at all. No intro, no character introductions (without MDK2 I wouldn&apos;t even know character names...), no storytelling, no dialogue, no epilogue... just nothing. Just a series of running and shooting sequences and then the game just ends like that. So unsatifying and thus weak replay value.

At least the game has it&apos;s own unique visual style, huge seamless levels, absurb moments and some funny suprises. But I still prefer MDK2 over this one anytime. </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">10</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>e42a6be4-597e-11ea-9284-fa163e62c76a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>MDK2 better</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e43da99a-301f-11e9-9583-00163e4e60cc -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e43da99a-301f-11e9-9583-00163e4e60cc">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-02-14T08:15:14</review:date>
        <review:description>I would like to say this is money well spent, but it&apos;s not. Get used to that scenery, cause you won&apos;t stop staring at the same building - painted in different colors - for the whole race. The dev(s) clearly tried to break up the monotony by splitting up the tracks into sections of these buildings, or other scenery elements - such as plants, tunnels, or open areas. Those sections do help but that trick can only do so much. However, racing is rather fun, and making the turns can be challenging. If you mess up, you could find yourself several places behind your opponents. Learn to drift, because you won&apos;t be winning a race without that skill - game journos might find that aspect too taxing, in which case I recommend they learn to code instead. I can&apos;t say with confidence the game is worth purchasing at full price, so wait for a sale.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">17</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>e43da99a-301f-11e9-9583-00163e4e60cc</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:rating>
        <review:title>Not Perfect</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">27</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e44269d8-b1b4-11e8-9312-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e44269d8-b1b4-11e8-9312-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2016-05-28T18:25:20</review:date>
        <review:description>If you like gameplay structure similar to metroid/simphony of the night, this game is for you.
It has the structure of metroid, but It also has similarities with dark/demon souls.
You play the role of Kaho, a priestess that wants to see the queen because of the curse that is spreading through the land.
You have a whole map to explore, and you really aren&apos;t locked on a linear progression on it. you can complete any area at any time.
The &quot;dark souls&quot; aspect of the game, is that you have bells that act as checkpoints (similar to bonfires), and If you ring the bell, your consumables are restocked. the enemies are incredible hard you you try to take a fast approach to them, since a lot of them either hit hard, can use status effects, guard against attacks or even all of them at the same time.
The story is told from the perspective of the side characters that you encounter during the journey, since Kaho is a silent protagonist. both of them and the enviroment tells that this game isn&apos;t really all sweet. 
Overall, this is one incredible game, that everyone should be playing.

PS: try inputting the konami code during gameplay to see what happens =3</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">9</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>e44269d8-b1b4-11e8-9312-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>A really good (and grim) experience</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">34</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e4529b2e-e26f-11ec-83a4-42010a340c25 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e4529b2e-e26f-11ec-83a4-42010a340c25">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-06-02T15:31:14</review:date>
        <review:description>Tras media hora no entiendo todo lo bueno que se habla de este juego. Uno entiende que ya tiene sus años pero es que hay juegos de la misma época que han envejecido mucho mejor gráfica y jugablemente.

Primero que solo está en inglés, segundo la configuración por defecto es terrible (de casualidad ya que no lo dicen descubrí que para moverse necesitas el teclado numérico) y tercero tiene una jugabilidad relativamente sencilla pero mut básica.

A pesar del estilo de batlla tipo barco, &quot;Rebel Galaxy&quot; me parece mucho mejor juego, y más teniendo en cuenta que este cuesta más de 9 euros.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>e4529b2e-e26f-11ec-83a4-42010a340c25</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>No entiendo qué le ven...</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e490b68e-6560-11ec-a5c5-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e490b68e-6560-11ec-a5c5-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-12-25T10:58:56</review:date>
        <review:description>this game completely surprised me, I expected to like it because of the previews of how it looked. The artstyle is obviously charming but what will sneak up on you is how much potential all your platforming moves and transformations and options give you.

also for a game about a demon trying to take over demon gangs and rule hell the characters and the story are surprisingly cute.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>e490b68e-6560-11ec-a5c5-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Cute Story, Great Art, Good Platforming</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">9</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e4aa897a-6058-11e9-ba89-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e4aa897a-6058-11e9-ba89-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-04-16T18:04:12</review:date>
        <review:description>This addon gives you a bit more of Pathfinder: Kingmaker, but not much. You start at level 5 (which is nice to test some builds that need a few levels to work), but at level 7 it&apos;s already over. Maybe you can make it to 8, if you face every possible encounter. I ended up with 6.5 hours of playtime.

Varn and his old friend do great roleplay, which makes the campaign feel more alive. There are three more pregenerated characters, but they are not interactive at all and they depend heavily on resting (mediocre defense, mediocre damage output, reliance on spells). The resting dependance totally backfires in the final dungeon - which is big, dangerous and with no way out but forward. I ran out of food due to resting and had to switch to story mode to finish - which kind of killed the relevance of the final battle.

Overall, the addon pretty much feels like the original game: Interesting characters, challenging battles and a decent story. On the other hand, it&apos;s highly linear and lacks the kingdom feature completely. Can&apos;t remember any bug in version 1.3.1, just a few translation quirks (German version).</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>e4aa897a-6058-11e9-ba89-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:rating>
        <review:title>Short but nice</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">28</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e4b1ff9a-863a-11e9-a2dc-00163e4e60cc -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e4b1ff9a-863a-11e9-a2dc-00163e4e60cc">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-06-03T23:05:11</review:date>
        <review:description>It is NOT as simple as it looks!

I can understand why some people do not like the combat, since it is quite simple (not too many choices), but there are still a lot of choices which matter!

Party composition, items equipped, and also items taken with you (you can&apos;t take too much with you else you can&apos;t loot stuff, because of the weight limit) do count quite a bit!

There are 10 different classes (+ your main character) every one is slightly different, and this does not only affect combat, but it affects the whole dungeon run!

You do not need to find a tactic which lets you win a combat, but which lets you survive the whole dungeon run! 

The problem is never a single combat, but the damage you accumulate over several fights. 

Do you use your special attack with the character yet for a good effect, or will it be more effective in the next fight, but will take longer to be useable again?

Do I equip the perception increasing item to the one which already has the best perception to be sure to find all traps, or do I want it on another character to disarm traps with them (and getting more super attacks from that character).

Should I carry an extra item with me to equip before the main boss, or is it not worth the extra weight used.

Should I have a height sleight character with me to get more loot and be able to get material to craft new items, or should I have a merchant with me to buy better stuff from the merchant instead?

All in all there are many &quot;small&quot; decisions, which add up and decide if you can conquer the dungeon or not and this makes it interesting for me.

**Fazit:**

I like this game ebtter than darkest dungeon, since it It looks better, has more story to it and it is just more of my taste (especially after the patches!) You do not need to kill your company.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>e4b1ff9a-863a-11e9-a2dc-00163e4e60cc</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Beautiful, a bit simple, but still fun!</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">41</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


