    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e7352d8c-f213-11ea-bf51-fa163e93294d -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e7352d8c-f213-11ea-bf51-fa163e93294d">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-09-08T23:43:08</review:date>
        <review:description>Nothing is broken and if you&apos;re desperate for more twin stick action, I daresay this is probably worth looking at. For me though, it was repetitive and lacked the visceral punch of the better games of this type. Upgrades were steady but uninspiring, not doing enough to switch up the gameplay. The shotgun is a 7 shot pick-up to begin with which makes it seem exciting, yet although it makes the enemy health bar fall quicker, it just doesn&apos;t FEEL like it packs much punch. Seems small, but in a game all about shooting and dodging, the shooting part is weak.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>e7352d8c-f213-11ea-bf51-fa163e93294d</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>Below average twin stick shooter</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">10</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e73aff1a-3d05-11e9-b19a-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e73aff1a-3d05-11e9-b19a-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-03-02T18:11:57</review:date>
        <review:description>Return of the Obra Dinn is one of the most immersive adventure games I have ever played. Everything is spot on and immensely fine-tuned - the graphics, the music, the sound effects and the gameplay. There is nothing quite like it and I have never thought that I am going to enjoy piecing together the fates of the sixty crew members this much.

I am seriously considering buying the game on Steam for a second playthrough. Sure, the mystery might not feel that fresh for a second time but Obra Dinn&apos;s atmosphere is something that I rarely experience in the world of video games. In this day and age, Lucas Pope deserves every bit of support we can give him!

If you enjoy detective and mystery games, you simply have to give this one a try!</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>e73aff1a-3d05-11e9-b19a-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>An Instant Classic</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e7416f30-94bd-11e8-8052-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e7416f30-94bd-11e8-8052-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2012-06-23T14:16:41</review:date>
        <review:description>What I really like about the Freespace games is the ludicrously over-serious narrative tone.

They start off profoundly, end-of-the-universely apocalyptic, and get progressively more grave and grim from there on in.

Even though it makes me chuckle, it&apos;s very effective - a player really feels in his gut that it&apos;s extremely important not to fail.

On top of that, the Freespace games are on their own in a field that ought to be crowded. Everybody loves a good 3D vector space shooter. Howcum there are so few of them about?

Probably because Freespace 1 &amp;amp; 2 are so completely definitive. Goodness knows how a developer could even begin to make something &quot;like Freespace, but better&quot;.

As you can probably tell, I kinda like Freespace. The only gripe I can imagine some people having is that it&apos;s complicated to play and there are so very many buttons to press. But hey; keep banging the rocks together, guys! ;)</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>e7416f30-94bd-11e8-8052-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>A very lovable series of games.</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e773ff62-f34e-11ea-8e36-fa163e93294d -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e773ff62-f34e-11ea-8e36-fa163e93294d">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-09-10T13:18:00</review:date>
        <review:description>First of all. I am not one of those: &quot;The remaster is underwhelming&quot; kind of reviewers. It is a re-master and not a re-make. I really like KoA and all I ever asked from the re-master was a DRM free version of the game AND a fov slider - which the game now povides. I would not have cared about bloom or high resolution textures or whatever...

...unfortunately for me (and belive me I am glad for everyone whose game runs decently) my re-encounter with KoArr is ruined by the worst performance I have ever experienced in a game since I tried to run the &quot;Crysis&quot;-Demo on my mothers notebook - many year ago.

While the originnal version of the game provides ~300 FPS on my RTX 2070 Super (https://youtu.be/IJDjnInJ06Q), the re-master offers sub 30 FPS in the very same spot (https://youtu.be/u_RwIzQ-Ib4) , dippinng to below 15 FPS in the first small village. A driveruptdate to 452.06 did not help.

I`d love to play this game, but right now it feels like re-jected love. I´d glady give 5 stars if any patches will change teh situation but right now I almost feel like asking for a refund. In fact I allready opened a case - but for some reason I still have hope that the devs show some love and optimize the game.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">23</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>e773ff62-f34e-11ea-8e36-fa163e93294d</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:rating>
        <review:title>re-jected love: terrible performance ruined my re-encounter with KoArr</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">58</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e775218c-19e3-11ec-96ea-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e775218c-19e3-11ec-96ea-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-09-20T10:25:17</review:date>
        <review:description>Played the demo, It&apos;s utter crap the AI cheats, The fights are bullshit and more often then not the enemies have too much of an advantage (and too much health) some unleashing up to 20 times on your character BEFORE you get a chance only to shoot you again and again especially with more then 1 enemy in other games you can Coax 1 enemy out from hiding nope not in this game the forced isometric angle is garbage maybe make it a bit more fair combat wise characters should NEVER be able to unload on you until it is their turn I would NOT buy this at all.

Everything is WAY WAY overpriced which is just lame can you actually loot decent material off bodies?

The story is good cross between the original SNES version of shadowrun and fallout games but more noir gritty but the combat JUST NO!

The demo - DO WE ACTUALLY GET 1 MISSION answer is NO you get this stupid gauntlet of fights one after the other it&apos;s absolute garbage you have literally NO DECENT GEAR whatsoever whoever thought this was a good idea for a demo has been smoking tea bags.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">35</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>e775218c-19e3-11ec-96ea-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:rating>
        <review:title>Played the demo and it was BS!</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">8</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e78ff522-1150-11ea-8a1d-00163e4e60cc -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e78ff522-1150-11ea-8a1d-00163e4e60cc">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-11-27T22:02:56</review:date>
        <review:description>Marble Nest is a standalone chapter of the series, so to speak. It was actually created way back in 2016 during the development of Pathologic 2, and it shows: while the gameplay and graphics are the same as the sequel, the characters and dialogue are more reminescent of the original Pathologic. Overall, it functions as a sort of bridge between the two games.

Due to the much more forgiving survival elements (they are in fact almost absent) and lack of combat, the chapter doesn&apos;t let you do much more than walk around, talk to people, and complete some quests. Still, the dialogue is fascinating as always, and there are a few different choices and endings to see. The short length also makes it easy to replay.

It&apos;s a shame that it can only be bought as DLC. You&apos;ll get more enjoyment out of it if you have at least some knowledge of the story in the main game, but as a standalone chapter it might work pretty well even for a new player.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>e78ff522-1150-11ea-8a1d-00163e4e60cc</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Pathologic 1.5</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">14</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e7c703ca-1be3-11eb-a31a-fa163e7e880a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e7c703ca-1be3-11eb-a31a-fa163e7e880a">
