    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e8e088b2-8f42-11eb-a549-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e8e088b2-8f42-11eb-a549-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-03-27T23:25:10</review:date>
        <review:description>It is very good strategic game, it could be a nice gem in RTS world I would say, but there are some issues making this game a bit annoying. The latest patch introduced some bugs, 3 games played, conquest multiplayer mode, and 3 crashes - time lost, no progress done. The main issue is linux support. Yes it is possible to install and run it in Linux, but support for this system is getting worse and worse.... It was and still is not possible to play any multiplayer, but now in the latest patch is not possible to play even the singleplayer, there is just story mode available, so about 75% of features disabled. Thats very pitty and I am starting to regret that I bought this game...

I hope that bugs will be fixed soon, but I very doubt that Linux will be supported in future :(</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">7</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>e8e088b2-8f42-11eb-a549-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>Good game, but lot of annoying issues...</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e8e3ff12-a10c-11ea-92fa-fa163e62c76a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e8e3ff12-a10c-11ea-92fa-fa163e62c76a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-05-28T20:59:00</review:date>
        <review:description>I bought Patho 2 elsewhere some months ago and I literally can&apos;t put it down, even though I already unlocked all the achievements and managed to save everyone on intended difficulty. The story is original and engaging, the art style unique and beautiful, the gameplay a wonderful pain throughout, the lore is so deep you literally can&apos;t reach the bottom. I played Patho classic too multiple times with all three protagonists and the main points of the story are still ambiguous and mysterious (as they should be!)

I really hope Ice-Pick Lodge gets to make the Bachelor and the Changeling playthoughs for Patho 2 as well. They deserve all the success in the world!</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>e8e3ff12-a10c-11ea-92fa-fa163e62c76a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Beautifully hurtful experience</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e93160da-53e5-11ec-85cf-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e93160da-53e5-11ec-85cf-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-12-03T05:05:46</review:date>
        <review:description>I remember picking this up at EB Games in the &apos;discount section&apos; for a sleepover. It was so good that we extended the sleepover another night so we could beat it and explore every possible option. I also remember nearly throwing up since we each got a bulk box of Airheads that kept us on a sugar high for the weekend.

Anyway, I&apos;ve played this various times in DosBox using the original media, so I&apos;m sure this will be a great experience via GOG. This version launched with no issues and full sound and video.</review:description>
