    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e97a8c34-948c-11ea-a964-fa163e62c76a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e97a8c34-948c-11ea-a964-fa163e62c76a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-05-12T23:12:32</review:date>
        <review:description>Okay, I am not a good writer so I&apos;ll try to keep it short. It is a really great game, but I will tell you just about DIFFICULTY and OPTIMIZATION.

The game is FANTASTIC. Really. It is not for everyone , but if you need some food for the mind - you are welcome.

DIFFICULTY. Some people say about hardcoreness. Yes, it is really difficult. And I recommend you play it with hardcore difficulty. Why? You will better understand the game. BUT you can always switch it to easy mode (it still will not be easy though, but you can save your personal time, which is super if you are a busy person). As for me, I played it with easy mode. Unfortunately. I didn&apos;t have much time to play it as it was designed by the developers. But I will replay the game after some time.

OPTIMIZATION
I&apos;ll just say that the best thing you can do is to download it on you SSD. That&apos;s all.

Try it yourself! And make up your mind about it.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>e97a8c34-948c-11ea-a964-fa163e62c76a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Great. Really great.</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e9912dfa-6b5d-11ec-988f-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/e9912dfa-6b5d-11ec-988f-fa163e9aa6fa">
