    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/ee672bd2-a9ec-11eb-a7ab-fa163e3a9b6e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/ee672bd2-a9ec-11eb-a7ab-fa163e3a9b6e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-04-30T22:47:44</review:date>
        <review:description>Antifa is NOT anti fascist!!! Anyone who uses violence to oppress those you don&apos;t agree with, is a fascist cunt themself. This game is literally the 2D version of &quot;Hatred&quot;. Nothing but a murder fantasy simulator for mentally unstable ideologists &amp;amp; freaks and without the slightest bit of satire or irony. I hate overly politicized games. Videogames should be DISTRACTION &amp;amp; fun. And not marxist propaganda.  I wanted to give this game a chance bit seeing as it is absolutely not satire but actually taking itself 100% serious i see absolutely no reason to touch this again. To me this is on the same level of political propaganda games like antisemitic &amp;amp; racist games of the late 90s and early 2000s from extremist groups who wanted to spread their hateful messages through videogames. This here is exactly the same kind of extremist propaganda.

Totally NOT recommended. </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">35</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>ee672bd2-a9ec-11eb-a7ab-fa163e3a9b6e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:rating>
        <review:title>Absolute tonedeaf developer &amp;amp; playerbase</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">24</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/ee823df6-f619-11e9-a32c-00163e4e60cc -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/ee823df6-f619-11e9-a32c-00163e4e60cc">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-10-24T07:51:24</review:date>
        <review:description>This was one of those games My older sister picked up spare of the moment when it came out when I was at the store with her. Thank you sis! Took it home and started it up and fell in love with this style of fps, since I was used to Doom, and Duke Nukem 3d, this was a big difference for myself. The multiplayer was fun even on 56k modem, and had some of the best times I could of asked for online. Heck it is even where my username came from. The default name is Blackhawk... and I wanted a cool bird name for online games.. thus blackcrow was born. 

Playing this in 2019 is still as fun as it was in 1998, although it has not aged the best, and some of the AI is not the best, I don&apos;t remember my team being so worthless, it is still worth a pickup and play if you loved the game back then. Love the Delta Force games then, and still love them now. Miss Novalogic and the games they put out back then.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>ee823df6-f619-11e9-a32c-00163e4e60cc</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Loved this game to death</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/eea3489e-df0e-11ec-bbc4-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/eea3489e-df0e-11ec-bbc4-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-05-29T08:19:36</review:date>
        <review:description>Super fun, super batty. Shoot the exploding billiard balls into the other mask fellows and try to get the all girls before the others do. Sounds simple, but the game is very random and the CPU is very stupid sometimes. Can be quite frustrating. There is an update somewhere out there to get it uncensored. Been awhile so Im not sure where. Found a link somewhere in the community hub on Steam. Lots of fun, must go, must buy.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>eea3489e-df0e-11ec-bbc4-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
