    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/eee43c00-7e40-11e9-8f3b-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/eee43c00-7e40-11e9-8f3b-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-05-24T19:28:16</review:date>
        <review:description>So, I hope the title is cryptic enough. I thought about writing a completely confusing review as a statement that not all of the things exist to be completely understood. But since I can&apos;t compete with Pathologic writing neither in skill nor in artfulness, I&apos;ll desist.

If anything truthful can be said about this game, it is that you are going to be surprised. Your existing gaming experience could make it more of a bad surprise, but since you are here on GOG, you might be better prepared than others.

My honest opinion is that this game is 4 out of 5. It really has some issues with keeping the player actually playing this game. It has one of the best stories ever told in the game industry, game mechanics are engaging and the town is mysterious. But somehow you are constantly being pushed away from the game by its depressing atmosphere, sometimes monotonous and repetitive (to a certain point) process and storyline conundrums.  But because it is such a unique experience, I gave it 5 stars. 

For me, this game is of unique genre – time management game. Labyrinthine town layout with multiple dead ends, slow walking pace, complex item exchange system, survival mechanics even opening cupboards and filling empty bottles serve the purpose of reducing players time.  Basically every and each mechanic in this game serves one purpose: to deprive player of valuable time. When you stop seeing multiple survival gauges pending your attention and instead start to see only one real meter behind it, which is time, after that the game becomes much more clear.
Developers describe their game as decision making simulator. Even making the proper turn and not making it while traveling from A to B could be life-changing. The time pressure is there to make your decisions really matter.

This is one of the few games, where you have to optimize your way of thinking, not your reflexes or tactics. You can’t loot your way to the win here or LMB spam all the enemies. Just cope as best as you can</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">8</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>eee43c00-7e40-11e9-8f3b-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>You had your second chance. </review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">152</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/eee61aa8-94ed-11e8-a00c-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/eee61aa8-94ed-11e8-a00c-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2013-04-12T13:13:56</review:date>
        <review:description>That is a great game, It does not reach Baldur&apos;s gate level but it&apos;s still pretty good.
The first part is marvelous, you can choose either to be a good knight defending the town. an inquisitor that is quite evil against the magicians or a magician tracked by the inquisition in the same town with really different quests. you can replay the first part with the three faction without doing the same thing twice...
The problem arise when you leave the town and start the real quest, your faction doesn&apos;t really matter anymore, the story from there is on rail without any freedom at all...
in summary a great first part that you can replay at least 3 times without seeing the same things and with really different mission with lot of freedom but with the rest of the story being pretty linear without much freedom and that is basically the same for all your character...</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>eee61aa8-94ed-11e8-a00c-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>The first part is marvelous</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">7</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/ef1ebb8a-c740-11e8-85f4-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/ef1ebb8a-c740-11e8-85f4-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2018-10-03T22:17:13</review:date>
        <review:description>Indiana Jones and the infernal machine is even today my favorite game. So a dream came true when I stumbled across it here. I realised the provided version is only English but still I didn&apos;t even hesitate to buy it. 
But directly in the beginning I got an uncomfy feeling when he started speaking in English. That was the point were I knew I have to play it German to get the full immersion back into my childhood. So I picked up my original disk of the German version I have in my drawer, picked two files (&quot;CD1.GOB&quot; and &quot;CD2.GOB&quot; if your interested) off of it and exchanged the gog version ones et voila texts and voices are now German. 
Unfortunately this removes the configuration for the controller mappings which I think has to do with the new files not being part of the original installation process where the linking between controller configurations and the game is done. As the settings for custom mapping your buttons ingame is broken they can&apos;t be adjusted afterwards.
But as of right now changing the language was not a problem what so ever so why wasn&apos;t it implemented in the first place.
I hope the Gog team fixes the controller mapping issue, then the two stars will turn into a solid five. </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">13</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>ef1ebb8a-c740-11e8-85f4-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>Why the language limitation...</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">19</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


