    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/f2152650-37fc-11ec-a4cc-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/f2152650-37fc-11ec-a4cc-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-10-28T17:40:07</review:date>
        <review:description>Приключения со всеми вытекающими обстоятельствами, вложены элементы психологии, детектива, ужастика и даже есть шанс погибнуть. Как положено, современная игра - приключение, классика жанра. 
Хорошей игре - хорошая цена: в цену должно всё входить, не только игра, но и что создавалось разработчиками, вот такой труд надо ценить.
Только когда цена больше чем у польского Ведьмака, и графическое исполнение дешевле, то и цена должна быть соответствующей.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>f2152650-37fc-11ec-a4cc-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Хорошей игре - хорошая цена</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/f21b3104-5969-11e9-90c8-00163e4e60cc -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/f21b3104-5969-11e9-90c8-00163e4e60cc">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-04-07T22:18:37</review:date>
        <review:description>I just finished this demo, and I have to say it was more fun than I expected. I thought it would be just a typing game, like Typing of the Dead, but there&apos;s so much more to it. The demo does not take long, about half an hour, so if you&apos;re wondering about the game I highly recommend checking out this demo.

The game is a mixture of typing game (a la Typing of the Dead) and 2D bullet hell (a la Enter the Gungeon). You use the arrow keys to dodge protectiles while simultaneously typing words and phrases to do things like attack the enemy, disarm explosives, etc. There is controller support, but I only played with the keyboard, so I can&apos;t comment on that.

The story doesn&apos;t take itself too seriously and is both fun and funny. The characters are over-exaggerated stereotypes, and there&apos;s a good mix of pop culture and meta references in the dialog. The game looks great, if you&apos;re into these types of 2D games, and sounds great, too! The soundtrack is available on GOG as a separate purchase, apparently. I haven&apos;t heard enough of the music to decide if it&apos;s worthwhile, though.

The game seems well-balanced, as well. I was able to beat the demo the first time through, but it wasn&apos;t a walk in the park. It took timing, adapting, and other skills. This is definitely a game you *play*, rather than just a game that takes you along for the ride.

Even though I&apos;m giving the game 5 stars, there are some minor issues like typos. You&apos;d think if any game had thorough spell-checking, it&apos;d be a typing game. Also, at least in the demo, I feel like the ration of cut-scene to game play was a bit heavy on the former. I&apos;m usually very patient and enjoy lore and story, but in this demo I found myself just wanting to get to the action. Even with as fun as the story is, I started to skim it just so I could get to gameplay faster.

The end result of playing this demo is that, I&apos;m almost certainly going to by the game at some point. Definitely give it a shot! </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>f21b3104-5969-11e9-90c8-00163e4e60cc</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Fun demo! Neat game!</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/f2254988-5960-11ec-8192-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/f2254988-5960-11ec-8192-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-12-10T04:29:05</review:date>
        <review:description>2000年前后经历1代和3代，不知道为何当时没有找到2代。再也不见的童年。游戏本身没有达到多高的成就，但承担这份回忆就够了。</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>f2254988-5960-11ec-8192-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:rating>
        <review:title>童年回忆</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/f2763346-f789-11ea-98f6-fa163e93294d -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/f2763346-f789-11ea-98f6-fa163e93294d">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-09-15T22:30:43</review:date>
        <review:description>I am a huge fan of roguelikes, first person shooters, rhythm games, and I&apos;m a musician. Rhythm is not an issue for me. I literally found this game to be unplayable. This has nothing to do with the unique concept that the game has, but everything to do with how poorly the game controls. I will have a hard time explaining it, but if you&apos;re planning to play with a controller, you&apos;re in for a nightmarish time.

The controls in this game are horribly unresponsive. I want to be clear about this too - I don&apos;t mean that the game thought I was shooting off the beat or not rhythmically on point, but rather the actual movement, and looking around just feels wrong. I tried different sensitivity options and nothing felt right. I literally stopped playing after 4 minutes with this game.

The idea seemed cool, music was not great, based on the first level, but the controls.... If you&apos;re planning to play with a controller, steer clear from this one. </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">46</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>f2763346-f789-11ea-98f6-fa163e93294d</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:rating>
        <review:title>Really Bad</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">16</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/f2d3b668-87d3-11ea-9281-fa163e93294d -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/f2d3b668-87d3-11ea-9281-fa163e93294d">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-04-26T18:38:17</review:date>
        <review:description>The first one is more horror than survival and the second one is more survival than horror.
But the secong does give you a coerent story and builds the characters and the world better.
The only thing that drags a bit is the stealth sections where you have to follow a specific script to progress.
This one is way more cinematic and there where times i wished to participate more in the form of QTE instead of just watching.
This one feels morte like a unique game although you can trace the inspirations.
It ends on a high note so i suppose shinji can just move on to another project.

It still suffers from some of the same troubles of the first one like texture pop ins and some glitches, but nothing that hurts the game for what it is.

Played both back to back and can surelly say that both are great, intense, deeply creepy and sometimes horrifying, with great music and sfx overall.

Few games make me want to play to the end.
This one is a step further and the next step can be what made both games great.

9/10</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>f2d3b668-87d3-11ea-9281-fa163e93294d</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>On a high note</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/f2d3c5b2-c5b6-11e8-866d-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/f2d3c5b2-c5b6-11e8-866d-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2018-10-01T23:16:58</review:date>
        <review:description>Disclaimer:I&apos;m a huge Indy fan(who isn&apos;t?)so my final score is not(maybe)as critical as it should be but nevertheless here we go.

Let&apos;s start with the obvious technical side since the game is pretty old,for the time the graphics were pretty good(although in the end i preferred Grim Fandango to this game back then)and i find them still &quot;charming&quot; now,the soundtrack and the sound effects are awesome of course(the snap of the whip is enought to take you back to the movies) and voice acting pretty good even if Ford is not providing his voice for Indy(in the italian version sold at the time we had the original voice actor from the films!)

The gameplay is good enough,i found the puzzles a bit less obtuse than some of the ones in the Tomb Raider series but of course there&apos;s still a lot of pushing blocks around that starts to get annoying when done too many times.

Indy himself is a little bit stiff in its movements and the shooting/combat stuff is definitely not the strong point of this game but not impossible to overcome(played on intermediate difficulty)

Regarding bugs and glitches i had a few crashes and encountered some bugs(quicksave and save often!)and one instance of &quot;stuck indy&quot; that i was able to fix by opening the console with F10 and typing &quot;fixme&quot; but i was able to complete the game without (major) problems.(Win7 64Bit)

All in all this is a great Indy game if you&apos;re a fan of the franchise.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>f2d3c5b2-c5b6-11e8-866d-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Not perfect but very good!</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">18</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/f2df6a8e-e022-11e9-b552-d2856434588f -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/f2df6a8e-e022-11e9-b552-d2856434588f">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
