    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/f3021930-3166-11eb-9bfe-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/f3021930-3166-11eb-9bfe-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-11-28T12:46:19</review:date>
        <review:description>This game is simply fantastic. It&apos;s a party based, real-time-with-pause, linear rpg with a very unique and lovely atmosphere. 

The setting is very unique and very much reminiscent of western European folklore. During the course of the game you will visit quite a number of different locations, from beautiful towns to dark swamps, mountain tops, dungeons, etc. All of which are hugely fun to explore and thanks to lightning and soundtrack offer a distinct atmosphere.

Character development is deep as well with each character being able to choose from learning spells, raising attributes or learning combat or non-combat skills. The different classes play and feel different. If you&apos;re starting out, I wouldn&apos;t recommend creating a character specialized purely on social skills, though. Most of the time it gives you better rewards, but your party members will have to carry all of the late game encounters which is probably not good for your protagonists ego ;)

Overall I highly recommend this game to anyone who likes Baldur&apos;s Gate, Neverwinter Nights, Dragon Age or Pillars of Eternity!</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>f3021930-3166-11eb-9bfe-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>The best RPG from Germany to date</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">48</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


