    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/f7f5d27a-f5d8-11ea-ab5c-fa163e7ab9c9 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/f7f5d27a-f5d8-11ea-ab5c-fa163e7ab9c9">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-09-13T18:51:21</review:date>
        <review:description>I&apos;d never played this game with its original release. However, I was enticed by a streamer playing Re-Reckoning and have been enjoying it. That being said, it clearly has some graphical and camera issues that I&apos;ve observed.

When talking to NPCs, occasionally the camera will be placed over their head, put your character in a weird place to converse with them or at an angle that obscures the NPC.

The graphics to me are good, I know some think they&apos;re not enough of an upgrade from the original game. Having not played the original, I&apos;d say they&apos;re pretty good.

The movement is pretty choppy and jarring. I&apos;m seeing poor framerates, which for a game of this graphical caliber shouldn&apos;t be the case.

Overall, I&apos;ve been enjoying the other aspects. The story is interesting, the crafting is fun. The combat is entertaining. It&apos;s a good game to pick up and play for a bit.</review:description>
