    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/f81f13ec-5033-11ea-b5fb-fa163e93294d -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/f81f13ec-5033-11ea-b5fb-fa163e93294d">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-02-15T22:44:32</review:date>
        <review:description>I was hoping that with the launch of this DLC we will finally have The Legacy Update here on GOG. 

For those who didn&apos;t know what have special this patch here is the info from the Patch Notes: &quot;The Legacy Update now gives you access to all of the major iterations of the game that we&apos;ve released. So, you can now play 0.0, 0.1, 0.2 and so on...Cool huh?&quot;

But here we are, more than two months from this patch and nothing. Funny thing is that in early versions the custom game wasn&apos;t possible, only via MODs that only works on Steam. Then, several months later we finally had an official custom MOD ingame, but at that time I lost the mood for playing, just because I had less time. Now I have some time again with this new launch and want to play some previous versions that I lost before play this new one and I can&apos;t. 

Just disappointed again...</review:description>
