    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/f8deae64-821d-11ec-801b-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/f8deae64-821d-11ec-801b-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-01-31T00:42:58</review:date>
        <review:description>I was looking for another fun platformer after playing Ori and the Blind Forest and Unbound delivers. It&apos;s a fun, short title. Not a lot of story but the puzzles are fun and it looks great. Portal mechanics are neat.

Some things to note are: 

- There are two endings depending on your completion of the &quot;optional&quot; levels. I skipped the optional levels because the first was super hard and consequently I got the &quot;bad&quot; ending.
- A controller (vs keyboard) will help out a lot
- There are a few bugs that aren&apos;t show stoppers. Boss music that doesn&apos;t stop after victory, double deaths, menus that can&apos;t be navigated when you change key bindings, etc. As mentioned elsewhere auto saves occur frequently so you lose almost no time restarting the game if, say, the music glitches.
- My experience on Ubuntu linux was a little frustrating as the game would lag, causing me to die even more frequently. This could possibly be a driver issue, but I thought it was worth mentioning.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>f8deae64-821d-11ec-801b-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Fun but difficult platformer</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/f8f2f1b6-93fc-11e8-9481-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/f8f2f1b6-93fc-11e8-9481-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2009-03-26T11:36:42</review:date>
        <review:description>I found this game have a exxelent story and furious gameplay.  You must try it!!</review:description>
