        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Heroes of Might and Magic formula works</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">84</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/fb2c635a-c2c9-11eb-bfdf-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/fb2c635a-c2c9-11eb-bfdf-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-06-01T14:10:32</review:date>
        <review:description>I really want to give this game a decent rating, but I can&apos;t. 

I bought it at an 85% discount. For that price, it&apos;s  not terrible -- so far -- but it is still needlessly annoying. 

There is NO excuse for any modern game not providing adequate in-game documentation and feedback, such as:

(a) info about the game basics, features, menus, icons, etc. There is a &quot;tutorial&quot; of sorts that  pops up ONE TIME, By the time you need that info, and don&apos;t quite remember which cryptic symbol represents what, YOU CAN&apos;T RE-ACCESS the tutorial data. Ridiculous. 

(b) Tooltips! Seriously, folks -- this is the PATCHED game, apparently with many IMPROVEMENTS, and it&apos;s clear the devs have been hearing about this from day 1. Sorry guys, but you cannot get even a neutral 3-star rating when your interface doesn&apos;t even show what a skill will do when you hover over it, or what a cryptic icon I guess we&apos;re all supposed to have memorized after one glance at a tutorial page means. 

This game feels like it could be pretty good. It could be worth a good bit MORE than $4.25 I paid for it. But if the devs haven&apos;t been willing, after more than enough feedback, to provide basic quality-of-life features the player has every right to expect, even from indie games ... sorry. The game currently gets a POOR rating. 

I might not ask for my $4.25 back. I&apos;m going to give it a couple more hours investment and see if the overall experience can overcome the sheer thoughtlessness of the interface. It seriously wouldn&apos;t have taken a lot of effort on the developer&apos;s part for the game to feel worth the investment at twice the price or even more. But as it stands ... I feel like I probably overpaid. 

As I said, the experience seems like it COULD be so much better. 

</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>fb2c635a-c2c9-11eb-bfdf-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>The experience could be so much better</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">21</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/fb45b2c4-0658-11ec-8829-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/fb45b2c4-0658-11ec-8829-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-08-26T13:32:58</review:date>
        <review:description>Maybe harder than it needs to be.
I have nearly six hours of gameplay at this point, and have barely crawled to level 5. I still get my head caved in whenever I leave the starting area, if I&apos;m not incredibly careful.

But sometimes it&apos;s good when games are hard, and frankly, you shouldn&apos;t be ashamed of just setting the difficulty lower. 

You know what? I don&apos;t have a lot of patience for most games. If I didn&apos;t like one, I would never GIVE it six hours - I would be unlikely to give it 30 minutes!

So don&apos;t be afraid of the difficulty, don&apos;t be afraid of setting the difficulty TO something you feel is fun, and explore a world where every corner you stick your nose into is hiding something.

And die. Die so much, oh my god.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>fb45b2c4-0658-11ec-8829-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>This game is hard</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">10</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/fb4bf186-83d5-11ea-b342-fa163e93294d -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/fb4bf186-83d5-11ea-b342-fa163e93294d">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
