    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/fd304cd4-330e-11eb-be40-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/fd304cd4-330e-11eb-be40-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-11-30T15:21:43</review:date>
        <review:description>&quot;Freshwater Frenzy&quot; est un add-on qui ajoute un grand nombre de fonctionnalités (toutes intéressantes), ainsi que de nouveaux animaux, mais cette fois, ils sont d&apos;eau douce !

- Une nouvelle campagne (centrée autour des nouvelles fonctionnalités), de nouveaux défis, de nouveaux aquariums/décorations et peintures, des accessoires à assigner à vos employés...

- Outre les poissons d&apos;eau douce, il y a des mécanismes à découvrir : la reproduction et l&apos;acidité de l&apos;eau.
La reproduction ajoute aussi des exigences pour que vos poissons se reproduisent et, pour que certains obtiennent de nouvelles couleurs et/ou motifs.

Si vous avez aimé le jeu principal, vous aimerez cet add-on.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>fd304cd4-330e-11eb-be40-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Très bon le poisson.</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/fdaadb78-b82d-11e9-b458-26a08e025e12 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/fdaadb78-b82d-11e9-b458-26a08e025e12">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-08-06T09:38:48</review:date>
        <review:description>In my opinion one of the best mystery/narrativ puzzle games out there. I call it narrative puzzle because that is what you try to solve here. As you piece together one fate after the other, the big picture becomes ever clearer. I felt the puzzles had just the right difficutly for my taste - sometimes hard but never unfair.
The best part for me, however, is the atmosphere this game manages to create. At first I was skeptical about the graphical style. But not only does it fit the scenery perfectly (realistic graphics would just not work that well here, I am sure), it also helps the gameplay along by forcing the player to look closely at the scenes they are presented with. The music adds to this as well, setting the right tone for these scenes.
All in all an original masterpiece.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>fdaadb78-b82d-11e9-b458-26a08e025e12</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Atmospheric Narrative Puzzle</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">8</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/fdb4d9f6-bef8-11eb-ac21-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/fdb4d9f6-bef8-11eb-ac21-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-05-27T17:36:58</review:date>
        <review:description>[1.0] Release Review

There is no contender to Sid Meiers Pirates and this game wont change that, however it has a good foundation to offer fun, for some time at least.

The graphics are average - bad but the gameplay works. You start with a Sloop that cant kill enemies and, unless you instantly understand the system at hand, will die in a few hits. Once you get some gear and especially the overpowered but often fun Abilities you are able to overcome your enemies.

Still, I found myself using damaging Abilities exclusively since using cannons exposes your ship to getting killed by return fire. The game is in need of some more balancing.

Trading is possible but doesnt really work since ports only buy 1 ware and sell you 1 other and there is far more profit to make by salvaging wrecked ships found around the map or killing enemies once youre stronger. There is currently no map in that ports arent marked anywhere so trading just doesnt work.

The story is nice - you can play as male or female - but it isnt a driving point.

The gear / loot system seems to be the main focus of the game, yet I didnt find as much good loot as I hoped and was most often than not selling what I got and buying the best gear in ports as opposed to looting it.

There is a skill tree that works but since there is a level cap most players will stop at that point. For games like this there really needs to be an incentive to continue playing the game. Borderlands gave you small % boosts on top of your skills and it worked for every character you created thereafter.

Ship selection is average, with only 5 possible ships, but items change the look of your hull and sails so there is variation to these.

I hope the developers got the means to improve on this foundation. A few patches could improve the games looting and fun moments and bring it closer to what Sid Meiers Pirates offered. Id currently rate it a 3/5 but its reasonably priced.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>fdb4d9f6-bef8-11eb-ac21-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Funny little gem but mostly raw</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">9</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/fdb6d378-611a-11eb-9d37-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/fdb6d378-611a-11eb-9d37-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-01-28T05:43:31</review:date>
        <review:description>Cyber Shadow plays a bit like the 8bit NES Ninja Gaiden games with some modern twists. While crouching and wall grabbing aren&apos;t present, the platforming and timing of strikes are spot on. The story boards in between stages capture a very NES Ninja Gaiden vibe. The music adds a sense of engagement to the stages. The subweapons system is more RPG like, with swappable upgrades, than the 8bit Ninja Gaiden games. Looks like Yacht Club is sitting on another winner thanks to the designs of MekaSkull.

Played on Linux Mint 17.3 64bit, with a Logitech F310. Should also be compatible with Ubuntu 14.04.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>fdb6d378-611a-11eb-9d37-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Yacht Club&apos;s Sitting On Another Winner</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">9</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


