    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/fde904fc-93f0-11eb-abb5-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/fde904fc-93f0-11eb-abb5-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-04-02T23:21:22</review:date>
        <review:description>Sorry to say, but I can&apos;t get the copy of Northgard I just bought to run. Run from GoG Galaxy I get a popup &quot;hl quit unexpectedly.&quot; Run from the commandline, I get a bit more info

$ ./osx/run.sh
Init GOG
dyld: lazy symbol binding failed: Symbol not found: _objc_opt_respondsToSelector
  Referenced from: osx/libSDL2-2.0.0.dylib (which was built for Mac OS X 10.15)
  Expected in: /usr/lib/libobjc.A.dylib

dyld: Symbol not found: _objc_opt_respondsToSelector
  Referenced from: osx/libSDL2-2.0.0.dylib (which was built for Mac OS X 10.15)
  Expected in: /usr/lib/libobjc.A.dylib

./osx/run.sh: line 1: 34706 Abort trap: 6           DYLD_LIBRARY_PATH=osx ./osx/hl sdlboot.dat &quot;$@&quot;

Notice the error message says the libSDL2-2.0.0.dylib library was built for Mac OS X 10.15 —I&apos;m on 10.14.6 (don&apos;t want to upgrade to a later version for compatibility reasons). Mailed the developer&apos;s support address, asking, &quot;Do you have a fix/workaround or should I request a refund?&quot; I await a reply.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">9</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>fde904fc-93f0-11eb-abb5-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:rating>
        <review:title>Won&apos;t run on my Mac (OS X 10.14.6)</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


