        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/ff49ccc4-1545-11ec-8cc1-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/ff49ccc4-1545-11ec-8cc1-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-09-14T13:24:52</review:date>
        <review:description>The devs must have been passing around the crackpipe when they created this game.
I have NEVER played a game with more futile navigation and combat tactics, and I have been a gamer since the mid-1980s, witnessing the evolution of gaming from choppy, pixelated, interpolated graphics and mundane story lines, to having compelling and complex plots, smooth, rich textures and intuitive combat and navigational options. I must stress; THIS GAME IS NOT ONE OF THESE. DO NOT WASTE YOUR MONEY AT *ANY* PRICE.
The camera POV is absolutely absurd!!! It literally has a mind of its own, and will have you nauseated throughout the entire game.
Not to mention, no matter HOW you buff and level up, the bosses are just too powerful and unbeatable.
The game just punishes you 100% of the time, making you scramble for healing every turn of the game.
Sadly, it has JUST ENOUGH intrigue that it hooked me for a long enough period of time, that I simply cannot ask for a refund, although I certainly deserve one, given all the time I&apos;ve wasted on this title.
I&apos;m proud to say that I have a pretty solid self-esteem, but woe to the person with security issues - this game will push you over the edge.
SHAME on the devs and SHAME on GOG for supporting them by releasing this product and promoting it to me via email like hucksters.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">134</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>ff49ccc4-1545-11ec-8cc1-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:rating>
        <review:title>PURE GARBAGE</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">13</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


