    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/ff81f256-deb7-11e8-a3ba-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/ff81f256-deb7-11e8-a3ba-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2018-11-02T17:57:28</review:date>
        <review:description>The game took me 8 hours to complete 100% (I think, I don&apos;t know if GOG counts the time when paused). It was very entertaining, not a kind of game you find often, and some things didn&apos;t go as I expected at all. A couple of bodies where difficult to find (the one in the window of a cabin, and the one in the barrel). Several identities I found by trial and error (specially within the same rank), but I don&apos;t know if I just missed clues. All in all, money well spent.</review:description>
