    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/ff9b7fa2-a55b-11ea-8e9c-fa163e62c76a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/ff9b7fa2-a55b-11ea-8e9c-fa163e62c76a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-06-03T08:35:13</review:date>
        <review:description>I have played all of the games in the series, and I believe this is the best one out of all of them. Each entry so far seems like it has one annoying flaw that holds it back from being really fun - the map being either too confusing or too simple, backtracking, selectively useful abilities, gameboy technical limitations, etc. But I finally feel like this entry has it all perfect. Even coming off the heels of Half-Genie Hero, as soon as you start this one you&apos;ll notice it feels different. The controls are somehow even tighter. The animations and backgrounds are fantastic as always. Voice acting is done for many of the characters. Fully animated cutscenes! Enemy and character variety is huge. And I think the balance of game mechanics is just about right.

Mechanically, here is what there is:
- The mostly linear layout of Half-Genie Hero is gone. The map is a single interconnected overworld with a lot of verticality, like classic Metroidvania. Fast travel is provided between the main regions to reduce tedious backtracking.
- From the overworld are gates to self-contained dungeons designed with the classic Zelda formula. Go in, explore, fight the midboss, get an ability, unlock the dungeon, fight end boss.
- Abilities are instantaneous transformations that work like the pirate tools from Pirate&apos;s Curse. They are very fast, versatile, and fun.
- Dances are done for more &quot;specialized&quot; actions (not transformations), but even then there are a surprising number of ways that each ability gets used. For example, Rejuvenate will heal you, make plants grow, damage undead, and purify water.
- Monsters drop cards which function a bit like the soul system from Aria of Sorrow, letting you choose a set of specific buffs you can equip to match your play style.

My main complaint is the somewhat lackluster boss encounter design. There are multiple Risky encounters which are virtually identical, and the main bosses felt like awkward pushovers. Still, I highly recommend this game.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>ff9b7fa2-a55b-11ea-8e9c-fa163e62c76a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>The best Shantae yet</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">16</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/ffa7b850-1a39-11eb-bbcb-fa163e41fb2f -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/ffa7b850-1a39-11eb-bbcb-fa163e41fb2f">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-10-30T00:56:37</review:date>
        <review:description>3D Platformers aren&apos;t the most common genre nowadays, but everyone once in a while we get presented with a game that does the genre justice.

Pumpkin Jack is the debut outing from solo developer, Nicolas Meyssonnier. It has the personal attention and detail of one person, but has the polish and execution of an entire team. Everything about the game is surpisingly well realized, from the music, the storybook plot, and overall aesthetic.

I have finished it yet, but I&apos;m at the last stage now after about 4 hours. Despite the shorter length it is perfectly paced. Nothing outstays its welcome, and I have faith that when I do get around to finishing it, I will be satisfied with the journey.

The only point of contention worth mentioning is the price. I bought this game on sale for 20% off, which feels about right for the content. However, $30 seems a bit much considering Hat in Time has a lot more content for the same price (plus an active mod community). 

That being said Pumpkin Jack is one of the best gaming experiences I&apos;ve had in a while, and recommend it strongly to anyone who enjoys 3D platformers or would like to try something new.
</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>ffa7b850-1a39-11eb-bbcb-fa163e41fb2f</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Best 3D Platformer Since Hat in Time</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/ffa8ab38-be41-11ea-b82a-fa163e62c76a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/ffa8ab38-be41-11ea-b82a-fa163e62c76a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-07-05T01:02:05</review:date>
        <review:description>Одну звезду  поставил за отсуствия выбора в формате, мп3 только, вы серьезно? давайте флак, я предпочетаю покупки делать за качество, а издатель думает и так сойдет, купят голимый мп3шник. Не обижайтесь если хотите исправится, даю второй шанс))) Покажите что вам не все равно.</review:description>
