    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/ffac1b60-03f7-11ea-83e0-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/ffac1b60-03f7-11ea-83e0-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-11-10T22:23:46</review:date>
        <review:description>Ok, so I don&apos;t have this on GOG. I own and have played through this two times. 

The art style is amazing and wonderfully detailed. This is not my kind of game for a number of reasons. However this really caught me off guard. My wife originally got it and I wound up playing it. If you love story and character depth as much as I do then this will cure that itch. I won&apos;t spoil the game and there are much better reviews on this here but its really worth it if you are thinking about it yes put it in your cart on sale or not this game is a buy. </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>ffac1b60-03f7-11ea-83e0-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>This game is a BUY</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/ffaf504e-9045-11e9-a106-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/ffaf504e-9045-11e9-a106-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-06-16T17:49:52</review:date>
        <review:description>Such a nice change from all the colorful games. I enjoyed the game very much, it was fun because it is not over-complicated and spartan graphics makes you think about the story much more, which I like. It could overwhelm at first but after a while, with some information collected,  it was very understandable understandable what to do. With such graphics sound is of paramount importance and this game scorces high on that front. </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>ffaf504e-9045-11e9-a106-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Very pleased with the game</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/ffd099f4-867f-11e9-8879-00163e4e60cc -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/ffd099f4-867f-11e9-8879-00163e4e60cc">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-06-04T07:19:52</review:date>
        <review:description>Return of the Obra Dinn is an acquired taste initially due to the graphics, but this is amazingly done and it is one of the historically accurate games I ever played in all my life. Even if you are not familiar with the time period or are normally good at puzzle games, the game will give you subtle nudges towards the possible answers. 

The voice acting and sound effects are key for this game and a lot of effort was done to make sure the accents would be correct and that the sound effects would match with what would be happening in the scene. 

Overall, this game is a pleasure to play and I highly recommend it to anyone that is a fan of logic-based deduction and/or good story-telling. </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>ffd099f4-867f-11e9-8879-00163e4e60cc</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>A masterpiece</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/ffdde578-93ff-11e8-a5e4-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/ffdde578-93ff-11e8-a5e4-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2010-12-02T17:07:01</review:date>
        <review:description>&quot;Lionheart: Legacy of the Crusader&quot; offers a unique roleplaying adventure which taking place in an excellent alternative history. You&apos;ll run in to the famous Knights Templars and the Spanish Inquistion as well as many famous historical characters such as Leonardo da Vinci, Joan of Arc and even Shakespeare. Despite having a great storyline and an incredibly amount of historical lore, the rest of the game doesn&apos;t quite hold up. It&apos;s hard to point to a specific reason as to why, most of the time it simply feels uninspired, especially the level design - the world just feels very cramped together and it becomes a bit frustrating navigating the claustrophobic maps back and forth (there is a lot of backtracking and running around). In the end this is still a GOOD game, but not as great as it could have been. If you truly love RPG&apos;s you should at least give it a try!</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>ffdde578-93ff-11e8-a5e4-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>A unique roleplaying experience</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/ffe12c1a-94f9-11e8-8084-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/ffe12c1a-94f9-11e8-8084-00163e97122a">
