    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/0c5abee8-9fe2-11eb-87ab-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/0c5abee8-9fe2-11eb-87ab-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-04-18T04:04:38</review:date>
        <review:description>Is it value for money? NO.  IS it as inmersive and story driven? NO. Does it have a Great twist? NO!!

It is artistic and interesting but not enduring nor surprising. Could have had quite a few more npcs with stories but didn&apos;t. Felt more like a test than anything else. 

Classic case of art over substance.  Get it on sale. Don&apos;t bother otherwise. I completed it in 3 hours whilst I was doing laundry.  I wont have a second playthrough for the achievements.</review:description>
