    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/0d663f7e-9ce5-11eb-b56d-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/0d663f7e-9ce5-11eb-b56d-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-04-14T08:48:35</review:date>
        <review:description>Old School.  It&apos;s a story wrapped in a game.

Note this is &quot;In Development&quot; with expected full release October 2022.

Notes of Bladerunner; a distopian, dirty future.  Meant to be played in a dark room.

The best thing about Colony Ship is that it eschews the paradigm whereby games studios construct games for profit by lowering all narratives to a common denominator.

The worst thing about Colony Ship is that it is not complete yet. http://irontowerstudio.com/colony-ship-news 

The other negative is that there is a railroady element in that skills must be obtained to a certain level to pass skill based checks - or else the story pushes you into combat (which is not as difficult as it was in Age of Decadence).  I expect this negative to be ironed out in the coming updates as locations and story unravel - as it was in Age of Decadence.

You are supporting a story in the In Dev/ Early Access, a piece of art, a new form of narrative literature - or depending on your play style - a brutal isometric turn based combat simulator.  You decide, Iron Tower has Both</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">12</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>0d663f7e-9ce5-11eb-b56d-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>for the 0.0003 pc of players</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">36</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


