    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/0d9ed0d4-6d53-11ec-849d-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/0d9ed0d4-6d53-11ec-849d-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-01-04T13:40:01</review:date>
        <review:description>I went in knowing very little about the game and I am so glad I did. Coming from someone who usually loathes non-linear storytelling I absolutely adored this and cannot wait to see what Lucas Pop has in store next. Finished it in three sittings totally around 11 hours to 100% complete the game and see the true ending.

Only negative I will say is that as you need to revisit memories it can be quite cumbersome. I found myself spending more time than I would like to admit moving from place to place in order to revisit memories. </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
