    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/00b65dfa-b2bd-11e8-8fc0-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/00b65dfa-b2bd-11e8-8fc0-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2018-04-14T22:55:18</review:date>
        <review:description>Once again I rage quitted a playthrough. 

Here is a description of one of the many bugs I&apos;ve been encounering since I got the game: 
I won a war against the US and tried to demand Callisto. I could select the planet but not confirm the selection.
Just to be sure I started a war with India which owned Ganymed with the same result: select planet and no confirm button was available. 

The game in general has some good ideas but imo is held back by mechanics that make no sense in a modern world scenario like claiming a neighboring province as a core. For me this feels more like an easter egg referring to Europa Universalis.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>00b65dfa-b2bd-11e8-8fc0-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:rating>
        <review:title>The same bugs as every year</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


