    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/0070b606-f9bb-11e9-a6d0-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/0070b606-f9bb-11e9-a6d0-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-10-28T21:41:57</review:date>
        <review:description>This is going to be a divisive little game.  It&apos;s really going to appeal to folks who played the original or already own the remake.

For folks who are new to Pathologic this is either going to encourage them to buy the full game or turn them off of it completely.  The game also makes more sense if you have some knowledge of the Pathologic&apos;s story before going in.

Personally, I dig it.</review:description>
