    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/019d70c4-e825-11ea-b2b9-fa163edf6d96 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/019d70c4-e825-11ea-b2b9-fa163edf6d96">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-08-27T08:20:22</review:date>
        <review:description>I read the reviews, but I found info online that said that Gog change logs were now the same version as steam now. Nope. doesn&apos;t seem that way. I bought the game today and checked the change log (which I could not see until I bought the game).  Aug 19 2019 is the last update I can see on Gog. On my partners steam account? updates in April 2020, May, June and the latest on July 30th. Gog users are peeved and rightly so. On the games steam discussion page, Gog users asked when Gog would get their update. 
The developer, Pathea games responded on 06 May,  saying thanks for the information, we will look into that,  followed by, our publisher just told us they are doing the test and translation，we hope it can be updated by end of this month. That was nearly 3 months ago now. 
All I hear are crickets.......... 
</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">13</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>019d70c4-e825-11ea-b2b9-fa163edf6d96</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:rating>
        <review:title>Pathea Games let Gog users down</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">50</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


