    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/033a53ee-a11e-11ec-b671-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/033a53ee-a11e-11ec-b671-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-03-11T11:31:21</review:date>
        <review:description>Je trouve que le jeu globalement très bien fait, mais il souffre de petits points qui vont peut-être vous embêter tout au long de l&apos;aventure.

Dans les points positifs, je dirais que j&apos;ai beaucoup aimé la direction artistique, la musique et l&apos;histoire.

Mais les points qui m&apos;ont gêné : 
- J&apos;ai l&apos;impression que le jeu est fait pour être jouer à la manette, car on ne peut pas intéragir avec beaucoup d&apos;éléments de l&apos;interface et il y a un raccourci pour chaque menu ;  et pour faire apparaître le peu d&apos;infobulles disponibles, il suffit d&apos;appuyer sur Tab.
- Clarté/Didacticiel insuffisants : à chaque fois que une petite icône apparaît lors d&apos;un bonus ou malus, on a aucune idée de ce qu&apos;elle peut signifier. Et il n&apos;y a aucun glossaire.
- Lors du recrutement des compagnons, on ne peut pas voir à l&apos;avance leurs capacités : manque de clarté/d&apos;infobulles.
- Les matériaux qu&apos;on ramasse sont presque tous utiles pour l&apos;artisanat, ce qui n&apos;est pas dit dans le didacticiel, mais ceux qu&apos;on ramasse sont trop aléatoires. Et vous ne pouvez pas les achetez, à part la fin ; mais du coup, ça ne sert plus à rien. De plus, ils pèsent assez lourds et vous ne pouvez les mettre dans votre coffre qu&apos;à la ville.
- On ne peut pas utiliser les objets de restauration partout, mais seulement dans les camps.
- Il faut penser à repasser en vue la ville à chaque début de chapitre pour être sûr de ne pas manquer de quêtes. De même, on sera amené à faire beaucoup d&apos;aller-retours si on ne veut pas manquer d&apos;entrées dans le codex (et même là, ce n&apos;est pas assuré !).
- Apès s&apos;être bien familiarisé avec les combats, les héros, etc. ; la majorité d&apos;entre eux ne sont pas vraiment difficiles et on commence à se lasser de les faire (+ les aller-retours ...).
- Il faut jouer le jeu 3 fois si on veut avoir tous les costumes.

Bon, j&apos;ai fait à peu près le tour. J&apos;ai quand même beaucoup aimé.
Pour finir, je conseille à ceux qui voudraient s&apos;y lancer de mettre plus l&apos;accent sur le marchandage que sur l&apos;artisanat.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>033a53ee-a11e-11ec-b671-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Pas mal de petits points gênants</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/0344861a-8750-11e9-ad00-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/0344861a-8750-11e9-ad00-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-06-05T08:08:53</review:date>
        <review:description>Never played the original 2 as I always hoped it will be released on PC one day. Also I am not a big fan of isometric games.
Nevertheless, I had the pleasure on playing it on the PS4 first, also at a heavy discount. While I did manage it, it is better on PC when you have full mouse control. 

The style is nice and I was excited to see the next cutscene. But the voice acting is just dreadful. No emotions in any of the stressful situations or any situation as such. It&apos;s like the actors were just requested to read the lines out. Also this must be the worst French- and Aussie accent I have ever heard.
The tactical option is more of a joke. Yeah, you can direct each character where to go and who they should shoot but the aftermath does not change that they still get shot at and just stand still after following their given path. 
Stealth is alright at the beginning of the game but later on it is more action driven. The AI is not very good as they midlessly run into your fire, occasionally take cover. 
And don&apos;t get me started on the underwater level. That is by far the worst part of the game with its quick healing monsters who still damage you regardless hitting air and incoherent where to go at times. Plus the character you play shoots slowly.

Regardless the negativities listed, it is engaging to keep playing. The romance between Hana and Rain is alright but heard that it was more daring in the previous titles with their sexual desires. Characters as such are alright and written well enough that you wont forget their names asap. 
The story is cheesy but interesting enough. The soundtrack is very good that it was worth getting the collectors edition, which was a dollar more. It is an OK game and I wnoder how the the remake or remaster will be like as it is an interesting universe.  
 </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>0344861a-8750-11e9-ad00-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:rating>
        <review:title>Worth it at a discounted price</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/038ecda0-2bfc-11ea-be6b-00163e4e60cc -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/038ecda0-2bfc-11ea-be6b-00163e4e60cc">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-12-31T20:33:17</review:date>
        <review:description>Love this game so far. I&apos;m quite a few scenarios in and enjoying all of them so far. This is a very faithful sequel to the original Fantasy General. It has a lot of the same feel and the mechanics feel familiar while all being updated for modern interface.

Graphics are solid and the game runs without any problems so far, even when leaving it running for a lot of hours at a time.

I especially like the use of the original soundtrack, really brings back memories and keeps that Fantasy General feel to the game.

My only real quibble so far is that I wish there was more unit variety or another faction. I am hoping this will come with DLC or mods. </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>038ecda0-2bfc-11ea-be6b-00163e4e60cc</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Faithful Sequel</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/04a3b768-80cb-11ea-9e69-fa163e93294d -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/04a3b768-80cb-11ea-9e69-fa163e93294d">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-04-17T19:46:43</review:date>
        <review:description>(My revised review from Steam)
Not a bad game - you should definitely buy and play it! - It just wasn`t was what I expected.

EW1 and it`s DLC scared the s@@t out of me. EW2 managed to do so until I got to the `open world part` and then it lost a lot of it`s drive. While the gameplay esp. in 1st P-mode made the game A LOT better, it threw away everything else that made EW1 special.

EW 1 was a tasty collection of truly demented and unique horror ideas. EW 2 feel very generic and 2 of the 3 bosses are lame. Esp the encounter with second boss (priest) is drawn out over 3 or 4 chapter (of 17) with basically no tension- or story-building. It just drags on. The first boss (photographer) I did not even consider a boss unitl the boss fight was over. This is the goofiest serial killer-trope you will came across by a long shot. Absolutley cringeworthy! 

Also there are like 4 basic types of enemies in the ENTIRE game, with the last new one appearing very late ingame and only 3 or 4 of them. The only unique enemies are the sawblade girl and the singing lady. Unfortunately encounters with them are rather short and note enough fleshed out but still easily the most scaring and interesting encounters in the entire game. The story is ok but rather one-dimensional. It also explains a lot where the original was twisted in a intriguing way and intentionally left some blank spaces to to build up the horror even more.

EW1 is like a B-Movie cult classic - lots of flaws but made with passion and imagination.
EW2 is what happens when the sequel gets the Hollywood-treatment to appeal to a bigger audience.
Also EW2 is a downgrade in scope similar like from Dishonored to Dishonerd 2. The Sequels just feel much smaller, even if they have better single features.

EW 2 isn`t a bad game in any way but it isn`t what made EW1 special. The change in tone in EW2 is  like Resident Evil 5, 6 compared to RE1,

</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">11</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>04a3b768-80cb-11ea-9e69-fa163e93294d</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:rating>
        <review:title>It just wasn`t what I expected</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">16</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/04a913e0-adbd-11ec-b701-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/04a913e0-adbd-11ec-b701-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-03-27T13:59:48</review:date>
        <review:description>Bardziej komfortowa rozgrywka, otwarte lokacje i fabuła kładąca nacisk na aspekt indywidualny. Miało to spowodować większą immersję a jednocześnie dać więcej funu graczom nie lubiącym świadomie niewygodnej rozgrywki. W korytarzowej części pierwszej gracz miał wrażenie, że głównym bossem są sami twórcy gry, rzucający wciąż kłody pod nogi gracza. Gracz musiał nie raz rozgryzać jedyny sposób na wyjście z opresji w oskryptowanych zdarzeniach. Dwójka z tego zrezygnowała. Żeby zginąć w części drugiej trzeba się bardzo postarać albo wyjść jak w Commando otwarcie na grupę potworów. Nadal więc najfajniejszym elementem obu części pozostaje skradanie i kombinowanie jak unieszkodliwić wroga. Dlatego więc szkoda, że nie postawiono na jeszcze większą swobodę rozgrywki w kontynuacji, bo zwabianie grupy wroga w kałuże rozlanej benzyny daje sporo frajdy. Cierpią za to projekty bossów, bo zamiast rozgryzać zagadki środowiskowe musimy się tylko martwić o pojemność magazynków.
Crafting ekwipunku i drzewko rozwoju bohatera rozdzielono i to bardzo dobre rozwiązanie. Gra nagradza za eksplorację. Ponownie - trzeba się bardzo postarać, żeby zabrakło nam amunicji albo części do jej stworzenia. Trzeba naprawdę bardzo źle grać.
Fabuła mnie niestety nie zaangażowała, mimo że jej przewodnią stawką jest jak najbardziej zrozumiała na płaszczyźnie emocjonalnej chęć uratowania córki. Nie wchodząc w spojlery - jedynka miała wyraźnego antagonistę i zwykłe pragnienie wyrwania się z koszmaru. Część druga rozmywa napięcie i stawkę w niepotrzebnych plot-twistach i mnożeniu antagonistów. I jeszcze samo STEM - jest tu gdzieś recenzja po angielsku punktująca absurdy istnienia i funkcjonowania takiego &quot;potężnego&quot; projektu. No ale... to w sumie tylko gra.
Podsumowując - podobały mi się obie części ale każda z nich ma inną filozofię rozgrywki. Część druga na pewno jest bardziej przystępna ale to chyba część pierwsza była bardziej satysfakcjonująca. W obu częściach bawiłem się dobrze, choć nieco inaczej.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>04a913e0-adbd-11ec-b701-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Też dobra, choć inna</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/04b27584-6183-11eb-9da8-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/04b27584-6183-11eb-9da8-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-01-28T18:08:11</review:date>
        <review:description>This is an NES game.  It&apos;s pretty crazy, but this could have reasonably been released on that hardware albeit at a much lower resolution and running on the NES&apos;s bagel toaster CPU.

And, yes, with that comes the difficulty that makes you want to blame someone in the room for falling into spikes.  It&apos;s all there.  I for one thank the devs for trying to make an &quot;actual&quot; NES game and all that entails.

This is more Batman on the NES than Ninja Gaiden to me, and I know Batman ripped that game off just very, very well.  I prefer Batman.  This game has that intense difficulty curve.  The bosses will require multiple failures to memorize their tricks so don&apos;t be disheartened.  There are infinite continues from dock stations as far as I can tell, but you get 5 or 6 hit points as you might have back then.

I also don&apos;t mind admitting I&apos;m a &quot;boomer&quot; to most of you at 37.  So being like Nintendo is nice to me.  But your milage may vary. </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>04b27584-6183-11eb-9da8-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Holy crap levels of precision NES.</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">24</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/04d86f3c-e559-11eb-9560-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/04d86f3c-e559-11eb-9560-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-07-15T13:40:06</review:date>
        <review:description>So little meaningful interaction.

It looks like a kids game, but there are crazy weird scary monsters, murdering and combat required to progress. 

I wrote a 4 star review when I got the game - it started well, but to progress the rather shallow story you have to continually grind.

The game play is - need object to help town - go mining / murdering.  Repeat.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">11</review:downvotes>
