    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/048b4190-4139-11eb-9306-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/048b4190-4139-11eb-9306-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-12-18T15:57:51</review:date>
        <review:description>It&apos;s obvious that this game is inspired by the classic RPG games, it has a lot of complexity, especially in character creation, game mechanics, and leveling,  something that might put off casual gamers, but I found it very attractive. It&apos;s based on a German table-top game, so anyone who has played D&amp;amp;D based RPGs should enjoy it. The story is pretty stereotypical, dragons, chosen one, the usual shebang. On the technical part, the game has been very stable, I played it for 50+ hours without any crashes at all.

On the downside, the character creating is somewhat limiting, classes and races are present, you can&apos;t play an Elven Elementalist or a dwarven necromancer, for example. Also, a lot of spells are race or class-restricted, unless you&apos;re playing with a human there won&apos;t be many offensive spells available for you to learn. 

I&apos;m giving it five stars not because the game is a masterpiece, but because it&apos;s fun and relaxing, after playing RPGs for over 20 years I&apos;ve learned to keep my expectations low.  If you played Dragon Age or Neverwinter nights this game will feel right at home.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>048b4190-4139-11eb-9306-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>A Decent Fantasy RPG</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">23</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/0482700c-40ac-11eb-a6dc-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/0482700c-40ac-11eb-a6dc-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-12-17T23:08:31</review:date>
        <review:description>This game has a demographic of people that love to smell their own flatulence, and call farts flatulence unironically...

I cannot for the life of me understand how anyone can rate this game a 5/5, or anything above 3 really, and the 2 stars are mostly for the effort and time it takes to put any game together.

If you are going into this &apos;game&apos; expecting a &apos;game&apos; you are sorely mistaken and honestly don&apos;t even get it. For whatever price you are getting it you will enter a drab grey city, the boring convoluted dialogue that loves to use pseudo intelectual conjectures and takes itself more seriously than any game has the right to and finally the plain embarassing combat mechanics makes this a sleepy, boring and outright crap game.

The 5 stars on this must be from people that like movies for their &apos;conceptual undertones&apos; rather than the actual substance. Just don&apos;t get it</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">69</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>0482700c-40ac-11eb-a6dc-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>Boring, tasteless garbage</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">12</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/05cfa1e6-9550-11e8-8640-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/05cfa1e6-9550-11e8-8640-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2014-08-18T20:03:15</review:date>
        <review:description>Just buy this. Really. Just do it. Then go download the FreeSpace Open Source Project installer, and the MediaVPs. You&apos;ll end up with a shiny &apos;new&apos; space simulator looking like it was written in 2013-ish with great gameplay, graphics, and the whole shebang.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>05cfa1e6-9550-11e8-8640-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>This + FSOpen = WIN</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/05f3d060-4647-11ec-9b70-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/05f3d060-4647-11ec-9b70-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-11-15T21:05:39</review:date>
        <review:description>I love the art, it&apos;s really beautiful and with the nice music it creates a great atmosphere.

But that&apos;s sadly about it. From the start on you&apos;re bombarded with information before you even started any real gameplay. And it&apos;s soley presented as a series of screens with copious amounts of text and some images. Not necessarily the most welcoming of entries, especially if you want to get into the game instead of reading stuff.

This is accompanied by a story in the style of an interactive novel. Again you&apos;re flooded with lore, names and plotpoints. I&apos;m sure those will probably be important at some point, but they aren&apos;t really well integrated into the gameplay. Also it&apos;s a rather average fantasy plot and as such there is definately too much of it at the beginning.

Finally the gameplay is okay, it&apos;s mostly lifted from &quot;Darkest Dungeon&quot; and differences in the mechanics to that title are rather superficial. Difficulty is jumping up and down, at one point i felt it too easy and then boom, two characters die in a fight. I didn&apos;t even really understand why the second one perished - Meh. 

The UI is made for joypads, playing with the keyboard is very fiddely. Mouse support is barely existent, this is obviously built with consoles in mind. You really need to like those kinds of games to enjoy this.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>05f3d060-4647-11ec-9b70-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>Beautiful art, but cumbersome gameplay.</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/05f446fc-952f-11e8-9795-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/05f446fc-952f-11e8-9795-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2014-03-15T03:23:41</review:date>
        <review:description>I forgot how fun this game really is. It had many cool features back in the day when it came out that most FPSs these day must include if they want to be the best. The game features some limited but fun interaction with NPCs, an original soundtrack (by Cypress Hill no less) and fast paced, frantic action. Oh and some awesome easter eggs from the Big Lewbowski and Pulp Fiction!</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>05f446fc-952f-11e8-9795-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Classic FPS</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/050ca1a8-8656-11e9-b7af-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/050ca1a8-8656-11e9-b7af-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-06-04T02:19:22</review:date>
        <review:description>This game is hard to pin down, a story driven survival horror/thriller game that has some simulation elements. The worldbuilding and music are great. The gameplay and story meld togeather very well to make you invested in both, the game is really hard, but you improve yourself and your character troughout. It you are looking for a grim world to sink into look no further. The missionstructure is really addicting, and might keep you playing for hours at a time. Its so great that they made this game! i could not get into the first one because of its rough edges, but this one has been on my mind for a while. Good luck on your journey to uncover the mystery of Pathologic.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>050ca1a8-8656-11e9-b7af-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>This game is unique</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">7</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/0510d1ba-93fe-11e8-bba5-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/0510d1ba-93fe-11e8-bba5-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2011-09-18T19:13:48</review:date>
        <review:description>Had a great time with that game. The action flow is fast, the level design totally wicked and the character control is very dynamic and responsive. Not to mention that very weird humour I am very addicted to now. This reminds me of an era where you did not have enough power not to focus strictly on crazy gameplay. You just don&apos;t see that stuff anymore.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>0510d1ba-93fe-11e8-bba5-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Aged relatively well!</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/0524350c-eb11-11ec-99eb-42010a340c26 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/0524350c-eb11-11ec-99eb-42010a340c26">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-06-13T15:04:47</review:date>
        <review:description>Having played many civilisation sims I thought this was worth a shot, but actually it wasn&apos;t. The game logic is poor and predictable, and the more you play the more predictable it becomes. Its not expensive so give it a punt if that&apos;s your thing but for me wasn&apos;t worth the time. </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>0524350c-eb11-11ec-99eb-42010a340c26</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:rating>
        <review:title>I should have read the reviews</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/05267e14-9455-11e8-9a57-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/05267e14-9455-11e8-9a57-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2010-12-25T14:28:33</review:date>
