    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/06ac6832-93fd-11e8-ac86-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/06ac6832-93fd-11e8-ac86-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2009-03-29T22:09:00</review:date>
        <review:description>What can I say about this game that hasn&apos;t already been said? Released in 1997, the graphics may look dated, but I assure you, here lies one of the nuttiest, most creative, and most varied games I&apos;ve ever had the pleasure to play. There would be no games like Ratchet and Clank if MDK had never come along. The levels are breathtaking, even today, bursting with cleverness and artistry, Tallarico&apos;s music is groundbreaking, the gameplay is addictive, fast-paced, and over the top in the best way possible. Flaws? A total of six worlds means it won&apos;t last you very long, but this is one of those games that demands replay, due to the never-flagging fun factor. If you truly enjoy creative, innovative, fun games, and you&apos;re not too chicken to play the classics, you *wil*l love this game</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>06ac6832-93fd-11e8-ac86-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>The DOOM of Third-Person Shooters</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">10</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/06be3b6a-b33d-11e9-8caf-f2193cf93094 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/06be3b6a-b33d-11e9-8caf-f2193cf93094">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-07-31T02:43:49</review:date>
        <review:description>My Friend Pedro is high adrenaline fun.  Pulling off the many moves in the game is satisfying and entertaining to look at.  Twirling down a rope while you shoot enemies surrounding you is amazing.  Kicking a frying pan into the air to richochet bullets off of is action movie levels of slick.  Each level usually introduces a new element or contains a themed component.

The game features high replayabilty, score chasing, and multiple difficulties.

The weakest part of the game, easily the story, serves its purpose to drive the character forward.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>06be3b6a-b33d-11e9-8caf-f2193cf93094</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Pure Octane Fun</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


