    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/065eddac-9ab7-11ea-841c-fa163e93294d -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/065eddac-9ab7-11ea-841c-fa163e93294d">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-05-20T19:29:06</review:date>
        <review:description>First, if you like a mix of Settler, Civilization, Warcraft3 and Age of Empire then don&apos;t read further and just buy it. On sale its a no brainer. For the DLC, well depends if you like multiplayer and skirmish then buy them, they do nothing to the single player campaign.

I play on an older system, FX8320e, Nvidia 1060, 16GB Ram, Windows 10 on a 4K display and its mostly a smooth gaming experience I had zero crashes during the single player campaign. 

German translation of the text is very good, so I suppose its the same with the other supported languages. (Voice is English during the small cut scenes with subtitles)

Pro&apos;s:
- very nice setting, well if you like Vikings you will love it
- story is very well written
- art-style and graphics kinda cartoonish but fits very well
- attention to detail to the max 
- very nice mix of various game mechanics, like in Warcraft 3 the hero unit gives several bonuses and each plays a bit different,  I simply love it
- for me very important, the UI and UX Design looks super polished and very well thought out
- you just feel its made by gamenerds
- the price, it took me now almost 20 hour to finish the single player campaign, its a steal on sale!
- music and sound are also quite a fit
- linux version = instant buy  (btw: Please GOG give us Galaxy for Linux!!)
- Multiplayer LAN MODE! (play it with your pals like its 1999 again)

Cons:
- the DLCS are a kinda pricey , I just bought them in hope to get a Northgard 2
- the fighting system can sometimes be a bit annoying, you need a lot of micromanagement for it in later missions of the campaign
- on the second difficulty level some missions can become trial and error

What I hope for a Northgard 2?

A kinda rework of the unit system when fighting, I dont know exactly how to do it, but maybe a more classic approach like build them inside the armory and not send workers to convert into it would be cool.
More cinematic and a campaign with all War Chiefs 

Just go wololo it ;)
</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">14</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>065eddac-9ab7-11ea-841c-fa163e93294d</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>A true Indy gem</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">138</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/06529026-e228-11e9-9710-16c7e410d44a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/06529026-e228-11e9-9710-16c7e410d44a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-09-28T19:41:54</review:date>
        <review:description>I remember getting this game not really knowing what to expect but sure enough, it didn&apos;t take long for me to be so immersed in the game I must&apos;ve finished it within the same week, school and all.

Not sure how it holds out the test of time or if it has the loving modding community of FS:2 but I recommend it to any FS fan. it part of the story of the FS universe and it is an epic one.

this game changed the definition of a space-sim for me</review:description>
