    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/06955ad4-d298-11eb-9f18-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/06955ad4-d298-11eb-9f18-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-06-21T16:53:15</review:date>
        <review:description>I liked the streamlined interface; the development trees; and random events. Battles are &quot;casual&quot; and not overly complicated. But, as KartoffelCheetah mentioned, too much time is wasted waiting for projects to be completed. Also, I feel the developers placed WAY too much emphasis on GDP to gain money (other then loans). So, even though you can play any country, if you play a &quot;less developed&quot; one, like I did, you&apos;ll spend even MORE time waiting to earn money to build your economy/GDP. At one point it got so boring I had a movie playing while waiting for tasks to get done. And God forbid your &quot;poorer&quot; country gets hit with a random negative world wide economic event, you&apos;ll be wasting more time still. But, I picked it up at low price and there is fun to be had. With a bit more rebalancing and reworks this game could&apos;ve been much better. </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>06955ad4-d298-11eb-9f18-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:rating>
        <review:title>Okay....at a sale price. </review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/0697ff5a-d5db-11eb-8e05-fa163e048183 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/0697ff5a-d5db-11eb-8e05-fa163e048183">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-06-25T20:30:25</review:date>
        <review:description>I really liked the game, the lore is well crafted, the art is beautiful and the soundtrack is on point!

The combat can get a little repetitive (once you find the right team for you), but personally I didn&apos;t mind, the game isn&apos;t long enough for the repetitive factor to become super annoying, and I didn&apos;t have to grind much in order to farm the materials for the relics I wanted.

Playing this game in 2021, I didn&apos;t find any bugs or errors, or at least not anything worth reporting, any problems that the game might&apos;ve had were probably patched.

Overall, I enjoyed my time playing Vambrace: Cold Soul, if you enjoy games like Darkest Dungeon and have a bit of money to spare, why not give it a try?</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
