    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/074d1424-25e8-11eb-b09e-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/074d1424-25e8-11eb-b09e-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-11-13T21:40:05</review:date>
        <review:description>Charming game that you can lose yourself in. Because of the simplistic graphics you can think that it will not offer much but it does. Not a game you can play for a few hours and you know what to expect as a lot of things come later in the game. The classes are distinct enough to make it replayabable.

It does have an old style feel to it but also a feel of it&apos;s own. Best played without the dungeon save where you can only save on the surface as it offers more of a challenge and force you to get stronger and play more intelligently.

It&apos;s more comparable to Divine divinity than Diablo in that it&apos;s more towards the RPG style of things than action orientatedMore meaning ful quests etc.



</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
