    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/08c0f218-93fe-11e8-8982-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/08c0f218-93fe-11e8-8982-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2009-06-18T16:54:12</review:date>
        <review:description>There is a community of dedicated fans at Hard Light Productions that have created a wonderful thing called Freespace Open, which improves gameplay, graphics, and brings a whole range of new campaigns to the field. You need a full version of Freespace 2 installed. GoG&apos;s version works perfectly. It also gives you &quot;Freespace Port&quot; which allows you to play Freesapce 1&apos;s missions, with full voice acting and music. With the bonus graphics!

The community has also re-made Silent Threat, cleverly named Silent Threat: Reborn. All worthy of the highest praise.

www.hard-light.net</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>08c0f218-93fe-11e8-8982-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Make sure to utilize FSOpen</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/08d1bf6c-943f-11e8-b769-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/08d1bf6c-943f-11e8-b769-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2010-02-22T15:08:06</review:date>
        <review:description>I bought the first Freespace years ago, played it then lost it the disk!!  The most interactive game I&apos;ve ever played, incorporating flight controls with squadron command.  It sucks you in with the story line.  Love this game.  And the sequel, FreeSpace 2.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>08d1bf6c-943f-11e8-b769-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Absolutely the best.</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/08e06c7e-7ff5-11ec-b255-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/08e06c7e-7ff5-11ec-b255-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-01-28T06:44:53</review:date>
        <review:description>Great storytelling, many hidden gems and overall experience that can&apos;t be given in may other games. Simply said unique and inspiring , for those who don&apos;t really understand the game make sure to play Anodyne 1 , it&apos;s not necessary but it will definitely help you out to appreciate this game far more than you are right now.

Works great on Linux with good performance so no issues there. 

10/10</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>08e06c7e-7ff5-11ec-b255-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>It makes you think afterwards</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/08e46364-0410-11ea-9000-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/08e46364-0410-11ea-9000-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-11-11T01:15:50</review:date>
        <review:description>I love everything about Battle Planet - Judgement Day. The gameplay, premise, and visual aesthetics are all superb. The permanent progression allows unspent upgrade chips to carry over to subsequent runs, while weapons, along with item upgrades can be shared by all characters. Meaning you only have to use your points on those two categories once. This allows you to focus on upgrading character specific traits between runs, or at upgrade posts after missions. The gameplay loop is based on being fair to the player, which makes it hard to stop playing.

Battle Planet feels fast, frenetic, and fun!! Controlling each avatar feels unique, and the overall feel of the game is buttery smooth. No complaints here, just a great game. Cheers to the development team.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>08e46364-0410-11ea-9000-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Awesome Game!!</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">13</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/080e6a56-3f66-11eb-9ac7-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/080e6a56-3f66-11eb-9ac7-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-12-16T08:15:01</review:date>
        <review:description>Drakensang vieillit très bien : malgré les années, il reste magnifique : ces environnements sont détaillés et colorés : cela rend l&apos;exploration très plaisante.

La musique est bonne : calme dans l&apos;exploration (J&apos;aime beaucoup les petites notes quand on charge une partie) et entrainante dans les combats. 

La VF est de bonne qualité même si tous les dialogues ne sont pas doublés. 

L&apos;histoire est sympa : rien de transcendant mais il y a quelques choix (sans grands impacts, hélas). 

On ne peut pas vraiment créer son personnage : on a accès à plus d&apos;une dizaine de &quot;classes&quot; et de races, il est simplement dommage qu&apos;il n&apos;y aucun impact dans notre aventure ; j&apos;aurais adoré qu&apos;on ait des commentaires sur notre race / classe. 

Petit bémol : les animations sont très rigides.

Je conseil fortement ce jeu !
</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>080e6a56-3f66-11eb-9ac7-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Très bon jeu </review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">8</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/08001758-28d2-11eb-a6db-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/08001758-28d2-11eb-a6db-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-11-17T14:40:10</review:date>
        <review:description>I&apos;m normally not a fan of action-RPGs and don&apos;t like games like Diablo so I was hesistant at first. But this game really surprised me. I didn&apos;t expect much when I purchased it but it&apos;s keeps me hooked for many days now. There are only four basic classes, but they play very differently, an intuitive and clean RPG-system, a big open world to be explored (a bit similar to Baldur&apos;s Gate 1, you explore the world on different maps but every part fits to the adjacent part) and many quests (most of them more on the &quot;traditional&quot; side, not overly complex, but entertaining nonetheless), a plethora of different equipment pieces, different climates and quite some settlements and cities to visit. The story is well written, there are different Kingdoms and factions (who will take notice of your actions), many random events on the road make the adventurer&apos;s life interesting (brigands, travelling merchants, hireable mercenaries,...). But beside all the features there is something very special about this game: It gives me a very &quot;classic&quot; feeling, the atmosphere is strong, everything is made with so much dedication and care that I enjoy it immensely. It&apos;s almost impossible to imagine that it&apos;s the work of one single genius. It&apos;s not an easy game however - especially for the first hours expect to die a lot. If you are easily frustrated I recommend using the &quot;casual&quot; mode - while it doesn&apos;t change the overall difficulty of encounters it allows you to quicksave your game in dungeons and your hero will recover up to 50 % of his/her health if not fighting - both features are a great help.
Overall Exiled Kingdoms is a great game for the RPG-connaisseur.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>08001758-28d2-11eb-a6db-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Great gameplay, interesting world, hard.</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">14</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/080650d6-9488-11e8-afc9-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/080650d6-9488-11e8-afc9-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2012-01-04T10:21:38</review:date>
        <review:description>This game defines all space shooters today, this is a well made, game, people like it. Its just a good game, and not to mention the 50,000 addons and mods for this game, it just rocks, get this game-- you wont be dissapointed</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>080650d6-9488-11e8-afc9-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>ONE OF THE BEST</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/081be41e-9456-11e8-b009-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/081be41e-9456-11e8-b009-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2011-01-05T16:25:15</review:date>
        <review:description>Freespace and Freespace 2 are amazing games. Even today, one would be hard pressed to believe they are over 10 years old. The graphics are simply stunning, and there is a community dedicated to supporting this even today. The story and voice acting are top notch. This is the deepest most well thought out video game I have ever played. Wing Commander series can&apos;t touch it. They just don&apos;t make them like this anymore. I could go on and on, but all the reviews under me speak for themselves. Do not hesitate to try this game or it&apos;s predecessor. You will be very pleased.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>081be41e-9456-11e8-b009-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Simply the best of space combat genre</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/08367366-beb6-11e9-935f-76ad47b73604 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/08367366-beb6-11e9-935f-76ad47b73604">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-08-14T17:07:44</review:date>
        <review:description>While the visuals are lovely, the gameplay itself is very repetitive and uninspiring. I did not find myself very engaged with the story of the game, so unfortunately it&apos;s not very enjoyable to me. This is a game you&apos;ll need to really love the story to enjoy in my opinion.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">12</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>08367366-beb6-11e9-935f-76ad47b73604</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>A Bland Gameplay Experience</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">17</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/0886264c-9494-11e8-9eef-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/0886264c-9494-11e8-9eef-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2011-12-17T04:56:23</review:date>
        <review:description>Brilliant controls, an engrossing storyline, awesome graphics (especially with mods) and a great atmosphere.

After the incredible game that was Descent: Freespace, this game expands and improves on its predecessor. Although I dream of a third Freespace being made, the amazing mods made by fans give you a massive amount of great content to experience.

Simply put, I cannot recommend this game enough. A true classic.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>0886264c-9494-11e8-9eef-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Best space simulator ever</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/089f6ab0-b20f-11e8-9ffa-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/089f6ab0-b20f-11e8-9ffa-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2017-02-13T01:23:08</review:date>
        <review:description>Ah, Freespace 2. I can talk hours about this series.

First of all, I&apos;d highly recommend Freespace 1. The gameplay is pretty much the same except Freespace 2 does everything better and more. But the story will make much more sense if you start from Freespace 1 and believe me, this is not just a simulation. This game has a lot of character to it and caring about the story will make it much better.

You will feel proud of your achievements as you move up the ranks in the Terran fleet, flying in various squadrons. One part of the game you&apos;ll fly a bomber, carrying heavy armaments that can take down capital ships, defending itself with heavy armor and auto turrets. Other times you&apos;ll be an interceptor, incredibly fast attacker that targets the bombs themselves, almost in a suicidal dive. There will also be occasions where you&apos;ll be included in projects with Vasudan, the alien species, but I&apos;d like to avoid spoilers.

You will care about the stations and main ships. You will gather badges. Your success on missions will unlock weapons faster and sometimes, exclusively.

And at least at some point, if you are me, you will shed tears.

Freespace series. More than a simulator.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>089f6ab0-b20f-11e8-9ffa-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>One of the best games ever</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">10</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/08910ee2-8f7b-11eb-b03d-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/08910ee2-8f7b-11eb-b03d-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-03-28T07:06:55</review:date>
        <review:description>I went in wanted to love this, I love the art, and the whole aesthetic of it, it&apos;s neat, I didn&apos;t get far to know if the story is as neat but I assume it&apos;s competent.

The major flaw to me is how the menu works, doing a simple thing like changing the order of your team is a major hassle, especially compared to Darkest Dungeon, the game is made for controllers so don&apos;t even think it&apos;s better on K+M.

During combat, hovering over skills doesn&apos;t say what they do, so you&apos;re blindingly clicking without knowing full well what type of attack it is.

It&apos;s the little things, the little things pile up to an unwieldy menu system, and guess what&apos;s the most important part of a turn-based RPG? Menus, it&apos;s what you&apos;re gonna keep using the ENTIRE GAME, so if it&apos;s a 30 hours game, that&apos;s at least 25 hours of menus, and if they are a hassle to get through or do simple things, then it&apos;s a failure of an RPG.

I&apos;m sure the game is good once you get used to that clunkiness, but it&apos;s too clunky for me, as much as I loved the art and style of the game, it&apos;s not enough to make me want to keep going.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>08910ee2-8f7b-11eb-b03d-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>Lost Potential due To Menu Design</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">8</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/09bc26c8-94c2-11e8-8f03-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/09bc26c8-94c2-11e8-8f03-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2012-07-18T21:39:13</review:date>
        <review:description>I played Freespace and i loved it. I missed the 2nd part because i had no time back then. Now it is awesome to finally play it. It is so much fun. But i actually just write this because many people say it doesn&apos;t work on WINDOWS 7. But it does. I bought it prior to check the compatibility. When i read it while i was downloading i was like &quot;crap&quot;. But it runs smooth and stable. No problems at all. Installed and played it. No  changes  or tweeks needed.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>09bc26c8-94c2-11e8-8f03-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Great game</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">7</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/09bda3d4-c51f-11e9-b3fe-3a3c94c3da20 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/09bda3d4-c51f-11e9-b3fe-3a3c94c3da20">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-08-22T20:54:30</review:date>
        <review:description>You play missions that only tell a story based on what you experience. No real story but simple fun. Destroy this. Eliminate these targets. Stop a convoy ....

This game is worse than Ghost Recon 1 imo but the fun level is somehow higher with a lower level quality. The first game somehow works better than the Delta Force 2 game on my PC.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>09bda3d4-c51f-11e9-b3fe-3a3c94c3da20</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Simple Fun</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/09eac214-2852-11eb-9b23-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/09eac214-2852-11eb-9b23-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-11-16T23:23:58</review:date>
        <review:description>I&apos;ve played a lot of glopol games in my time (Supepower 1 and 2, Supreme Command, etc.), and this seemed interesting, so I thought I&apos;d give it a shot.

Like many strategy games out there, you can pick any nation in the world. Unlike even some glopol simulators like Superpower, there are (to my knowledge) no real life alliances in play at the start of the game. That means no NATO, no EU, etc. You&apos;ll find Russia allying with Poland, Mexico allying with Cuba, and a host of other peculiarities as a result. Of course, as with many glopol games, that can lead to some interesting game routes, so this may not be a big deal to the casual gamer.

Political decisions are similar to Hearts of Iron 4, where there are paths you can take to improve your economy, become more of a dictatorship, etc. However, if you&apos;re looking for something as detailed as some of Paradox&apos;s titles, you won&apos;t find it here. Things are SUPER basic in terms of internal politics, and even government types range between democratic, authoritarian, and totalitarian. (Literally, those are the only ones you can use.) The result is that you will find yourself doing a lot of clicking, but after a while feeling super underwhelmed.

How wars are resolved, I really don&apos;t know. You have to select different kinds of strategies, whether the defender or attacker, but how all this works is hard to tell. It&apos;s also not entirely realistic. I played as Iran and went to war with Iraq, and basically launched my entire nuclear arsenal at them. What happened? Their army was still intact, and still kicking my butt... even though I&apos;m pretty sure if you nuked all of Iraq, things would be... not so good for them. Either way, if you&apos;re looking for strategy that goes beyond hitting the &quot;declare war&quot; button... again, look elsewhere.

Overall, I wouldn&apos;t call it a BAD game, but... would I invest money in it? Maybe if it went for sale for super cheap, but there are better titles out there you can invest your money in.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>09eac214-2852-11eb-9b23-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>Average Strategy Game</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


