        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">7</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/098d9534-2670-11e9-b932-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/098d9534-2670-11e9-b932-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-02-02T00:23:45</review:date>
        <review:description>Even if it had bit of a rough start, this game is definitely worth checking out. Especially when you&apos;re familiar with games like Harvest Moon or Animal Crossing, you&apos;ll find yourself at home. Even if not, this is a good one to jump into the genre. 

It sure does involve lots of grinding at some point, but it&apos;s still fun. And of course there&apos;s more to it than just chopping down wood and crafting things. The world and the characters are interesting and the relationship system is solid, making it fun and rewarding. RPG elements round off the whole experience.

TL;DR: Ignore the 1 star reviews about the update delays. The essential updates are now live anyway, so there&apos;s no point in that. Just buy this lovely game and get started! </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>098d9534-2670-11e9-b932-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Fun and addictive Harvest Moon-like game</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">20</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/09882234-359b-11eb-98ef-fa163e5fb782 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/09882234-359b-11eb-98ef-fa163e5fb782">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-12-03T21:09:16</review:date>
        <review:description>First, I ran into a bug where it would flip out with my controller, and I see zero support for it on the GOG forum, it&apos;s crickets in there.  Fortunately, it does work with the keyboard, but this is suboptimal, so this may have tainted my experience with it.

It&apos;s a quick paced, modestly fun shooter played in tiny, bite-size pieces.  They describe it as &quot;rogue-lite,&quot; and I suppose it is, in the sense that death is inevitable and you can keep some of your points to upgrade and try again, but it doesn&apos;t feel &quot;punishing&quot; like I expect a rogue-lite to be.  It&apos;s just... you go in and shoot a bunch of bugs until they eventually whittle your HP to the point where death is inevitable.  It feels more like an old-school arcade game where you try to see how far you can get on a single quarter than it does like a Rogue-lite.

Other than that, it&apos;s alright.  I wouldn&apos;t pay the asking price for it.  Wait for it to go down at least 30%, more likely 50%.  Or pick up a different shooter.  There are plenty that stand out.  This one feels more like an &quot;also-ran.&quot;</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>09882234-359b-11eb-98ef-fa163e5fb782</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>My Twin Sticks aren&apos;t Twin Sticking</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/1a0f8680-f3a4-11ea-81e4-fa163e93294d -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/1a0f8680-f3a4-11ea-81e4-fa163e93294d">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-09-10T23:27:52</review:date>
        <review:description>...mit leicht gruseliger Atmosphäre. Die deutschen Texte sind gut übersetzt und die Rätsel sind meist einfach. Steuerung und Technik sind einwandfrei (habe mit Controller gespielt).

Alles in allem eines der wirklich guten Adventures, die ich in letzter Zeit gespielt habe. Bin echt sehr positiv überrascht worden :)</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
