    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/1e44a24a-9531-11e8-8197-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/1e44a24a-9531-11e8-8197-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2014-03-28T14:16:16</review:date>
        <review:description>Few game have been so disappointing as this one. The universe they have created is genius, and it has so much potential. Yet, they squandered it. The combat system is broken and the game feels rushed, especially after early game. They should have made it a PS2 hack&apos;n&apos;slash, like brotherhood of steel, because unlike brotherhood of steel, it would have worked. But this? An apprentice of both hack&apos;n&apos;slash and RPG but a master of neither.</review:description>
