    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/1ee8d60c-d469-11ea-a5eb-fa163e62c76a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/1ee8d60c-d469-11ea-a5eb-fa163e62c76a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-08-02T05:37:34</review:date>
        <review:description>Run around for over an hour back and forth between 3 backgrounds, trying to get this cheese, so I can give it to a bird for some part.  I was selecting the &apos;good guy&apos; options and none of them would progress, so I did the bad option eventually and the guy went to attack the bird, he wouldn&apos;t give me the cheese cause he didn&apos;t like the bird, but the part is for him.  Having fun yet?  Nope.  So I remember I have an inventory, even though it apparently doesn&apos;t have a hotkey, who knows, there&apos;s no way to check.  In my inventory is a lock pick, so I use it on some box to try to free some guy and it&apos;s just random &apos;lock pick&apos; tools.  No direction, no idea what I&apos;m supposed to do with them.  Left click and now your mouse cursor is one of the tools, left click again on practically every pixel on the screen, nothing happens.  

Even if everything about this experience wasn&apos;t completely annoying, I wouldn&apos;t care for whatever the story is, because they are going for zany humor rather than any substantial story.  I hate puzzles, and puzzle games that you basically have to follow a guide in order to consume a sub par story.  If you like to be stumped for trivial things then you might like it?  I think the art style and the way the characters interact is pretty nice.  It changes scenery to a zoomed in perspective when you have dialogue options.  

The voice acting is off.  The main character volume is too low and just sounds like a teenager or something.  The other voice actors sound like teenagers that are imitating something else.  I guess that works since the purpose of the writing is to be humorous.  They should have had more cat.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>1ee8d60c-d469-11ea-a5eb-fa163e62c76a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>Annoying</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">19</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/1ef48fee-da0f-11ec-85d4-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/1ef48fee-da0f-11ec-85d4-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-05-22T23:38:22</review:date>
        <review:description>I&apos;ve been following the progress since it was first announced. 
The game is early acess and it shows. The devs are very open for discussion, the in-game report bug feature is neat (also the open reported bug list)!

Even for an early acess, the game has the basics set-up - and they work beyond expectation for ea. This is what an ea should look like. The price tag reflects that too.

If you looking for a HoMM 3/4 game, don&apos;t bother. SoC resembles HoMM 3/4, but goes it&apos;s own way, especially the magic system, base building and recruitment of troops (no mixed faction troops, heavy focus on research and scouting ahead to counter o

pponent). 

4/5 since it&apos;s an ea. If the devs keep on adding improvements, it&apos;s a 5/5.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>1ef48fee-da0f-11ec-85d4-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>SoC &amp;gt;&amp;gt; HoMM</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/1ef94380-901e-11ec-9da7-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/1ef94380-901e-11ec-9da7-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-02-17T20:19:18</review:date>
        <review:description>
Playtime: About an hour? (tutorials + first mission and Babylon 5 tutorials)

==Intro==

FS2 is a space combat game. You play through various missions in a linear campaign which involve protecting allies and/or fighting enemies. There are also dozens of mods that add new content, from new missions to total conversions.

I used Knossos to install mods. Vanilla FS2 worked too but looks worse, obviously.

==Review==

As a kid i used to play Fury³, Terminal Velocity, X Wing/TIE Fighter, Rebel Assault II and the like. FS2 is a similar straight-forward flight combat game. There&apos;s no open world, no trading, no wide variety in ships and weapons, no factions - just simple missions. It&apos;s alright for what it is, and it&apos;s definitely cool to install the Babylon 5 mod and pilot an actual Star Fury, but i miss the freedom and options of X3TC or even Rebel Galaxy.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>1ef94380-901e-11ec-9da7-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>A cute little relic</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


