    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/1101fcd0-6ee3-11ea-9d44-fa163e93294d -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/1101fcd0-6ee3-11ea-9d44-fa163e93294d">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-03-25T23:53:31</review:date>
        <review:description>A side scrolling adventure game that has an art style and scenery going for it. Unfortunately, it doesnt have much else. 

The story is confusing, underexplored and ends in a kind of cliffhanger. 

The gameplay is kind of boring by itself and doesnt really tie in well with the story in a meaningful way.

I played this in Russian, so the voice-acting and sound was fine for me.

The game is also short. Like, 3 hours tops if you fiddle around with the puzzles too long. Now, I welcome such a thing as I feel a meaningful short experience is better than a dragged out broing one. Considering the games substance, its hard to say whether its a plus or a negative here.

If youre in the mood for some interesting atmosphere, I think this could be worth it. Otherwise, not much going for it.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>1101fcd0-6ee3-11ea-9d44-fa163e93294d</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:rating>
        <review:title>Good for the scenery/art</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">16</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/111bee76-b29a-11e8-b960-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/111bee76-b29a-11e8-b960-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2018-01-07T04:31:32</review:date>
        <review:description>This is my all-time favorite game... Amazingly fun, eternal replay value, 100&apos;s of user created missions... go read someone elses review for the rest. 

This review is to alert you to the fact that since the source code got released ages ago, this game has an amazing MODDING community that has updated the sourcecode, AND CONTINUES TO RELEASE UPDATES 17 YEARS LATER. No other game has 17 years worth of mods exept for Doom. Go to http://www.hard-light.net/ to get started learning what this engine can do. Go to http://www.fsoinstaller.com/ to upgrade to the OPEN engine.  Modern graphics, modern lighting effects, standalone games based on the engine... If you are &quot;nostalgic&quot; and you looked this game up. Stop. Google &quot;Freespace Open Source&quot;. This game will be better than you remembered it. The best part is that none of the &quot;game&quot; is really different than you remember.  I played this game minutes ago on three moniters, with voice activated wingmates, and had my mind blown by the fact that my missle lit up a trail on the side of a completely remodled Orion that had me jizzing myself. It will take you... a little time to figure out how FS OPEN works, but it is worth it 19282882%</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>111bee76-b29a-11e8-b960-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Download FREESPACE OPEN NOW</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">18</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/1117ea32-9168-11ec-b28b-fa163e99870e -->

