    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/112fc474-4a41-11ea-bf16-fa163e62c76a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/112fc474-4a41-11ea-bf16-fa163e62c76a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-02-08T09:03:10</review:date>
        <review:description>KINGPIN is all about a gang-banger getting revenge.  You&apos;re a thug - beating, shooting, and cursing your way through the ghettos.  It&apos;s not quite Shakespeare, but it&apos;s relatable - had a bad day?  Fire up the game, pick up a pipe and start beating the living crap out of someone you think deserves it.  When they are nice and dead - steal their last $2 off their bloodied corpse.  There, doesn&apos;t that feel better?

KINGPIN was originally going to have more of a roleplaying aspect to it, and remnants of that are still in the game.  There is an etiquette system (approaching people with a weapon out draws immediate violence your way), you acquire tips and quests by talking to people, there are shops, you can modify weapons, bars where help can be bought, etc..

Money, weapons, and muscle are the three primary commodities in the game.  You need money to buy weapons, weapon-mods, armor, and medkits.  You also need money to hire muscle.  KINGPIN is a tough game, and it&apos;s nigh impossible to beat it without hiring goons to be in your gang as you take on the other denizens of the underworld.

While other shooters of the time were throwing aliens, monsters, and undead nazis at you; KINGPIN came along with a more grounded, gritty realism that was refreshing.  It was in-your-face violence with no sugar-coating.

The story is serviceable.  The graphics stand up very well even today.  The action is excellent.  The AI is pretty good (though elevators are real hazards).  It can have a Dark Souls-like difficulty curve in some situations.  This is not a run-in-guns blazing game.  In most instances you are going to want to deal with as few enemies at one time as possible, and the greater the distance you can deal with them at - the better.  

Be sure and download the latest version of Monkey Harris&apos; KINGPIN patch (version 7, as of this writing).
</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>112fc474-4a41-11ea-bf16-fa163e62c76a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Great, stylish, brutal FPS game</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">7</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/11205a38-4f33-11ea-86ab-fa163e93294d -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/11205a38-4f33-11ea-86ab-fa163e93294d">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-02-14T16:05:33</review:date>
        <review:description>Hat Spaß gemacht, ist nicht zu schwer und recht gut steuerbar.
Ich empfand es als recht recht kurz, weil ich am zweiten Tag das Ende gesehen habe.

Bzw. ich habe zwei Enden gesehen. Es wird deutlich eingeblendet, wenn man das &quot;Bad Ending&quot; hat.
Fand ich ziemlich gut, denn das hat mich noch einmal zwei Stunden motiviert!

Die Bosse sind alle gut machbar, spätestens nach ein paar Runden.

Gefehlt haben mir besondere Höhepunkte oder besondere Gamplay Mechaniken.
Das Spiel mach Laune und kann ein Wochenende versüßen. Aber es gibt nichts besonderes.

</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>11205a38-4f33-11ea-86ab-fa163e93294d</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:rating>
        <review:title>Gutes Anfänger Metroidvania</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


