    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/1199ea86-4cf0-11eb-98c4-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/1199ea86-4cf0-11eb-98c4-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-01-02T13:45:53</review:date>
        <review:description>What a perfect game for 2020 - a game about &apos;waiting patiently&apos; released in March 2020 right when lockdowns had started being imposed on many of us. 

I hesitated a bit before buying this game because of the &apos;400 days&apos; concept - would I really need to wait a full 400 days in real life as well to finish this game? The good news is you can finish the game in considerably less time than that. I forget exactly how long it took me to play through the game to a satisfying conclusion, but it was somewhere around a month. I often kept the game running in the background and enjoyed keeping the lonely shade company while it explored or relaxed. I hope it enjoyed my company as well. 


</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>1199ea86-4cf0-11eb-98c4-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Patient and Introspective</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">15</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/12a7d248-b2e8-11e8-af3d-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/12a7d248-b2e8-11e8-af3d-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2018-07-17T08:35:59</review:date>
        <review:description>simply to say, there will never be another that is this good.  i&apos;ve looked around, this is the pinnacle.  what else can i say.  it&apos;s 20 years later and i still have it on my HD and play it often, over and over.</review:description>
