    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/1291f03c-adb8-11ea-80d5-fa163e93294d -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/1291f03c-adb8-11ea-80d5-fa163e93294d">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-06-13T23:54:28</review:date>
        <review:description>I think it&apos;s a brilliant game but after a few hours of gameplay, I wish it had more depth, like what I&apos;d get from other RTS games. Even hits from the early 90&apos;s, like Command &amp;amp; Conquer had more meat on the bones.

Wishful thinking from me would be that Shiro Games would dive-in and make some quick updates but that&apos;s not going to happen.They strike me as the kind of company that has a simple formula, and that&apos;s that. Not designed for power-users but instead mouse-clickers.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>1291f03c-adb8-11ea-80d5-fa163e93294d</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Very fun. Too simple. Love it...</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/13a19fd4-4d3d-11eb-a474-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/13a19fd4-4d3d-11eb-a474-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-01-02T22:57:08</review:date>
        <review:description>What a unique premise and what a great game. Each scene is a beautifully crafted diorama - pore over it in detail. If you can find all the &apos;clues&apos;, no guesswork is needed to identify who&apos;s who. I have moderate motion sickness (many first person games cause it for me, third person games are usually OK). The dithering effect here caused me motion sickness but the game was amazing enough that completing it was still entirely worth it. Short play sessions and playing the game in a much smaller &apos;window&apos; helped immensely. </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>13a19fd4-4d3d-11eb-a474-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Amazing, causes motion sickness</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/13a214e2-c3f5-11e8-8936-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/13a214e2-c3f5-11e8-8936-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2018-09-11T20:07:33</review:date>
        <review:description>Played this game when I was a kid. Played it in school, played it two years ago, played it now. Never gets old. 

The Vanilla game is fine, if you want 1080p and some other goodies, like speech commands (albeit basic ones), get the Open-Source re-implementation from Hard light. 

The game is better played on a controller. You simply can&apos;t pull up with a mouse for so long. 

The game is immersively challenging. You don&apos;t have access to anything that your avatar wouldn&apos;t have access to. Each mission, you need to beat in one go, no saves scumming. You can get in trouble for things that other (non-Deus ex) games wouldn&apos;t notice, and when you&apos;ve managed to pull off the optional stuff you do feel like you&apos;ve accomplished something. You, essentially, feel like a pilot stationed at Vega. 

The gameplay systems are well rounded, and well balanced. To survive the end-game, you need to master all of them, and also adeptly trick the AI. 

Overall, give a try, and persist. The game is tough, but fair.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>13a214e2-c3f5-11e8-8936-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Infinitely replayable</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">17</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/13d2ddd4-c94c-11eb-a57a-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/13d2ddd4-c94c-11eb-a57a-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-06-09T20:56:55</review:date>
        <review:description>Drakensang no envejeción bien, sin embargo contemplamos a un juego hecho con amor y dedicación, el diseño de misiones hace del juego entretenido y divertido, las conversaciones entre personajes mientras vas explorando son geniales, acorde a lo que en ese momento estás viviendo, los personajes son divertidos y cada uno tiene su propia característica y forma de ser. para ser un juego creado por un estudio pequeño, se puede tomar para que sirva de ejemplo a empresas más grandes y con enormes presupuestos, debes aprovechar el precio que GOG te ofrece de este gran clásico de RPG que no te debes perder sí eres amante de este género.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>13d2ddd4-c94c-11eb-a57a-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Un RPG de culto</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/13d7a668-62b1-11eb-9e0e-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/13d7a668-62b1-11eb-9e0e-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-01-30T06:10:24</review:date>
        <review:description>I picked this up since I love retro games and absolutely adore Shovel Knight.  I was disappointed. I found the story disjointed and uninteresting.  I also dislike the 2 button control scheme when I have other buttons to do actions instead of having to press a direction and the attack button with no option to change it that I could find.  I get that they were going for a retro feel but we have newer technology why not utilize the additional buttons. The platforming is challenging and often requires pixel perfect jumps, combat simplistic but varied.  The aerial enemies the game constantly throws at you or the sheer amounts of bullets makes me feel like i&apos;m playing R-Type not a platformer and when I died I felt like it was cheap.  </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">10</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>13d7a668-62b1-11eb-9e0e-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>Messenger was better</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">11</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/130378a4-72d0-11ec-b667-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/130378a4-72d0-11ec-b667-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-01-11T13:17:33</review:date>
        <review:description>Nie umiem pisać recenzji, dlatego całkiem krótko: UJDZIE!</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>130378a4-72d0-11ec-b667-fa163e99870e</review:id>
