    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/14f804ce-9189-11ea-90d6-fa163e62c76a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/14f804ce-9189-11ea-90d6-fa163e62c76a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-05-09T03:07:33</review:date>
        <review:description>Tonight We Riot is a wonderful little brawler. It&apos;s got gorgeous pixel art visuals that&apos;s not too cluttered in gameplay and striking in cutscenes, the music is nothing but bangers, and the gameplay while somewhat simplistic is compelling. 

The writing is funny and on-the-nose, it pulls no punches, it&apos;s leftist and it&apos;s proud of it. I can see myself losing a lot of time to this game over the coming years, especially with co-op. At its low price, it&apos;s well worth picking up just to check it out and support a co-operative indie dev that rewards all it&apos;s workers equally rather than paying the actual workers a pittance and some already rich exec a fortune.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">141</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>14f804ce-9189-11ea-90d6-fa163e62c76a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>WORKERS OF THE WORLD UNITE! FOR FUN!</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">79</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/1402e0d6-953f-11e8-b055-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/1402e0d6-953f-11e8-b055-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2014-06-12T23:11:30</review:date>
        <review:description>This is one of the best games ever! How do you use or play multiplayer?  Are there any Multiplayer servers around as I went to www.kingpinforever.com, but not finding any ways to see or configure multiplayer</review:description>
