    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/17c7bca2-534b-11ea-a1da-fa163e62c76a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/17c7bca2-534b-11ea-a1da-fa163e62c76a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-02-19T21:07:37</review:date>
        <review:description>Although the Bad Seed DLC is not explicitly tagged as linux game, there is the linux install script available after buying it. Just downloaded and installed without problems on Linux Mint and could even transfer my saves from version 1.3.9. I don&apos;t have a clue, why Motion Twin does not clearly tag the DLCs as linux games, same thing with &quot;Rise of the Giant&quot;.

Great game nonetheless! Cheers</review:description>
