    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/1849163e-d309-11e9-a55c-82e52fd17640 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/1849163e-d309-11e9-a55c-82e52fd17640">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-09-09T13:52:42</review:date>
        <review:description>I have replayed Fantasy General more than any other game. When I saw this game announced I was hoping they would get it right.

They got it right. This is how second parts should be. Taking the original concepts, replacing bad mechanics and adding a few new ones.

I like my strategy games when I have to think beforehand and come up with a good plan. Instead of mindless clicking. The game is fair with no random involved and the difficulty is brutal but beatable (on hard). The units are cool and balanced

There is only a mechanic I dont like and the dev said on the forums they are gping to tune it down. Kudos for good communication.

I really recommend this game to any strategy lover. The panzer general formula looks deceptively simple but it is extremely good fun and tough to master. I really want to go home and play it now!



</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">10</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>1849163e-d309-11e9-a55c-82e52fd17640</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>True to its heritage</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">13</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


