    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/1893222a-d2ec-11ec-a560-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-05-13T21:40:00</review:date>
        <review:description>So the Basics is good it adds good features like high advantage in fights nothing innovative but solid.
The Balancing is off, some units just can walk over the map in one turn and oneshot everything others are useless , the difficulty in the campaign missions also, one is like a walking in the park and the next you get outnumberd 10:1 and it looks just impossible. The Caster Heros are also completly overpowerd the fighters are useless, it dosent matter to give my units +30% deffence as a fighter they still get oneshootet. so needs still polishing.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>1893222a-d2ec-11ec-a560-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:rating>
        <review:title>Adds good features to Gameplay</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">10</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/19a90d02-3db0-11e9-8fff-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/19a90d02-3db0-11e9-8fff-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-03-03T14:30:16</review:date>
        <review:description>Review is based on playing using SCP, get it here: https://wiki.hard-light.net/index.php/Source_Code_Project_index Also, read up on FS2_Open. In this game, you pilot various spacecraft and accomplish various objectives. The story is a continued war between the Galactic Terran Alliance and the Vasudans. The Shivans are back, and it&apos;s up to you and your wingmen to stop them. Pretty much everything in this game is awesome. Using the aforementioned mods/conversions, visuals are stunning, audio is awesome. The base game is great. There are detailed briefings for each mission, sometimes you fail objectives as part of the plot... it&apos;s a reminder that things don&apos;t always go your way. The difficulty level is adjustable, and is useful, because some of the missions suffer from poor design. There are capital ships of various classes that have various subsystems that can be disabled or destroyed. This can hamper a ship&apos;s speed, reduce the effectiveness of its weapons or knock out its sensors. Brilliant design. The campaign left me longing for more, at which point in time I played various mods. I can&apos;t recommend the Blue Planet mod enough: https://wiki.hard-light.net/index.php/Blue_Planet It will blow your mind.

Note that beam weaponry and EW is much more important in this game than in the previous one.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>19a90d02-3db0-11e9-8fff-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>epic space pew-pew</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">11</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/19fa1e46-b23b-11e8-adbc-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/19fa1e46-b23b-11e8-adbc-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2017-06-03T23:59:59</review:date>
        <review:description>It&apos;s composed largely in a Western style with some Japanese instrumentation, rather like the soundtrack of TWS2&apos;s Fall of the Samurai expansion. The mood and pace of the tracks varies to a great extent with the story. The 5 bonus tracks seem to be alternate versions of tracks that made it into the final release; Steathly Battlefield in particular is very similar to The Siege of Osaka.

The main thing I wanted to point out however is that it is missing a number of tracks that play during the later parts of many stages, after one or two major objectives is complete. To name a few, there should be extra tracks for Osaka and Sunpu Castles, Lord Yabu&apos;s Mansion, Mastuyama and Kanazawa Cities.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>19fa1e46-b23b-11e8-adbc-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Great but incomplete</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">24</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/19fd3dec-93ff-11e8-956f-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/19fd3dec-93ff-11e8-956f-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2009-09-03T22:05:03</review:date>
        <review:description>Allright, if youre reading this you probably have already heard everything else there is to know about MDK from the other reviews. Frantic action, stunning level design, offbeat humor, sniper helmet, etc. However, Ive noticed from some of the other reviews that some people do not believe there is a save function in this game. They are wrong. You CAN save the game. I&apos;ll admit youre never told to save except for between levels but yes it is there whenever you need it. Just press F2, make a file name, and press enter. That&apos;s it. F3 brings up your saves so you can load. Dont let something that isnt true dissuade you from buying a game that, while short and somewhat dated, is something that I personally believe that every gamer should try at least once. 

Also, for full enjoyment of the game I feel that one has to tweak the controls a bit as they are truly archaic in design. Luckily by going to the options screen in the main menu or F12 in game you can configure both the keyboard and mouse commands to suit your style be it WASD, arrow keys, or whatever else. 

Lastly, if you feel like you would like the game then go for it. The difficulty really isnt that hard and now that you know how to save it wont impact you as much when you get to a difficult section.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>19fd3dec-93ff-11e8-956f-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Yes it&apos;s Great and Yes you CAN Save</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">212</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/191e6a92-eee6-11ea-93cd-fa163e93294d -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/191e6a92-eee6-11ea-93cd-fa163e93294d">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-09-04T22:37:41</review:date>
        <review:description>I get it... the premise of the game pisses people off. It pisses off people (like me) who believe in order, being recognized for your hard work by earning a wage at a job, and having a government that allows people to pursue their dreams but allows them to fail if they don&apos;t try hard enough.

This game openly mocks &quot;capitalism&quot;... but it mocks it in such a way that it is almost... laughable. IT&apos;S SATIRE PEOPLE! If you don&apos;t know what satire is, go read Gulliver&apos;s Travels. It was all a joke against certain groups within society like scientists, government, and others. It&apos;s great. It also upset a lot of people who had no sense of humor.

Now, in this game you fight as a masked civilian who decides to rebel against capitalism... (I imagine because you&apos;re tired of having to work for a wage, while others work harder and receive more...) You think you deserve more, so you take violent action against those who have more... more power and money than you have. Cuz *violence solves everything, right? (*sarcasm)

The plot is dull... but the controls and graphics and music are great. You like blowing stuff up? This game will scratch that itch! So many will play Grande Theft Auto and say it&apos;s a great game, but then claim this game is evil because it&apos;s agenda. (You fight cops in GTA also, but no one says that&apos;s evil?)

Take a deep breath and enjoy the humor here. You eventually fight a giant presidential mech! This is obviously not meant to be taken seriously. It&apos;s a big joke. I hate marxism/communism, too, but I can appreciate a good joke.

Plus, find me a game that doesn&apos;t have some kind of hidden agenda... There isn&apos;t one. There&apos;s always a message somewhere. But you don&apos;t have to agree with it to enjoy the game.

Again, from a game perspective Tonight We Riot is fantastic, if not a little corny. If you like explosions and starting fires and breaking things, then you may really enjoy this! I have. It scratches an itch... similar to the old Rampage arcade games.

Try it out.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">17</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>191e6a92-eee6-11ea-93cd-fa163e93294d</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>No actual Game reviews yet so...</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">10</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/19246d98-3ae5-11eb-8b72-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/19246d98-3ae5-11eb-8b72-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-12-10T14:42:00</review:date>
        <review:description>besides all that has been already mentioned, the objectives are not always clear and are not updated in the ( i ) objective button.
I had a good time at challenging difficulty level but in the map &quot;we&apos;ve run into a bit of delay&quot; it is unclear what the objectives are next. Keep kicking ork butt or save the maximum possible amount of units. I&apos;ve tried both exiting leader on the designated area along with other units but I get the message &quot;imperial guard surrendered&quot;.
The game could benefit a lot from a decent patch.
</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>19246d98-3ae5-11eb-8b72-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>puzzle</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/194fc324-1719-11ec-83cf-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/194fc324-1719-11ec-83cf-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-09-16T21:08:30</review:date>
        <review:description>Après avoir fini ce dlc, je suis loin d&apos;être méga emballé (je n&apos;ai pas encore pu voir ses répercussions sur la campagne principale). Ce n&apos;est pas une catastrophe mais ce n&apos;est pas vraiment un chef-d&apos;oeuvre non plus.
Si cette petite campagne a quelques moments sympas, j&apos;aurais tendance à dire que la fin traîne en longueur ( et ce malgré une faible durée de vie, environ 6h). En effet, si l&apos;idée de base concernant le lieu où elle se déroule est plutôt sympa (bien que pas forcément ultra originale non plus), elle s&apos;essoufle au fur et à mesure que l&apos;on avance dans celui-ci. On finit par savoir contre quels ennemis on va tomber et dans quelles pièces et l&apos;effet de surprise disparaît complètement, ça devient juste redondant. J&apos;avoue m&apos;être un peu ennuyé sur la dernière heure/ heure et demi (ce qui mine de rien fait beaucoup).
En revanche, j&apos;aime bien l&apos;idée d&apos;avoir le point de vue de Varnhold et de se détâcher du groupe principal. L&apos;écriture des personnages n&apos;est pas trop mal et le fait de faire de vous un subordonné de Maegar est bien trouvé. le seul petit problème avec ça c&apos;est que vous n&apos;êtes pas aux commandes du groupe sur la carte &quot;de campagne&quot;. Certaines personnes ont trouvé ça gênant, personnellement, au vu du format du dlc, je peux comprendre le fait que les devs aient optés pour cette option.
Maintenant si vous êtes un peu juste niveau argent, je pense que pour ce prix, il y a moyen de faire un bien meilleur investissement que ce dlc. Après si vous êtes vraiment hypé comme c&apos;était mon cas pourquoi pas mais ne vous attendez pas à des merveilles </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>194fc324-1719-11ec-83cf-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:rating>
        <review:title>Un dlc loin d&apos;être indispensable</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/197dea06-d4af-11e8-8e58-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/197dea06-d4af-11e8-8e58-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2018-10-21T00:28:34</review:date>
        <review:description>It took a little over 9 hours to get to 100%, and Obra Dinn was fun for pretty much all of that. I particularly enjoyed the latter half of the game, once you&apos;ve unlocked all the different scenes and can quickly bounce around between them.

The pacing is excellent. Obra Dinn is basically a huge first-person Sudoku puzzle with clues, except that when you get three items correct, the game verifies them. What that means is that you start with a huge range of mysteries and gradually whittle them down, and every time the game says that you were correct about some things, you can use those as definitive proof to solve more mysteries. So the speed of solving actually accelerates over time, which is quite a bit of fun.

The graphics are awesome, the voice acting and soundwork are atmospheric, the controls are tight, the book interface is particularly helpful. The game world was carefully designed to provide just the right amount of detail for focusing on your objectives. Every scene looks carefully arranged with that purpose in mind, and the environmental hints feel fair.

I strongly recommend this game if you would enjoy piecing together a mystery.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>197dea06-d4af-11e8-8e58-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Fun Murder-Mystery Game</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">207</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/1977163c-c2dd-11e9-9063-ca05e8e3acd9 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/1977163c-c2dd-11e9-9063-ca05e8e3acd9">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-08-19T23:57:28</review:date>
        <review:description>Visually Pathologic 2 very interesting, the town along the Gorkhon river overs varied and atmospheric environment to explore and to survive in. While the colors are largely muted, the attention to detail is excellent. After many playthroughs  one can still discover things that were missed previously.

Choices you make have very real consequences. To guarantee success you might choose to do terrible things, or you might suffer terrible consequences but never give up your morals. Once the events begin rolling, they will not stop to wait for you. You need to act regardless if you are ready or not. It creates a challenging and engaging experience.

I recommend this game, but the game invokes some negative emotions that are not necessarily enjoyable for everyone. There will be stress, helplessness and desperation depending how immersed you become with the game, its story and characters.

The plague will take you to your limits. What are you willing to sacrifice for your patients as a surgeon?</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>1977163c-c2dd-11e9-9063-ca05e8e3acd9</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Haunting, Atmospheric and Relenting</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">16</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/2a05a36e-b1e6-11e8-a342-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/2a05a36e-b1e6-11e8-a342-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2016-10-11T22:46:25</review:date>
        <review:description>First off, let me just say, I love this game. It&apos;s a very serious subject, and a very well done perspective on it. Kudos to the makers.

Now let&apos;s get the standard scoring out of the way.

Graphics: A-.  Mostly 2D with perspective effects, &quot;pencil&quot; sketching adds to the atmosphere.

Music: A.  Very well done, perfectly suited to the style of the game.

Sound FX: B+. Most of them are top notch, but some of them feel like they&apos;ve just been recycled from certain post-apocolyptic titles. (I swear I heard some of the Fallout New Vegas effects in there.)

Gameplay: A-. Yes, it&apos;s great, but there are a few things that bug me. For instance, there&apos;s no way to tell what skills the characters have, or what occupations pertain to which skills when you create a new character, until you get your game started. If you get into the game and don&apos;t like the skills each of your chosen characters have, you have to go through the whole process of setting up a new game map, picking characters, etc.


The only *major* things that I don&apos;t care for in this game are that, when scavenging, you can only have one character bringing in loot. Probably just a game balance thing, but it still is a gripe for me. Also, I realize they weren&apos;t going for this particular style, but.... in scavenging mode, I would have preferred being in first person. Personally, it just has a more &quot;real&quot; feel to it when I&apos;m viewing the scene from my character&apos;s perspective. Also, those little bits of &quot;graffiti&quot; in the game? The ones with trash like &quot;F@#k the war!&quot;? Yeah, sure, they might be more realistic to the average person, but believe it or not, some of us would have preferred a language toggle to switch off profanity. The &quot;mature&quot; toggles in games seem to be something we&apos;ve lost, like with the original Unreal Tournament, or with the N64 classic Perfect Dark.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">57</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>2a05a36e-b1e6-11e8-a342-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Great Game, With A Few Drawbacks</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">26</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/2a0889f4-1f6f-11ec-9603-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/2a0889f4-1f6f-11ec-9603-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-09-27T11:44:44</review:date>
        <review:description>Something is wrong! It seems that GOG has cheated me, as I may have played a different game! The game I played had interesting quests, either funny or more serious, such as a zoologist (who is named after a famous person) who doesn’t care about animals, but only about his pockets to be full. Or when you have to track down giant chickens. Or to sabotage (or not) a wedding ceremony. Or Polly the parrot. Or to uncover a murderer. Or the fact that a simple rolling pin is the strongest blunt weapon in the game!
Also, the hero’s voice actor from the first game returned, but in another, and smaller, role.
I finished it in 22 h.
Just one negative: the wildlife was very scarce in the map. But it didn’t mind me, as I already was high leveled from main game and Pirates expansion.
All in all, I’m truly glad that I dared to try the Two Worlds series (even though in discount), despite the negative things that I had read about it (especially about 1 and Tenebrae). I fully enjoyed the total of 216 hours that I spent playing, and finishing, all Two Worlds games (1, 2, Pirates, Tenebrae).
I’m really looking forward for Two Worlds 3 (when it’s released), but only if it’s brought in GOG.
</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>2a0889f4-1f6f-11ec-9603-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Seems that I’ve played a different game.</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/2a11de2e-eddb-11ec-b002-42010a340c25 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/2a11de2e-eddb-11ec-b002-42010a340c25">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-06-17T04:16:50</review:date>
        <review:description>I have been playing this game for dozens of hours. I am obsessed with it. It&apos;s a game that throws you into a world and let&apos;s you figure things out. Big feel of adventuring, risk and reward. Very cozy too.

It&apos;s a game that is very much made in the mold of Morrowind and Gothic. If you liked those games, you should try Outward.

I will be paying close attention to all future games made by Nine Dots Studio.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
