    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/2cfc40c8-6217-11e9-9042-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/2cfc40c8-6217-11e9-9042-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-04-18T23:18:49</review:date>
        <review:description>This is what all murder mystery games should be like.
This game invites you to solve mystery after mystery without holding your hand or without depending on game mechanics. It&apos;s all up to your deduction and attention to details to puzzle all the pieces together.
This game deserves to be played by anyone who wants to feel like a detective and take their time to unravel a mystery envolving dozens of character most of which you will remember after spending so much attention investing in the cause of their disappearance
</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>2cfc40c8-6217-11e9-9042-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>A Masterpiece Of Mistery</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/2cfea2b4-ca25-11eb-bf46-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/2cfea2b4-ca25-11eb-bf46-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-06-10T22:50:58</review:date>
        <review:description>I used to play this back when it came out, and loved it.  Seeing it here, I bought it with a cringe, knowing it must have aged terribly, but wanted a taste of nostalgia.   Oh how wrong I was.  The hyper simple, deadly gameplay has aged extremely well.   With complexity, it would just be overshadowed by the decades of games that have upgraded all of the aspects of tactical shooters.   Since it has no complexity, it basically plays like the Doom 1 of tactical shooters.  Short missions, go in there like Chuck Norris in Missing In Action 3, take care of business or die trying.  Gonna have to go through all these missions again, and am looking forward to it.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>2cfea2b4-ca25-11eb-bf46-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Why is this still so fun......</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


