    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/2d6e58b2-93fe-11e8-be13-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/2d6e58b2-93fe-11e8-be13-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2009-07-02T18:51:56</review:date>
        <review:description>This one is quite possibly one of the best Sci-Fi shooters ever.  It has an incrediby compelling single player campaign that really keeps you wondering what will happen next.  I would recommend also buying Freespace 1 &amp;amp; playing it all the way through first, though, in order to become more familiar with the plot line.  

I also have the original CD, so I found it nice when GOG was offering a download that wouldn&apos;t require a CD.  

Be advised; however, that the GOG version was somewhat modified from the original CD version in that there is no longer a basic setup utility (i.e.; there is no utility to allow you to set up screen resolutions, choose between OpenGL or Direct3D, etc).  Because of this, it doesn&apos;t run very well on my aging Athlon XP 3200+ PC with 2 GB of memory and a 512 MB AGP GeForce 7950 GT.  At the time of the original CD-ROM title release, I was running this with a much older 500 MHz K6-2 desktop and a GeForce2 card, and it ran far better.  

Either way, I must give this five stars--for many of you with much newer computers, this game should run flawlessly.  I just need to upgrade.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>2d6e58b2-93fe-11e8-be13-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Highly recommended</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


