    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/2e50ad38-7f65-11ec-b2da-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/2e50ad38-7f65-11ec-b2da-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-01-27T13:35:08</review:date>
        <review:description>Yes, I did play a demo version back then in 2003 or so, in that time is seemed like a solid arcade shooting game... 

Many things have already been written. The game on it&apos;s own isn&apos;t bad, it is quite playable, doesn&apos;t have bigger bugs etc. Yes, the enemy AI is simple, but does it&apos;s job, and I would say it doesn&apos;t have to be hardcore for a this type of game.

Sadly, maybe I am just getting to old, but now, when I try to play this game for more than a minute or so, I almost had to puke. 

Is this because of the camera or the tank motion/moving or when shooting? I don&apos;t know. 
Sorry for this, but it is hard to explain. 

The FOV isn&apos;t that bad, I guess, and after all you can modify it (also the resolution for widescreen), if you want, with editing the DT.ini file in the games directory.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>2e50ad38-7f65-11ec-b2da-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Don&apos;t play if you&apos;re motion sick</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


