    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/2e80b912-2876-11ea-8d67-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/2e80b912-2876-11ea-8d67-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-12-27T08:57:43</review:date>
        <review:description>So i decided to try this game, because reviews are like 50/50. After around 7hrs of gameplay (i played for years mostly MMOs) i must agree with few problems. One is that this game is more &quot;visual novel&quot; than action game, because almost half of time is walking, climbing or interacting with barriers/items. This is not bad, but hungry action player will be sad. On the end also i find that there are few monsters then you have to kill many waves of monsters. I cant rate story, because i didnt read original novel &quot;Equilibrium&quot;, so i dont know how far or close is this game.

Technical condition is good, not perfect, but without any big problem. In gabriel hotel i found missing &quot;ground&quot;, so in version 1.5.0 i fell one floor down, then i got one game crash (but game have many checkpoints, so i didnt lost any significant progress) and on the end, i had problem with character control which was stucked, but that was fixed by entering into game menu.

I dont think that i have &quot;so powerful&quot; machine, as i have &quot;obsolete&quot; 6C/12T 5390K and Vega64 LC and on &quot;epic&quot; settings with v-sync on 1920×1080 i havent any problems with framerate.

Overall, i dont think that this is as bad as players think, i had worse problems with &quot;AAA&quot; games after many patches, so this is almost without problem. Story is as is, main characted was very weird and annoying from beggining, then later i understand why they made him as he is. If you doesnt seek something deep or pure action, this should be good for you, otherwise, you should try different game.

And also, this seems to be first game from Layopi game studio, so i hope that they contiue with another game, maybe more deep one.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">13</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>2e80b912-2876-11ea-8d67-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Average game from written novel</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">34</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/2ea60588-3626-11ea-a8cb-00163e4e60cc -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/2ea60588-3626-11ea-a8cb-00163e4e60cc">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-01-13T19:00:20</review:date>
        <review:description>The story is imaginative and the characters are created as individuals, which is not the case in every adventure game.

Unfortunately because the game lacks stability (in my case on Windows 10) , you have to save often. There are not many different branches in the story and at some points it seems, that the developers were running out of time.

Nevertheless, I enjoyed playing the game I bought with low price as a special offer until the end.</review:description>
