    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/2f72b392-93fe-11e8-bb94-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/2f72b392-93fe-11e8-bb94-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2009-07-03T13:21:30</review:date>
        <review:description>A sensible space combat sim is almost dead genre today. Even if it wasn&apos;t it would be very hard to match greatness of Freespace. Good missions, choice of fighter and equipment, decent AI on wingmen and enemies - it&apos;s all here. With upgraded graphics and engine (hard-light.net) it&apos;s great again.

The only bad thing is craptacular mouse handling and not so great handling of cheap joysticks.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>2f72b392-93fe-11e8-bb94-00163e97122a</review:id>
