        <review:id>2faa1322-100d-11eb-b3fd-fa163edf6d96</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:rating>
        <review:title>A disappointment.</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">13</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/2fd844d2-b6ad-11e9-8916-fab18a45f36d -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/2fd844d2-b6ad-11e9-8916-fab18a45f36d">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-08-04T11:44:16</review:date>
        <review:description>I got Realpolitiks and the New Power DLC when it was on sale and that was my first and only experience, so I will be leaving the same review on the main game page as well as the DLC page. I suppose I think I&apos;ll be the first person to give the DLC itself a review since nobody seems to have done that yet. I just want to say that I really had a lot of fun with the game. It does have its pros and cons.
Pros: wonderful atmospheric sounds that make you feel like there are lots of really intense tiny battles happening in the distance. I really felt the game nailed that spot on. That was really cool. I really loved how the game was a good balance between some of the other more &quot;overly-complicated&quot; games of this similar type, but not too simple either. It landed in a very special &quot;Just right&quot; kind of good spot that other games seem to miss, so this was very special for me since it was not simple, but also not complicated to the point where I went crazy. It was just flat out simply just a good FUN game and I would recommend everyone grab it on sale some time in the future and play it for days and days, I REALLY enjoyed this.
Cons: The clicking. So much clicking! ahhhh! This game is VERY fun but you need to click and click and click and click, click to do every single action and make everything happen. My hands and wrists did get kinda sore, but they&apos;re okay. Game speed is also a little weird, some things happen too fast, but sometimes the game makes you wish there was an 4X or 5X speed button. Another thing I notice is that even after all the financial related upgrades and opening those little stock market things with everyone, I can never stop my &quot;GDP&quot; from going down into the red zone forever, never to be saved from the depths of doom ever again. I just don&apos;t know how to save that from happening. It does get a little tedious and grindy because of those cons. Otherwise, this is an excellent game that I&apos;m really happy I was able to experience. Loads of fun! :)</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>2fd844d2-b6ad-11e9-8916-fab18a45f36d</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Great fun game gets right what most dont</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/2fda9f9c-06b4-11e9-a41f-00163e4e60cc -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/2fda9f9c-06b4-11e9-a41f-00163e4e60cc">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2018-12-23T15:10:57</review:date>
        <review:description>Return of the Obra Dinn est un excellent jeu d&apos;enquête qui nous plonge dans une histoire aussi intriguante qu&apos;atroce. 

Le style graphique du jeu joue beaucoup sur l&apos;ambiance sépulcrale et sombre des scènes que nous visitions. La narration, volontairement chaotique, nous force à reconstituer l&apos;histoire des soixante personnages pièce par pièce, tel un immense puzzle. La musique et les dialogues sont toujours de très bonne qualité, soigneusement arrangés. Une foultitude d&apos;éléments sont disséminés çà et là dans le bateau et servent d&apos;indices. Ces derniers, plus ou moins évidents, nous aideront à mener à bien l&apos;enquête. Le seul défaut que je pourrais trouver au jeu est son manque de rejouabilité : en effet, une fois le mystère résolu, il n&apos;y a plus vraiment d&apos;intérêt à refaire le jeu.

Bref, Return of the Obra Dinn est un chef-d&apos;oeuvre, extrêmement précis, réussi en tout point.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>2fda9f9c-06b4-11e9-a41f-00163e4e60cc</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Un excellent jeu d&apos;enquête</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/20a46740-4829-11e9-a720-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/20a46740-4829-11e9-a720-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-03-16T22:21:49</review:date>
        <review:description>I would have given this a higher rating but there were too many factors. i think a lot of the puzzles were well thought out and entertainingly challenging but the boss battles were jusrt ther worst. you have to hit them a million times and they just have to hit you once. the first boss splits into two parts when you shoot it and you have to keep shooting and splitting it to make any progress. this is fine but the fact that it is constantly shooting at yopu too. bouncing balls of pain and misery that back you into a corner just as your getting some where, kills you and forces you to start over. everything about this game was great, the music (and i hate modern pop) the levels the assthetic. but that freaking boss battle. an hour into it and i was done. i&apos;m not returning to this game because there are no save states therefore i would have to start from the begginging. and its just not worth it. it&apos;s like going to college getting your degree but whoops the college screwed up and you have to start all over again. i didnt find college fun so i dont find this game fun. sorry.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>20a46740-4829-11e9-a720-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:rating>
        <review:title>great game... but...</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/20e53a64-9599-11e9-a1a8-ce2bf10ddff3 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/20e53a64-9599-11e9-a1a8-ce2bf10ddff3">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-06-23T09:27:32</review:date>
        <review:description>Плюсы:
- графика приятная и простая, тормозить там нечему особо
- несколько видов оружия (можно убить даже сковородой, есть достижения по этому поводу)
- простая, но ритмичная музыка
- классно набивать комбо
- управление простое и понятное

Минусы:
- довольно короткая
- под конец немного задалбывает однообразностью
- история очень довольно банальная

В общем если хотите провести немного времени за ней тупо пострелять и повыбивать комбо - смело можно покупать.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>20e53a64-9599-11e9-a1a8-ce2bf10ddff3</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Короткая, но затягивает</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">10</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/20142d6e-f661-11ea-a8fd-fa163e93294d -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/20142d6e-f661-11ea-a8fd-fa163e93294d">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-09-14T11:05:59</review:date>
        <review:description>FS2 was the first game I ever bought on GOG, when I first learned about the FSOpen project, the still ongoing open source development of the engine, which has spawned countless mods and some complete conversions. Now, almost exactly ten years later, I finished the original campaign for the first time. What took me so long? Well, back in the day I began by playing the port of FS1 on FSOpen, with original graphics and a mouse. When I was done with that I decided that I needed a joystick and a better PC for improved graphics before I could continue. Several years later, I got both, and played through the FS1 campaign again to get the best experience out of it. After that (but not immediately, as there were a lot of other games to play on my new system at the time) I continued with the excellent Silent Threat Reborn, an improved and expanded version of the FS1 expansion. In between, I played a bit of &quot;The Babylon Project&quot;, a Babylon 5 total conversion based on the FSOpen Engine. Only then I got around to start the original FS2 campaign, I guess it was around 2015... however, I interrupted that playthrough because of a mission that I just could not beat (until I disabled the improved graphics mod, for some reason), only for it to be followed by an even more impossible mission... Maybe I didn&apos;t realize that these were skippable bonus missions that were meant to be hard, and that it would get easier again afterwards.

Anyway, if you like flying through space and shooting things, this is your game. You don&apos;t really do much of anything else. The campaign is mostly good and the missions are somewhat varied, although they are usually variations of fly there, shoot this, protect that. In my opinion, the last third of the campaign was a bit of a letdown, and the last mission either incredibly easy or incredibly frustrating, depending on how you approach it. There are countless mod campaigns offering potentially unlimited playtime, but I guess most are mainly more shooting.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>20142d6e-f661-11ea-a8fd-fa163e93294d</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Great for the mods, outdated campaign</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/202a7758-f708-11e9-a165-00163e4e60cc -->

