    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/2081b21c-20a1-11ea-8d0c-00163e4e60cc -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/2081b21c-20a1-11ea-8d0c-00163e4e60cc">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-12-17T09:44:59</review:date>
        <review:description>Simply one of the most boring games I&apos;ve ever encountered in my life.  Just walking from place to place is so slow and cumbersome I couldn&apos;t even stand to tolerate it anymore.  I don&apos;t even know how difficult or frustrating the gameplay is because it&apos;s just so damn boring.  Waste of money for zero entertainment.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">56</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>2081b21c-20a1-11ea-8d0c-00163e4e60cc</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:rating>
        <review:title>SNOREFEST!</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">8</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/209d0bc6-4d3f-11ec-94ec-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/209d0bc6-4d3f-11ec-94ec-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-11-24T17:56:46</review:date>
        <review:description>Thematically, O:IS is an update on its predecessor: Where the first game was about the post-9/11 surveillance culture many of us associate with the name Snowden, the second incorporates the European migrant crisis, and first and foremost the perceived rise of misinformation in a world where everybody has instant access to unqualified data and opinion broadcast by, well, anyone. Consistent with these themes, the focus of O:IS shifts away from the essentially private and easy to empathise with individuals encountered in the first title: Your main antagonist may be a traumatised refugee in a wheelchair, but by his social media presence he&apos;s also a major force in the politics of two countries. The characters by his side feel a bit perfunctory, but that&apos;s because you don&apos;t really investigate them- you just use the juicy bits you find to shape public opinion.

Players of the first game will feel right at home. Phone calls have voice acting now, but the interface has mostly remained its familiar self, calm blue controls and tessellated pictures. Time is limited now and used up by uploads, so you&apos;re meant to be smart about them, though in practice I never felt limited. The last day gives you a new tool, the Influencer, which twists datachuncks you upload into hashtag friendly smear campaigns to spread across social media, ruining you opponent&apos;s credibility.

I felt the Influencer took away from the nuance, and also the realism of the Orwell games: Apparently people who read blogs are all partisan to the point of being biploar. A clever hashtag can turn their opinion into its opposite within an hour. If you&apos;re a blogger, your wife&apos;s personal life can stop a civil war. There&apos;s no deftness to it, just aim below the belt and win. I expect real manipulation to be more subtle. Where O surprised me with the amount of player choice, O:IS at times feels like playing the blueprint of an over the top conspiracy theory.

Still a good game, but not entirely as convincing as the first.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>209d0bc6-4d3f-11ec-94ec-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Solid second game, not as convincing</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/2091f17a-7191-11ec-bdaf-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/2091f17a-7191-11ec-bdaf-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-01-09T23:14:27</review:date>
        <review:description>Died over 100 times before I finished the game because I&apos;m bad at games, never gave up because it&apos;s just so interesting. Pathologic 2 tries a lot of uncommon things that are difficult and stresses the player out. This game really succeeds in making you feel negative emotions (I mean this in a good way), which is a rarity in games.

Not for everyone, and I really have to be in the mood to play it. Pathologic 2 is worth playing because there is almost nothing else that resembles it, even Pathologic 1 is different.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>2091f17a-7191-11ec-bdaf-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Good miserable time</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/2093bb6e-291b-11eb-881c-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/2093bb6e-291b-11eb-881c-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-11-17T23:23:25</review:date>
        <review:description>Este juego tiene un muy buen diseño de dibujos, eso sí. Incluso creo que fue inspirado en &apos;Valiant Hearts: the Great War&apos;, puesto que tiene casi las mismas mecánicas de juego y un estilo visual muy parecido. Tiene como lugar de acontecimientos un futuro posapocalíptico, También se nota cierta influencia del arte soviético en el diseño gráfico. Otra cosa es que tiene una muy buena banda sonora que que te da gusto poner auris para disfrutar del juego aún más.

¡Pero que no te agarra la historia para nada! Optas por este juego pensando que te quieren meter de pies a cabeza en una historia llena de ciencia ficción, y resulta que casi no tiene ciencia y tampoco hay mucha ficción que sea atrayente e interesante. Al final ni siquiera entiendes bien cuál es el origen de la linterna que tiene el protagonista. Además, parece que no funciona bien el sistema de logros de GOG para este juego. Ah, y tened en cuenta que &quot;The Great Perhaps&quot; requiere de tan solo 2 horas para completarlo y no tiene ningún valor de rejuego.

No voy a reembolsar el dinero. Pienso que los desarrolladores podrían hacer algo mejor por si les surge seguir con la 2ª parte o algún juego parecido. Tal vez hayan tenido problemas de financiación para sacar a la luz todas las ideas que hayan tenido sobre cómo tenía que ser el juego original, pues es la única explicación lógica que tengo del porqué de tan mala realización.

P.D. ¿Es este juego &apos;the Great? Perhaps&apos;, pero a mí no me ha gustado.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>2093bb6e-291b-11eb-881c-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>Me vendieron gato por liebre</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/21aac9be-b27d-11e8-8a8e-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/21aac9be-b27d-11e8-8a8e-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2017-11-21T20:11:51</review:date>
        <review:description>I remember MDK from being included on the CD-Version of a PC Gaming Magazine back in 2001. When I tried it for the very first time I was really impressed by the game and until today I count MDK as one of the best games forever who should get more attention.

What is MDK?

In MDK you play Kurt Hectic (great name for a character) who works for Dr. Hawkins. Hawkins has got a dog called bones and together they are trying to infiltrate the extraterrestrial Steamriders throughout the Earth.

The levels itself are pure art and differ so much from each other so you don&apos;t know what to expect when you enter a new area. 

To make it short: Get it and expirience it!</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>21aac9be-b27d-11e8-8a8e-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Until today one of the best games</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/210a3590-606c-11eb-b5e1-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/210a3590-606c-11eb-b5e1-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-01-27T08:51:49</review:date>
        <review:description>This game came out of nowhere. I noticed Yacht Club was involved and being a huge retro and
Shovel Knight game, decided to check it out.
I love the GOG! I love the fact that within a few minutes, I was playing on my modest little Vostro
2510 laptop with Ubuntu. I love that it supports Linux. I love the fact it was coded properly and
runs on old hardware unlike many modern games which don&apos;t, yet should.
Games like this should not require crazy systems, it&apos;s inexcusable when they do.
It plays great, seems to be more fluent than The Messenger, which is another Ninja Gaiden style
game that was released recently but I did not like for multiple reasons, a big one being the lack of
Linux support. (Worse yet, the said they would but then backed out!)

Have not played it through yet but just want to say support this game.
Support DRM free Linux games. Don&apos;t support games that aren&apos;t/don&apos;t.
Kudos to the authors and publishers! If you like Ninja Gaiden, you&apos;ll love this!</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">12</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>210a3590-606c-11eb-b5e1-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Very fun!</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">48</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/21099688-9447-11e8-b3e5-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/21099688-9447-11e8-b3e5-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2011-06-16T16:44:47</review:date>
        <review:description>I remember when this game was released, i did not have a pc powerful enough to run it. now finally 11 years later i got to play it, and it was GREAT. One of the most engaging and compelling space combat shooters ive ever played. The storyline is actually better and more immersive then the majority of Twitch fixes released today. I cannot remember the last time i was so engrossed. The graphics are still up to the job and can easily be brought into the 21st century with one simple mod. I came to this after having played Starlancer,Freelancer and tachyon and i must say, this is the daddy.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>21099688-9447-11e8-b3e5-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Amazing, the definition of a GOG!!!</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/2117cc30-25fe-11eb-a211-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/2117cc30-25fe-11eb-a211-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-11-14T00:18:17</review:date>
        <review:description>...Ausatmen.
Die Musik kommt, der Bildschirm stellt sich scharf und dein Herzsschlag schlägt im Beat und die Waffe ist dein Instrument!

Das Spiel ist brilliant. Es lässt sich an einem Abend durchspielen und hat dank den verschiedenen Chars, Fähigkeiten und Waffen einen angenehmen Wiederspielwert.

Kein Fürimmerspiel aber ein Immerwiederspiel!
Ist sein Geld absolut wert.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>2117cc30-25fe-11eb-a211-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Einatmen...</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/211934ca-7e32-11ec-babf-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/211934ca-7e32-11ec-babf-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-01-26T00:57:11</review:date>
        <review:description>At the point where you need to get past the hybrids, and in the snow terrain, i cannot proceed forward. I need a pass code key. But there is no pass code key, i wasted 2hrs running around back, and i cannot teleport to past locations to find it. Kinda a major game breaking issue.

I CANNOT recomend anyone buy this game until that portion of the game is corrected as i literally am stuck and am deadlocked doing anything.

That said, game is &quot;okay&quot; up to that point, but the camera can be very very big hassle at the points when your in the forest environment. Kinda headache enducing really.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>211934ca-7e32-11ec-babf-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:rating>
        <review:title>Hit a point thats impassable</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/212bc41a-6766-11ec-95c2-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/212bc41a-6766-11ec-95c2-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-12-28T00:41:28</review:date>
        <review:description>Bientôt à son 4e anniversaire, mais le jeu applique une configuration &quot;AZERTY&quot; dès que le joueur règle le jeu en français, et ce même si le joueur est un Canadien qui utilise un clavier &quot;QWERTY&quot;. Pour un studio français, c&apos;est surprenant! J&apos;ai demandé un remboursement.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>212bc41a-6766-11ec-95c2-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:rating>
        <review:title>Manque de polissage</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/2131fb00-40e7-11ec-8601-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/2131fb00-40e7-11ec-8601-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-11-09T00:56:38</review:date>
        <review:description>Вкратце:
Сюжет +
Боёвка +
Мир + -
Геймплей + -
Графика + 
Музыка +

Игра затягивает всем, кроме самим миром. Конечно, он мил и прекрасен, но &quot;стакан скорее на половину пуст, чем полон&quot;.  
Думаю, что столь низкой оценки как &quot;3&quot; игра не заслуживает. Kingdoms of Amalur достойна большего признания. Музыка, боевая система, эффекты, локации, сценарий + стилистика схожая с Fable = игра не устаревает. Видно, что люди старались. 
Возможно, не хватает разнообразия геймплея и реализма в 100% фэнтези. </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>2131fb00-40e7-11ec-8601-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Художники и воители! </review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/2137feea-93f9-11e8-9f0b-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/2137feea-93f9-11e8-9f0b-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2008-09-09T13:28:02</review:date>
        <review:description>Oh boy! GOG are geniuses for making this title one of the inaugural titles! It is, to my mind, one of the best space sims ever released! The explosions and size of ships have never really been bettered, and beam weapon destruction no better rendered! The AI is superb and the story of high quality. The missions are all very different and unique in space games! The fact that for $5.99 you get this AND the expansion is just brilliant and probably makes this title the best value item of the initial range! 

If you have</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>2137feea-93f9-11e8-9f0b-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>THE Space Sim of the last decade!</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">9</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/21443dac-848c-11e9-a5d7-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/21443dac-848c-11e9-a5d7-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-06-01T19:41:39</review:date>
        <review:description>It&apos;s short (beat it in 2.5 hrs) but it was really enjoyable experience - I bought it on sale for 1 € but I wouldn&apos;t feel cheated even if I payed the full price. I liked the unique art style and the idea of having to follow the subtly evolving background track to get into the rhythm. I can imagine this kind of game (with many segments being very timing-sensitive) getting very frustrating - however, thanks to very frequent checkpoints, this is not the case, as you&apos;ll usually only have to replay a short segment before progressing further - and I didn&apos;t find any of them too hard. The key is to stay calm and focused, especially in the boss fights. If you think they&apos;re too hard, you&apos;ve probably never played any old school arcade scrolling shooter - or you&apos;re raging too much :) They&apos;re challenging (which is good) and it took a me a couple (dozen) attempts to beat the final one but it&apos;s only about learning the rhythm and once you do, you&apos;ll realize there&apos;s nothing unfair about them.

The only thing where I could see an improvement was the choice of color schemes - I&apos;ve found most of them rather unpleasant and aggressive on eyes, with little harmony between the colors and some of them being too bright and/or saturated for being used in large areas. I really wish the authors would have spent more time creating more subtle color schemes for the levels - this simple improvement could have drastically enhance overall vibe and feeling of the game.

Anyway, it&apos;s still a really nice little game.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>21443dac-848c-11e9-a5d7-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Great game, little hard on eyes though</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/215cd1b0-83e0-11ea-a25e-fa163e62c76a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/215cd1b0-83e0-11ea-a25e-fa163e62c76a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-04-21T17:55:24</review:date>
        <review:description>I heard fantastic things about The Evil Within 2 and yeah, it has some really good elements. 

Gameplay is classic stealth, decent gunplay and survival-crafting-limited resources. For some reasons, Tango Gameworks decided tries with more open world kind of locations. It&apos;s lame. It&apos;s doesn&apos;t look good, it doesn&apos;t feel right, especially at the beggining when your hero is extremely slow and fragile. The game is also buggy as hell, nothing really big, but it immediately kills any suspens. 

First half has some moments of great horror (thanks to monsters design) but it&apos;s sluggish. Second mostly abandon sandbox stuff, focus on solid linear survival horror experience, driven by emotional story. Yeah, background with stupid Matrix premise and bad organisation is cliche as hell, but family moments between Sebastian and his daughter/wife are mostly handled really well. You want to see succeed this characters till the end.

The Evil Within 2 has many flaws but I can recommend it. If you looking for okay survival horror game, play it.  </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>215cd1b0-83e0-11ea-a25e-fa163e62c76a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:rating>
        <review:title>It&apos;s almost great</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/21973d98-784d-11eb-af34-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/21973d98-784d-11eb-af34-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-02-26T18:10:23</review:date>
        <review:description>This game still has me hooked after almost 100 hours. Solid gameplay, interesting story and mostly-okay UI. The different units are good and weak at the things you would expect from their descriptions and stats, and it&apos;s a fun puzzle to figure out how to best break a cluster of enemies with the right sequence of attacks. The upgrade trees are also fun to explore, and it&apos;s good that you can spend surplus resources on training existing troops to give them new buffs. Oh yeah, and scouting really matters.

My niggles:
- The map should really be able to zoom out more and not lag so much. The graphics are so relatively simple that it really shouldn&apos;t be be an issue on a modern PC.
- You can&apos;t set units as done for the round, so it becomes a hassle to find the units that still have moves when moving a large army.
- It&apos;s bloody annoying finding and assigning items to units.
- On the minimap, it&apos;s impossible to tell used from fresh units, and the same for explored and unexplored locations.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>21973d98-784d-11eb-af34-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Best turn-based fantasy tactics in years</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/22c83004-9ee5-11ec-9652-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/22c83004-9ee5-11ec-9652-fa163e9aa6fa">
