    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/23d18988-9588-11e8-a4a2-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/23d18988-9588-11e8-a4a2-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2015-05-08T00:05:46</review:date>
        <review:description>Well I remember this game, high  off fallout 2 I would buy anything Black Isle would have sneezed out. Sadly they revamped the whole fight system into some sort of real time fighting, similar to diablo. My estimated guess is that they saw the success of Diablo 1 and tried to emulate it. Sadly it ruined what I thought would have been a rather nice RPG.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>23d18988-9588-11e8-a4a2-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:rating>
        <review:title>They tried a diablo</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/23e11f7e-9a3d-11e8-bbdc-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/23e11f7e-9a3d-11e8-bbdc-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2016-04-24T06:38:16</review:date>
        <review:description>I had more fun with this game than with many modern games in similar-ish genre. The world of MDK is ridiculous: mad scientist, six-armed robot dog, aliens that wave target signs on you, suit that has ribbon parachute, nuclear healing items and the world most interesting bombs. There is very little exposure and no infodumps (most of back story is in manual) but those little bits that can be seen here and there in the game add to enjoyment of fast-paced 3P arena shooter. Running around under upbeat music with a speed of motobike and shooting baddies with infinite ammo across quite colourful environments tuned to be much more fun than I&apos;ve ever expected once I figured out how to configure mouse to look around freely. 

For a such old games there are certainly some quibbles but I love this game even more than the sequel.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>23e11f7e-9a3d-11e8-bbdc-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>To save press F2</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/2344555e-d5a0-11ea-a93f-fa163e93294d -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/2344555e-d5a0-11ea-a93f-fa163e93294d">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-08-03T18:43:55</review:date>
        <review:description>The game has an required taste for its graphics meaning not everyone will like it the quality feels ok score it a 6.5.
Quests are mostly do this make that usually forcing you to follow a certain path which hurts the replay value of the game somewhat the space is quite limited as well as you develop certain buildings during main story. the combat is mostly lacklustre and in someways can be realistic that we dont have several powers etc but the AI should be a bit better to give it any meaning. difficulty is not existing. gameplay wise i&apos;d score it a 4.
NPC&apos;s Backstories are very superficial, NPC&apos;s say stuff but it feels just so generic like their looks some annoyed me very very much voice acting makes you wish it was a mute game at times so score it a 3 

Well it&apos;s an ok building game for price range 10-15dollar/euro. You might like it for a bit its not a masterpiece and people shouldn&apos;t call it that. It is not an unique nor a good copie it lacks  any  AI it has some decent ideas but those arent well executed.  </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">7</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>2344555e-d5a0-11ea-a93f-fa163e93294d</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>doing my time at portia </review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


