    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/23804d16-c368-11e9-9221-2a88eff2d357 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/23804d16-c368-11e9-9221-2a88eff2d357">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-08-20T16:32:45</review:date>
        <review:description>Absolutely thrilling. A game that made me feel a broad range of emotions, has invaded my dream world and has continued to occupy my thoughts long after the curtains have been drawn - I keep coming back to thinking about the characters, the Town&apos;s conflicts and mysteries and the choices I have made.

I personally have appreciated the difficult mechanics. The concentration and effort that one puts in pays off emotionally. Most importantly, in this game failure is a feature, you are supposed to fail. I am an anxious perfectionist, I think that a lot of technology and other features of the modern lifestyle exacerbate that kind of tendency. Either way, I found being put in a world where I&apos;m expected to fail, with all the bitter sweetness that involves, profoundly liberating. So to me, this is more than a game. Like a handful of other great games that I&apos;ve had the pleasure to play in my life, this has been a life experience.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>23804d16-c368-11e9-9221-2a88eff2d357</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>More than a game</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">12</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/239e68d0-924a-11ea-a39d-fa163e93294d -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/239e68d0-924a-11ea-a39d-fa163e93294d">
