    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/2393d35c-08d9-11ea-8de7-00163e4e60cc -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/2393d35c-08d9-11ea-8de7-00163e4e60cc">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-11-17T03:25:28</review:date>
        <review:description>While some players have issues with the graphical style and music, I got used to it quickly. I agree though that there are sometimes issues with the interface and that you need to scroll a lot to see certain infos. I certainly agree that there are problems with the logic. Terrorists appear with a whole army everywhere in the world and are even announced beforehand (hello, next year we&apos;ll appear in Cape Town from out of nowhere with infantry, tanks and planes). On the other hand, nuclear strikes don&apos;t seem to bother the attacked nation very much. Some events are clearly scripted, as they always appear and always at the same time. There is a certain lack of usefulness of blocks for alliances, as they are rather suitable for expansion. It is still sometimes unclear to me what my choices actually cause; I can enhance the industry and other things of a single territory, but how that adds to my score is sometimes intransparant to me.

Still, I like playing around with the game, trying different countries and ways to play. I also like the humorous texts (on a side note for native German speakers: the translation is rather good, even though it contains a couple of small errors. It was clearly done by an Austrian who probably doesn&apos;t know that many Germans are unfamiliar with the word &quot;lukrieren&quot;). The game is certainly not aimed at the Paradox community, but some of the ideas I found interesting, even if they are somtimes flawed. For those who are more focused on details and who do not wish to hop from country to country or scenario to scenario this game can indeed become dull after a while</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>2393d35c-08d9-11ea-8de7-00163e4e60cc</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:rating>
        <review:title>Uneven</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/24a6ac8e-93f9-11e8-9c39-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/24a6ac8e-93f9-11e8-9c39-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2008-09-10T13:21:12</review:date>
        <review:description>When i got to play this game i was really surprised, its not a simply action game, you will have to think before acting! posses the right person, at the right time and don&apos;t let the watch you ! 
It gets very challenging at some points, and thats something that i like !
but i would like more the game with classic fps control, WASD and mouse free look...</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">13</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>24a6ac8e-93f9-11e8-9c39-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>A little wonder</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">17</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/24afe92a-195a-11e9-b05d-00163e4e60cc -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/24afe92a-195a-11e9-b05d-00163e4e60cc">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-01-16T08:44:16</review:date>
        <review:description>The graphics is obviously a bit outdated but on the other hand the gameplay more than compensates. Besides I like the voxel graphics here as I do in Outcast. The AI is not flawless, but it is certainly good enough to make this a very challenging game. The gameplay mechanics are very good. I did note one problem that has been mentioned in forums, namely that pressing the fire button does not trigger the satchel charge. No worries, the LAW and the grenade launcher alternatives work well. But in general, everything works as expected. In any case, I enjoy this game very much.  I can&apos;t give it 5 stars due to the lack of a map editor. </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>24afe92a-195a-11e9-b05d-00163e4e60cc</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Exceeded my expectations</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/24b0ef4a-93ff-11e8-ae46-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/24b0ef4a-93ff-11e8-ae46-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2009-09-08T17:21:08</review:date>
        <review:description>i purchased this game during the interplay promo, i really didn&apos;t know what to expect except the typical shiny crazyness. 

truly the awesomess of this game caught me unprepared, from the first level to the ending scene i was amazed with the amount and quality (well compared to the time it came out of course) of content. just hearing the menu intro music already glued me on the screen. 
the level design is mostly... crazy, from the stuff you can do to the actual design. but the game itself is a bit short.

the worst thing is that the gameplay isn not really fluid (at least by today&apos;s standarts) and the controls need some time for tweaking.

but apart from that you should really enjoy the game. i reccomend to finish it just to see theending outro, despite the fact that i don&apos;t have a what&apos;s it about it&apos;s awesome.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>24b0ef4a-93ff-11e8-ae46-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>I&apos;ve been blown away</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/241ef7fa-97a1-11ea-b410-fa163e62c76a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/241ef7fa-97a1-11ea-b410-fa163e62c76a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-05-16T21:14:53</review:date>
        <review:description>The game is good at pretending to be deep, but it feels empty and barren. It wouldn&apos;t be mysterious at all if you could actually hear or read the dialogues. As it is, now you are left to imagine what is happening. While much of it is plain enough, other parts are vague. It just feels like a cheap trick to achieve an impression of depth. Even the creator says that he does not know what the game is about and that any interpretation is valid. I don&apos;t like that approach to art. If i wanted to imagine a story I&apos;d rather just write one myself. Not sit here and have very limited means of using my imagination.
I like part of the editing. The music is good. Graphics are sometimes good. Environments are dull and very plain, with a few exceptions. I liked a few scenes and areas, which makes me rate this a two. It was worth the money as i bought it at a huge discount. Quite bad but at least it&apos;s different and for that sake perhaps worth to play for some.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>241ef7fa-97a1-11ea-b410-fa163e62c76a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>Cheap smoke and mirror tricks</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/24287380-e001-11eb-b169-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/24287380-e001-11eb-b169-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-07-08T18:28:27</review:date>
        <review:description>This game is a good party based RPG. If you like games like Dragon Age (the first one), you should enjoy this one too. However, I have several gripes with this game.

First, the story, the setting, the characters are little too much generic. You have your classic fantasy setting with dwarves, elves, mages, dragons... You name it. You have story with the chosen one and magical artifacts. You have companions who fit the templates - charming rogue, beautiful elven lady with connection to nature, strong dwarf warrior that likes to drink, evil necromancers with evil plans and so on. You will get everything you would expect from classic fantasy setting - but nothing more. However, it all works together really well. The unique (at least for me) Dark Eye rules set with refined gameplay makes it enjoyable experience. Just know what you can expect from this.

My second issue is lack of fast travel.

Overall, very enjoyable game with refined gameplay and lots of content. Recommend.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>24287380-e001-11eb-b169-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Well-crafted RPG</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">17</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/24333364-b474-11eb-a43b-fa163e3a9b6e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/24333364-b474-11eb-a43b-fa163e3a9b6e">
