        <review:title>just not good</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">20</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/245a69a4-8df5-11e9-a821-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/245a69a4-8df5-11e9-a821-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-06-13T19:06:02</review:date>
        <review:description>Отличная игра, на то время практически единственная в своём жанре с таким размахом, хоть и графика фоксельная, но если попробывать поиграть с друзьями, настроив по хардкору всё и с одной жизнью на миссию, то будет однозначно интересно.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>245a69a4-8df5-11e9-a821-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Дедушка Армы и Батлы</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/246ba9e6-5421-11eb-92f2-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/246ba9e6-5421-11eb-92f2-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-01-11T17:24:48</review:date>
        <review:description>Return of the Obra Dinn è un capolavoro, sprizza originalità da tutti i bit e secondo me è un&apos;esperienza imperdibile, lo definirei il The Last Express del nuovo millennio.
Ci sono alcune similitudini, nella meccanica di gioco, con il titolo di di Jordan Mechner ma l&apos;aspetto che li accomuna veramente è la genialità degli autori, conferma che è sempre possibile creare qualcosa di innovativo quando si ha la capacità, e la volontà, di uscire dagli schemi dell&apos;omologazione videoludica. Dato il presupposto, soffermarsi sulla qualità assoluta della grafica minimale e del comparto sonoro diventa riduttivo, a farla da padrone è l&apos;atmosfera pazzesca che ne deriva e la capacità del gioco di risucchiarti totalmente nell&apos;indagine: almeno una quindicina di ore che scorrono senza neanche rendersene conto. 
Se vi piacciono le avventura a sfondo investigativo dovete giocarci, per quanto mi riguarda da oggi posso aggiungere Lucas Pope ala mia lista di autori preferiti.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>246ba9e6-5421-11eb-92f2-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Un gioco eccezionale</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/25ad52a8-9d57-11eb-ac6f-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/25ad52a8-9d57-11eb-ac6f-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-04-14T22:25:18</review:date>
        <review:description>Spielt sich sehr gut und bei mir auch absolut stabil. Die Story ist nicht schlecht und der Flow genau richtig. An sich spiele ich eher klassische RPGs wie Baldur&apos;s Gate etc., aber KoA hat mich trotz der Betonung der Action wirklich begeistert!</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>25ad52a8-9d57-11eb-ac6f-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Überraschend gut</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/25b26256-8abd-11e9-a518-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/25b26256-8abd-11e9-a518-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-06-09T16:47:39</review:date>
        <review:description>I really was enjoying the game but there are some severe issues. The most and important of all is the save points. It ONLY saves when you sleep. Need to leave in a hurry? Tough shit, drop everything go home lose an ingame day of work because... reasons. Spent who knows how long doing stuff and got a lucky drop of a bunch of work and game crashes? Well screw you sister and the colorful llama you rode in on cause it is gone. Seriously even a Dark Souls like save style would have been better. Even an auto save or SOMETHING.  I am tempted to refund the darn thing.


The game has voice acting which is good. Can tell it was chopped together and probably recorded in various parts of the world in someones bedroom or car. The voices sound good, but they sound disjointed.  Despite that I still like them.

The game looks great and has a nice feel, but the save game nonsense is severely annoying. 
</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">14</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>25b26256-8abd-11e9-a518-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>Disappointing.</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">18</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/25cf6726-9472-11e8-8e26-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/25cf6726-9472-11e8-8e26-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2011-07-14T09:52:14</review:date>
        <review:description>I have not played a better space combat game since I first played this in 2002 (yes I was late to the party). I did however play its predecessor for many years prior to getting it (and still do). If you are looking for a way to spend countless hours blowing up aliens on the cheap I would highly recommend this game. That said more than ten years after its release with FSO it can be made to have graphics comparable to any 2007 era game. So even for those who feel that graphics are everything (which I&apos;ve never understood) this game won&apos;t disappoint. Not surprisingly it also has an incredible diverse and motivated modding community given its age. Between all the fan work and the original two games you will get many hours out of this game. That said go buy the original as well if you can (Freespace + Expansion) to help support GOG in bringing all these awesome good games back to computers everywhere.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>25cf6726-9472-11e8-8e26-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Buy this</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/25e1e28c-5b64-11eb-95bc-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/25e1e28c-5b64-11eb-95bc-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-01-20T23:12:05</review:date>
        <review:description>Es ist schwer, dieses Spiel zu beschreiben, da es im positiven Sinne total verrückt ist. Man spielt einen kindlichen Engel, der in eine Science-Fiction Stadt à la Blade Runner geschickt wird, um eine Verschwörung aufzuhalten. Man kann fliegen und von NPCs Besitz ergreifen, indem man in sie &quot;hineinfliegt&quot;. Jeder NPC hat andere Fähigkeiten (z.B. Kampf, Reparatur, Autorisierung für bestimmte Türen...), die man kombinieren muss um weiterzukommen. Neben diesem Puzzle-Gameplay muss man auch sein fliegen / gleiten nutzen und es gibt Schießereien inkl. freiem Wechsel zwischen Ego- und Schulterperspektive.

Was das Spiel so genial macht, ist einerseits sein absolut einmaliges Setting und andererseits die extrem guten Puzzles, die man durch Kombination der Fähigkeiten aller Charaktere lösen muss. Absolute Empfehlung!</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>25e1e28c-5b64-11eb-95bc-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Göttlich</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/25f874fc-f943-11eb-bc46-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/25f874fc-f943-11eb-bc46-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-08-09T21:53:56</review:date>
        <review:description>Awhile back there was some issues with saving but I haven&apos;t had that problem personally.

As for the game it takes a good while to get into but that&apos;s because it&apos;s surprisingly deep! There&apos;s a bunch of auxiliary skills to train in addition to combat techniques, spells, and &apos;practical&apos; abilities which I really appreciate. One of your team can train to harvest plants or animals, fast talk civilians, pick pocket, lock pick, or craft items in addition to filling fighting roles.

The map is very forgiving (showing all landmarks and un-hidden quest locations as well as enemy markers) even if the turn-based combat is the right kind of challenging, juggling stamina and energy for fighters and wizards and allowing you to use any skill in combat so you can break off and bandage wounds or mix potions mid-battle with a paused menu.

The story is generic but unapologetically so: no meta jokes or memes. There&apos;s so many little details I&apos;ve come to appreciate in the journey like the party celebrating victorious quests, graphical niceties like fluttering feathers and warriors with drawn weapons adopting looks of determination. There&apos;s sporadic voice acting verging on ridiculous with some wonky but not deal-breaking translations.

This is slow-paced, not action packed although there&apos;s a lot of methodical fighting. If you enjoy managing team members, planning out class/skill progression with experience you can spend at any time, and don&apos;t mind lots of walking through pretty surroundings and talking to people between encounters this is a very pleasant and highly customizable roleplaying experience.  </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>25f874fc-f943-11eb-bc46-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Fixed Up, Charming, Deep RPG</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">20</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/250d83fc-cffd-11ec-8206-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/250d83fc-cffd-11ec-8206-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-05-10T04:04:29</review:date>
        <review:description>First off, the game is great. I don&apos;t understand the reviews criticizing the grind/saving method, most likely your new to the genre of life sims. This game saves exaclty like Stardew and the grind is equivelent to Stardew. Intead of farming of course (but is an option), you&apos;re a new builder who will play a big role in the town of Portia, from building things that are significant and needed for the story, or building a variety of objects for sidequests. Another thing I see many reviews have a problem with is the social system, socializing is obviously optional and isn&apos;t needed to progress in the game. The social system is to be friend someone, all characters have their own personality and gifts from which they like and love. Eventually you&apos;ll have the option of dating from the handfull of bachelor or bachelorette. Agian, the social syrem is very similar to Stardew, but defenitley more grindy which I personally didn&apos;t mind. 

Overall, My Time at Portia is a very  good game, I didnt run in to any bugs and if I did I cant even recall what those were. The negative reviews for this game on GOG are baffling compared to the ones on Steam. There are a ton of things to do ranging from the main storyline, side quests for lots of the characters, seasonal events that the town and you can participate in, dating, getting married, having a child, minin games, mining, dungeons to explore, many ancient artifacts to peice together, building a large variety of objects, farming, fishing, and more. 

This is a great game for all who enjoy life sim games, one of the best in the genre and can&apos;t wait for the sequel arriving in early access this May. I hoped this review helped anyone who hasn&apos;t played My Time At Portia and are intrested in buying the game.

If you&apos;re intrested and having nothing else to play, 29.99 is 100% worth it, you&apos;ll get plenty of content and hours of fun. 
If you&apos;re still doubtful and not in need of a new game, I&apos;d say wait for a sale.  :) </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>250d83fc-cffd-11ec-8206-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Why So Many Negative Reviews?</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


