    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/26f80a28-93f9-11e8-a986-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/26f80a28-93f9-11e8-a986-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2008-09-10T17:34:01</review:date>
        <review:description>The only problem with this game is that they never made 3rd installment. Other major pain-in-the-neck - lousy XP compatibility is gone now.

I still remember countless hours spent hunting Shivans with my trusty 3DFx Voodoo on board :)

To say something more about the game: many ships, differences between them, feeling that you are a part of a huge war effort, sinister and interesting aliens, wonderfully crafted missions.

A big flaw is that the game ends. Booo to that - get 2nd part if you haven&apos;t already as it&apos;s even better!</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>26f80a28-93f9-11e8-a986-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>A true Masterpiece</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


