    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/289ef74a-bc49-11ea-81ef-fa163e62c76a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/289ef74a-bc49-11ea-81ef-fa163e62c76a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-07-02T12:48:18</review:date>
        <review:description>I love Anodyne 2 and it&apos;s predecessor. A lovely world with great characters. Like all games by Analgesic Productions plays in a unconventional world and it&apos;s very fun to explore. The graphics are great with the mix of &quot;old-style&quot; 3D and the 2D passages with their pixel look.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>289ef74a-bc49-11ea-81ef-fa163e62c76a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Great game</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/29b7624a-b2d0-11e8-a058-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/29b7624a-b2d0-11e8-a058-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2018-05-25T15:27:10</review:date>
        <review:description>This is a wonderful chapter, taking things way further over the dark side. Psychological horror spikes upwards in a genuine manner and the bad ending affects everybody, even people that had nothing to do with the series of freaky accidents, homicides and disappearances... Lets start!

Satoko is the youngest girl who pulls pranks on everybody and sometimes injures others (traps etc). Ill mannered, a problematic kid. Up to now, we didn&apos;t cast a glimpse into her past, her inner self and circumstances around her. Well now, we do. She had to endure horrible child abuse and her only protector, brother Satoshi, run away. Her uncle suddenly returns and turns her into a broken thing, shedding misery all over her life. The nice times and the small ray of hope, built in previously with Keichi, not only vanishes, but is horribly twisted, not even undone. The rest would be spoilers.

Before the main story starts, we have a small intro, during which a corpse is found. The presentation is so apalling and disgusting, that even veterans might have their stomachs churned. Especially due to the manner the bystanders talk during the event and their pitiful attempts at black humor, or cold/indifferent description.

Our protagonist manages to survive, only to die later in a much more miserable manner. This whole crush hope entirely in the most sadistic manner ever, by killing somebody off right after you get the impression they are ultimately saved, is simply THE WORST! It feels strangely satisfying. And resolves the story adequately enough, in a convincing manner (no witnesses make it, nobody learns of the truth etc).

Goes without saying, that a true fan of the series, should get all chapters. But especially this one, is a great addition to the story. I would prefer it way more, over the previous 2 entries. And the music used, started differring a little, adding much needed variety into the mix. I rate the whole series 5/5. You might call me biased, but it&apos;s great. You cannot go wrong.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>29b7624a-b2d0-11e8-a058-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Here things start getting serious</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


