    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/2920fb6a-9440-11e8-9cc5-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/2920fb6a-9440-11e8-9cc5-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2013-11-01T19:29:19</review:date>
        <review:description>This game have received a lot of praise over the years, and I enjoyed it as well. Still, there&apos;s some flaws at this game. Basically, it&apos;s a space shooter, and a great one as well. it never gets too complex, most of the missions  is just &quot;shoot the bad guys and make sure we don&apos;t get hurt&quot;... 
One problem is the overall universe and plot, which is narrated some extremely boring briefings, that you will want to skip instead of plowing through long pages of space-military-blah blah forever. Other than that, pretty nice game, and do yourself and install FSopen, that will improve the graphics radically, and give you  the opportunity to play new campaigns.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">21</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>2920fb6a-9440-11e8-9cc5-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Lots of fun, but a bit overrated</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">7</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/2921e4c4-13dd-11ec-939e-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/2921e4c4-13dd-11ec-939e-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-09-12T18:21:54</review:date>
        <review:description>After a strong opening sequence and well-designed character builder, you&apos;re thrust into a game with wildly uneven difficulty and lack of balance. While it can be argued that Iron Tower is going for an &apos;old school&apos; RPing experience with Colony Ship, I&apos;d say there&apos;s a lot more trial and error and arbitray punishment dealt than is reasonable for most gamers. Rather than immersively &quot;playing a role&quot;, it felt like my playtime was spent trying to be/do exactly what the game wanted me to, in order to progress.

CRPGs are one of my favorite genres - I&apos;m a big fan of Fallout 1 &amp;amp; 2, the Wasteland series, the Planescape/Torment series, the Shadowrun series, and indie titles such as Stellar Tactics and Encased. That said, I cannot recommend Colony Ship.   </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>2921e4c4-13dd-11ec-939e-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>Too Unbalanced to Currently Enjoy</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">19</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/2954a03c-9599-11e8-94e9-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/2954a03c-9599-11e8-94e9-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2015-06-11T06:57:14</review:date>
        <review:description>Honestly, Kingpin is a great gritty FPS that feels like you&apos;re part of an experience close to the film, Scarface. The guns feel great, the dialog is hilarious, and overall, it has the makings of a great game. However, my main complaint is the difficulty. Mainly, the AI. The AI are the most self-aware AI I&apos;ve ever seen in a game, which for the time, was something pretty neat. The problem is that everything you do matters, and I mean it does matter. Even if you take the smallest step around the corner to the point where an enemy cannot see you, they will somehow see you and get to you. Again, I do like it when AI is a challenge, but when it&apos;s this challenging, and on the normal difficulty mind you, then there&apos;s a problem. However, this is still a great game if you don&apos;t let the difficulty get to you.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>2954a03c-9599-11e8-94e9-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:rating>
        <review:title>Overshadowed by punishing difficulty</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/29861910-94b2-11e8-85d9-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/29861910-94b2-11e8-85d9-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2012-04-16T18:20:38</review:date>
        <review:description>This game wasnt about singleplay. The core of the game was in multiplayer with great variation of CTF called Bagman. Good tactics and team coordination was the key to succes in bagman. It was suited for Clan battles. I spend a lot of time with this game on old server gamezone.cz, in my clan Marcello Assasins. It was a good time and I have to recommend this game.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>29861910-94b2-11e8-85d9-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>FPS with unique multiplayer </review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/299d1b74-9cdf-11ea-8d56-fa163e93294d -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/299d1b74-9cdf-11ea-8d56-fa163e93294d">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-05-23T13:21:27</review:date>
        <review:description>Beautiful modern game in the retro coat and oldschool game mechanics! You&apos;ll learn how to drive pretty quickly. The rest is just taking a few races per day and enjoy this beauty.

It really pushes hard on the nostalgia (played these games on my old Sony Ericsson phones). Set into the 80s it might also touch those who like relaxing synthwave music. Color palettes, car designs, menu... It&apos;s just as described. Unless you are into this, I don&apos;t think Slipstream has a lot to offer.

It&apos;s great for casual gaming. After a dinner, you&apos;d make a cup/glass of your favourite drink and play several races in this game. It&apos;s pretty simple, doesn&apos;t require anything to study, read super long dialogues, collect and equip items. You just sit and play, yet it feels that you actually play something (it&apos;s not static) while not being boring (like NFS). I don&apos;t mind if I win or lose, I just like to drive. Some races are simple while there are hard ones too.

I see others criticize this title. I&apos;ve had no issue with drifting (it&apos;s activation is equal to going turbo in the Crazy Taxi series). Note that this is fairly simple game from a small developer, so you basically get everything what&apos;s in the game description.

I don&apos;t give 5 stars because I only think this game is still a bit pricey (at least to me, may differ due to the PPP if you live in different country). I am waiting for a sale and will get it, to me it&apos;s a super relax.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>299d1b74-9cdf-11ea-8d56-fa163e93294d</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Easy to get into and just relax</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/299e184e-aa67-11eb-9e9f-fa163e3a9b6e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/299e184e-aa67-11eb-9e9f-fa163e3a9b6e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-05-01T13:22:42</review:date>
        <review:description>Some of the reviews here are just baffling in how loudly they defend capitalism, and how little actual argument said reviews bring, its all basically &quot;X is all bad because some of X is Y&quot; or people trying to attribute whatever trade or economy-related positive subject to being a product of capitalism. (Gives me flashbacks to when christians try to attribute whatever positive aspect of society to being a product of their religion, with just as little sustenance to support their claims.)

That being said, this is a game that obviously takes a rather over-the-top take of it though, and at least the &quot;power to the workers/community&quot; sort of message is very refreshing in todays time, even if one doesnt have to agree with everything, and though I havent played more than just a tiny bit yet, so I reserve the right to change my opinion should other sort of ideas or morals be presented aside from the aformentioned, I find this is a fantastic little game so far.

(Would give the game 4 Stars, but I feel that with how the playfield is tilted by all those who just mindlessly rate this game low, I cant do anything else but give it a full 5 Stars instead.)</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">67</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>299e184e-aa67-11eb-9e9f-fa163e3a9b6e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Yikes</review:title>
