    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/3b25f366-9462-11e8-8e23-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/3b25f366-9462-11e8-8e23-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2011-05-08T12:48:23</review:date>
        <review:description>I see that almost no one here seems to remember that a Linux client was originally released for this game. I was a beta tester for the Linux version. There is also a Linux server for the game as well.  You can grab an installer here:
http://icculus.org/~ravage/kingpin/
http://liflg.org/?catid=6&amp;amp;gameid=2

Both have Linux installer that read the cd/files and install it under Linux automatically. It is a great game with some features that games never repeated, the location damage.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>3b25f366-9462-11e8-8e23-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Linux game</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">12</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/3b32531a-5d72-11ea-a17d-fa163e93294d -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/3b32531a-5d72-11ea-a17d-fa163e93294d">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-03-03T19:12:58</review:date>
        <review:description>I own the game on steam, sadly it was not available on GOG at this time :( . I played several hundred hours. If you like a survival simulation with drama you should get this. There is no story, so do not expect to be guided to your goal. But the good news is, the goal is simple: Build a ship and escape - and on the way recruit people, do not starve. The game has the best injury system I know of and it counts to the top three survival sandbox simulations for me. I rarely give a 5 star rating and I am pretty sure the last one is the biased star because I really like it. The graphics are... well you see screenshots. I was turned down by this quite a bit before I decided to buy it - it was well worth it. However prepare to have fatalities, drama, inner and outer conflicts with wildlife and humans and the deadly mechanoids cutting off limbs of your dear colonists. Rescue them and research to replace their severed body parts, so they again can be a working part of your community.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">14</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>3b32531a-5d72-11ea-a17d-fa163e93294d</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Great one</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">39</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


