        <review:title>von Darkest Dungeon weit weg...</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/3bfb6c5e-e2b8-11e8-8e49-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/3bfb6c5e-e2b8-11e8-8e49-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2018-11-07T20:09:14</review:date>
        <review:description>This game is the best indie game of the year, even more than that, it&apos;s one of the best games of 2018. It&apos;s a masterpiece. While graphics may deter people from playing it, it wasn&apos;t the case for me. 

I enjoyed various awesome video settings. Gameplay is incredible, the game feels like a real investigation. Story is engaging and mysterious. 

It&apos;s so good you&apos;re doing yourself a disfavor not playing it right now. It cost only 20 bucks. Bear in mind this game was made by one man. The whole design: music, sound, graphics, story - is all his.

Took me about 11 hours to solve everything and enjoying every little detail in the game. I can&apos;t recommend it enough. Lucas Pope is an auteur of video games. Buy this game and experience it yourself.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>3bfb6c5e-e2b8-11e8-8e49-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Amazing piece of art</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/3c0f7d00-8bce-11ea-ae42-fa163e62c76a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/3c0f7d00-8bce-11ea-ae42-fa163e62c76a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-05-01T20:07:27</review:date>
        <review:description>This was a very fun game back in the day. However, I cant get it to launch on windows 10 and its too much trouble to try to research and figure it out. Easier to move on to other games. If you are a casual buyer I would recommend giving it a pass simply because of compatibility issues.</review:description>
