    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/3ecb37a8-0a79-11eb-bc99-fa163e7ab9c9 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/3ecb37a8-0a79-11eb-bc99-fa163e7ab9c9">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-10-10T00:49:02</review:date>
        <review:description>Hi people, 

I have now more than 150hours into this game.
And its pretty addicting, first tip... dont open the box when you are low level. 
Try to open it as 40 that the gear is also level up (at least some of it)
Second join their discord, very friendly people who help you with problems and the devs are on to help you out there as well.

Gameplay :
Gameplay is what you expect in a more mmo-isch style game. Loads of side quest with a mainstory.
It rewards the ones who do all the exploring with hidden doors and tresures and extra buffs.
And there are a lot of sidequests. 
Iam not sure i have done em all, although it feels i did, but as soon you did the main quest/sidequest its back to grinding mobs and do the repeat quest. And at that time its getting a bit boring. But than again you are 150plus hours in. So well worth your money.

Also if you have this game already, iam not sure you are getting something extra out it though. From other reviewers i seen online it was exactly  the same with a little difference to the orginal, so dont count on a remake or something like that.

Still bugs in this game some fun and some just crashes your game to desktop. So save often or at least before you do something  importent :)

To be short i enjoyed the game even it was a oldie, but for some odd reason i missed it back in the day. Glad it had a second chance. I can recommend this to anyone who liked fable, i think that is the closest game that comes to this.

have fun </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>3ecb37a8-0a79-11eb-bc99-fa163e7ab9c9</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Great Game with some bugs.</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">12</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/3edf63ce-51d5-11eb-bafa-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/3edf63ce-51d5-11eb-bafa-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-01-08T19:16:28</review:date>
        <review:description>Battle Planet: Judgement Day, aside from the Rogue-Lite elements, would be a huge arcade hit circa 1985. You jump in, run around like your hair is on fire for 5-30 minutes, and enjoy the chaos on a 3D planet that greatly differentiates the gameplay from side-scrolling shooters and other rogue-likes.

There&apos;s no complex story, no puzzles to solve and no long cut scenes. It&apos;s just straight unadulterated arcade fun for you and a friend (friend highly recommended) in a way you have likely never experienced before.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>3edf63ce-51d5-11eb-bafa-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Fun Arcade-like top-down shooter</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


