    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/313a3c7c-3bf9-11eb-8d48-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/313a3c7c-3bf9-11eb-8d48-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-12-11T23:38:22</review:date>
        <review:description>I like Darkest Dungeon, and this feels like basically the same game in a new, fresh setting. Great! 

Unfortunately, the game design is very harsh and unforgiving. While the first few hours are easy enough that it doesn&apos;t matter, the game later becomes more difficult, and the unforgiving mechanics just ruin the fun. The game has two difficulty settings: normal and a special super hard mode. It desperately needs an easier baby mode that will cut you a break and just let you enjoy the story without perfect mastery of the game&apos;s systems.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>313a3c7c-3bf9-11eb-8d48-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>Nice, but needs an easier difficulty</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">12</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/314df142-c584-11e8-9cbe-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/314df142-c584-11e8-9cbe-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2011-05-12T04:06:39</review:date>
        <review:description>The game is pretty cool.

It has a very cartoon superhero feel to it.

Diverse opponents will engage you in various ways with a good variety of attack styles and are often over the top. Some of the more sophisticated opponents will require you to find their weak spots and aren&apos;t simply &quot;shoot it to death&quot; affairs.

Your character looks pretty slick in his costume and has good moving and shooting animation. He also has a very very cool parachute feature that allows him to glide. Both the animation and the feel of it are very good and by the end of the game, I still wasn&apos;t tired of it.

Mouse-using shooter purists might be disappointed at the lack of precise aiming (your gun works like a machine gun and there is no vertical aiming... the vertical axis is auto-aim), but that setup works well with the action as you&apos;ll be moving and jumping all the time to dodge various attacks and also to access different parts of the levels while fighting. Also, there is an sniper feature that works like you&apos;d expect a sniper riffle to (except that you can shoot explosive rounds when you find some!) and for some parts of the game, you have to use it so purists won&apos;t feel like they are completely left out.

The puzzles are pretty ingenuous without being frustrating (you&apos;ll have to stop and think, but if you look around, you should get it) and while the environment isn&apos;t destructive per say, there are many scripted environment changes that are pretty cool and dramatic.

Part platformer, the game makes good use of the vertical axis to navigate across the levels and will make sure you need to use that cool gliding feature on various parts of the levels to move on (or to avoid hurting yourself when you fall from great heights). Also, the gliding feature makes it more user-friendly as a platformer, because you&apos;ll be able to use the glide to correct your fall.

The graphics are somewhat dated, but they do an adequate job at portraying the alien vessel-asteroids (a lot of earthly-metallic colors) and the architecture the levels will look refreshingly weird and alien. Level design in this game is top notch and never plain or boring.

With all this praise, I should mention the few bad parts of the game.

The game is fairly short. I did not play with a chronometer, but I&apos;d say I finished the game in 8 to 12 hours.

Also, while you can save between levels, you can&apos;t save during the levels. However, this isn&apos;t as bad as you&apos;d think as the levels are fairly short and you should complete them in 1 to 3 attempts unless you are new to shooters or platformers.

Furthermore, I found the initial key setup unintuitive (in particular, the ability of the mouse to move you forward or backward instead of just sideways) and if you are anything like me, you&apos;ll have to adjust it to make the game enjoyable. Given the number of games I played lately that got the initial key setup right, this issue stuck up for me.

And finally, there is a music video at the end of the game that is just weird. Its in French and frankly, you are better off if you don&apos;t understand it, because the lyrics are nothing to write home about.

Overall, the complaints are minor and the greatness of the game greatly overshadows its weaknesses, hence the 5 stars.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>314df142-c584-11e8-9cbe-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Great Shooter/Platformer</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/31427476-b2d7-11e8-b7f3-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/31427476-b2d7-11e8-b7f3-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2018-06-09T08:33:06</review:date>
        <review:description>This theater saw some of the most intense fighting that took place in ww2 and &apos;before the war.&apos; You play as the Japanese and it is a heavy infantry fighting campaign. I found the campaign to be well done, good atmosphere and a pleasure to play. Grab it if you are looking for infantry and urban siege based fighting.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>31427476-b2d7-11e8-b7f3-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Boom</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">7</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/31610106-a128-11eb-8896-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/31610106-a128-11eb-8896-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-04-19T18:59:16</review:date>
        <review:description>Pathologic 2 is a story-driven survival game that never holds your hand. It is an open world game set in a bizarre town where you must try to solve an ongoing plague. It is one of the most dynamic narratives in gaming, and the quest design is so unforgiving as things never wait on you, anyone can die at any moment just about, and you really have to use your own intuition and create your own strategy for dealing with the problems at hand. In this regard, it is most reminiscent of the first two Fallouts as far as quest design goes, though without the heavy role-playing element. 

This game is not only riveting for its immersive world, but also its art design and soundtrack. It has some lack of polish; it runs terribly on a Ryzen 9 3900X and GeForce RTX 3090 on higher settings and AI is buggy, but that&apos;s all easy to look past. Pathologic 2 is refreshingly original, thoughtful and artistic.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>31610106-a128-11eb-8896-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Best story driven game in recent years</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/32b5a9f8-9453-11eb-ae0d-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/32b5a9f8-9453-11eb-ae0d-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-04-03T11:04:21</review:date>
        <review:description>This is NOT the game for you if you enjoy building bridges, it IS the game for you if you enjoy minmaxing costs in order to maximize shareholder profits. 

The games difficulty is entirely dependant on you keeping yourself to the insanely underbudgeted situation you&apos;re put in and as such you are always tasked with finding the shittiest bridge solution that still somehow manages to hold itself up for once test run and here is where my personal issue with this game comes.

You are NOT building bridges, you are building safety hazards. 

What did I expect out of this title? 
A bridge builder game. 

What did I get? 
A money management game.

I want to build bridges, I don&apos;t want to balance budget constraints and the cashbag you&apos;re given for each mission is so limiting in its size that there is only ever one solution to each problem. You are not rewarded for thinking differently in your build as you can&apos;t, you can&apos;t afford thinking differently. This makes the game incredibly repetetive as the most efficient answer is usually the answer for most of the puzzles. </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>32b5a9f8-9453-11eb-ae0d-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>Great for economists</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">47</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/32d8fd44-9493-11e8-910f-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/32d8fd44-9493-11e8-910f-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2011-12-15T14:39:28</review:date>
        <review:description>One of the best from the era. I remember especially the beautiful textures and environments and the disappointment that the real game didn&apos;t look at all as good as the CG demo mpeg file that was up on the site and took forever to download back in the 28.8 baud days. But this was as artistic as Shiny Entertainment ever got, and has nice Tommy Tallarico orchestrated music, very smooth (if jumpy) controls (you get used to them). Still playable today - but be warned it&apos;s a bit short. One wishes that they had made the sequel as Bioware did not really seem to get Shiny&apos;s style. 

Nick Bruty and Bob Stevenson, Tim Williams, Shawn Nelson and Andy Astor should be commended for the artwork and design in this game. Dave Perry should be commended for seeing that the game was fun throughout. 

It feels like it moves at almost too rapid of a pace and I always wished it had been longer. You can run fast in it and it was one of the first games to introduce the &quot;headshot&quot; ability (sniping off heads) -- your helmet itself -- your whole head -- is your sniping weapon. The game mixes bizarre ideas with comedy, but it dark throughout.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>32d8fd44-9493-11e8-910f-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Kind of perfect!</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/32dc7ff4-ceed-11eb-bc05-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/32dc7ff4-ceed-11eb-bc05-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-06-17T00:52:52</review:date>
        <review:description>Finally played it after receiving the game free.

I would like to say I am not a full-on gamer, I play one or two games a year.  

Gave it 5 stars to annoy the right-wing snowflakes.  If I am honest probably more entertaining watching the &quot;don&apos;t cancel me&quot; mob quickly scream CANCEL (in keeping with the typical right-wing meltdowns) 

Does it deserve 5 stars? maybe, in truth not my type of game genre.  Momentary fun but became quickly monotonous.  One of the reviewers said it reminded them of streets of rage, I can see that but again played it in my youth and again was quickly bored by it.

If you like this genre then go for it, might be your thing.

Well comrades that my first (probably last) review.  

Cheery-bye snowflakes :-).</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">30</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>32dc7ff4-ceed-11eb-bc05-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Bash the Fash :-)</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">11</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/320ca266-93f9-11e8-96d4-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/320ca266-93f9-11e8-96d4-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2008-09-12T22:20:33</review:date>
        <review:description>Besides the offbeat humor and the entertaining variety of the gameplay, MDK has one major thing going for it: presentation.  This decade-old game holds up rather well thanks to some inspired level design and art direction.  The colors really pop out; the game is dark, but isn&apos;t afraid to throw in vivid reds and oranges amidst the browns, blacks and grays.  The dated graphics inadvertently give an otherworldly quality to the world&apos;s architecture.  It&apos;s true that the assets are blocky, yet manage to be discernible and even look futuristic somehow.  There are some seriously awesome textures here that are meant to disorient the player and try to turn genre conventions upside-down.  

The game is a joy to look at, listen to, and play -- despite an old-fashioned control scheme layout.  WASD-inclined players will end up making some sense out of the archaic controls after some time-consuming fiddling before the game starts.  Surprisingly, the sniper interface is still stunning, and is a real testament to the care this game was given.  There are three sub-screens that help you see where your bullets are going.  You can even look at all three at once.  

Levels typically take 10-15 minutes to complete, but offer few - if any - checkpoints.  It&apos;s kind of a pain to have to restart from the beginning.  However, the aforementioned variety in gameplay and excellent pacing among the different action and platforming setpieces helps alleviate this.  When your play session is over, you&apos;ll likely feel gratified and wanting to keep playing; MDK is a very original piece of work.  It is a very worthwhile, steadfast example of the action/platform genre that everyone should check out.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>320ca266-93f9-11e8-96d4-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Unreal art direction</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">129</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/3222e17c-94ba-11e8-9c0e-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/3222e17c-94ba-11e8-9c0e-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2012-10-20T07:24:48</review:date>
        <review:description>This would not make any list of my favorite games of all time, but I just had to chime in that it&apos;s really enjoyable.  The graphics are dated and the dialogue is ripped directly from Pulp Fiction, but hard to imagine someone not finding something to enjoy here

At one point in the game you can obtain bodyguards and I have to say the AI is quite good as your companions will do as they&apos;re told

Intense firefights.  Recommended</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>3222e17c-94ba-11e8-9c0e-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:rating>
        <review:title>Don&apos;t let the 3 stars fool you</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/323a0af8-93f9-11e8-9dbd-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/323a0af8-93f9-11e8-9dbd-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2008-09-13T01:23:32</review:date>
        <review:description>I was too young to play this game when I did...
That said I loved every minute of it.  The graphics were excellent at the time.  Lots of blood and gore, and don&apos;t forget the over the top, Tarantino-esque swearing.  Frills and chills aside, this game had some of the better single-player level design of it&apos;s time.  The run down buildings, docks and factories all looked and played very well.  Xatrix, I feel, always did an excellent job turning a real-world sort of area and making it work really well in a FPS.  For more proof of that check out the Redneck Rampage games when they hit GoG here soon.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>323a0af8-93f9-11e8-9dbd-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Mother %#@&amp;amp;!</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">19</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/32335118-5f13-11ea-b4c6-fa163e62c76a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/32335118-5f13-11ea-b4c6-fa163e62c76a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-03-05T20:57:43</review:date>
        <review:description>There are some minor gripes, like you can not save during a battle but over all I am hooked on this game. Nothing like seeing a magazine explosion on a ship you just hit or secondary explosions to make you smile. Landing torpedo hits are a fun challenge too. </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>32335118-5f13-11ea-b4c6-fa163e62c76a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Very Addictive and fun</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/32347232-93f9-11e8-98bf-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/32347232-93f9-11e8-98bf-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2008-09-13T01:09:29</review:date>
        <review:description>I want to give this game a 5, but it really deserves a 3.5. The game is fun and challenging.  There are some really unique and memorable moments in the game, but there really aren&apos;t enough of them overall and there are some frustrating and annoying points as well.  The game is fun and definitely worth the GoG price.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">27</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>32347232-93f9-11e8-98bf-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Original idea and Fair Execution</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">77</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/32373a9e-93f9-11e8-8c0e-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/32373a9e-93f9-11e8-8c0e-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2008-09-13T01:17:06</review:date>
        <review:description>This was the last game that Interplay and Black Isle made.  Unfortunately it was their worst RPG ever.  If it were any other company than Black Ilse saying it is the worst might mean don&apos;t play it.  It isn&apos;t a bad game, it just can&apos;t hold a candle to the other games the developers made.  There is a lot of potential in the game just on the fact that it uses the SPECIAL system from Fallout.  Unfortunately that potential wasn&apos;t really tapped.  There are some high-points in the game and it has a unique and interesting setting.  Lionheart just misses on more marks than it hits.  Not a bad game but far from what it could have been.  Black Isle fans should pick it up for sure at the GoG price, but I imagine most of them already spent more $$ hoping for more.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">15</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>32373a9e-93f9-11e8-8c0e-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:rating>
        <review:title>Sad but True</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">25</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/324f0248-7c56-11ec-91bb-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/324f0248-7c56-11ec-91bb-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-01-23T16:10:19</review:date>
        <review:description>Someone compared Strange Horticulture with Papers, Please, which I agree is a good comparison. Main difference is that there are no timers here to consider but solve puzzles and identify plants in your own pace. Very enjoyable and occasionally challlenging. I have only unlocked one ending so might give it another go at a later time. This labour of love makes a fantastic start of 2022 in PC gaming and it might make it to many top-lists when the year is over.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>324f0248-7c56-11ec-91bb-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Excellent Botanic Puzzle</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">18</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/324126e2-93fb-11e8-8fe4-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/324126e2-93fb-11e8-8fe4-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2008-12-30T13:59:59</review:date>
        <review:description>When I first played MDK I wasn&apos;t fully impressed with the graphics engine. Thing is, it wasn&apos;t the quality that impressed me but the content. The game had an easy plot line, but kept me entertained. The jokes and slap-stick humor is what made the game different. I feel as if MDK is in a genre of it own.  Very fun game to play.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>324126e2-93fb-11e8-8fe4-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Fun at every corner.</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">13</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/3248ad04-d1c3-11ec-a754-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/3248ad04-d1c3-11ec-a754-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-05-12T10:14:43</review:date>
        <review:description>I am very pleasantly surprised by the storytelling, the general experience, and the simple mechanics of the game. It is probably that fact, that it is not overly complicated, that made me dive in and recollect the countless evenings with HOMM 3. The game goes beyond though. The interesting game mechanics of different troops and map heights, make the battles not so much repetitive.

I am very fond of it, as a very infrequent gamer.

* it works for me on my M1 mac, in contrast to the other review.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>3248ad04-d1c3-11ec-a754-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Diving back into the world of magic</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">29</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/32495986-93f9-11e8-bb85-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/32495986-93f9-11e8-bb85-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2011-11-04T08:11:26</review:date>
        <review:description>Lionhearts story is interesting twist on our past and there are a nmber of good quests at the start. 

The game was rushed out  with the second have of the game feeling barren with few quests. The whole feel of the gmae felt unfinished the animation felt wooden. The music would repeat itself so much that after a while i would turn off music. 

It is a shame given more time and money i think this would have been a really good game.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>32495986-93f9-11e8-bb85-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Ok RPG</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/3254b642-82f4-11e9-8ba9-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/3254b642-82f4-11e9-8ba9-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-05-30T19:01:33</review:date>
        <review:description>Przecież tytuł był w polskiej wersji. E... na drzewo.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>3254b642-82f4-11e9-8ba9-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:rating>
        <review:title>I znowu brak polskiej  wersji</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/3272a95a-4637-11ec-949e-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/3272a95a-4637-11ec-949e-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-11-15T19:12:22</review:date>
        <review:description>Overall this is one of my favourite naval strategy games I&apos;ve tried so far. If you&apos;re into military history you&apos;ll love it. The way the physics modelling and the way ships list and slow when flooding gives the game an element of realism. There&apos;s a lot of strategic choices you can make (stuff like you took out the spots on the enemy BB and she couldn&apos;t hit you on the last two salvos, do you try to take out the main guns or do you shift your fire to the CL closing on your DD?) and the AI is pretty good so in most cases they&apos;ll react in a realistic way. You can use historical tactics with good results which makes it incredibly satisfying if you have some WWII history knowledge. The user interface is good at breaking down the complexities of managing a ship/fleet into something that&apos;s easy to navigate without feeling like it&apos;s doing everything for you.

The game has a few weird quirks though. At first the turn-based approach feels a little weird, especially when dealing with aircraft. Land-based airstrikes arrive instantaneously while torpedoes can take  3-4 turns to cover the distance to the target. You get used to it though. I also wish there was a way to disable the 3rd person world view in the options (leaving only plotting map and periscope/spot view) for more of that sub-sim feel. Some people don&apos;t like that you can&apos;t save during a battle but it&apos;s never bothered me. In my experience this isn&apos;t the kind of lighthearted game you play for 20 minutes after work anyway. It something you sit down with for an hour or two and get really into.

Overall I&apos;d give it a 4.5 if I could give half stars. You notice the quirks when you first play, but they don&apos;t define the game.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>3272a95a-4637-11ec-949e-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>If you&apos;re into history you&apos;ll love it</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/3282f982-aec3-11ec-80ca-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/3282f982-aec3-11ec-80ca-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-03-28T21:16:33</review:date>
        <review:description>Shantae and the Seven Sirens is a game about having a relaxing beach vacation. Or it is a highly enjoyable metroidvania, who can say. What I can say is that it is worth the full price. Good purchase decision, my past self.

Pros:
 + Gorgeous art
 + Precise controls
 + Fun map to explore with plenty of secrets
 + Collecting enemy cards for powerups is addicting

Cons:
 - There are not as many genie forms as previously, but using them is generally much faster.
 - Backtracking returns, but as moving around is fast, it is less tedious than before.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>3282f982-aec3-11ec-80ca-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Highly enjoyable</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/3293c9cc-aabb-11eb-89d6-fa163e3a9b6e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/3293c9cc-aabb-11eb-89d6-fa163e3a9b6e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-05-01T23:24:14</review:date>
        <review:description>So, I really don&apos;t get the &quot;One Star, it&apos;s communism, Mueriaaa FTW&quot; reviews. But the game itself is just not really good. For just that reason it gets just two stars.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">31</review:downvotes>
