    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/37e07666-88a0-11ea-8dc3-fa163e93294d -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/37e07666-88a0-11ea-8dc3-fa163e93294d">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-04-27T19:00:30</review:date>
        <review:description>I have currently logged over 70 hours in this game. This is a great chill destress game. I would put it similar to Animal Crossing and Stardew Valley. I haven&apos;t had nay major bugs or errors. I only had one crash the entire time that I have been playing. 

The game does get a bit grindy at times as you are developing resources to build. To help break the monotony definitely take advantage of the relationship aspects of it. This adds in other mini games to help break things up. There are also chances to do more than farm. You build items, battle monsters, and play mini games. It&apos;d also be a great game for kids as well. </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>37e07666-88a0-11ea-8dc3-fa163e93294d</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Fun Chill Game</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


