    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/38805440-f192-11eb-81b3-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/38805440-f192-11eb-81b3-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-07-31T02:59:48</review:date>
        <review:description>I haven&apos;t played the GOG version, but I have the original MS-DOS versions from COSMI&apos;s &quot;Top 10 Solid Gold&quot; and &quot;Top 10 Solid Gold Volume II&quot;. 

If these are the same games, then Super Huey I is kind of boring. There are only 3 &quot;missions&quot;, training, explore, and combat. Only the combat one is interesting, but it is the same every time.

On the other hand, Super Huey II was quite fun. I&apos;d give SH1** and SH2 *****.
It&apos;s great that they bundled them together, because the tutorial in SH1 was useful to learn the game while SH2 was the &quot;real&quot; game.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>38805440-f192-11eb-81b3-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:rating>
        <review:title>Super Huey1 was Meh, but SH2 was fun.</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/39aa401c-69b3-11ec-975e-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/39aa401c-69b3-11ec-975e-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-12-30T22:58:22</review:date>
        <review:description>I really enjoyed my time in Sveti Kotar, spend about 10 hours with the game, which makes the price quite reasonable. I read a lot of reviews criticising the voice acting. Its very important for me to state:

Voice acting has been redone and updated, it is absolutely fine.

What I like about the game:

- Nice setting in a fresh location (Dont know about any other game taking place in Croatia)
- Very nice story, atmosphere and narrative.
- Sublte horror and supense
- Elements of moral, ethics, religion
- While the game is not perfect, the Devs seem to have put a lot of love and work into the game. They have anounced more content, DLCS, etc. which will continue and enhance the story.

This game should be for you, if you like the above and look for a nice narratively focused game.
Gameplaywise the game is not hard at all, so if you look for a classic point and click adventure, to work your brain, this is not your game.
If you like a focus on story, you will be pleased.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>39aa401c-69b3-11ec-975e-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Nice story-focused game</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/39ad11d4-3acf-11eb-994b-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/39ad11d4-3acf-11eb-994b-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-12-10T12:05:26</review:date>
        <review:description>Thank you for releasing this game drm free.
I have come a long way in the Barbarians campaign, this is a really good game.
This game and its expansions are Worth every penny!

The good:
-What I have seen the AI does not cheat, AI plays the game following the rules witch is really impressive.
Few strategy games have this good programmed AI.
-Game play is captivating, and really solid.
-The campaign story is good, really enjoying my first campaign play trough 
-Beautiful graphics
-Not seen any bugs, good programmed game.

The bad:
Nothing bad to say about this game
</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>39ad11d4-3acf-11eb-994b-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Really good game excellent programmed AI</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/39bb047a-9692-11e9-a464-1229876dead8 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/39bb047a-9692-11e9-a464-1229876dead8">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-06-24T15:10:38</review:date>
        <review:description>Was expecting an old school racer and found a weird boring drifter racing game. Really after the first race, i was bored to death. most of the time you are by yourself and you just drift by other cars with no issues. the backgrounds are the same thing over and over. I guess i was expect pole position or top gear, but it just wasn&apos;t what I expect. Let my buddy play it too and he said the same thing. Maybe i didn&apos;t make it far enough into the game, but it was a letdown and i have no want to try it again anytime soon. </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>39bb047a-9692-11e9-a464-1229876dead8</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:rating>
        <review:title>Just plain boring</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">8</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/39bbaa04-9500-11e8-b193-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/39bbaa04-9500-11e8-b193-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2013-07-12T04:20:17</review:date>
        <review:description>But what about the fact that there exist no real characters? Everyone&apos;s just called Alpha, and as such the protagonist&apos;s interaction with the world is bizarre and stilted. A squad that sticks by you, a sense of movement as you move from division and division, the fact that command is constantly pulling some suspicious sh*t never becomes a factor in the story, and Bosch the narrator and point of interest fades anticlimactically out of the story. Now I&apos;ve also tried to make some excuses for the strange ending, it could be kind of a cool anticlimax if the preceding game had been suitably involving, but it wasn&apos;t. I felt cheated.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">8</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>39bbaa04-9500-11e8-b193-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>Good Space Combat</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">7</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


