    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4ae46424-13ed-11eb-a296-fa163e7e880a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4ae46424-13ed-11eb-a296-fa163e7e880a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-10-22T01:32:24</review:date>
        <review:description>I skipped the last Shantae game because it was linear and didn&apos;t resemble the games of the past. With Seven Sirens Wayfoward has returned to the classic Metroidvania style that fans have grown to love. Why they went linear is beyond me, but I&apos;m glad they had enough sense to get back to true Shantae style. 

This game is packed with style and charm, as usual, but it is accentuated now by the cartoon art style. The anime style opening doesn&apos;t seem to fit the rest of the art style though. The classic gameplay is here and intact with towns, finding squids and earning money to power up Shantae as much or as little as you like. There is a mini game that I didn&apos; t see the point of and was pretty difficult, but at least they tried. 

For as great as the game is though, it feels like a  rushed game by the bare bones nature. There is only one special mode and very few unlockables, and the unlockables are tied to clear time which is a bad idea since not many people are into speedrunning.  The game lacks that little bit extra attention that would have gotten it a full five stars, but it a great romp in the lovable Shantae wolrld that I hope we&apos;ll see more of soon.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>4ae46424-13ed-11eb-a296-fa163e7e880a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Return to Form, but Still Needs Work</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4af54b30-da74-11e9-9afc-7e7bd49fe254 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4af54b30-da74-11e9-9afc-7e7bd49fe254">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-09-19T00:27:42</review:date>
        <review:description>I learned that when the editor is released, it won’t have a random map generator. You’ll have to make a map from scratch in the editor, which takes too much time for some of us with a busy schedule. HOMM III &amp;amp; AOW SHADOW MAGIC had this feature.
Also with only two main factions in the game and only 3 sides available in the skirmish mode will make the player lose interest in the game after a few weeks of playing and move on. This game needs to be heavily discounted at this stage for what it offers.

</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">10</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>4af54b30-da74-11e9-9afc-7e7bd49fe254</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>More elements need to be added.</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">13</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4b1484d6-7ef9-11e9-bdf3-00163e4e60cc -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4b1484d6-7ef9-11e9-bdf3-00163e4e60cc">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-05-25T17:27:58</review:date>
        <review:description>It&apos;s hard to explain but Pathologic 2 is simultaneously a remake of Pathologic 1, a sequel, a reimagining, and a game unto its own. It&apos;s probably one of the strongest contenders for &quot;games as art&quot; and in this case, a device to induce a kind of performance art... starring you, the player. 

The most important thing to remember is that this game wants you to quit. Much like our deranged overlords on this ball of mud, it wants you to give up and not reach the finish line. Don&apos;t let it. You will learn the hard way how to keep on preserving. The story is a tragic one, but a testament to the tenacity of the strength of the human spirit. Will you not like it, but you can do it. It may seem hopeless, but there is hope.

There&apos;s never been a better time than before to play this game.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>4b1484d6-7ef9-11e9-bdf3-00163e4e60cc</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Don&apos;t EVER give up.</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">8</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4b855012-b7b0-11ea-adb7-fa163e93294d -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4b855012-b7b0-11ea-adb7-fa163e93294d">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-06-26T16:23:59</review:date>
        <review:description>C&apos;est tout bonnement une œuvre d&apos;art.
Dans ce jeux d&apos;enquête qui vous fera réellement réfléchir avec un système qui encourage la déduction faite par le joueur, c&apos;est bien le gameplay et l&apos;interactivité qui amène l&apos;histoire au joueur.

Avec une qualité artistique très appréciable  aussi bien dans les musiques que dans les images, ce jeu m&apos;a tenu une dizaine d&apos;heure sans jamais m&apos;ennuyer.

A jouer seul ou accompagné (pour réfléchir à plusieurs) ce petit bijou sera, je n&apos;en doute pas, un classique à ne pas rater.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>4b855012-b7b0-11ea-adb7-fa163e93294d</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Une Oeuvre d&apos;art !</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4b92e054-93fb-11e8-a73b-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4b92e054-93fb-11e8-a73b-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2009-01-05T17:34:38</review:date>
        <review:description>This was one of the first titles that offered true 3D environment to real world. The controls and presence of captivating character ensured the success, I commend!</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>4b92e054-93fb-11e8-a73b-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Brilliant!</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4bb89f8a-93f9-11e8-a547-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4bb89f8a-93f9-11e8-a547-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2008-09-24T17:37:19</review:date>
        <review:description>I remember playing this game about a week after it came out and I was hooked. Where the story in Wing Commander got a bit weak after #3, the story here was actually pretty good. The graphics were top notch and still don&apos;t look bad even today. The dogfighting was fast and furious. One of the great parts of this game is that winning/losing a missing has consequences rather than just &quot;you lose&quot; or &quot;next mission in line&quot;. An all around intense game, a very fun game and a must-have for space sim armchair pilots. And you cannot miss Freespace 2 either...</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>4bb89f8a-93f9-11e8-a547-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>One of the greatest space fighters</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4bf95848-9568-11e8-8c2a-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4bf95848-9568-11e8-8c2a-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2014-11-30T12:01:13</review:date>
        <review:description>even 15 years after its release is still the BEST game of the genre. A great story, a great engine, graphics that are still acceptable even by today&apos;s standards. (for those that want better graphics there are enhancements made to the game that you can install, ever since the source code was made public; Open Freespace Project is one option). This game has it all. Ship system management in-flight, fully customisable controls, and believe me, almost every key on the keyboard is used for something, not that you need every one of them, but the level of control offered is amazing. The implementation of capital ships and capital ship combat is truly innovative. The campaign itself will keep you busy for quite some time. It has secret missions which you can access only if you&apos;re good enough and your very own medal case if you feel up to the challenge of filling it up.

I am one of the really lucky ones that were also able to (briefly) play this game while the original multiplayer servers were still online. The multiplayer is even more engaging than the single player campaign. The varied choice of ships and weapons really comes into play in MP and the battlegrounds ranging from empty space to massive shipyards hosting capital ships will keep your skills challenged and yourself entertained for hours and hours. For those interested, there are still active communities out there that organize MP games.

No other game ever made can match up to this level of immersion. there is one candidate that might, coming soon from Chris Roberts, but I still have doubts it will outclass this masterpiece.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>4bf95848-9568-11e8-8c2a-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>The space sim that</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4c11b21c-f9ca-11ea-9fb3-fa163edf6d96 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4c11b21c-f9ca-11ea-9fb3-fa163edf6d96">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-09-18T19:16:24</review:date>
        <review:description>#1: - XINPUT1_4.dll file is missing, prohibiting game from launching.

#2: - Offline Backup Installer is missing UE4 Prerequisites, needed to Verify / Repair with
GOG Galaxy to &quot;finish&quot; the install, except additional Galaxy Verify / Repair attempts result
in repeats of the identical 101MB download . . . WITH NO FIX!</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">10</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>4c11b21c-f9ca-11ea-9fb3-fa163edf6d96</review:id>
