        <review:title>Broken Release!</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4c6fd9cc-299c-11ea-8d88-00163e4e60cc -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4c6fd9cc-299c-11ea-8d88-00163e4e60cc">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-12-28T20:03:06</review:date>
        <review:description>My first impressions, in order of appearing: 
1. Oh god, I hate the controls
2. Oh god there&apos;s so much and I feel so lost
3. What the &amp;amp;@(*$!??
Repeat step 3 for at least an hour.

It&apos;s a game unlike any others I&apos;ve played so far, and yet it truly shows how some stories can be put to another level by video games. The story itself isn&apos;t overly complicated, but since the player has to connect all the dots by themself, the intensity of the experience rises up to the sky. It makes the game surprisingly hard - clues can be very small, hidden or otherwise easy to miss - but extremely rewarding. 

The way the story is discovered reminds me of Bloodborne, in a way. Nothing is given to you straight on a platter and many pieces make sense only after you piece together the larger context. Just as real detective work. If you like detective stories and mind-twisters, absolutely give this one a go, it&apos;s a real treat.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>4c6fd9cc-299c-11ea-8d88-00163e4e60cc</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Truly unique detective experience</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4c7e5d24-eab9-11ea-89d2-fa163edf6d96 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4c7e5d24-eab9-11ea-89d2-fa163edf6d96">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-08-30T15:06:56</review:date>
        <review:description>..... wait...... wait..... wait..... 400 days....

I have to say, once I watched the trailer I felt a wave of joy wash over me, finally a game that was completely different to anything I have ever played before and crafted with such care and thought into the &apos;meaning of time&apos; of &apos;loneliness&apos; of &apos;patience&apos;.

Playing this will slow down your world and open up a new experience. This would be in my top-5 games of all time.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>4c7e5d24-eab9-11ea-89d2-fa163edf6d96</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>An absolute Gem!</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4c9d64fa-40f2-11eb-a6ee-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4c9d64fa-40f2-11eb-a6ee-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-12-18T07:31:37</review:date>
        <review:description>The game is ok. Not terrible but not really as spectacular as it initially looked (gameplay wise). Combat is pretty straight forward. No real special moves. There is a combo attack but it&apos;s automatic and not done by pressing any certain button combination. Just basically spam the attack button, hit the enemy till they die (again lol) and you can dodge by rolling out of the way. Enemies spawn it groups and you gotta kill them before you move on. You do aquire different weapons as you go along that do behave differently.

The one thing it does pretty well is the presentation. Good graphical style and really harkens back the PS2 days.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>4c9d64fa-40f2-11eb-a6ee-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Harkens back to PS2 era</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4cc30df0-7d0f-11eb-85bf-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4cc30df0-7d0f-11eb-85bf-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-03-04T19:30:23</review:date>
        <review:description>Игра достаточно интересна, но совсем не стандартна, для понимания многих вещей в ней нужно или отыграть не один десяток часов или что быстрее, посмотреть на ютубе видео о ней и тогда все станет более понятным.</review:description>
