    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4d3ca280-4eb2-11ec-b699-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4d3ca280-4eb2-11ec-b699-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-11-26T14:13:44</review:date>
        <review:description>I&apos;m a huge fan of the Adeptus Mechanicus but this new faction in Gladius looks a lot like the Imperial Guard to me. However, they have specificities like canticles or the way buildings can increase/reduce production, but it feels over complicated compared to other factions specific rules.

Anyway, I&apos;m happy to be able to play my favorite faction :)</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>4d3ca280-4eb2-11ec-b699-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>New faction but not really innovative</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4d722544-9520-11e8-b7f5-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4d722544-9520-11e8-b7f5-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2013-12-27T23:25:26</review:date>
        <review:description>Few games could hold up to this one when it came out, and even today this game provides me more entertainment than many 2013 games. Through the power of open source projects I&apos;m playing this game at 2560x1600 res with beautiful graphics and 3d sound...I&apos;m playing the freespace 1 campaign on freespace 2! For Free! 

I&apos;m so glad this genre is being revived in 2014...but until that happens, you gotta play this game!</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>4d722544-9520-11e8-b7f5-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Irresistably playable with mods</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4db0768e-68fb-11ec-8a71-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4db0768e-68fb-11ec-8a71-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-12-30T01:01:49</review:date>
        <review:description>This is a wonderful little 3D platformer that knows exactly what it is, and tries as much as possible to recapture that feeling you got from PS2-era platformers as a kid. Being someone that played a lot of Jak, Rachet+Clank and the like, Pumpkin Jack absolutely delivered. Short runtime, but well worth the experience!</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
