        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>A great indie 3D Platformer</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4db2d83a-945a-11e8-a318-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4db2d83a-945a-11e8-a318-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2011-02-28T20:42:53</review:date>
        <review:description>The original game was critically acclaimed but there is so much more here.
This game enjoys a strong mod community who have created new graphics, new models, new missions, many new and continued continued story lines and several conversions to other story universes including Star Wars, Battlestar Galactica reimagined, Babylon 5 and Wing Commander.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>4db2d83a-945a-11e8-a318-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Perfection in a Space Sim</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4db80134-7255-11ec-a8d7-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4db80134-7255-11ec-a8d7-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-01-10T22:38:44</review:date>
        <review:description>Прежде чем в нее играть, надо точно убедится, что это игра для вас.

Из реальных проблем - видимо не очень хорошая оптимизация. Видеокарта напрягалась как будто включен Киберпанк на максималках.

Но если жанр &quot;игра вас ненавидит&quot; вам по душе и вы любите преодолевать трудности, то дерзайте! Сюжет интересный, образы и персанажи очень атмосферные и метафоричные. Многие упрекают в плохой графике, но мой глаз это не цепануло, наоборот некая стилизация персонажей подчеркивает их род деательности, красивая в своём роде игра в общем.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>4db80134-7255-11ec-a8d7-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Сложно, красиво, почувствуй мор</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4dd315fe-6e19-11ec-a5ed-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4dd315fe-6e19-11ec-a5ed-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-01-05T13:19:10</review:date>
        <review:description>I really love Northguard.
Im Hooked for the past week and cannot stop playing :-)

Pros:
- Love the graphics / sound
- Love the gameplay</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>4dd315fe-6e19-11ec-a5ed-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>A true gem</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4dd54cfc-94fb-11e8-886c-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4dd54cfc-94fb-11e8-886c-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2013-06-20T20:54:42</review:date>
        <review:description>This is a really good spacecombat game.

You get a briefing for the battle, then depending on your rank you might get to choose your ship and loadout and later your squads ships and loadout.

Then the BATTLE starts. This game has really really good battles. You can only fly smaller fighters and bombers, but the battles has cruisers, destroyers, titans...you will see huge bams going off, you will see flak defence fire. And you are in the middle, part of a bigger battle. But you can influence it in a lot of ways.
Run interceptors and catch enemy torpedoes so your capital ships win. Or fly air superiority fighters and get those enemy bomers. Or fly a bomber and disable enemy capital ship components.
Or make your squad bombers and protect them with your fighter....

But its not all allout battle, you can have scoutmission in a nebula where you can see anything. Or you get invited to a blackop mission behind enemy lines. Or you are stationed near a civilian structure and have to make sure nothing goes wrong!




But you know what the best part is?This game went open source, there is a fanproject that you use that updates the graphics quite a lot.
And there are countless of total mods with new storyline and everything.


btw, this game is perfectly fine with mouse and keyboard, at least the open source project version is.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>4dd54cfc-94fb-11e8-886c-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Best spacesim</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4deaedd6-2ad7-11eb-a589-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4deaedd6-2ad7-11eb-a589-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-11-20T04:22:57</review:date>
        <review:description>Great platformer with tight controls, cool graphics and nice soundtrack. It&apos;s on the easy side, so if you are looking for a challenge this is not the game for you, but that&apos;s a huge plus for me: I&apos;ve never felt frustrated while playing, I spent the whole time relaxed and having fun.
 
The only thing that I didn&apos;t love were the cinematics in between the chapters. Although they&apos;re well animated and narrated, they simply serve as a recap of what just happened, making them quite pointless.

This comes from a solo developer, which is even more amazing. I&apos;d love to see a sequel with a bigger budget and more people working on it, but not a too many. Let&apos;s say nough to be able to flesh out the levels, maybe with the addition of  a few genre tropes like hub worlds, more collectibles and NPCs... but not too many that the awesome home-made labor of love feeling gets lost).</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>4deaedd6-2ad7-11eb-a589-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Fun!</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">7</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4dedd8c4-93f9-11e8-a443-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4dedd8c4-93f9-11e8-a443-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2008-09-25T18:45:49</review:date>
        <review:description>First I was absolutely delighten by the game&apos;s intro and soundtrack. Then the visuals, story and fights. Finished the first Freespace just a few weeks before playing no.2. I loved the continuity and many new features. What I stil remember from Freespace 2 is the soundtrack and great &quot;tough&quot; voiceacting (Admiral Petrarch? I am not sure about the name but I loved it). I have used the Freespace lines in my English classes in high school :-) but had oscillating success with the teachers - Our school was not a military academy after all :-)...

My quest to get it was also memorable - It was not released in Czech republic and I had to buy it from the UK. No UK shop at the time was shipping to Czech so I had to persuade (using persuadentron, of course :-) my UK friend to buy it and send it to me (sent him cash in an envelope - no paypal then :-). It was a great service for me and I never will forget his brave deeds. 

NOW I REALLY HAD TO BUY THIS GREAT BUNDLE OF BOTH FREESPACE 1 and 2 and Re-Live it again with all the sweet mods and additional goodies.   5 of 5 stars - That&apos;s and order. Thanks GOG!!!</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>4dedd8c4-93f9-11e8-a443-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Consumed by the atmosphere...</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4e027946-d8b1-11eb-9b99-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4e027946-d8b1-11eb-9b99-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-06-29T11:09:19</review:date>
        <review:description>Plot &amp;amp; writing are excellent. The gamey-ness of the game is always heavily emphasized, but it never takes away from emotional moments and never overplayed. Depending on your sense of humor, some dialogues and locations may be hilarious. The humor is sometimes very subtle, for example, repeating an oddly specific thing that an optional NPC says elsewhere. Doesn&apos;t feel like it&apos;s trying too hard.

The gameplay segments are generally easy, with the exception of some 2d puzzles later in the game. Also, navigation may be confusing and it will require you to memorize a lot of places. It&apos;s rewarding if you do, because there is a whole lot of shortcuts. Not really comparable to super metroid, but there&apos;s a similar feel.

I STRONGLY advise everyone to play Anodyne 1 first. It puts you in the right mood for the second game.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>4e027946-d8b1-11eb-9b99-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Meta and self-referential in a good way</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4e181210-dca2-11ec-87b5-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4e181210-dca2-11ec-87b5-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-05-26T06:16:59</review:date>
        <review:description>Before I begin, I just want to thank GOG for opening up to sex games with the naughty parts intact! Now for the review. This is a pool style game with a naughty twist! The Idea of the game is to hit the other balls to extend the length of your turn. During your turn, you go around and fuck bunny girls, six in total! You try to fuck them all while killing the other guys that are doing the same thing.
As you complete levels, you will unlock the &quot;Gallery Mode&quot;. This mode allows you to fuck the girls in various positions! You can unlock more girls (more than six in this mode!), positions, and even watch them dance! You can unlock more dances as you progress in the game too! The animations are really well done and arousing! The game&apos;s page says you can make your own levels, however, I haven&apos;t try that yet. If you are into anime bunny girls, hentai, or sex games in general, I strongly recommend this game!     </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>4e181210-dca2-11ec-87b5-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>This Is What I&apos;m Talking About!!! </review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">25</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4e3b87ce-f2fe-11eb-9ac1-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4e3b87ce-f2fe-11eb-9ac1-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-08-01T22:26:01</review:date>
        <review:description>I love the struggle.
Because that is life.
I&apos;m 45 so listen to a man who has played almost everything since the invention of pixels.

This is one of the best games for people like me.

I want to have a good story.
I want to struggle.
I want a bad ending.
I want a game.
I want to expand.
I want to shrink.
I want to learn and retry.

This game gives you a lot of what you want and its just plain fun and relaxing to play.
Give it a go, have a laugh, have a long night :)

Kind regards
Oliver

P.S. Elon Musk should play this because he would then realize how hard human interaction in such a situation really is :)</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>4e3b87ce-f2fe-11eb-9ac1-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Elon Musk should play this.</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">29</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4e46c036-a8c6-11ea-9a36-fa163e62c76a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4e46c036-a8c6-11ea-9a36-fa163e62c76a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-06-07T16:53:45</review:date>
        <review:description>
Pour faire simple, je dirais que si vous aimez le mélange entre Civilization et Warcraft3, achetez &quot;Northgard&quot; sans réfléchir.
Les DLC, par contre, ne sont utiles que pour le multijoueur (ils ne servent pas pour le mode solo).

Le positif :
- Le graphisme est beau, très agréable et coloré.
- L&apos;histoire est bien écrite, même si elle est assez simple.
- La bande-son est bonne, musiques comme bruitages, mais le doublage laisse à désirer.
- Le mélange Gestion/STR.
- Le jeu est fluide (je n&apos;ai eu aucun crash).
- On a le multijoueur en LAN !

Le négatif :
- Les DLCS sont chers, et n&apos;ajoutent rien au jeu de base (le mode solo).
- Les textes du jeu ne sont pas tous traduits.
- Le doublage narratif du mode solo (en Anglais) est clairement pas terrible.

Bref, certes non sans défaut, &quot;Northgard&quot; est un bon jeu à l&apos;accent Viking.
Il saura faire passer un bon nombre d&apos;heures de jeu aux fans du genre.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>4e46c036-a8c6-11ea-9a36-fa163e62c76a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Déjà un classique.</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">8</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4e72440c-9443-11e8-a182-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4e72440c-9443-11e8-a182-00163e97122a">
