    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/43b02b38-b2c0-11e8-bf90-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/43b02b38-b2c0-11e8-bf90-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2018-04-22T21:53:46</review:date>
        <review:description>The music was great (especially the FLAC format) but the marketing is a bit deceptive. Maybe I was just being naive, but when it says &quot;to play this item you also need Baldur&apos;s Gate: Enhanced Edition&quot; I just assumed that maybe it would upgrade the in-game music sound track. However, it doesn&apos;t appear to do that at all. (I guess my first clue should have been the fact that there are no FLAC or MP3 files in the BG:EE game directory to begin with.) So all this download is good for, as far as I can see, is for playing the BG music on an MP3 player or something similar. It doesn&apos;t appear to add anything to the game itself. So I&apos;m not sure why the description on GOG&apos;s website says you need BG:EE in order to play this. You do not. If you just want the music to play on your own outside of the game, then by all means get this. It souds great. But if you are looking for an enhanced music experience in game, this is not going to do that. I guess I&apos;m not going to bother buying the soundtrack for BG2:EE after finding this out. Oh well, live and learn.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">11</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>43b02b38-b2c0-11e8-bf90-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:rating>
        <review:title>Not entirely happy</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">20</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/43d4e1da-acf1-11ea-a30c-fa163e62c76a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/43d4e1da-acf1-11ea-a30c-fa163e62c76a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-06-13T00:11:21</review:date>
        <review:description>Szukasz gry survivalowej, gdzie twój kolonista dostaje szału i zaczyna mordować, bo nie spełniły się jego wymagania? Zapraszamy do Rimworlda, najbardziej nieludzkiej gry, gdzie możesz wycinać organy, aby potem kupić za nie 50 tabliczek czekolady, bo twój handlarz to miękka faja jest. Chcesz ataki reptilian, których bombardujesz pociskami atomowymi, a potem dobijasz ich antlionami z half life 2? Miliardy modów czekają na ciebie. Ta gra jest tak prosta, że pójdzie na ziemniaku graficznym (serio potrzebujesz procesora i RAM i to tyle). Dla mnie 10/10</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>43d4e1da-acf1-11ea-a30c-fa163e62c76a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Cudna, bogata i długowieczna gra.</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/43d95cf2-b1fd-11ec-82d8-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/43d95cf2-b1fd-11ec-82d8-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-04-01T23:49:46</review:date>
        <review:description>The art style is gorgeous. The music gets repetitive, but there&apos;s certain places where that shines too. The portal mechanic is neat, though you don&apos;t get to pick which one you get even if you &quot;unlock&quot; several.

But the difficulty just spikes hard at places. I think I reached my limit in the third world. I can&apos;t get past an obstacle. The hidden lost villagers that you can optionally find are a pita to get to as well, so I simply started ignoring them. For someone who enjoys tough challenging platformers, this game may just be right up your alley.

I don&apos;t know if I can finish this game. I wish I could.

One annoying bug - if you fall, the game can think that that counts as a jump and you can&apos;t double jump out of it.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>43d95cf2-b1fd-11ec-82d8-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:rating>
        <review:title>Good art, high difficulty</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/430f4110-a971-11ea-a00d-fa163e62c76a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/430f4110-a971-11ea-a00d-fa163e62c76a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-06-08T13:17:30</review:date>
        <review:description>If you loved the base game, this adds more of the same things. It&apos;s just a great content add-on that makes the game even better. Well-worth the price.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>430f4110-a971-11ea-a00d-fa163e62c76a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>So worth it</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/435072d4-9401-11e8-912b-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/435072d4-9401-11e8-912b-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2009-12-23T11:38:33</review:date>
        <review:description>This game is amazing.  The plot and dialog feel very authentic and you really get sucked into what is going on.  With a joystick, this game is a dream to handle.  Check out the open source Freespace 2 project and download and install all of fancy new graphical updates to really enjoy this classic reborn.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>435072d4-9401-11e8-912b-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>The pinnacle of space combat simulation</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/436b34b4-8f0c-11e9-bda6-00163e4e60cc -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/436b34b4-8f0c-11e9-bda6-00163e4e60cc">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-06-15T04:24:04</review:date>
        <review:description>I am aging myself, but I played this game when it was brand new. I revisited this game and it is every bit as wonderful as I remember.

There are no space combat sims that exist today that can hold a candle to this title. A must play for anyone who loves games. The FSO mod is a good update to the visuals of the game.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>436b34b4-8f0c-11e9-bda6-00163e4e60cc</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>A Must Play for Young and Old</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">9</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/43617678-9a2e-11e8-ad0e-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/43617678-9a2e-11e8-ad0e-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2016-03-05T05:11:24</review:date>
        <review:description>The Saint&apos;s Row series was a mistake, because Voltron should have been pumping sequels for this aging, ugly and beyond bad-ass masterpeice. Buy it, and murder ALL the shivians</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>43617678-9a2e-11e8-ad0e-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Jesus Christ is this good</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">10</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4362389a-93fa-11e8-9172-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4362389a-93fa-11e8-9172-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2008-10-25T12:16:17</review:date>
        <review:description>This game is epic. However, to get the full expecience, look up the the open source &quot;Freespace Source Code Project&quot;. You need the data from the game, which this will get you. This new engine includes multitudes new features, and combined with the &quot;MediaVP&quot; packs, brings the graphics up to par with today&apos;s games.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">7</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>4362389a-93fa-11e8-9172-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Excellent</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">31</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/43642c56-de34-11e9-80a6-ba8347d8655b -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/43642c56-de34-11e9-80a6-ba8347d8655b">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-09-23T18:59:26</review:date>
        <review:description>The gameplay is very slow due the characther&apos;s speed and the bad experience with keyboard. Aestetics and histoty are good but they ruined everything since looks like they don´t even play games. This is more like a movie with viewer interacctions.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">9</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>43642c56-de34-11e9-80a6-ba8347d8655b</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>An slow game with good dark aesthetics.</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">24</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/43677288-9481-11e8-bb95-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/43677288-9481-11e8-bb95-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2011-09-30T14:53:32</review:date>
        <review:description>Definitely the best in it&apos;s genre. Not only a great simulator but a climactic story (much better than SC), and it&apos;s just a load of fun. I would definitely buy if I didn&apos;t have my original CDs. One of the best game purchases I made.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>43677288-9481-11e8-bb95-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Worth every penny</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4376b19a-2f51-11eb-b25c-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4376b19a-2f51-11eb-b25c-fa163e99870e">
