    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/439c4ac6-0014-11ea-bcfd-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/439c4ac6-0014-11ea-bcfd-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-11-05T23:36:02</review:date>
        <review:description>I wasted about 5 hours of next next next...

- Animation is ... static, so game starts to look very cheap after 2 h of seeing same sprites again and again.
- Dialogs are dull and full of water. Unreal and useless.
- Main character is too aggressive as for me for no visible reason.
- Choices? I remember 2 or 3 of them during my 5h gameplay, and they weren&apos;t really important to me.
- Replayability? I gave up on the first run. 

Really, you can go to the coffee shop and talk to random real person and it&apos;ll be much more exiting.
or you can buy a good book and read it if you hate people. You can even buy a book with branching storyline if you like.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>439c4ac6-0014-11ea-bcfd-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>most boring game I played, ever</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">7</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/44a04426-e221-11ec-aab9-42010a340c26 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/44a04426-e221-11ec-aab9-42010a340c26">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-06-02T06:08:25</review:date>
        <review:description>Looks lovely, sounds wonderful, great and catchy soundtrack, feels like the devs are actually trying to evolve the HoMM formula.

Limited unit stacks is good at making early units still viable, putting the whole town into the map makes it feel a bit more &apos;real&apos;.

I&apos;m not certain if this makes the game-play better, but it does wonders to making this type of game feel new and unique.

The worst thing I can say about this game is I wish there was more of it. More factions, more units, more everything.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>44a04426-e221-11ec-aab9-42010a340c26</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Wonderful.</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/44a916a0-3f07-11eb-a3d7-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/44a916a0-3f07-11eb-a3d7-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-12-15T20:56:41</review:date>
        <review:description>I found this game on GoG, bought it, played it and today I&apos;ve finished it. The game was only 6 hours long but it was so much fun that I really want to give it 5 stars.
Almost everything here was done right. The graphics look gorgeous (especially the lighting), the controls via mouse and keyboard is pretty responsive and the music fits perfectly. The game also offers some fun mini-games and some (easy) puzzles.

I highly recommend this game to any fan of 3D platformers!
</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>44a916a0-3f07-11eb-a3d7-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>My surprise hit of 2020</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/44c57fd4-a790-11ea-9654-fa163e62c76a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/44c57fd4-a790-11ea-9654-fa163e62c76a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-06-06T03:54:25</review:date>
        <review:description>If you wanna relive the glory days of action flash games, but with today&apos;s production values, this is one of your best options

Yes, the later levels lean more on the puzzle side but there&apos;s still enough shooting to make it worth it, my only real issue is with the last &quot;normal&quot; boss battle where the boss uses the same dodge move you have but it isn&apos;t really clear when you can actually inflict damage again</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>44c57fd4-a790-11ea-9654-fa163e62c76a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Pure, fun, knows where to end</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/44e8cdcc-aab4-11eb-bd75-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/44e8cdcc-aab4-11eb-bd75-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-05-01T22:34:39</review:date>
        <review:description>Political content aside, the gameplay is just mindless and boring. There&apos;s very little in the way of good game mechanics, any sort of strategy or even colorful, entertaining beat downs. It only gets away with it because it&apos;s dressed up in controversial material. 
If the game was identical but used a different skin (such as &quot;Baldies&quot; vs &quot;Hairies&quot;) it would be left to the dustbin of unknown games, since there are much better Beat em up/Hack &apos;n slash games out there.
Basically If you are the type to get gleeful from sticking a rich persons picture onto a punching bag then this is your game. But If that strikes you as insipid, then pass.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">25</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>44e8cdcc-aab4-11eb-bd75-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>Weak game grabbing low hanging fruit</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">94</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/44edacb4-1a57-11ea-8fb1-00163e4e60cc -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/44edacb4-1a57-11ea-8fb1-00163e4e60cc">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-12-09T09:41:10</review:date>
        <review:description>I&apos;ve never written a review before, but I felt with this game I just had to get my feelings out on it.
This game is a genuine masterpiece, and I say that about very, very few games. This is easily one of my top ten games EVER.
The atmosphere, the choices, the way things are structured, and OH GOD THE WRITING.
It is just fantastic. Genuinely fantastic.

A lot has been said about how hard the game is, and absolutely it is. But I will say, I don&apos;t normally enjoy games that are super hard and frustrating for the sake of it, (it took me a very long time to take to the Dark Souls series for instance) because I don&apos;t enjoy having to constantly restart and repeat myself every time I fail.

But this game I took to immediately. 

You genuinely learn something every time you fail, and because the game is so expertly designed around this experience, and heavily embedded into the themes and the writing, even every failure is unbelievably compelling. You feel like you&apos;re struggling against something, but even while it&apos;s punishing you, the intentions of the game are with you as you do it. And it means that all the little victories you have feel really important and well earned. Everything might be falling apart, BUT YOU HAVE SAVED LIVES IN THE FACE OF EVERYTHING TELLING YOU YOU CAN&apos;T.

Seriously, can&apos;t recommend the game enough. Really hope that it gets the recognition it deserves, really hope it&apos;s successful enough for them to release the other two stories. BUY THIS GAME AND THEN PLAY THIS GAME AND THEN TELL EVERYONE YOU KNOW TO DO THE SAME SO THEN THE DEVS GET MONEY AND THEN MAKE MORE PLEASE AND THANK YOU.

P.S. DO NOT TAKE THE FELLOW TRAVELLER&apos;S DEAL. EVER. </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>44edacb4-1a57-11ea-8fb1-00163e4e60cc</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>One of my top ten games ever.</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">9</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/442535de-4c2c-11ea-9077-fa163e62c76a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/442535de-4c2c-11ea-9077-fa163e62c76a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-02-10T19:39:19</review:date>
        <review:description>The Long Reach est au final un bon petit jeu d&apos;aventure à la sauce Point &amp;amp; Click. Les contrôles sont simples : Bougez votre personnage et interragissez avec l&apos;environnement. 
Les énigmes sont simples et efficace et nous pousse à l&apos;exploration. Certaines sont logiques, d&apos;autres moins. Mais on ne se prend pas la tête bien longtemps à force d&apos;explorer et de tester différentes combinaisons.
Le style pixel art est maîtrisée et on passe un bon moment devant ce jeu. Il faut compter 3 heures pour le terminer et il n&apos;y a aucune rejouabilité.
Le scénario fait son office et permet de se plonger correctement dans ce monde où la réalité côtoie le cauchemar.

Si vous avez quelques ronds de côté et que vous voudriez vous mettre à un jeu d&apos;ambiance horrifique, The Long Reach est sympathique.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>442535de-4c2c-11ea-9077-fa163e62c76a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Un petit jeu à ambiance cauchemardesque</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4434d2a0-b231-11e8-a9a7-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4434d2a0-b231-11e8-a9a7-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2017-05-13T13:06:33</review:date>
        <review:description>The game does a good job at abstracting and streamlining important aspects of managing modern nation-state. GDP, HDI, population, unemployment are all there and make sense. However, it completely fails at making them interesting and gameplay consists of waiting until your next project gets implemented. International politics is completely separated from any factors we recognize, as geopolitics or common interests, and instead consists of single concept of relations that you can influence, and thus be an ally or enemy to anyone. Wars are only somewhat interesting, you send your troops to and abstract &quot;operations&quot; on a strategic level that can achieve their goals or not. Overall, this will probably be more interesting to fans of economic sims than strategy games.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">10</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>4434d2a0-b231-11e8-a9a7-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>Rather dull</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">28</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/445f6d18-93f9-11e8-8bc3-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/445f6d18-93f9-11e8-8bc3-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2008-09-23T10:21:53</review:date>
        <review:description>Innovative, fun and completely insane!  A massive load of fun to play.  Not too challenging.  Well designed and well made.  Good replay value.  This is what games are supposed to be like!</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>445f6d18-93f9-11e8-8bc3-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Great, fun game</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">17</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/447190b6-b2e8-11e8-8b78-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/447190b6-b2e8-11e8-8b78-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2018-07-17T21:45:43</review:date>
        <review:description>Descent: Freespace the Great Conflict or Descent Frespace for short was a milestone for space simulators. At the time Wing Commander saga and Privateer were the pinnacle of the genre. D:FS took that and added a few ideas native to the Descent series and typical combat craft simulators that ultimately led to Freespace francise.

The first game isn&apos;t so huge in terms of the feeling how vast space is, but it gave a well told, mission-driven story about the fight against Vasudans and later Shivans. Game progression gave access to better units and weapons, which gave a natural feeling of how technology developped as the war and research went on. New technologies were neatly introduced in Command briefings and mission briefings. Moreover D:FS taught peole NOT to skip briefings like in Wing Commander for it was a sure way to fail a mission. Of course there were a few bugs as well but it hardly impeded gameplay. Fred editor gave rise to numerous campaings and high demand for the game spawned the sequel FS2, the greatest game of the old space sim era.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>447190b6-b2e8-11e8-8b78-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>D:FS opened the way and FS2 did the rest</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">17</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4476256c-b299-11e8-bf91-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4476256c-b299-11e8-bf91-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2018-01-04T05:05:03</review:date>
        <review:description>I still have the original 2 disc set, this game was in my opinion ahead of its time. And is still good today. As soon as I started playing again I forgot how old the game was, still captures my attention. The intro movie is by far one of the best I have still ever seen, would make an epic movie.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>4476256c-b299-11e8-bf91-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>STILL AWESOME!</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">11</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4489ff92-e262-11ea-8d59-fa163e62c76a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4489ff92-e262-11ea-8d59-fa163e62c76a">
