    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/46f7afac-34f3-11eb-ac95-fa163e4cd76b -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/46f7afac-34f3-11eb-ac95-fa163e4cd76b">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-12-03T01:08:23</review:date>
        <review:description>
There are some annoying problem with the combat party AI  and pathfinding, and especially at the beginning it&apos;s very annoying.

Pratically, no matter if the party AI is set to aggressive or passive, your companions more often than not straight up charge to the enemy, or they can&apos;t position themselves properly but starts to run around like headless chicken.

There are some  other minor nuisances like an incredible slow running speed and corridors dungeon that are filled with one, maximum two kind enemy. It becomes boring pretty fast.

Otherwise the game is good, i suggest to edit the party run speed.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>46f7afac-34f3-11eb-ac95-fa163e4cd76b</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:rating>
