    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/482cc70a-93ff-11e8-bcdf-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/482cc70a-93ff-11e8-bcdf-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2009-09-08T21:11:46</review:date>
        <review:description>Everything freespace 1 did this Freespace 2 does better. It really made you feel like you were apart of an epic space battle, especially when your a small little ship flying in between two GIGANTIC Behemoths firing off HUGE laser beams that can incinerate you if you get a little too close. Needless to say its simply exhilarating and I heavily recommend it. The only flaw I can think of is that the map/mission editor is convoluted but I was never good with those anyway.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>482cc70a-93ff-11e8-bcdf-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Why aren&apos;t you playing it YET!</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/48246024-93ff-11e8-b280-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/48246024-93ff-11e8-b280-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2009-09-08T21:08:18</review:date>
        <review:description>I remember when I first picked this game up. I never heard of it or knew what to expect, but I was immediately wowed. Before it I was a big wing commander fan, but this raised the bar so fricken high that nearly forgot wing commander existed. I still dream of doing bombing runs and panicking with the shield controls and getting that same thrill. I can&apos;t recommend it enough.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>48246024-93ff-11e8-b280-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Incredible Space Flight Sim</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/48266fb4-e9be-11eb-a6bf-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/48266fb4-e9be-11eb-a6bf-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-07-21T03:55:02</review:date>
        <review:description>Its early access in reality.

Feels unfinished, large parts need graphics upgrade esp the character scenes. Very cheaply drawn considering what this world has in terms of technology.

For me, the homing fireball is just a lazy way of solving a problem, how to balance the battles and give the player something to get their teeth into, trouble is, its a game changer, this weapon in the hands of the enemy with precise aiming destroys half your ship, half your crew and half your guns.....seriously, what are they doing ! its just die and try again, et al until you either get lucky or you just end up fighting the boss, his escorts and a couple of ghost ships that appear now and again or even a Navy galleon as well just to make sure you understand that this game is rigged.

Oh, and all you&apos;ve got is a sloop. lol.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>48266fb4-e9be-11eb-a6bf-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>Starts strong then lazy plot creeps in.</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">9</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4854af74-c018-11ec-be3f-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/4854af74-c018-11ec-be3f-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-04-19T22:38:26</review:date>
        <review:description>Мне очень понравился оригинал и теперь продолжение. Из проблем хочу выделить болото, оно очень скучное и медленное. В какой-то момент меня даже посещала мысль бросить игру из-за этого. Из более локальных внутриигровых проблем хотелось бы выделить то, что несмотря на то что можно и узнать скорость противника и местность на которой он скрывается, всё равно часто бывает такое что я знаю на какой клетке противник, я в этом уверен, но никак не могу на это повлиять, хотя бывает важно пройти возле этой клетки не попав в засаду. И по поводу финальной надписи &quot;Продолжение следует&quot;, оно тоже будет через 25 лет?)</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>4854af74-c018-11ec-be3f-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Прекрасно, чудесно! Но...</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/487179ae-9594-11e8-b3c8-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/487179ae-9594-11e8-b3c8-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2015-06-04T18:36:25</review:date>
        <review:description>I want to start with a disclaimer: I didn&apos;t play it since back then, so this is a very basic nostalgia review.

Thus said, i loved this game. From the Multiplayer with realisitc damage mode (aka 1 headshot and you&apos;re dead, which was rather rare back then) to the crime fueled story, to the fact that it didn&apos;t only have &quot;go from start to finish and shoot everything&quot; level design, it was something very special, which only a few other FPS did since then, even up to now.

The only reason why i wouldn&apos;t give it 5 stars is, because I remember it having a lot of &quot;industrial&quot; levels in the later parts, where you had less civilian interaction and it went more towards the classic &quot;shoot everything&quot; approach, with enviroments that are less recognizable from &quot;real world locations&quot;</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>487179ae-9594-11e8-b3c8-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Forgotten classic indeed</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/488e7424-93fe-11e8-9442-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/488e7424-93fe-11e8-9442-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2009-07-10T03:28:56</review:date>
        <review:description>One of the classic RPGs that was highly under rated during its time. Developed by the groups that made Fallout, it had plenty of freedom, unfortuantly unlike Fallout it bottlenecked at specific points in the story line, resulting in difficulty if you had not prepared yourself well enough.

Storyline was excellent and the way history was deviated and warped to fit the story was fascinating if you knew the people and places of Europe during the 16th/17th century. The magical element was also exceptional.

If you like mixing fantasy with history then this is well worth a look at, especially if you want a story line and world that is both unique and fascinating.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>488e7424-93fe-11e8-9442-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Good RPG, bottle necks annoying</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/48965054-6108-11e9-b54b-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/48965054-6108-11e9-b54b-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-04-17T14:59:41</review:date>
        <review:description>The game is good, there are plenty of reviews on its qualities (and drawbacks) already. However, the game as GOG offers it is only half the deal: Stardock has long abondoned selling Crusade as an expansion and bundles it with the base game. GOG does not: instead it requires you to buy the Crusade expansion separately, which isn&apos;t even available anywhere else! 

Effectively, you only get half the game, and because of that, a massively buggy game: Stardock has been releasing tons of updates and fixes, but since they started bundling Crusade with the base game, they no longer appear to be supporting the original base game as much as they used to. This leads to broken technologies, broken race abilities, and massively unbalanced game elements, because everything keeps being changed with disregard to people who do not own the Crusade Expansion.

If you want to play the game and actually have fun with it, you can choose to buy the game here, disable automatic updates, and accept the flawy of the original release, or you can choose to buy Crusade as well - but in that case you&apos;ll get a much better deal at Stardock or Steam.

I&apos;d rate this game at 4 stars, but because I got only half of it, it&apos;s two from me.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>48965054-6108-11e9-b54b-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>GOG only offers half the game!</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">20</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/49a8e562-9a57-11eb-8876-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/49a8e562-9a57-11eb-8876-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-04-11T02:48:45</review:date>
        <review:description>Colony Ship opens with the musical strains of a melancholy western and a main menu that looks like the well-worn cover of a paperback space opera from the 1960s. The menu reveals the subtitle: &quot;A Post Earth Role Playing Game.&quot; From the outset, the game pays homage to a trio of core inspirations: HBO&apos;s Deadwood, Heinlein&apos;s Orphans of the Sky, and Interplay&apos;s Fallout. If you enjoyed any of those works, the question is not whether you should play Colony Ship but when you should play.

CS is about a &quot;generation ship&quot;: a slower-than-light vessel sent, lifetimes ago, from Earth to Proxima Centauri in hopes of establishing a colony at that nearest, yet still vastly distant, star. A generation ship rests on an unusual social compact. The first generation willingly sacrifices for sake of the last generation, who will have a shot at freedom and utopia in a new home. But the intervening generations have no choice and yet bear a sacrifice even greater than the founders&apos;. For them, the Ship is neither Ark nor Mayflower; it&apos;s a prison and pressure-cooker. The game begins after a failed Mutiny has nearly wrecked the Ship and its society.

You are a scavenger eking out an existence in the Pit, a cargo hold converted into shantytown. It&apos;s a perfect starting hub that offers rich opportunities for any character build. The process of creating that character cleverly weaves in the game&apos;s backstory. Gaps in your abilities can be filled by companions. They have their own personalities and values, but as long as your goals and theirs align, they can assist both inside and outside of battle. 

CS is an open game. You immediately have the run of the Pit, and soon add the Hydroponics Lab and the Armory, both full of NPCs, foes, environmental interactions, traps, loot, etc. If you like combat, there&apos;re tactical turn-based battles. If you don&apos;t, there&apos;s stealth, diplomacy, and hacking.

Bottom line: CS combines the heart and soul of a small team with the depth and polish of large developer.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">14</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>49a8e562-9a57-11eb-8876-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>A worthy successor to Age of Decadence</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">65</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/49b859c0-9d26-11ec-933b-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/49b859c0-9d26-11ec-933b-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-03-06T10:20:31</review:date>
        <review:description>Graphiquement le jeu est vraiment pas terrible, les textures sont baveuses voir même d&apos;un autre âge pour certaines. Certes, le paysage est agréable à regarder mais il faut pas regarder de trop près ! 

Just Cause est bourré de problèmes qui rendent l&apos;expérience pénible  : 

- Synchronisation labiale totalement foirée... Enfin quand les personnages ouvrent la bouche pour parler parce que beaucoup semble être doués pour la ventriloquie ;

- Physique qui n&apos;a aucun sens : les véhicules se retournent pour rien (notamment les chars : WTF ?) ; 

- Maniabilité terrible : cela devient même insupportable par moment, on a l’impression de conduire sur de l&apos;huile ;

- Histoire clichée : nucléaire : OK, femme qui met une gifle au héros à leur rencontre : OK, etc. ;

- Quêtes secondaires sans intérêts ;

- Ennemis qui apparaissent en boucle par moment (fainéantise) ;

- Point de contrôle : alors oui, c&apos;est sympa mais quand ça SAUVEGARDE PAS le jeu quand on quitte, ÇA FAIT SUER ;

- Interface des menus imbuvables : impossibilité d&apos;utiliser la souris, obliger d&apos;utiliser les touches fléchées même sur la carte pour zoomer ;

- Peu ou pas d&apos;interaction avec le décor : tirer sur une voiture, aucun impact ; 

- Bugs en tout genre : herbes qui flottent au dessus du sol, passage à travers certains arbres, etc ;

- Pics de difficultés par moment : ça vient de nulle-part et c&apos;est très énervant surtout avec les points de contrôle qui vous oblige à recommencer trop loin. Mention aux hélicoptères qui vous focus même dans la forêt : pire que des moustiques ;

Nous avons deux compagnons : quelle est leur utilité ? A part faire les guignols ? Je me demande d&apos;ailleurs comment ils peuvent être toujours en vie : c&apos;est incroyable qu&apos;ils se soient pas fait butés !

Just Cause est pour moi une déception, ce n&apos;est qu&apos;un jeu parmi tant d&apos;autres dont sa seule originalité est la possibilité de réaliser des cascades. Certes, c&apos;est marrant mais ça n&apos;en fait pas un jeu exceptionnel. </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>49b859c0-9d26-11ec-933b-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:rating>
        <review:title>Plutôt moyen</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/49c7d33a-93fe-11e8-a9f3-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/49c7d33a-93fe-11e8-a9f3-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2009-07-10T11:09:00</review:date>
        <review:description>When I was about 12, my friend showed me a game called freespace. It kicked butt and I was immediately engulfed into the story. A few years later we found out that a true sequal had been made. But for which ever reason, the game was nearly imposable to purchase at a store. Thanks to GoG now I can finally finish what I started so long ago.

But enuf about that. This game is a great title and I would recommend it to anyone. Beautiful explotions, challenging missions, a heart griping story, and easy pickup and play controls make this simple the best space flight sim, ever.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>49c7d33a-93fe-11e8-a9f3-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Best Space Flight Sim, ever</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/49f7e0a4-b54b-11eb-bdb5-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/49f7e0a4-b54b-11eb-bdb5-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-05-15T10:00:53</review:date>
        <review:description>I like this game, especially given that&apos;s been made by one man only and uses a lot of the Flare stuff which I also like. Having spent the last few months playing it occasionally I&apos;ve now gotten to the point of giving it up. It doesn&apos;t work out.

Either I still completely lack the understanding of how the game works or it&apos;s just off-balance. In short, the game is much too difficult, even on the easiest setting.
Even after grinding for weeks (and I&apos;m no stranger to to long grinding sessions) I couldn&apos;t get anywhere. The balance is completely off, your health does regenerate in time but only a small fraction of it and most enemies do much more damage than that. So you need to drink health potions, lot and lots of them, all the time. But there&apos;s a waiting interval between drinking two potions and in most cases that&apos;s enough for an enemy to get you.
I&apos;ve resorted to editing the savefiles to gain hundreds of large healing potions and have to repeat this regularly, but it&apos;s not enough.

At level 24 you&apos;d expect to be able to handle two level 9 or a level 12 enemy, but I&apos;m lucky if I survive a level 7 one and it&apos;s mostly a close call. I tried with several different characters and skillsets but it doesn&apos;t make much difference.

So either I&apos;ve stumbled onto a bug (wouldn&apos;t be the first one), or the game simply doesn&apos;t work with me.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>49f7e0a4-b54b-11eb-bdb5-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:rating>
        <review:title>Balance</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">7</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/496d369e-b27d-11e8-b7e9-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/496d369e-b27d-11e8-b7e9-00163e97122a">
