    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5a2764c0-93f9-11e8-9d1c-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5a2764c0-93f9-11e8-9d1c-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2008-10-02T15:19:11</review:date>
        <review:description>On the one hand, Kingpin is an unusual approach to the FPS that takes place in a bizarre and intriguing anachronistic setting, features the most distinct character design this side of Team Fortress 2, surprisingly good voicework, and maintains a grimy, very memorable atmosphere throughout.

On the other hand, Kingpin is a sloppy and at times transparently half-assed game that never delivers on its promise and eventually descends into an unstructured shooting gallery, one marked by silly boss fights, outrageous difficulty, and enemy behavior that could be most leniently described as complete bullshit.

Yet I can&apos;t help wanting to defend and recommend it, because it&apos;s something different. Even at its cheapest, most derivative moment, Kingpin is more interesting and fun than any number of well-made but run-of-the-mill shooters.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">8</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>5a2764c0-93f9-11e8-9d1c-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Quake Theft Auto</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">89</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5a421cbc-9448-11e8-aa32-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5a421cbc-9448-11e8-aa32-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2012-05-24T09:41:30</review:date>
        <review:description>I know this will be totally biased but to me this is the best space combat game in existence. It has such a variation in its missions and its so much fun flying around and dog fighting amongst the flak and beams of capital ships. Or trying to navigate through a nebula full of enemies who you cant see until they are right on top of you. The story line is epic with twists and turns and just when you think your safe your thrust into the epic finale of missions to defend Galactic Terran-Vasudan Space from the Destroyers (Shivans)

The environment is gorgeous and for those who are really crazy about graphics if you download FS_open from Hardlight.net there are updates to the graphics and numerous other things, there are also mod tools and a multitude of player made campaigns.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>5a421cbc-9448-11e8-aa32-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Aliens Beware!</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5a4cf186-93f9-11e8-aa39-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5a4cf186-93f9-11e8-aa39-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2008-12-07T02:29:29</review:date>
        <review:description>the reason i give this three stars is for the expansion. I am going to be very clear about this. The expansion SUCKS! as for the main freespace campaign, its good but not as good as Freespace 2. The last level is a bit over the top in my opinion and the difficulty was too high on normal ( i dont like playing on easy). So i give the main campaign a 4/5 while i give the expansion a -4.5 out of 5 (notice the negative symbol). For 6 dollars this game is definitely worth it.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">7</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>5a4cf186-93f9-11e8-aa39-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:rating>
        <review:title>Stars are for the expansion</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5a4e217a-ca13-11eb-8bbb-fa163e31363f -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5a4e217a-ca13-11eb-8bbb-fa163e31363f">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-06-10T20:43:23</review:date>
        <review:description>Игра мне не понравилась, в отличие от музыки. Захотел купить только OST - нет, просто так нельзя. Чтобы купить музыку (совершенно отдельные от игры файлы), в библиотеке должна быть игра...
OK, CDPR. Музыка у меня теперь все равно есть, но мои деньги вам не достались...
</review:description>
