    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5a5487c0-93f9-11e8-9762-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5a5487c0-93f9-11e8-9762-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2008-10-04T10:58:18</review:date>
        <review:description>Look, Freespace 2 is the greatest Space Sim ever made, and that includes Tie Fighter.  But it definitely has aged over the years.  So for everyone getting ahold of this game through GOG, give the SCP project at Hard Light Productions a look.  Not only will you get superior graphics, you&apos;ll also find dozens of high-quality fan-made campaigns, some with complete voiceacting.  Freespace 2 is a gift that keeps on giving.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>5a5487c0-93f9-11e8-9762-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Something every FS2 owner should know</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">14</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5a5a26b8-8005-11ea-bb96-fa163e62c76a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5a5a26b8-8005-11ea-bb96-fa163e62c76a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-04-16T20:11:46</review:date>
        <review:description>The first Evil Within is one of the worst survival horror games of all time. The only reason I can say I am glad it exists is because we don&apos;t really get survival horror games anymore.
I beat this game on steam when it came out. I think it&apos;s better in the mechanics department than the first game. The open world gives you a feeling of space in a weird way that works for this game. Like the first game, though, this game is incredibly not scary. It&apos;s so not scary that it&apos;s scary how not scary these games are. It&apos;s almost like they don&apos;t really want them to be so babies who don&apos;t play scary games because they&apos;re too scary will play them.
The first game had fights straight out of Naked Gun where you just run around a pole 50 times and shoot a thing with your gun until it dies. it&apos;s the silliest thing ever. This one thankfully doesn&apos;t have that problem. Again, mechanically this game is leaps and bounds better than the first- so it feels good to kill the incredibly not scary monsters in it.
The monster designs are decently generic- none of which hold a candle to Silent Hill but really really want to.
The story is slightly better only mainly because it&apos;s much less a focal point. This game is open world so you kind of open up missions by finding them with the radio. It&apos;s a neat idea, but it means if you think the story is dumb don&apos;t worry there&apos;s another one over there you might like. This was smart given how much of a rip off the story is. Don&apos;t think I&apos;m just saying that- Shinji Mikami was very open that he is ripping off Inception with the first game, and he still is here. I think he does it better this time than he did in the first one.
I don&apos;t think Shinji Mikami is a very good video game developer. Resident Evil 4 was bad and The Evil Within was bad. At least with this one it has good mechanics- so it feels good to kill the monsters unlike in those two awful games. So get this one and skip those. Saves you money.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">117</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>5a5a26b8-8005-11ea-bb96-fa163e62c76a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:rating>
        <review:title>A deeply flawed rip off</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">17</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5a659cc8-9b6c-11ea-95ff-fa163e93294d -->

