    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5a7c2d0a-cfba-11e8-a0f2-00163e4e60cc -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5a7c2d0a-cfba-11e8-a0f2-00163e4e60cc">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2018-10-14T17:06:32</review:date>
        <review:description>In the contrary to the other review on this page, i can confirm, that you can complete level 7 just fine. I downloaded the game on the same day it released on GOG and i had no issues completing level 7 (i am currently in level 15 - infernal machine).

The game itself is wonderful as it was on release. My xbox controller is recognized by default, which helps a little with the clunky controlls of the game. But if you can get over this you are in for a misterious adventure through a lot of unique and fun locations. if i compare the two 3d indiana jones games on pc, the emperors tomb may have better controlls and graphics but the infernal machine hast a lot more indiana jones feeling too it and is imho the better game of the two.

can recommend the game for any indiana jones or tomb raider fan.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>5a7c2d0a-cfba-11e8-a0f2-00163e4e60cc</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>GOG Version is completly playable</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">146</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


