    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5b12e7be-9468-11e8-ac6b-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5b12e7be-9468-11e8-ac6b-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2011-05-30T12:04:52</review:date>
        <review:description>This game is incredible! Gameplay is fantastic and the storyline is top notch! You must play this game! Actually, because the story is a continuation from Freespace: The Great War, play that first. Then play this game!
Also, be sure to check out the graphical enhancements freely available with the FS_Open mod and all of the great fan built campaigns. Go to www.hard-light.net and use the installer package they provide. It will give you fantastic graphical updates and dozens of hours worth of quality campaigns.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>5b12e7be-9468-11e8-ac6b-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Absolute must have!</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5b46daee-9448-11e8-b040-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5b46daee-9448-11e8-b040-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2010-09-25T10:27:23</review:date>
        <review:description>The developers tore out the native coop mode that all Quake2 engine games had built-in (probably due to rushing for deadline) but a friend and I wrote a mod to add it back in.

http://downloads.kingpinforever.com/mods/Co-op_Mod/

The one we wrote is in the &quot;Old_Coop_Mod&quot; subdirectory there (ours was done in 2002) - somebody has apparently revamped it a bit and upped the player limit from 4 to 9. (And removed friendly fire? Huh. Well, I guess some people like that.)

But our version came with Linux binaries and source as well and the new one doesn&apos;t do Linux - nor the source code to show his changes...  :(</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>5b46daee-9448-11e8-b040-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Coop mode</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


