    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5b5f7eac-2994-11ec-a0af-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5b5f7eac-2994-11ec-a0af-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-10-10T09:36:10</review:date>
        <review:description>This is a game that splits the waters. Either you enjoy the micromanaging or you find it tedious.
Either you enjoy adapting to the hundred small things that can (and will) go wrong, or you find them distracting from getting to play the actual game.

Personally I almost love this game, but having to mod it in order for it to be fun is a pain.
The expansion is almost the opposite of what I wanted in the game.

TL;DR Not my cup of tea, but there&apos;s clearly something here to enjoy for a lot of players.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:downvotes>
