        <review:title>Nostalgia</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">11</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5c9189ee-e140-11e9-8260-029c9a0e1f51 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5c9189ee-e140-11e9-8260-029c9a0e1f51">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-09-27T16:03:35</review:date>
        <review:description>The little movie ran fine (albeit low resolution) and then the game crashed while apparently trying to change Win/my monitor&apos;s resolution (from 1920x1080 to 800x600, maybe?) - I dunno. I had to evoke Task Manager to exit the game. Might look fine on a legacy system. Got it free from GOG, so no win no loss. </review:description>
