    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5dd17f20-93f9-11e8-ad42-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5dd17f20-93f9-11e8-ad42-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2008-10-06T17:49:44</review:date>
        <review:description>I have never played space sims. I only played arcade style ship games like Rogue Squadron and Crimson Skies. So I did not know what to expect from Freespace. By reading the reviews I decided to get it and I must tell you I&apos;m glad I did. The game is quite captivating, you feel like you&apos;re part of the war. Also you do feel the scale of the world when you are next to a command ship and parts where everyone is shooting at each other. So if you only played arcade shooters give this one a try there is plenty of action and maybe will get you into this type of space sims.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>5dd17f20-93f9-11e8-ad42-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>In space no one can hear you click.</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">10</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5dfa4c9e-8222-11e9-8cd7-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5dfa4c9e-8222-11e9-8cd7-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-05-29T17:59:32</review:date>
        <review:description>I&apos;ve hardly played more than one hour, but my first impression is... pretty bad.
First, the game is slow: you can run in town but not outside, there is a bit of text that doesn&apos;t print fast enough for my taste (though I have to admit that amything that isn&apos;t instant isn&apos;t far enough for me), and the combat animations are slowish.
And the combat itself doesn&apos;t sound interesting: it&apos;s basically Darkest Dungeon, but with neither the choice of skill (every character has only a normal attack and a special once they can use every so often)  nor the importance of placement (or at least, it&apos;s a very basic one).
I will give it another shot tomorrow, but had I bought it on another store, I would have asked a refund. </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">22</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>5dfa4c9e-8222-11e9-8cd7-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>First impression: slow and uninteresting</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">23</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5e197086-94cc-11e8-a75d-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5e197086-94cc-11e8-a75d-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2013-10-24T17:39:06</review:date>
        <review:description>I grew up an avid, AVID fan of the Wing Commander series for just about every reason you could think of.  Then I played the first Freespace game.  Wow.  I was blown away.  I still liked Wing Commander, but for different reasons, but Freespace was amazing, for the same reasons other reviews have mentioned.

Then Freespace 2 came out.  It would take a lot to top the first one, with its incredible story and epic battle sequences.  Well, it did just that, except for maybe the story (more on that later).  FS2 was just jaw-dropping.  After I had installed it form GoG YEARS later, I was actually STILL impressed with the graphics, the immersive feeling this game gives of space, the sounds, and just about everything else.  This is truly a timeless game.

Now about the storyline:  *SPOILERS*  I really felt like this game was part two of a trilogy, and they never made a third.  It ends on a pretty depressing note.  At first I thought I had messed something up with earlier missions, but no:  It really does end with a bunch of ships being wiped out...and the story ends.  It *definitely* feels like they intended a part three. *END SPOILERS*  But all of this in NO way would contribute to me lowering this game from the highest rating.  Everything else is almost flawless.

The bottom line:  If you have never played a game from the space combat genre (an unfortunately dying/dead genre), but are worried of wasting your time, play this.  If you hate this, then I couldn&apos;t think of one that you&apos;d like.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>5e197086-94cc-11e8-a75d-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>No Space Combat Rival</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5e2459f2-93f9-11e8-a7ec-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5e2459f2-93f9-11e8-a7ec-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2008-10-05T18:55:59</review:date>
        <review:description>Just an amazing space sim. No - Physics isn&apos;t fully obeyed, there&apos;s not a million and one functions needed to perform - but it&apos;s an immersive story from start to finish. You&apos;re part of an armada, and no you don&apos;t get to pilot capitol ships, yet you&apos;re able to make the difference each time targeting key areas of enemy ships, or scanning areas and leading other squadrons and special ops missions. Like halflife 2 which has a story unwind before you as you play, Freespace 2 matches it as your squadmates or commander add their bit over the ships radio. Get some nice headphones, check out the spruced up scp mods for better graphics, and enjoy.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>5e2459f2-93f9-11e8-a7ec-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>The defining moment in space sim history</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5e2fca7e-6108-11eb-8949-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5e2fca7e-6108-11eb-8949-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-01-28T03:30:13</review:date>
        <review:description>I&apos;ve actually been waiting for this game to release for quite a while, and now that I&apos;ve played it for several hours, I can safely say that it&apos;s okay. It starts out a bit frustrating, but keeps a steady pace the the next several levels. The bosses are pretty enjoyable and range from challenging to rage inducing. I cam currently stuck on a boss that I&apos;ve literally tried to beat more than 20 times (I had to walk away for the sake of my controller remaining intact). Overall the game is very enjoyable and plays similarly to other platformers like Mega Man, Shovel Knight, Metroid and Castlevania. Keep in mind that this is NOT a Metroidvania, but rather a platformer. It does borrow elements from various other games in this genre but it still manages to stay original in it&apos;s own right. It&apos;s definitely worth picking up for the price.  </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>5e2fca7e-6108-11eb-8949-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Solid Four Stars. No More</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">18</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5e3af538-1673-11ea-86b7-00163e4e60cc -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5e3af538-1673-11ea-86b7-00163e4e60cc">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-12-04T10:52:14</review:date>
        <review:description>I first played this back in 2000 when I was 17 or 18. It didn&apos;t look particularly revolutionary, even seemed downright childish. But I was a big Indy fan at the time and figured I&apos;d give it a whirl. Despite its clunky controls and cartoonish graphics, it was surprisingly engrossing, with emaculate level design, a wide-ranging variety of environments, excellent puzzles, and a fun story. It wound up being one of my favorite games from that time period.

My jaw dropped when I saw it on GOG. I figured it was probably unplayable by today&apos;s standards, but I was curious enough to see for myself. Wound up playing through the whole game in like two sittings. It&apos;s still so good! 

Comparatively, I recently played Tomb Raider 2, which I also remember loving as a teenager. I figured if the Infernal Machine somehow held up so well, maybe same-era Tomb Raider would too. And yet I found the latter to be truly unplayable. I couldn&apos;t even make it through the first level before giving up in frustration.

Not sure what set the two games apart, as they&apos;re nearly identical twins, aesthetically and mechanically. Perhaps its just the IP? The nostalgia? I don&apos;t know. All I know is this game&apos;s just got &quot;it&quot;.  There&apos;s something magical holding it together. It works, and it works well. Just as good of an installment as any of the films. So glad to have it back.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>5e3af538-1673-11ea-86b7-00163e4e60cc</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Severely Underrated</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">8</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5e53737a-b1c4-11e8-81a5-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5e53737a-b1c4-11e8-81a5-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2016-06-23T17:58:25</review:date>
        <review:description>I remember playing this on a Compaq Persario 2240, i saved up and bought a brand new Voodoo3 2000 PCI gpu and the game got even better, yeah that&apos;s how old i am, now fast forward to 2016, i still love playing this game (have it on Steam).

I Love this game, the controls are awesome and very intuitive, the graphics, for its time, are freaking awesome, the story is SICK AF, specially the 1st time you see the C........... sorry no spoilers here.

i will add this, i suggest you mod it to bring it up a notch, took me months of trying to learn how to mod, and fail, till i came across this gem
http://www.fsoinstaller.com/
simple installer, though does take a while due to size of some mods and your speed, it even includes a story where you play prior to the great war against an ancient race that has some sexy asp ships, if you do get stuck modding the community around fso installer are really helpful and some are super patient with noobs like me.

will i ever stop playing this game, nope, because i suck but want all the medals.
will i force my kids to play this, you bet your bottom dollar i will
will my kids force their kids to play this, they better or else &quot;that&apos;s a paddlin&quot;</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>5e53737a-b1c4-11e8-81a5-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Had it before, got it again</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">7</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5e871e98-ff5e-11ea-96a0-fa163e7ab9c9 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5e871e98-ff5e-11ea-96a0-fa163e7ab9c9">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-09-25T21:38:56</review:date>
        <review:description>Addicting game that&apos;s easy to jump in and out of for a few runs. Uninspired enemies, a poorly implemented shotgun and visuals that obscure envrionmental rewards aren&apos;t enough to hold it back for me. I would like to see them improve on what they have made here, but that won&apos;t happen unless we give them our support. </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>5e871e98-ff5e-11ea-96a0-fa163e7ab9c9</review:id>
