    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5eca4c6c-6260-11eb-8ccc-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5eca4c6c-6260-11eb-8ccc-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-01-29T20:32:41</review:date>
        <review:description>This game is quick, short and fun.  Once you master drifting through an S turn and hitting a slipstream (8 minutes max) the game becomes EASY but that&apos;s ok.  There are a few different modes of gameplay in both single player and 2-4 Couch co-op.  PS4 controller support is nice as it feels tighter with a D-pad. No GOG achievements, No Online multiplayer and there is a bug with the slipstream mechanic where the opponent you are racing can accelerate with you on your own slipstream if they are on the screen and not ahead of your front bumper, that last one is the only challenge in the game.  There is a hard mode if normal gets easy.   

I feel the strength in this game is 4 player couch co-op.  You can spend 10 minutes or an hour.  The fast moving road colour changes can mess with you, if there where a way to blend them more so it wasn&apos;t so contrast it would be more enjoyable.  
Very reminiscent of Sega games from CD→Saturn era of time.  For a $12 game, 9/10 .  Well done.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>5eca4c6c-6260-11eb-8ccc-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Fun Drifter</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5f2d2a94-e21e-11e9-9270-16c7e410d44a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5f2d2a94-e21e-11e9-9270-16c7e410d44a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-09-28T18:32:48</review:date>
        <review:description>Where to begin... wow, freespace! it was such an exciting game to play. played the first and could not wait to get the second. everything about it was EPIC! the story is awesome, the graphics and scale of battles, ships were insane! I loved jumping in the editor and create huge battles :-)
Figthers feel agile and you can execute some really cool manuvers and tactics. bigger ships are so freakin... well, big!

Oh, and there&apos;s plenty of mods out there after you&apos;re done with vanilla.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>5f2d2a94-e21e-11e9-9270-16c7e410d44a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Top dog of spacesims</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


