    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/51b39e24-1851-11eb-b4cd-fa163e41fb2f -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/51b39e24-1851-11eb-b4cd-fa163e41fb2f">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-10-27T14:38:30</review:date>
        <review:description>I don&apos;t remember the last time I had so much fun with a 3D platformer.
Amazing game and look beautiful! love the artstyle!
just a few things that bothered me:
1) On the ferry , sometimes when I die and spawn on the boat I insta-die, then respawn and contine as usual.
2) On one of the ghost horseriding parts, FPS dropped to below 5 for a few seconds which made me lose because I crashed into a wall. happened around 5 times until I managed to pass that part. other than this specific part, smooth 144FPS 2560X1440 gameplay. Locking to lower FPS did not solve the problem. (R9, RTX 2080, 32GB RAM)
3) Change to &quot;leave a rating on GOG&quot; or just ask for rating and don&apos;t specify the platform.
4) We will highly appreciate achievements here as well.
Other than that, I had a blast! </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>51b39e24-1851-11eb-b4cd-fa163e41fb2f</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>I love it!</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


