    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/523f7262-0197-11eb-9299-fa163e7ab9c9 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/523f7262-0197-11eb-9299-fa163e7ab9c9">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-09-28T17:31:39</review:date>
        <review:description>I don&apos;t have a problem with Northgard. I have a problem with this version of Northgard, for sale on gog.com.

I&apos;m a Linux user. This is a native Linux game, which makes me very happy (Shiro Games, thank you for supporting my platform. I&apos;m about to say some slightly mean things, but other than not properly notifying me of this issue on your store page, you didn&apos;t do anything wrong here, and I&apos;m really really glad you made a port for the Linux community. For most developers, Linux ports aren&apos;t financially beneficial, so I fully understand that about 90% of the ports we get are acts of charity or shows of support from developers, and I am extremely thankful).

HOWEVER. GOG Galaxy doesn&apos;t support Linux. At all (because CDPR are many good things, but they have never, ever cared about Linux as a platform and their actions have continually made that clear). And substantial portions of this game&apos;s content (multiplayer modes) REQUIRES the use of GOG Galaxy. For a lot of people, this won&apos;t be an issue, but for Linux users, this means that this version of the game is essentially a rip-off: You&apos;re paying the same $30 that you would pay on Steam for about half of the game (and since multiplayer is such a big part of RTS, arguably less than that). The GOG store page won&apos;t warn you about this, so it&apos;s only when you attempt to PLAY the game that you&apos;ll learn you got screwed.

As such, the degree to which I like Northgard is immaterial. This version of Northgard, at least for users like me, is irredeemable, and I can only endorse buying Northgard on another storefront, like Steam. I recognize that for many users this won&apos;t be the case, but I can only review based on my on experience.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">16</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>523f7262-0197-11eb-9299-fa163e7ab9c9</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:rating>
        <review:title>If only it bloody worked (Linux)</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">29</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


