    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/527722e2-aa0d-11eb-bd0b-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/527722e2-aa0d-11eb-bd0b-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-05-01T02:39:35</review:date>
        <review:description>After playing through the first level and a bit of the start of the second level, I had to just quit the game because it was just bland and boring. I&apos;m sure someone would find this game interesting; simply put, this game isn&apos;t worth the 5-stars some of these reviewers are giving it. I don&apos;t know what the &apos;message&apos; they are trying to go for with this because I couldn&apos;t even get into the GAMEPLAY which is clearly lacking. I genuinely enjoy Beat &apos;Em Ups, but this just isn&apos;t a good one.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">74</review:downvotes>
