    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/53bb1a2c-1f2a-11ec-b192-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/53bb1a2c-1f2a-11ec-b192-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-09-27T03:31:59</review:date>
        <review:description>Better than the messenger.
Better than ninja gaiden.
Wall jumping and flash jumping off floating doo-hickeys are gimmicky bullshit.
Unless it is offering me new ways to hack and slash, it&apos;s just not helping the core gameplay.
This plays like a Ninja Gaiden 1 with less annoying sticking to the wall when you don&apos;t want to.
At first I was unhappy I couldn&apos;t duck, but the enemy projectiles are easy to read an it makes the crouch un-needed, similar to the fact that megaman never ducked back in the day.
I am however missing a dash or slide, but that will be one of the power ups I&apos;m sure.
So far, found a bunch of secrets and had a run in with a memory that made my character vomit up cyber spew.  GREAT ! ! !

Don&apos;t believe the other people. This thing is 5 stars if you&apos;re a 2D platformer connoiseur.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>53bb1a2c-1f2a-11ec-b192-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Freaking Awesome!</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/53c0c144-93f9-11e8-bca0-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/53c0c144-93f9-11e8-bca0-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2008-09-28T18:44:13</review:date>
        <review:description>Absolutely perfect, awesome soundtrack, fast action, exceptional challenges, great puzzles, stunning graphics. Every from 6 loooong levels are completely different and fascinating.

I played MDK about 100x times, so I know better than you! 

Later MDK2 wasnt so perfect.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>53c0c144-93f9-11e8-bca0-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>best game ever 10/10</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">11</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/53d3f148-4d57-11e9-bdcd-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/53d3f148-4d57-11e9-bdcd-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-03-23T12:35:07</review:date>
        <review:description>The campaign is extremely weak, consisting of a short series of puzzle-like missions in which the player *has* to solve each one the way the mission designer envisaged it, otherwise failure becomes a certainty. Similar to the main game, each mission has an artificial turn limit set frustratingly low, enough to suppress any attempt at creativity or enjoyment outside the one and only way the mission is supposed to be played and won. Consistent with the limited production value of the whole add-on, the unit roster is severely limited with very few new units to choose from and deploy. 

The final nail in the coffin is the game-crashing bug at the end of mission 6 &apos;We&apos;ve run into a bit of a delay&apos; which prevents the campaign from advancing; the error message lists &apos;invalid vector  subscript (0)&apos;, &apos;Struct exception with code 0x80000003 (0)&apos; as the source of the problem, whatever that means.

To be avoided.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>53d3f148-4d57-11e9-bdcd-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:rating>
        <review:title>Sub-par add-on</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">17</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/53db1958-6315-11ea-8e85-fa163e62c76a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/53db1958-6315-11ea-8e85-fa163e62c76a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-03-10T23:23:04</review:date>
        <review:description>I have to be honest, at first I didn&apos;t think that this game is something for me.

An idle game with story, seems like a strange combination.

BUT! If you give the game some time, it sucks you right in. Even though everything takes a lot of time, you have always something to wait for. The timer in the game runs even if you&apos;re not in the game. So if you have to wait for something that takes a week, you can go back into the game after a week.

The whole atmosphere and concept of the game oozes with compassion for a new and definitely unique experience. 

Of course, if you&apos;re impatient this might be the wrong game for you. But if you want to experience something really special, give this game a try!
</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>53db1958-6315-11ea-8e85-fa163e62c76a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>A Pleasant Surprise</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">46</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/53e11798-5ded-11ec-82f7-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/53e11798-5ded-11ec-82f7-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-12-15T23:24:03</review:date>
        <review:description>This isn&apos;t a bad game, but I don&apos;t understand where all the excess hype for it comes from. I know from experience how tempting it is to get excited for this game when you look at screenshots and videos, and read all the glowing reviews. 

...But actually playing it reveals a more anemic experience than it should be, with highly derivative and repetitive quests, boring characters, dodgy camera limitations, and shallow world interactivity for a game of its ilk. So despite the generous size of the world and numerous quests, everything quickly starts to feel &apos;samey&apos; and derivative, leaving you fatigued with boredom before you get anywhere near done with the campaign.

The combat is also more shallow and repetitive than it at first seems to be, and gets old just as quickly as everything else. On top of this, the game commits the unforgivable sin of enabling every enemy attack with a very fast &apos;home in&apos; effect on the player. This creates a ridiculously frustrating experience of constantly being stun-juggled out of combos all the freaking time. Yes, you can block, but that means you&apos;re always playing a tedious turtle game rather than justifying the more exciting combo options provided.

A lot of the above complaints are probably due to the fact that the original framework of the game was purportedly built to be an MMO, but got converted to a single-player experience at some point in development. But that knowledge doesn&apos;t negate the diminished enjoyment these issues bring against the overall experience.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>53e11798-5ded-11ec-82f7-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:rating>
        <review:title>Fun in general but overstays its welcome</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/53e3b740-9470-11e8-a24a-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/53e3b740-9470-11e8-a24a-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2011-07-03T14:11:16</review:date>
        <review:description>Makes me wish for a return or exchange policy, even at the cut-rate price I paid.
I was really hoping for more humor and puzzles out of Shiny.  This really plays like an early and uncertain FPS.  You&apos;ll want to remap the controls to something more standard, but even then don&apos;t expect the same response as a modern FPS.
You&apos;re often overwhelmed by rooms full of enemies as powerful or more so than yourself, and your only hope is to keep jumping from body to body, trying to get behind enemies without being turned into a game of &apos;kick the baby&apos;.  So far I haven&apos;t encountered any humor, other than the intro where some game developer argues with his 6 year old, which doesn&apos;t hold up well.
I&apos;ve played worse games, but rarely paid for them.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>53e3b740-9470-11e8-a24a-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>Meh-siah</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/53fc10f4-e97a-11ea-ab31-fa163e93294d -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/53fc10f4-e97a-11ea-ab31-fa163e93294d">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-08-29T01:03:39</review:date>
        <review:description>Я прошел «The Evil Within 2» и это было классно. Я давно не получал такого удовольствия, хоть и не сверх яркого. Даже как-то жаль, что продолжительное время оставлял игру на потом и только сейчас умудрился её вытащить из бэклога.

Весьма трогательная и красивая история с приятным дизайном говорящих персонажей. Но не скажу, что именно сюжет оказался для меня главным блюдом. Хотя вот постановка многих моментов тут просто потрясающая. Например, погружение в прошлое или путешествие между терминала сети. Но по большей мере Я остался доволен именно игровым процессом. Прогулки на корточках по кустам в здешних полуоткрытых локациях провинциального городка в поисках припасов и забав на свою пятую точку, с уклоном на незаметное и экономное устранение не особо запоминающихся и однообразных противников оставило самые приятные впечатления. А ещё кофе и холодная, но очаровательная Татьяна в сейфхаусах. Именно на эти сегменты у меня и пришлась большая часть веселья. К сожалению, каждый раз, когда игра прерывала подобные моменты и вынуждала прибегать к открытому бою оставались довольно неприятные впечатления. Хотя в целом боёвка тут соответствующая жанру и более-менее удобоваримая. Управление отзывчивое и приятное. Но мне не хватало возможности переназначить кнопки на геймпаде, хоть и имеющие раскладки вполне удобные и понятные.

Остался дико не удовлетворен здешним дизайном врагов и некоторых локаций. Да и анимации в игре периодически сходили с ума и ломались, что оставляло не лучшие впечатления. Хотя большая часть окружения и редизайн действующих лиц оставили меня довольным, особенно Кидман. В целом, игру Я так и характеризую – вполне уютной, с парой провисающих аспектов. Ну и печалит, что некоторые весьма конкретные намеки так и не получили продолжение в виде DLC или стенд-алона. Но, видимо, “успешные” продажи внесли свою коррективу. А пока есть соблазн пройти её на «New Game+» и сложности «Nightmare», да выбить часть оставшихся ачивок.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>53fc10f4-e97a-11ea-ab31-fa163e93294d</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Уюный Сурваил Экшен, но с Огрехами</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/531fcc90-d986-11ec-9b88-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/531fcc90-d986-11ec-9b88-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-05-22T07:19:08</review:date>
        <review:description>As an old player of Heroes of Might and Magic 3 (HOMM3), I was really excited about this game, but after playing part of the first campaign, I have to set it aside until it&apos;s out of early access to see if has matured enough to capture the magic.

The innovation that you only start getting mana at the start of a battle (combined with the limits on the number of units in stacks) makes the battles more interesting. The fact that there are no longer spells on the strategic map also helps. Now your position on the map and the defensibility of your cities actually matters.

But that leads to the bad stuff: The towns don&apos;t have a unified screen for buildings and upgrades, and not one for troops either, unless you have a visiting hero. The build sites are interesting in principle, but I can&apos;t even see what I&apos;ve already built when considering what to build, and I can&apos;t see which small buildings are prerequisites for larger buildings until I want to build the larger building, in a separate menu for a medium or large building site. The game really needs a unified town menu with clearly marked upgrade paths. I still have no idea how to build walls around my town.

The pixelated art is fun enough, but it&apos;s so heavily pixelated that I have trouble telling units apart, especially base units and their upgrades. On the strategy map, the goodies are hard to tell apart, and it&apos;s not clear which ones you&apos;ve already visited. If the graphics resolution were doubled, that should take care of the problem, but for now I need to spend an unnecessary amount of time squinting at units.

In general, the UI just needs a lot more work. In battle, you get a list of the statuses affecting a unit when you click on it, but you can&apos;t get the details of what that effect does anywhere that I can find.

In summary, I&apos;m putting the game away for now and hoping that it will in time become as good as it could be.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>531fcc90-d986-11ec-9b88-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:rating>
        <review:title>I really want to like this game more</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">23</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/534ca458-70a6-11eb-8ff6-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/534ca458-70a6-11eb-8ff6-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-02-17T00:28:42</review:date>
        <review:description>Great platformer with a variety of maps. It was my first platformer after many, many years that i&apos;ve played. I got some donkey kong vibes out of it. Difficulty is rather low, i would have liked it on crash bandicoot n sane trilogy levels or maybe rayman. It ramps up after levels 3-1 but it&apos;s still fairly easy. . Secrets are not that hard to spot as those on the above mentioned games either. Maybe the target group is a younger audience than myself. As a mid 30s gamer this was a refreshing break from my main game and i really enjoyed it.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>534ca458-70a6-11eb-8ff6-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Great platformer</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">30</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5347b7dc-dd32-11ec-8bde-fa163e99870e -->

