    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5362aed8-9444-11e8-ad4a-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5362aed8-9444-11e8-ad4a-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2011-04-10T15:45:43</review:date>
        <review:description>This won several Game of the Year Awards for a reason. Even by today&apos;s standards, this game leaves little to be desired. Other than some of the giant ships having that &quot;wallpapered&quot; detail look (but hey, this was made in like 1998 or something), this game has an easy-to-follow and outstanding storyline, fantastic gameplay, and lots of thing to customize, including HUD and the layout for your weapons and ships. There are tons of awesome controls that will take you a while to master, but it is still easily playable with just some basic targeting and movement controls they teach you in the training. For a measly six bucks, this game is the best game I&apos;ve ever bought (well, Freespace 2 is equally awesome) And if that isn&apos;t enough for you, you can download the Freespace Open Installer for free, which uber enhances all the details and effects in the game. There are alos tons of free mods and extra missions online. Like I said, this is, in my book, the best game of all time, and will be for a long time to come. (plus, you don&apos;t have to have a very good computer to play this; pretty much anything under ten years old should be fine!)</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>5362aed8-9444-11e8-ad4a-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Epic!</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


