    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5948732e-a187-11ec-b973-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5948732e-a187-11ec-b973-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-03-12T00:05:23</review:date>
        <review:description>Je l&apos;avais acheté vu que c&apos;était en promo en même temps que le jeu. J&apos;ai bien aimé les musiques du jeu, elles sont de qualité permettent de bien ressentir l&apos;ambiance des lieux traversés. Les morceaux dépassent rarement les 2 minutes malheureusement, même si en jeu ce n&apos;est pas notable.
Cet OST est limité à 60 musiques par &quot;limite technique&quot;. La version physique tient sur 2 CD, ceci est uniquement le &quot;Side A&quot; qui est acheté.
La &quot;Side B&quot; est disponible sur internet (soundcloud/youtube...) et contient des musiques inutilisées, une musique qui est plus une ambiance inquiétante dans une certaine zone du jeu, et des minis musiques comme celle jouée quand on bat un boss.
Dommage de ne pas avoir inclus le Side B qui donne une impression d&apos;incomplet, et encore le Side B pourrait avoir les petites musiques qui jouent quand on joue les morceaux à la flute, 2 sont présentent ici (dans le Side A) et une dans le Side B mais il en manque encore 3...
I buyed it since it was on sale with the game. I really liked the music of this game, they are of good quality and allow us to feel the ambiance of the places we&apos;re passing by. Unfortunately , the tracks are rarely over 2 minutes, even if in-game it&apos;s not noticeable.
This OST is limited to 60 tracks due to a &quot;technical limit&quot;. The physical version is on 2 CD, here you buy only the Side A.
The side B is avilable on internet (soundcloud/youtube...) and have unused tracks, one focused on having a worrying ambience in a certain area of the game, and small tracks like the one that plays when you defeat a boss.
It&apos;s a shame that the Side B isn&apos;t included, and yet the Side B could have the musics that plays when you play a song scroll with the flute, 2 are present in the Side A, an other in the Side B but there&apos;s still 3 musics missing...</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>5948732e-a187-11ec-b973-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Bonne OST, mais qui n&apos;a que le Side A...</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5982d25a-33c4-11e9-a570-00163e4e60cc -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/5982d25a-33c4-11e9-a570-00163e4e60cc">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-02-18T23:30:01</review:date>
        <review:description>What made me to uninstall the game:

1. Awkward controls (I don&apos;t have a game pad, unfortunately), so keyboard is real clumsy, even with redefining controls. Didn&apos;t have trouble with Escape Goat 2, for instance.
2. Whatever difficulty level I took, I got killed by 3 hits, ouch. Which would have been fine, except for the 3 and 5 (see below).
3. The enemies&apos; missiles collision detection is ridiculous, meaning the area of effect is huge and too much troubles to avoid them, when you are not sure where the boundaries of a missile are.
4. Sounds are ridiculous and annoying, especially of enemies.
5. Check points... are just plain stupid these days. Avoid at all costs.
6. Graphics... can I get it even more pixelated and indistinct? Nope. Even old SNES and DOS games we re much more detailed.

What&apos;s good about the game? I don&apos;t know, nothing comes to my mind. Not sure why the game has 4.5 score, really. Honestly tried to give it a go for several times, but nope, not wasting my time.

Giving it 2 stars, just for the work the developers did.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">11</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>5982d25a-33c4-11e9-a570-00163e4e60cc</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>Why does this game have 4.5?</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">7</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/6a17fff6-93fa-11e8-910c-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/6a17fff6-93fa-11e8-910c-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2008-11-04T09:55:15</review:date>
        <review:description>Freespace 2 (1999) is becoming an oldie, but i have to say, it still up there with the best. An amazing story, extremely well designed gameplay and music that gives you goosebumps. This game has it all. And for 5.99$ this game is a steal.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>6a17fff6-93fa-11e8-910c-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>One of the best?</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/6a1ad0a0-f888-11eb-8e56-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/6a1ad0a0-f888-11eb-8e56-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-08-08T23:37:14</review:date>
        <review:description>A game world that is held up by it&apos;s unusual mythology and the developer&apos;s commitment to it.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
