    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/6a7cd944-b4f8-11ec-90b5-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/6a7cd944-b4f8-11ec-90b5-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-04-05T18:52:37</review:date>
        <review:description>Tolles Spiel, welches die Intelligenz des Spielers fordert. Ich finde, fast alle Schicksale lassen sich logisch erschließen, bei einigen wenigen, muss man dann ein wenig raten. Stil und Gameplay finde ich bemerkenswert gut und simpel zu gleich. Die Geschichte fällt ein wenig ab, da sie mir eher unzusammenhängend, ohne größeren Bogen, erscheint. Das Spiel hat mich auf jeden Fall die ganze Zeit über bei Laune gehalten, so dass ich unbedingt alle Schicksale entschlüsseln wollte.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>6a7cd944-b4f8-11ec-90b5-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Ist kreativ und fordert den Spieler</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/6abae306-94f9-11e8-a328-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/6abae306-94f9-11e8-a328-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2013-06-16T17:15:49</review:date>
        <review:description>The problem with this game is that you never (!) fight on your own but always as part of a fleet. At first sight this might seem to be a good thing, as it is the more realistic situation in a war and gives you a kind of part of the battle feeling.
However, the problem is that there are always so many allied ships that most of the time it feels like it doesn&apos;t matter what you are doing. Actually, in many missions you can succeed by flying away watching the battle from afar and letting the others do the work. For me this took every motivation/fun out of this game.
Another contra is that the story is boring: alien nation attacks, you fight back alien nation. That&apos;s it, basically.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">18</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>6abae306-94f9-11e8-a328-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:rating>
        <review:title>Can&apos;t see what others see in it</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">12</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/6aed6026-dd57-11ea-bd9f-fa163edf6d96 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/6aed6026-dd57-11ea-bd9f-fa163edf6d96">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-08-13T14:23:31</review:date>
        <review:description>Tech:
-in very good condition, the engine also runs on average machines
-the game is constantly updated, which also includes new features
-nice graphics and good sound

Gameplay:
-strategy, emphasis on building and construction, time-consumer in larger worlds :) Fun!
-not easy, but you learn quickly, and when the first opponent is defeated, you are proud.
-There are different strategies and techniques for each clan
-It is very important to collect all resources, but especially food, whether field, whether fish, whether animals, but the other resources are also important, and once you have the balance, then you can attack! But pay attention to the balance!


Hints (no spoiler)
-Start with lumberjack hut, house, scout
-bear clan is my favourite clan: in the training camp is Kaya, the tank bear right at the beginning. He is very useful for quickly cleaning up some areas from wild animals. Later on, the shield maiden and regular troops reinforce him. But this is only one of many clans and one of many strategies!
-The Free Game is the most fun, with card sizes large or huge. 3-4 Enemies and setting dominance. No mercy! :)
-Don&apos;t expand too fast, nature is against you, there are very cold winters (food/wood), plagues of rats (silos), earthquakes (3 buildings are burning, is quickly repaired). But this is all quickly under control and doesn&apos;t annoy you - Collect a lot of resources for a long time and use the marketplace to buy some. 
-Jötnar!!  These giants live somewhere on the map, discover them with your scouts and let your trading posts give them food. It&apos;s worth it, because one day you&apos;ll be able to have your own giant in your troop.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>6aed6026-dd57-11ea-bd9f-fa163edf6d96</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>A few quick facts to read:</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">35</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/6afed550-be01-11eb-9506-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/6afed550-be01-11eb-9506-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-05-26T12:04:46</review:date>
        <review:description>I&apos;m a big fan of Pirate themed games (Sid Meier&apos;s Pirates!, Port Royale, Windward, ...) so this game appears right up my alley. It&apos;s promising right now but there are some technical and design issues right now that prevents me from playing further.

The Good:
+ Nice graphics and lovely artstyle
+ Good performance for an UE Game
+ Even tough it&apos;s a barebones story/setting it has it&apos;s charm. Weird choice for character portait art tough.

The Bad:
- No mouse support at all, I know you get the &quot;Real Yakuza use a Gamepad&quot; prompt at the beginning but even those games have mouse support for basic menu usage. You literally do not use your mouse in this game, ever.
- No rebindable Keybinds. Note: A Patch has been promised for the end of June that will allow mouse usage.
- No Achievements on GOG (come on devs, the API is not that difficult)
- Quite a few bugs, some of them are show-stoppers. For example being killed during fetch quests will not advance the counter anymore and all AI do not attack any longer (Who playtested this?). You need to restart the process after each death, even quitting to main menu will not resolve this.
- If you play with Keyboard when firing your cannons port or starboard (left vs right side) becomes a frustrating exercise because the controls do not invert to the relative position of your ship. Visual indicators like arrows before a shot could help with this. Literally 50% of my shots miss because I don&apos;t know which side my ship is currently on. Other games solved this problem already so why reintroduce solved problems!? - frustrating as hell.
- Appears to be very light in content in terms of ship and mission types (Counted 5 Ships so far, and most quests are either fetch or kill) no base or land interaction.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">9</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>6afed550-be01-11eb-9506-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>Promising but wait for Patches</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">78</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/6b16d4e2-d037-11ea-9edb-fa163e93294d -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/6b16d4e2-d037-11ea-9edb-fa163e93294d">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-07-27T21:31:42</review:date>
        <review:description>So before i start I have to say I only own this game on android, with that said I would definetly recommend people to try it out on any platform!

The game is made by a 1 man team, and man did he do a good job. The graphics are not good but who cares when you got such good writing!

Every oldschool RPG fan should give it a go at this price, and a better looking sequel/spinoff is in the works!</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">9</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>6b16d4e2-d037-11ea-9edb-fa163e93294d</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Best Android RPG</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">39</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/6b4b235c-b223-11e8-96ea-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/6b4b235c-b223-11e8-96ea-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2017-04-11T10:36:31</review:date>
        <review:description>Non-linear quests. Interesting dialogs. Dozen of playable builds with absolutely different gameplay. Captivating buildmaking.
The problem is most of new players cant create proper build. Moreover, there are no useful guides about builds (except russian guides on steam of course, but not everyone speak russian).
For example the most frequent mistake is Mage have serious problems with mana replenishment. If you think so try to google &quot;Lionheart Red Witch Build&quot;. Its the full walkthrough for fire mage. Better to see once than hear a hundred times.
All of known proper mage classes (Inquisitor, Heavy Priest, Red Witch) have no mana problems. If you have any then you do something wrong.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>6b4b235c-b223-11e8-96ea-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>The most replayable game Ive ever seen</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/6baa5ba2-ffe6-11ea-aad7-fa163edf6d96 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/6baa5ba2-ffe6-11ea-aad7-fa163edf6d96">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-09-26T13:52:50</review:date>
        <review:description>This is the first game I feel ambivalent about. On the one hand is a fantastic mix of game mechanics, on the other hand you have unfair challenges that are unplayable, even on easy difficulty setting. E.g. you have to take up (fight)  3 AI-players that team together! On top of that, the AI cheats (see other reviews).

I really love this game, the developers must have the right mindset, but the scenario&apos;s that are frustrating makes me dismissing the game for an indefinite period of time. 

This game makes me happy, but unfortunately, sometimes it makes me mad.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>6baa5ba2-ffe6-11ea-aad7-fa163edf6d96</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Ambivalent</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/6bb7a0f2-dce9-11ea-b051-fa163e62c76a -->

