    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/6ceaba1c-a3ce-11ea-a348-fa163e62c76a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/6ceaba1c-a3ce-11ea-a348-fa163e62c76a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-06-01T09:09:17</review:date>
        <review:description>Mix Civilization (without turns), Frostpunk winter survival themes, dota combat system, and Settlers building management together and you get Northgard. Such a combo you would think would be interesting, but Northgard is simply not my cup of tea. Obtaining resources and upgrades feels unrewarding, combat lackluster, building management frustrating, boring units, rather slow gameplay at times, getting too far behind in standings means game becomes impossible to win, and it takes forever to move your units when your land becomes too large. It&apos;s a good time sink if your pc can&apos;t handle more demanding games or if your looking for just killing time and have nothing better to play, but otherwise I can&apos;t recommend it.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">8</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>6ceaba1c-a3ce-11ea-a348-fa163e62c76a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>Can&apos;t get into it</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">10</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/6d288a38-4c77-11ec-b340-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/6d288a38-4c77-11ec-b340-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-11-23T18:07:15</review:date>
        <review:description>Every now and then a game comes along which just cements itself as an instant adventure game classic, Chicken Police is such a game. If you like unique games with a superb atmosphere and art style my recommendation couldn&apos;t be any higher. I can&apos;t believe that this is studios first game, can&apos;t wait to see what they do next.

If there are any criticisms I can make it&apos;s that the game is one the easy side, you&apos;re very unlikely to encounter any showstoppers unless you miss anything. This is more of a &quot;come along for the ride&quot; kind of game. And nothing wrong with that honestly.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>6d288a38-4c77-11ec-b340-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Instant adventure game classic</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/6d5385de-2f5a-11eb-b080-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/6d5385de-2f5a-11eb-b080-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-11-25T22:11:39</review:date>
        <review:description>Game of childhood</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">35</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>6d5385de-2f5a-11eb-b080-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Love this game</review:title>
