        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:rating>
        <review:title>Average</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/6f12b2e8-9400-11e8-9445-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/6f12b2e8-9400-11e8-9445-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2009-11-14T22:54:33</review:date>
        <review:description>This was actually a fun game but i was expecting a little more. While this may be a fun game the controls were hard to learn and the graphics were kinda sad. When i played i did not expect so much cursing but got over it, but the violence was just weird. When you hit someone with a lead pipe three times holes appear on their shirts. If you like games that are somewhat strait-forward/mission based the buy this game if not I would suggest Gothic (A awesome RPG) or The Redneck Rampage Collection (a humor based FPS). This is a fun game once you get around it&apos;s flaws but this game is not for most people.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>6f12b2e8-9400-11e8-9445-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:rating>
        <review:title>Decent Game</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/6f22f7ac-d803-11ec-98f9-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/6f22f7ac-d803-11ec-98f9-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-05-20T09:09:40</review:date>
        <review:description>I was born in &apos;93, and I&apos;ve played HoMM my whole life. The old stuff, the new stuff. All of it. To varying degrees of success. Songs of Conquest scratches that itch so well, while not trying to clone HoMM itself. The gameplay loop is similar, but little changes here and there help Songs of Conquest stand out. Towns are managed outside of a screen, and buildings are constructed on plots of land outside the main town. Magic is accumulated in combat based on skills, artifacts and the units you have in your army. Combat has much more strategy involved with units gaining momentum upon successfully killing a stack; units having a &quot;Zone of Control&quot; that triggers an attack of opportunity should an opposing unit try to move out or inside the zone, and Defend and Wait being exclusive to certain units. 

The artwork and music are beautiful and everything ties together in a wonderful meld. There is height to the terrain but without having awkward camera angles like in HoMM5. There is already a map editor included which can generate random maps for you, and a growing community of map makers already hard at work making beautiful maps. 

There are currently two 4 mission campaigns available that help introduce players to the world and its 4 factions. The factions feel fleshed out without trying to copy or mimic anyone else, all the units feeling very unique and like they belong. 

This review is getting long: If you like HoMM I think you&apos;ll like this.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>6f22f7ac-d803-11ec-98f9-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>A breath of fresh air</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/6f90751e-39cc-11ec-81cf-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/6f90751e-39cc-11ec-81cf-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-10-31T00:57:54</review:date>
        <review:description>The game is pretty and atmospheric on the first look but it&apos;s too lean and repetitive then: click, click, click... One auto-save slot in a game with a) bugs; b) where you may fail a quest selecting in dialog &quot;do not mention now&quot; is a bad design also.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>6f90751e-39cc-11ec-81cf-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:rating>
        <review:title>Nice, but...</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/6fa19ef0-de71-11ea-8047-fa163edf6d96 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/6fa19ef0-de71-11ea-8047-fa163edf6d96">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-08-15T00:02:17</review:date>
        <review:description>I love dead cells, it was my No1 game of the year when it came out.
I took the DLC to support a great developer, the way same I took the game on gog because reasons.

So, to install the DLC:
go to your games page on gog site.
go to your dead cells page
click on download offline installers
get the DLC setup file (last on the page for now)
click on it, it installs in your game directory and it should work for now (it did for me).</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>6fa19ef0-de71-11ea-8047-fa163edf6d96</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>garden DLC Installation howto.</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">7</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/6faeac38-32f2-11ea-a5c0-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/6faeac38-32f2-11ea-a5c0-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-01-09T17:12:22</review:date>
        <review:description>Llevaba tiempo queriendo jugarlo y por primera vez lo hice en 2019 y no me ha defraudado. Sabía que era antiguo y me imaginaba que el control no sería tan cómodo como en los juegos actuales y cierto es que tiene los clásicos controles de tanque de juegos como los primeros Tomb Raider. De hecho creo que bebe mucho de ellos en su mayoría (no he llegado a jugar a esos y no lo haré hasta que pueda probarlos en español, aquí y en Steam solo están en inglés, pero he visto cómo son los controles y creo poder hacerme una idea). Algunos señalan que hay pocos puzzles, algo que no le falta razón pero tampoco es exactamente así. Si vienes de las aventuras gráficas de Indi (La última cruzada y El destino de la Atlántida) te dará esa sensación, pues ha abandonado el point and click por el entorno 3D, lo que posibilita muchas cosas que los otros no permitían pero también exige un cambio en la mecánica. Esta vez significa que en lugar de tener los escenarios libres de esos juegos estamos ante un mapa mucho más lineal que en lugar de ser la búsqueda de objeto X para juntarlo con objeto Y y cambiárselo a personaje Z para conseguir la llave de la puerta donde se esconde el McGuffin de turno, los puzzles son en su mayoría de plataformas en las que lo difícil es encontrar el camino, pues no es especialmente obvio. Creo que en su mayoría tiene el punto justo como para que tengas que explorar el escenario pero sin tener una flecha indicandote ni tener que hacer cabriolas imposibles porque la cámara no se pueda posicionar en un punto en el que se pueda ver ese agujero del techo por el que se tenga que pasar. Hay ciertas partes donde disparar a los enemigos comunistas y niveles en los que la mecánica principal cambia como cuando hay que bajar por un río, otorgando variedad al juego.
Los controles son muy cómodos. Yo soy de los que juegan con mando y cuando intenté adaptarlos al mando se me hizo difícil, pero cuando me resigné al teclado y el ratón me adapté con mucha facilidad.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>6faeac38-32f2-11ea-a5c0-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>preciosa primera incursión al 3D</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/6fe86912-c14f-11ec-a073-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/6fe86912-c14f-11ec-a073-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-04-21T11:45:46</review:date>
        <review:description>Disgustingly overhyped title, after 1.5h of playing I have been so annoyed/bored with it I had to remove it from my machine for eternity.

The &quot;game&quot; is basically 2 things: 
1) watching movie from the end to the beginning 
2) trying to map dead people and their fate to a documentation book and reconstruct the whole story. The idea maybe does not sound so bad, on the paper, but:

For part 1) there is endless series of cutscenes and those are SO INCREDIBLY SLOW with no possibility to skip no matter what key you press - like well yeah I saw the beast crushing a guy already so lets move on now but you will be forced to stay at that cutscene for another 2minutes - ANNOYING AF!

For part 2) The book is enormous, there are like 40 dead people on the boat and you have to solve each and every individual fate but honestly - I DO NOT ****** CARE about what happen to third or second mate or what is the henchman name are or whatever! I am interested the important things like the main storyline and actually playing a game not endlessly browsing through some ***** book and trying to map 40^3 things to its place  - what a terrible game design. (If I would like to do think like that, I would just find myself mathematical/logic riddles like &quot;Einstein&apos;s five houses riddle&quot; which is actually fun since you have all the requirements at hand without watching 10hours of cutscenes and retrospectively spending 20hours browsing through them through the ***** book)

I recommend not waste my time/money on this **** - unless you are a masochist, with a lot of free time and no goals in your life then you can &quot;play&quot;(read grind) this game to completion.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">8</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>6fe86912-c14f-11ec-a073-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:rating>
        <review:title>Beware</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/6ff3d916-1fab-11ea-a316-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/6ff3d916-1fab-11ea-a316-00163e97122a">
