    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/633be736-9ae4-11ea-a96a-fa163e62c76a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/633be736-9ae4-11ea-a96a-fa163e62c76a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-05-21T00:53:49</review:date>
        <review:description>This game is combination of civilization and RTS or moba game as you will not control many units. It is played in realtime but you fight for map tiles similar to civilization. Also discovering the map is really similar to civilization.

I own it on steam and played 8hours before I finally gave up. This game is super slow. You are waiting for resources all the time and you have nothing to do but watch your units to move around the map. I had a time to chat with friends while playing &quot;RTS&quot; game!</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">26</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>633be736-9ae4-11ea-a96a-fa163e62c76a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>Slow and shallow</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">16</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/637f40aa-e9ed-11ea-b48d-fa163e93294d -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/637f40aa-e9ed-11ea-b48d-fa163e93294d">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-08-29T14:47:17</review:date>
        <review:description>Das Spiel ist im Grunde Zeitmanagement, man muss Arbeiten, Videos anschauen, Essen, Schlafen jonglieren - und dabei die richtigen Hinweise und die richtigen Schlüsse sammeln. Im Grunde ein primitives Spielprinzip, das aber schlicht funktioniert.
Das Spiel hat mich absolut süchtig gemacht...gäbe es Erweiterungen, die neue Stories/Bildschirme hinzufügen, ich hätte ein Abo! Selbst nach dem dritten Mal durchgespielt und noch öfter angefangen wird es nicht langweilig, es reizt mich herauszufinden, was passiert wenn ich etwas anders mache oder einfach nichts tue...
Klar, irgendwann hat man alle Stories durch, aber bis dahin macht es wirklich Spaß. Die Geschichten sind gut erzählt, witzig und spannend. 
An manchen Stellen wäre es cool, wenn man noch mehr beeinflussen könnte, aber naja, that&apos;s life ;)</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>637f40aa-e9ed-11ea-b48d-fa163e93294d</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Eins meiner absoluten Lieblingsspiele</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/64a1cef0-3e23-11eb-a3ca-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/64a1cef0-3e23-11eb-a3ca-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-12-14T17:45:29</review:date>
        <review:description>I ran this on LinuxMint 20 Cinnamon 64-bit. Bridge Constructor version 1.3. It installed, played and performed flawlessly. 

I returned the game for a refund. I found it too simplistic, casual, and repetitive. I think this is a game for more casual players that want to play fifteen or twenty minutes at a time and come back to it another day. The puzzles did increase in difficulty over time, but it really is the same thing over and over. Also the in game music is really limited. It&apos;s probably less than a thirty second loop. Turn off and listen to your own selection of music. 

If you are a casual game player that likes to work hard on puzzles you&apos;ll like this.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>64a1cef0-3e23-11eb-a3ca-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:rating>
        <review:title>A casual but repetitive game.</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">17</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/64acf700-6143-11ec-b82b-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/64acf700-6143-11ec-b82b-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-12-20T05:17:42</review:date>
        <review:description>While it is blatant propaganda if you strip it down to its base components it&apos;s a solid beat em up. don&apos;t expect the triple a slog made to eat your attention for life its a skill based game with some challenges that naturally reward good work. Mechanics are simple to understand and are intuitively introduced. I&apos;ll never politically agree with the developers but they&apos;ve made a solid foundation of gameplay that can excuse any story to it. The limo level was torture though maybe a grace of one or two hits before catapulting the score marker fighters through the windshield? Just never been a fan of blind perfection levels.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>64acf700-6143-11ec-b82b-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>No heart but some decent design</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/64b599f4-6b8a-11ec-8980-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/64b599f4-6b8a-11ec-8980-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-01-02T07:11:08</review:date>
        <review:description>Это было весело и увлекательно. Прошёл на лёгкой сложности (как написано, самой сбалансированной), но была возможность и самому регулировать сложность прохождения. Если не торопиться, то проходить очень легко, если же стараться пройти быстро и красиво, тут тебе и челлендж будет. Мне зашли юмор и атмосфера.

Поставил 4 из 5, потому что есть куда идеальнее, но о потраченном времени и деньгах не сожалею.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>64b599f4-6b8a-11ec-8980-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>5 часов веселья</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/640b85aa-946e-11e8-ac9c-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/640b85aa-946e-11e8-ac9c-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2011-06-24T00:29:04</review:date>
        <review:description>Well this game is amazing pure and simple, I played the first one all the way through with no cheats......seriously no cheats. I figured with the sequel there would be some improvements but there has actually been much more. The gameplay is familiar and easy to learn so its good for novices and experts alike, above all the story has a tie with the first and there is an improvement in scenario and atmosphere. Worth the download.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>640b85aa-946e-11e8-ac9c-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Back.....with a vengeance!!</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/640fac70-409c-11eb-82ef-fa163e99870e -->

