    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/663a3fe0-e4df-11ec-90a2-42010a340c25 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/663a3fe0-e4df-11ec-90a2-42010a340c25">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-06-05T17:54:28</review:date>
        <review:description>Bis jetzt die beste Neuverkörperung von HMoM. Für alle Fans sehr zu empfehlen. Läuft solide auf Mittelklassen PCs und sieht vom Stil extrem schick aus. Gameplay ist genau das was man erwartet und mehr.  Unterstützt dieses fleißige Entwicklerteam für ihre Arbeit.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>663a3fe0-e4df-11ec-90a2-42010a340c25</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Wirklich gut!</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/66324f12-939b-11e9-9d28-4a95b0daf307 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/66324f12-939b-11e9-9d28-4a95b0daf307">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-06-20T20:38:45</review:date>
        <review:description>The artstyle is cute, but there&apos;s some questionable character design thrown in there, which put me off from it. The platforming in this game is okay, and the fighting is a nice challenge, but the story is very generic and didn&apos;t offer much to keep me engaged after that one encounter. I regret buying it, but I can see how it might appeal to some people.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>66324f12-939b-11e9-9d28-4a95b0daf307</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:rating>
        <review:title>Decent game, but nothing special.</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/664214bc-93f9-11e8-b3e4-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/664214bc-93f9-11e8-b3e4-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2008-10-12T00:23:48</review:date>
        <review:description>I can&apos;t imagine anyone enjoying this game ten years ago or today.  The gunplay is horrible, the art style is flat out stupid and insulting to the player&apos;s intelligence, and even the most basic tasks are next to impossible.  I&apos;m a big fan of FPS games, and Shogo, another one available on GOG.com, is one of my all time favorites - but Kingpin misses the mark in every way.  It wasn&apos;t worth $50 in the 90s, and it&apos;s not worth $6 in the 2000s.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">46</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>664214bc-93f9-11e8-b3e4-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:rating>
        <review:title>Don&apos;t waste your time.</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">18</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/66432384-a207-11ea-b82c-fa163e62c76a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/66432384-a207-11ea-b82c-fa163e62c76a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-05-30T02:52:05</review:date>
        <review:description>I got into the Shantae series when ½-genie hero came out. I loved that game. 
This game mostly gets rid of the stages the previous game had and is mostly a completely connected world with a classic map. 

The cutscenes look like they were picked directly from a cartoon. In fact i kinda want a Shantae cartoon now. Because those animations were great and the voice acting was pretty decent for what little lines the characters had. 

They added a card-system which you can have three equipped at a time. they each give a bonus to things ranging from damage or speed of your spells and such. Some cards require multiple to be usable. And some requires some other steps to acquire. I didn&apos;t collect all of them. It was fairly tedious to get some cards. And those i had was the once i used throughout most of the game anyway. 

I liked the system with the transformations and the dances and how they cleverly put some of the collectable loot in your path after you&apos;ve aquired the powers requried to get them. You could have passed by and seen it before, then your return travel would take you by and allow you to pick it up. 

On the difficulty side it&apos;s pretty easy. You will have plenty of food and money throughout the game.

If you want a pretty relaxed metroidvania this is it.  
Playtime for me was close to 8 hours. But as i mentioned i did not collect all cards and missed some other collectables. </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>66432384-a207-11ea-b82c-fa163e62c76a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Great casual metroidvania.</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">48</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/665064a4-93f9-11e8-9eee-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/665064a4-93f9-11e8-9eee-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2008-10-12T01:57:02</review:date>
        <review:description>Not sure how it holds up today but back in the day i had loads of fun playing this game.  The graphics were pretty decent at the time and the game is a fun 3rd person experience.  The first time you get knocked out of your body its kinda tough but you get used to positioning yourself so that you can hop from body to body without getting killed in the process.   The story isn&apos;t particularly engaging but the game is very satirical and funny at times.  There is a little exploration and some problem solving to do but for the most part its a 3d shooter/platformer with a well implemented possession mechanic (aim for the upper back).  Nothing more i can think of to say except the final boss fight is incredibly challenging, but worth it when you finish.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">10</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>665064a4-93f9-11e8-9eee-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Loved this Game</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">15</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/67b00e32-551f-11eb-b0f7-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/67b00e32-551f-11eb-b0f7-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-01-12T23:44:53</review:date>
        <review:description>Carto est une très chouette expérience. 

En suivant les aventures de Carto, une petite cartographe séparée de sa mamie, on visite des lieux au coup de crayon charmant, en resolvant des petites énigmes et en croisant des personnages tous plus accueillants les uns que les autres. 
Un jeu mignon, parfait pour les soirs où la fatigue fait qu&apos;on a besoin d&apos;un petit jeu tranquille et positif !</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>67b00e32-551f-11eb-b0f7-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Un adorable jeu de puzzle </review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/67da45c0-2f41-11eb-a5ff-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/67da45c0-2f41-11eb-a5ff-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-11-25T19:12:32</review:date>
        <review:description>Excellent game with interesting plot, good graphics and sound, and also addictive gameplay. Hope that River of Time/Phileasson&apos;s Secret will also find a way to the GOG store, would love to buy them too.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">10</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>67da45c0-2f41-11eb-a5ff-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Great game of the Dark Eye family</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">23</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/67ddc8a2-1897-11e9-84b0-00163e4e60cc -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/67ddc8a2-1897-11e9-84b0-00163e4e60cc">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-01-15T09:30:17</review:date>
        <review:description>A murder mystery and detective story, notable for presenting freeze-framed scenes at different moments in the past. I&apos;ve really enjoyed that the game rarely gives out obvious information. It does not draw attention to clues or their significance. I had to actively make observations and incorporate them into the growing web of hard facts, suspicions, and mental notes. The game keeps this process very convenient and organized through the in-game logbook and the structure for confirming your guesses. It felt very satisfying to gradually piece together what happened, all the while getting intimately familiar with the events, the people, and the location. This ties into how surprisingly emotional I felt about the story, in spite of being slightly disappointing in the traditional &quot;narrative&quot; sense. I thought the minimalist visual style and the sounds added a lot to the story by creating a stark and grim atmosphere, and many scenes even looked beautiful and moody. After completing the game pretty thoroughly in about 9 hours, I wouldn&apos;t say it&apos;s very long or replayable, but I felt it&apos;s the right length and a good value. I believe this is an extremely well-made, clever, satisfying game that sticks with you after playing, and I&apos;d highly recommend it.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>67ddc8a2-1897-11e9-84b0-00163e4e60cc</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Challenging and atmospheric mystery</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/670802fc-82c4-11e9-b9b1-00163e4e60cc -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/670802fc-82c4-11e9-b9b1-00163e4e60cc">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-05-30T13:19:26</review:date>
        <review:description>A l&apos;heure actuel où je post mon avis, je suis actuellement au chapitre 3, mais en l&apos;état actuel des choses, c&apos;est pas nécessaire d&apos;aller plus loin pour discerner les problèmes dont le jeu souffre

J&apos;aime ce jeu, je l&apos;ai attendu depuis mon expérience sur un de leurs précédant jeu, ceci dis, difficile de le poser sur un piédestal tant il souffre de problèmes de déséquilibre :

- On ne peut pas consulter la fiche technique des personnages à recruter

- Dans les donjons, impossible de retirer un équipement sans être à un camp
Ce qui fait que quand on tombe sur un événement qui fait qu&apos;on peut recruter des personnages (donc en renvoyer un), on ne peut pas lui retirer son objet, et il est donc perdu à jamais si on décide de le renvoyer pour en prendre un autre qui pouvais être potentiellement plus intéressant 

- Beaucoup trop aléatoire, surtout au niveau des campements
On peut très bien croiser 2 ou 3 campements à la suite, et aussi bien ne rien avoir pendant des niveaux entiers
Cette idée est particulièrement stupide, sachant qu&apos;on peut utiliser les item de restauration uniquement dans ces phases là, c&apos;est donc au bonheur la chance si peut arriver jusqu&apos;à la fin du niveau en court, c&apos;est le principal soucis, actuellement, des phases de gameplay

- Il est peut ergonomique
Pour consulter à quoi correspond chaque icone, il faut retourner voir le tutoriel, pourquoi n&apos;avoir pas fait de bulle d&apos;info ?
Aucune trace de journal, pour un descriptif des quêtes, on est donc bien marron si on oublie quelque chose

- Concernant la traduction (et celle-ci ne pourra pas être réparer via un patch, je suppose), et ben... elle est catastrophique
Non pas dans ses fautes d&apos;orthographe (même si il y en à des basiques), mais les dialogues ne font tellement pas naturel, et ne colle parfois pas
Sachant qu&apos;il y à parfois pas mal de dialogues, ce &quot;détail&quot; à son importance, on à même du mal à définir un caractère clair aux personnages (enfin, surtout l&apos;héroïne)

Le jeu clairement besoin de patch</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>670802fc-82c4-11e9-b9b1-00163e4e60cc</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:rating>
        <review:title>Besoin de patch</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">13</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/6723eaae-307f-11e9-a099-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/6723eaae-307f-11e9-a099-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-02-14T19:38:56</review:date>
        <review:description>Return of the Obra Dinn plays very uniquely and feels entirely alien. It feels knowable but unknown. That&apos;s the best way to sum my time on the Obra Dinn. You play as a claims investigator in the age of sail investigating the mystical return of a ship with no crew with the help of a magical pocket watch. You have to identify all the 60 crew of a ship and how they died and who killed them from standstill memories of the moment of their death and some audio cues and lines of dialogue. All you have to help you are three pictures of the crew together, a crew manifest, and the ability for the book you&apos;re using to tag correct crew ID and their deaths in bulks of three. 

The game lays its story out bare and allows the player to slam their head against its wall as much as they want. It plays as a very free-form crime puzzler, maybe a very complex twist on Cluedo, but i was amazed to see the amount of reasoning and deduction the player can employ from just observing the environment. I never saw &apos;game pieces&apos; or the design strings behind it, and i was entirely focused on the actual characters and the world, trying to discern details in this very uniquely shaded game. 

While some elements do stand out as Rosetta Stones for solving the identity of certain members of the crew, even at the end when i had unlocked all the corpses and had free reign over the ship, it still wasn&apos;t easy, moreso the fact that unlocking sections of the ship require a very keen eye and may be very easily missed. After finishing it, i can definitely say that it was easier and less daunting than it originally seemed, and some puzzle pieces may have been a bit too hamfisted compared to the extreme subtlety of others, but i never felt i had no avenues open to me. 

However, sometimes i just tried to fit pegs in holes with no real logic behind it and the game obliged me, a bit to its detriment. However, it is a balancing act and i would have much rather what we got now than a much more nitpicky experience.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>6723eaae-307f-11e9-a099-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>A game created in an alternate universe</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">14</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/6732abc0-b20d-11e8-a026-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/6732abc0-b20d-11e8-a026-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2017-02-07T17:46:55</review:date>
        <review:description>NOTE:I do not own the GOG.com version, so if extra content is available in this version I couldn&apos;t tell you. If I could do 3 1/2 stars i would probably give it another half star for at least not falling into the worst tropes of the sub-genre. If you don&apos;t like the use of the term &quot;walking simulator&quot;, I&apos;m sorry but it is applicable here. 
           A decently compelling story helps it stick out above some of the worse examples cough-gone home-cough, and enough interactivity to justify its existence as a video game instead of a visual novel, but it still didn&apos;t peek my interest like TSP did with its witty sense of humor and subversion of tropes, and didn&apos;t strike me visually like Journey. It&apos;s just an okay walking simulator, if you like the sub-genre then check it out on sale. If you don&apos;t like these types of games normally, I don&apos;t think the story or characters are interesting enough to warrant putting up with a style of play you don&apos;t care for.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">52</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>6732abc0-b20d-11e8-a026-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:rating>
        <review:title>If ya like walking simulators, good news</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">44</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/675a491e-c635-11e8-a2d6-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/675a491e-c635-11e8-a2d6-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2018-10-02T14:22:10</review:date>
        <review:description>The best Indiana Jones Adventure Game FOREVER</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>675a491e-c635-11e8-a2d6-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Indy</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">11</review:upvotes>
