    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/675c4818-93f9-11e8-ba23-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/675c4818-93f9-11e8-ba23-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2008-10-13T03:52:03</review:date>
        <review:description>But this game really stands up todays space sims. The mission design in compelling, the story is really well told, and the way upgrades and new ships are handled make these additions feel really integrated into the game world.

Downsides? 640x480! Ack! Pro tip: Dig into the GOG.com folder and find the Freespace.exe launcher and turn off hardware rendering (my Nvidia card gave me a few graphical glitches, also, pull of the &quot;Properties&quot; view of FR.exe and turn on Win98 compatibility mode. The game plays a whole lot more naturally with these tweaks.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">14</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>675c4818-93f9-11e8-ba23-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Maybe I&apos;m just nostalgic...</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">236</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/677a5bf2-4879-11e9-8bb4-00163e4e60cc -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/677a5bf2-4879-11e9-8bb4-00163e4e60cc">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-03-17T07:56:27</review:date>
        <review:description>I&apos;m generally horrible at platformers and things that require precision and some reviews kinda scared me off, but I didn&apos;t find this game that hard. Sure, enemies hit pretty hard, so you&apos;ll die often and have to reapeat some screens, but to me it wasn&apos;t enough to make the game annoying to me. I generally play these kind of games as an uphill battle in short sessions. It took me around 9 hours to get to the end (with 100% exploration of the map, because I wanted to see it all and I&apos;m not replaying it anythime soon!). All in all, it was a lovely short story, challenging enough to be fun and very pretty to look at. I&apos;m glad with my purchase.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>677a5bf2-4879-11e9-8bb4-00163e4e60cc</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Fun and not too hard!</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/6776aa82-5f09-11ea-bc84-fa163e62c76a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/6776aa82-5f09-11ea-bc84-fa163e62c76a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-03-05T19:47:38</review:date>
        <review:description>The graphics are nice, but they lag the gameplay a lot. I had to play on low, which felt like a pixel game without the performance. There is a lot of combat mechanics but they are not introduced well. The dialog texts are way too small and I wish there was more emphasis on the combat and stealth instead of the inventory diversity. The mood of the game was well delivered. I wish the difficulty didn&apos;t scale up that fast because it feels impossible to backstab an enemy without bumping into them. Pretty good to get a taste of the game, but due to clunky controls I will not buy the full game.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>6776aa82-5f09-11ea-bc84-fa163e62c76a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:rating>
        <review:title>Interesting but not so well executed</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/678e7432-93f9-11e8-8402-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/678e7432-93f9-11e8-8402-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2008-10-13T12:50:49</review:date>
        <review:description>This is the perfect space combat game.  When I first discovered it, copies were going for $100+ on ebay.  Buy this game if you&apos;re a space combat fan.  For $6, buy it even if you aren&apos;t

As others have mentioned, the game engine&apos;s source code was released as the Free Space Open project.  There are some stellar mods (BSG and Babylon 5) and some top-notch new missions.  The people on the project have even redone the graphics.  FS2 still looks pretty good in 2008, FSO looks fantastic.  (Though X3&apos;s graphics are nicer.  Pitty the game-play isn&apos;t as good as Freespace.)</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>678e7432-93f9-11e8-8402-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>My favourite game... ever.</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">19</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


