    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/69622212-2399-11ec-836f-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/69622212-2399-11ec-836f-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-10-02T18:57:14</review:date>
        <review:description>The game is a arcade tank shooter.
I bought it at the time of release and I had fond memories of this title.
Truth is that... is not much good.
Yes, it is one of the few tank game out there but the reality is that most of the times you run and gun against dumb enemies.

Enemy tanks are a joke. They rarely spot you and are so slow to repond to your fire, that you destroy them long before they pose a treat.

Mines and RPG soldiers are the true danger here.
Other than that the structures are mildly distructible but, most of the times, that is not very satisfying to do.
The story... well.... I&apos;ll let you guess it.

Also, it made me a bit sick after a few levels, as the tank movement is a bit too wobbly.
So stopped playing.

Worth for nostalgia and if you can&apos;t find any other tank game out there.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>69622212-2399-11ec-836f-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:rating>
        <review:title>Aged worse than I thought</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">9</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/7a7ca412-3106-11ec-bd56-fa163e99870e -->

