    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/7fee786c-a9ad-11ea-88b0-fa163e62c76a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/7fee786c-a9ad-11ea-88b0-fa163e62c76a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-06-08T20:28:42</review:date>
        <review:description>This is an awesome game no doubt, I bought it on release and besides what I considered a long loading time in between sections I haven&apos;t had any issues at all, the game ran very well.

Hardware requirements are a way too high, I think that is for 8K. 

The gameplay is fast but easy to learn, the game is not pretty hard unless you go without upgrading you may get a more challenging experience.

The music has this 8  bit like tone added to it, it&apos;s not bad but I was expecting more like 1/2 Genie Hero, now I like it.

Now the cutscenes, they look cheap, to be honest, but considering the game&apos;s theme, it makes sense that they use a more cartoonish scheme.

This game worth the try, It&apos;s not a big AAA release or a Symphony killer but it&apos;s fun to play and that&apos;s what&apos;s matter, Shantevania for the win.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>7fee786c-a9ad-11ea-88b0-fa163e62c76a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Awesome Game</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/70bb148e-93f9-11e8-a197-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/70bb148e-93f9-11e8-a197-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2008-10-23T15:19:25</review:date>
        <review:description>Anything but that. I remember being amazed by the graphics back then and even today, it looks pretty good. AI is decent, level design amazing, soundtrack by Cypress hill awesome. The only problem may be the graphical style - retro sci-fi may not be suitable for anyone, but I liked it. 
Bottom line: if youre looking for a challenging decent shooter, look no further.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">14</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>70bb148e-93f9-11e8-a197-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Pretty good old school shooter</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">54</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/70c49f68-d819-11e8-9743-00163e4e60cc -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/70c49f68-d819-11e8-9743-00163e4e60cc">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2018-10-25T08:47:21</review:date>
        <review:description>As a metroidvania title, I really enjoyed this game. It&apos;s atmospheric, the controls feel nice and snappy. Combat is simple but satisfying. I don&apos;t really have any complaints, just noticed some small ways the game could be better...

-The game lacks ambient noise. Not a big deal, but would contribute to the atmosphere.

-Music sounds very midi-ish. It&apos;s understated and ambient, but the low quality sound was constantly noticable, the music itself is nice though. While the game is retro in a lot of ways, i would have enjoyed sampled instruments and modern synths.

-Lack of items/weapons/abilities. It just felt limited in that regard. 

-Limited abilities in general. You can only have a small number of passives and active items. Wish they could have found some other way of handling that.

-Lack of lore text... I feel like the game could have gone all out with lore, just finding random bits of text and items that delve a bit more into the world than is currently avaliable. Characters talk to you and wander around the map, but it feels like more of this would have added a ton of intrigue.

I really enjoyed the game and would recommend it to fans of the genre, technically though, it could be more robust.

</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>70c49f68-d819-11e8-9743-00163e4e60cc</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Really good!</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/7020feb8-a5a4-11e9-ae10-9ebff0c18a44 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/7020feb8-a5a4-11e9-ae10-9ebff0c18a44">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-07-13T19:28:48</review:date>
        <review:description>Pour moi, c&apos;est un jeu parfait. Tout fonctionne correctement, les graphismes avec ce style particulier le sound design et les musiques et surtout, surtout le scénario. Je suis un grand fan de ce genre d&apos;histoire mais la narration designée par Lucas Pope est ici parfaitement juste. J&apos;ai fait le jeu il y déjà plusieurs mois et j&apos;y repense encore régulièrement tant je n&apos;ai rien à lui reprocher.

Je ne veux pas trop rentrer dans les détails pour éviter tout spoil, donc il faudra juste faire confiance à mon avis et ceux des autres utilisateurs, mais franchement n&apos;hésitez plus et essayez le. </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>7020feb8-a5a4-11e9-ae10-9ebff0c18a44</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Une narration parfaite</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/70216d3e-7bc7-11ec-866a-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/70216d3e-7bc7-11ec-866a-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-01-22T23:08:25</review:date>
        <review:description>De premier abord, Momodora ne donne pas l&apos;impression de viser la couronne du best metroidvania ever...

Et il a bien raison !!! Il y a trop de monde à bord du bateau, il faudrait se lever de bonne heure ne serai-ce que pour se mesurer sérieusement aux vieux classiques.

Là où il réussi très bien par contre, c&apos;est en étant un bon petit jeu plaisant à jouer, tout simplement !!!
Manette en main le feeling est dynamique, les actions tombent sous les doigts naturellement. 
Les mécaniques de jeu sont bien carrées. Timings, placements... tout colle bien.
Puis le level-design est quand-même bien cool à défaut d&apos;être inoubliable.

Je lui met 5 étoiles parce que j&apos;ai envie de le mettre en valeur, voilà ! Note max en gardant en tête qu&apos;il faut pas demander à un jeu qui coûte moins de 10 balles d&apos;être le GOTY.

Excellent rapport qualité/prix :P

[ j&apos;allais oublier : oui, il y a un peu un carton jaune spécial sorcières à gros seins, fort heureusement tout étant représenté avec d&apos;adorables pixels encore plus gros que les nibards ci-avant mentionnés, il n&apos;y a pas lieu de demander l&apos;intervention de la brigade des mœurs. Ouf !!! Sauvés par l’hommage 16bits !!! ]</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>70216d3e-7bc7-11ec-866a-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Sans prétention mais très éfficace</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/703404a8-b2b2-11e8-83c3-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/703404a8-b2b2-11e8-83c3-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2018-03-15T22:51:45</review:date>
        <review:description>If you like adventure games, if you consider yourself a connoisseur of point and clicks - this game is a disappointment in every regard. If you are new to adventure gaming, this is not the place to start, and I would advise you to look elsewhere for something better.

I&apos;ve attempted to play this game twice and have given it every concession low budget adventure games can be allowed. The concept from the outset is unbelievable and its hard to like the characters you are introduced to, this is not taking into consideration the poorly delivered dialogue. It has a very flat tone, and it sounds like the voice actors are struggling with pronunciation. It does nothing to help how you feel about the people you meet, and certainly does not make you care about their situation. 

The &apos;lovable rogue&apos; is the archetype aimed for, and its missed by a long shot and its a disappointment.

Technically the game looks dated even for 2010, and its pre-rendered scenes are somewhat &apos;ill&apos; looking and basic. This is not helped by jarringly simple animation and rudimentary interaction with objects that you have as a player.

This game is a curio of point and click,  and should be treated as such. If you really must experience every single adventure game of the naughties, then give this game a go by all means. Just brace yourself for a total lack of charm and execution.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">10</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>703404a8-b2b2-11e8-83c3-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:rating>
        <review:title>Total waste of time</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">38</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/70435086-c584-11e8-99f5-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/70435086-c584-11e8-99f5-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2012-04-06T11:05:28</review:date>
        <review:description>Twelve years ago I picked this game off a shelf in Office Depot because, hey, it looked kinda cool and a bunch of us at college had been having a blast with running Descent LAN parties.  

Twelve years.  Wow.  In game years that&apos;s more like two hundred, and I&apos;ve gone through hundreds of games since then - picked them up, played them for awhile and either lost interest or beat them and forgot them.  Freespace, though, is different.  I keep coming back to it, time after time, year after year; I&apos;ve long since forgotten how many times I&apos;ve won the game, but I still keep a copy because I keep coming back.  Good games come and go, great games stick around for awhile, but it takes a masterpiece to survive more than a decade and still be just as fun as it ever was.

There are a lot of reasons for that.  The gameplay is balanced, intuitive, and polished, easily configurable for keyboard, keyboard &amp;amp; mouse, or joystick (and you can use a utility like Xpadder to extend it even more to use an XBOX360 controller).  It ramps the difficulty up almost without you realizing it, offering more ships and more weapons the deeper into the story you get.  The graphics hold their own even in the original unmodded game, but if you want to make it really pretty (and I mean, REALLY pretty) then get the Freespace SCP installed (http://scp.indiegames.us/).

But graphics and gameplay are only a part of it - great graphics are the norm today, and plenty of games have decent gameplay - it doesn&apos;t mean they&apos;ll still be around after a decade plus change.  What pulls it together and makes a great game into a masterpiece is the story of FS2, and how perfectly the game allows you to experience that story through great graphics and killer gameplay.  It engages you, pulls you in and takes you along for the ride.  Every mission drives the story, every dogfight feels like it&apos;s important.  It lets you start to feel like you&apos;re the big man on deck, and then delivers a punch that makes you sit back in awe as huge ships, hundreds of times your size, suddenly appear and remind you how big this war really is.  The next minute you&apos;re put in a situation that shows how one soldier, one pilot, can turn the tide.

Get this game.  GOG has it for less than lunch at McDonalds, and the Freespace SCP is completely free.  Then compare it to one of the recent games that ran you 49.99, and you&apos;ll see why this still sets the standard after all these years.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>70435086-c584-11e8-99f5-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>This sets the standard</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/705a785c-b2d2-11e8-91e4-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/705a785c-b2d2-11e8-91e4-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2018-06-01T04:37:36</review:date>
        <review:description>MDK is the best example of &quot;short but sweet;&quot; it might only take you two or three hours to finish, but it&apos;s awesome all the way through. The levels are varied with tons of collectibles and secrets to keep replayability high, the enemies are fun to fight, and the controls are super tight, making the platforming fun. This is one of those must-have games, along with the sequel.

https://youtu.be/MVAtAtOXJU8</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>705a785c-b2d2-11e8-91e4-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>An awesome classic, but a bit short</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/705fbc80-ce69-11eb-aa54-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/705fbc80-ce69-11eb-aa54-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-06-16T09:09:41</review:date>
        <review:description>Level design, sound effects, sound track, character design, ambiance, story... I&apos;d thank all of these people but it seems there is a gifted person out there who actually did a team&apos;s effort on his own making a memorable or perhaps classic game that frankly I believe every platform lover should experience.

My one slight gripe with this game and is really not that much of an issue was ethical... I won&apos;t spoil the details but Jack is no Fortesque ... 

Deserves a standing ovation for each of those roles fulfilled... It could only be more jaw dropping if this was done on assembly or COBOL seriously, there are some talented people out there. Oh ... Get the soundtrack I will after writing this!</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>705fbc80-ce69-11eb-aa54-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>A fun, artful and polished work </review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/7050a0c8-ceb1-11ea-ae67-fa163e62c76a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/7050a0c8-ceb1-11ea-ae67-fa163e62c76a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-07-25T23:00:07</review:date>
        <review:description>В игре не понятно половину того, что надо делать. Первые 1,5-2 часа что-то делаешь сам не понимая, а потом резко все жители оказываются недовольными, все хотят жрать и ты не знаешь что делать! Игра отстой полный!!! И езе полноценного русского языка нет!</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">31</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>7050a0c8-ceb1-11ea-ae67-fa163e62c76a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:rating>
        <review:title>Отстой!</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/7068a05a-fd82-11eb-8d63-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/7068a05a-fd82-11eb-8d63-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-08-15T07:37:03</review:date>
        <review:description>Absolutely fantastic.... until a game-breaking glitch preventing any further progress. This glitch has been around for forever and never fixed. Just another broken game from good old GOG, who for two weeks haven&apos;t even responded to any of my seven refund requests.

Sound familiar?</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>7068a05a-fd82-11eb-8d63-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>Nope.</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/70800bf0-d01f-11ea-9b1d-fa163e62c76a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/70800bf0-d01f-11ea-9b1d-fa163e62c76a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-07-27T18:40:03</review:date>
        <review:description>For a one-man Indie game this is astonishing. The writing, quests, loot.


Yes, compared to a high-budget studio the graphics are a bit janky, though it does run on a low-end machine. But the lore, RPG mechanics, story, exploration, it&apos;s all fantastic. Very dedicated community on the author&apos;s website forum.

Incredibly good fun. Highly recommended.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">14</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>70800bf0-d01f-11ea-9b1d-fa163e62c76a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>An astonishing achievement</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">111</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/709af41e-e81f-11ec-9375-42010a340c25 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/709af41e-e81f-11ec-9375-42010a340c25">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-06-09T21:10:27</review:date>
        <review:description>Strange Horticulture est jeu qui, malgré son histoire et atmosphère plutôt occulte et grise, est très relaxant. 
On deviendra, au fil des quelques heures nécessaires pour le compléter, un·e horticulteur·trice à l’œil aiguisé (et au grimoire toujours indispensable) pendant qu&apos;au fil des visites de clientes et clients, une intrigue sombre nous est présentée. 
Le jeu a de vagues airs tantôt de The Room, pour les fréquentes énigmes impliquant des objets, tantôt de Cultist Simulator, pour l&apos;ambiance et le côté mystique. Les systèmes sont simples mais bien fichus et rendent l&apos;expérience agréable ; une légère réserve pour les étiquettes dont l&apos;option d&apos;automatisation efface parfois nos notes (j&apos;aurais aimé que ça n&apos;automatise que pour les plantes sans étiquette, ou propose de juste compléter). 

A titre perso j&apos;ai plus été pris par les mystères ponctuels et la tâche d&apos;identifier les plantes, que par l&apos;histoire globale. Elle reste prenante et vaut le coup de compléter le jeu. 
A noter qu&apos;une fonctionnalité d&apos;astuce permet de ne jamais être totalement coincé et l&apos;échec n&apos;est pas un game over dans ce jeu, évitant de la frustration inutile. </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>709af41e-e81f-11ec-9375-42010a340c25</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Ambiance pesante pour un jeu chill </review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/71ba059c-70d4-11eb-a7ca-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/71ba059c-70d4-11eb-a7ca-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-02-17T05:58:50</review:date>
        <review:description>2 hours of getting stuck on every tree, rock, mine cart and torch was all I could take. </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">11</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>71ba059c-70d4-11eb-a7ca-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:rating>
        <review:title>The controls are terrible</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">10</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/71d79b32-6db0-11ec-9f69-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/71d79b32-6db0-11ec-9f69-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-01-05T00:48:33</review:date>
        <review:description>Funny saying that about a metal rhythm game, but let me explain. 

The main draw of the game is doing - nearly – everything to a 4 or 8 count beat.
1-2-3-4
Shoot-Shoot-Shoot-Shoot
or 
12-34-56-78
ShootShoot-ReLoad-ShootShoot-ReLoad

Hitting flow in those moments of chaos by balancing staying on beat with surviving &amp;amp; outputting dps, IS the fun of BPM. This game is awesome on that merit alone.

That being said, the visuals of the game make it hard for me at times to differentiate enemies from the backgrounds. 

The Levels are all stylistic firey reds, blacks, oranges, yellows, etc. 
The enemies are also colored in similar reds, blacks, oranges, and yellows. 

They have a little glow about them, and its not impossible to tell enemies from floor tiles, but many a time I&apos;ve walked past a slug or a spider I just didn&apos;t see and took damage because of it. 
Totally my fault, I am sure of it. Maybe I was in the zone and missed them. But I feel if they were in more contrasting colors, it would make it easier to keep track of them. They might clash with the descending into firey Norse hell aesthetic the designers seem to be going for though. 

I also wonder how friendly this color pallet is to colorblind players.

Good arcadey fun regardless. Just keep your eyes peeled. 

FYI:
I don&apos;t own it on here. I have it on console. </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>71d79b32-6db0-11ec-9f69-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Fun, but visually noisy.</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/71ee3904-d850-11ec-b244-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/71ee3904-d850-11ec-b244-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-05-20T18:20:56</review:date>
        <review:description>The game is by no means a Heroes of Might and Magic 3 clone – in some aspects it feels better – good game design decisions in the form of army and hero limits that curb certain tedious and boring strategies and shorten player turns, so far better balance, campaign story worth reading through and a community that is bustling with life .

In other aspects it is worse – especially the atmosphere, visual design and music imo – but that&apos;s a bar set very high and, mind you, those aspects are still at a competent level.

With the level of balance and amount of content the game could easily pass as a finished title rather than early access, and a finished title very much worthy of your time.

Claims of AI cheating *a bit* seem kind of true, at least in the campaign mode, but you can still finish it and enjoy it (I certainly did). 

Two thumbs up from me. I&apos;ll be playing the game for a long time.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>71ee3904-d850-11ec-b244-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Superb turn based strategy!</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/7107c8de-2f64-11eb-bdea-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/7107c8de-2f64-11eb-bdea-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-11-25T23:23:20</review:date>
        <review:description>In nearly all the scenarios it is quite easy to build a bridge that works, as long as you apply the structural engineering knowledge you aquire as you progress.  There are still likely to be a few that cause you difficulty, as is the nature of puzzle games, but you can generally get a good sense of achievement and progress.  As such, you&apos;ll probably get through all the puzzles quite quickly but there is plenty more scope in trying to optimise your designs.  Depending on how obsessive you are, that could take two or three times longer than &apos;just&apos; making something that works.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>7107c8de-2f64-11eb-bdea-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Easy to play, hard to master</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">13</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/7135ed92-f934-11ea-a787-fa163e93294d -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/7135ed92-f934-11ea-a787-fa163e93294d">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-09-18T01:23:42</review:date>
        <review:description>I was hyped since its announcement.
Stay away from this game, the visuals make it literally unwatchable, it&apos;s hard to see enemies giving they are the same color of the environment (red), the game sometimes has painful slowdown for no reason.
The slowdowns are room and visit based: you enter the room and it starts to stutter visibly, it won&apos;t go away unless you enter another room. Sometimes if you re-enter it doesn&apos;t stutter anymore. And imagine when that happens into the boss room, where you can&apos;t leave.
You die, and must start the level from the beginning, and giving they are random generated, it&apos;s a different level, with different power-ups and everything.
Oh, and you get variations like reduced gravity or slippery floor. That is nice, exactly what you need to play a game where movement seems important (that is sarcasm).
Some power-up are also unreachable, I can&apos;t see how you can get to higher floors when you don&apos;t have stairs or something.

It lacks of visual queues, like when you are out of ammo (you have to change clips, but they are infinite) and audio is not clear enough.
Also it&apos;s not clear that you have to dodge how the game tells you, doesn&apos;t matter if you are outside of the ray shoot by the draugr: you have to dodge in the direction shown by the cross-hair (I think).


Tip for developers: NEVER build columns into an FPS. You corner yourself thinking there is space to move, but you in fact you are in a corner between the wall and a protruding column and you are going to die. I don&apos;t know any other FPS that does this, except Halo (and it sucks). Maybe there is a reason why.


I tried really hard, I wasted hours trying to find something good.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">17</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>7135ed92-f934-11ea-a787-fa163e93294d</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:rating>
        <review:title>Stay away...</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">8</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/715514ca-3b57-11e9-93d8-00163e4e60cc -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/715514ca-3b57-11e9-93d8-00163e4e60cc">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-02-28T14:50:36</review:date>
        <review:description>Just one more day! I was pleasantly surprised by how much I enjoyed this game, particularly because I&apos;m typically not that wild about crafting anything. It may be because it&apos;s a more laid-back kind of title. The general gameplay loop is quite pleasant even if it is a bit on the grindy side. Having the factory (for automated crafting) earlier in the game would have been nice. The play/date and tournament mini games are fun diversion albeit quite simple. There&apos;s almost always something to do. Some lacking sounds seem a bit puzzling and the patchwork of voice acting is a bit of a letdown, but I ended up turning voices off anyway because what&apos;s there isn&apos;t all that great. All in all, I had a good time in my 80+ hour run with the game.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>715514ca-3b57-11e9-93d8-00163e4e60cc</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>An imperfect but enjoyable game</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">11</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/718cbb9c-2448-11eb-9f89-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/718cbb9c-2448-11eb-9f89-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-11-11T20:05:12</review:date>
        <review:description>The game is incredibly bad. 
It is the laziest mobile port I&apos;ve ever seen, and lacks basic PC features. 
The UI is horrendus and not at all intuitive for mouse and keyboard.
The interact button is TAB for fucks sake!
The gameplay and graphics are not worth mentioning.

Now I could forgive all of this if the character deveopment system was really cool, but it&apos;s sub par. Few abilities and stats to choose from, and only the 4 bog standard classes.

Save yourselves, and skip this shite.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">23</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>718cbb9c-2448-11eb-9f89-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:rating>
        <review:title>Woefully bad.</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">16</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/719ec29e-922d-11eb-ab77-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/719ec29e-922d-11eb-ab77-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-03-31T17:29:04</review:date>
        <review:description>Otherwise a nice game (title length was too limited).
It runs mostly smoothly, even on low-end hardware when using single-player games.
However, the server for online gaming sometimes seem to be a bit overloaded.
It takes quite some time to start a game and it sometimes becomes laggy. 
At least that&apos;s not disrupting game experience too strongly.

So it&apos;s fun to play and even the single player campaign is ok, but I mostly recommend playing it online with some friends.
That&apos;s however my largest minus, they mainly target Steam (which makes sense due to a larger user base). However, therefore you might run into issues if not all of your friends are on the same platform.

Furthermore, despite of Gog&apos;s official claims of being DRM free, there are quite a few (possibly singleplayer) components which don&apos;t work without galaxy+internet connection, which can become an issue once they shut down their servers. Those issues can stack if you are on linux, since gog doesn&apos;t offer galaxy for linux yet. If you use windows or steam you should be fine however.
So please inform yourself in the forum discussions for details before buying.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">7</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>719ec29e-922d-11eb-ab77-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>issues with crossplay and linux</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">21</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/71952d22-93fe-11e8-b8d6-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/71952d22-93fe-11e8-b8d6-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2009-07-22T05:37:44</review:date>
        <review:description>Starts out GREAT! Wicked atmosphere. Run-down slummy backstreets riddled with gangs, gun shops, pubs and, of course, crime. Hire gangsters, buy weapons and weapon upgrades to survive through the levels. But, a few hours into the game (once all your weapons are upgraded) it turns into a typical, shoot everything that moves, FPS with nothing very special to keep you playing... Just target pratice and health packs really.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>71952d22-93fe-11e8-b8d6-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:rating>
        <review:title>GREAT game!!... For the first few hours</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">12</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/723ed18e-fced-11e9-babf-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/723ed18e-fced-11e9-babf-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-11-01T23:20:36</review:date>
        <review:description>The game is fun. It&apos;s very addicting and has a very nintendo-esque feel to it. The graphics are beautiful, bright and lovely. 

Had 40+ hours in it on my old PC build. (i5 2500k, gtx 770, 8gb ram) so it&apos;s definitely not a very demanding game and I highly recommend it for anyone looking for a good game to pass the time or even get lost in.

Also ignore the bad review(s) that are still on top. They are outdated and downright wrong at this point. (not that they were wrong before of course)</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">7</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>723ed18e-fced-11e9-babf-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Quirky </review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/724ba776-df9c-11ec-b9d8-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/724ba776-df9c-11ec-b9d8-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-05-30T01:12:36</review:date>
        <review:description>So, I am reviewing this after recently playing it earlier this year, and its a good honest attempt at a metroidvainia, but is very basic by todays standards. The first major downside of this game is the length, it&apos;s too short, five hours in total for the fourth installment in the series, really? The second downside, what little story there is, can be hard to follow, especially since it serves as a prequel to three other games that also have next to no story, but very rich lore and history behind them; so much so, they got a prequel. The third grip I got, it has recycled asset, from previous games that were done in a different artstyle from this one; yes some of the enemies here stick out like a sore thumb from the new pixel art included in this game, which is superior in comparison to an enemy like bakman, for example. Lastly, The dodging mechanics too, seem limited in comparison to a game like i dunno, blasphimous, which is basically the same idea only it has more story and allows you to perry attacks as well. The pixel art is good, the soundtrack is good, but again, blasphimous has these two factors going for it, and so do many other metriodvainias... so, I can&apos;t give it a five star rating in the year 2022.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>724ba776-df9c-11ec-b9d8-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>A very basic game in the year 2022</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/72864fba-b28d-11e8-a428-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/72864fba-b28d-11e8-a428-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2017-12-12T07:12:43</review:date>
        <review:description>A very chill, laid back game. If you&apos;re looking for a short game with catchy tunes and cute dad jokes then I would recommend this. 
Combat is clunky and hit detection gets kinda weird sometimes, but the game is very generous with the autosaves so it doesn&apos;t become much of an annoyance.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>72864fba-b28d-11e8-a428-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:rating>
        <review:title>A game with villain songs, actually</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">35</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/73a3202e-2a75-11ea-9f7f-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/73a3202e-2a75-11ea-9f7f-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-12-29T21:57:32</review:date>
        <review:description>It looks like Darkest Dungeon but it is not and that&apos;s fine.

Fights and explorations seem easy and/or weird at first ? Yeah, the challenge is among the boss fights and... that&apos;s fine too because it gives more interest to the main story. 

Give this game a chance. &quot;Vambrace: Cold Soul&quot; really deserves it. </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>73a3202e-2a75-11ea-9f7f-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Worth to explore</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">7</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/73b3f02e-93fa-11e8-aa69-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/73b3f02e-93fa-11e8-aa69-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2013-10-06T01:56:59</review:date>
        <review:description>Before going on to make lackluster movie tie-ins, Shiny made some of the most creative games on the planet. MDK was a technical tour-de-force when it was released, with ridiculously large levels and insane draw distances. The game also had a crazy, dark sense of humor that permeated the whole design, from taunting enemies that held targets up to their faces, to weapons like &quot;The World&apos;s Smallest Nuclear bomb&quot;. 

There is a frantic pace to the whole experience, only pausing for breath between levels (but even there, there&apos;s no progress bar, just a long tunnel to keep running through). It&apos;s an extremely linear experience, but in a good way, focusing on quality over quantity. 

By today&apos;s standards, the visuals have aged a bit, but I think MDK is still one of the best 3rd-person shooters ever made, and the core gameplay still shines through.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">8</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>73b3f02e-93fa-11e8-aa69-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Shiny at it&apos;s best</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">221</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


