        <review:id>75422c5e-ca4a-11e8-aabd-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Good Old Game</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/7581fdc6-9470-11e8-8392-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/7581fdc6-9470-11e8-8392-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2012-03-24T03:08:43</review:date>
        <review:description>Read the reviews and was expecting something great for a space sim game. I was disappointed. The graphics were worse than Freespace and the gameplay and missions weren&apos;t any different or improved at all. This ended up being more of a rehash of Freespace and nothing more. Good thing i didn&apos;t have to pay much for this or i&apos;d actually be mad about it.
Back to Freelancer and Mechwarrior.</review:description>
