    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/76322804-5620-11ea-86bc-fa163e62c76a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/76322804-5620-11ea-86bc-fa163e62c76a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-02-23T11:40:01</review:date>
        <review:description>Игра проходится на одном дыхании, вернее на 3-х дыханиях в моём случае, при первом прохождении мне поддалось от силы 15% игры, но в этом и суть игры, не надо боятся проходить её заново, во второй раз вы сможете проходить её буквально на протяжении часа, но сможете ли разгадать все секреты? Игра методично воспитывает в вас детектива, обращайте внимание на мельчайшие детали, не бойтесь предполагать, ведь то что вы видите практически во всех случаях есть именно тем что вы предполагаете. Проходя игру в третий раз я чуствовал себя настоящим детективом, замечал мельчайшие детали, строил цепочки логических выводов. Маст хев для любителей головоломок.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>76322804-5620-11ea-86bc-fa163e62c76a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Уникальный игровой опыт</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">11</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/764e4e6a-93fa-11e8-b78f-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/764e4e6a-93fa-11e8-b78f-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2008-11-08T14:46:52</review:date>
        <review:description>I can&apos;t even begin to describe the overwhelming joy I felt when I found this site, and then proceeded to find a version of Freespace 2 that was stable and Vista compatible to boot!!! 

I would have to agree with anyone who says that this is THE defining game of the spaceflight/combat sim genre. This is only confirmed when, as was stated before, when you look on e-bay and see it going for $100 and up. If you enjoy flight/combat sims you must pick this game up!!! Really, for $6 you can&apos;t go
wrong. Keep those good &apos;ole games coming GOG.com!!</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>764e4e6a-93fa-11e8-b78f-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Freespace 2 FTW!!!</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/765d2bba-9889-11eb-82ed-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/765d2bba-9889-11eb-82ed-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-04-08T19:42:52</review:date>
        <review:description>Сама по себе игра довольно интересна, но за 3 года (или сколько она уже существует) много чего не исправленно.
Это самый сырой и не удобный интерфейс что я видел в стратегиях, куда не ткни будет реализовано не так как нужно, постоянно немного не так как удобно из-за этого печатление от игры портится всё сильнее с каждым часом игры.
Так же создаётся впечатление что есть проблемы с балансом, при чём я не про баланс пвп, а про общий темп игры он постоянно скачет из-за различных событий, микроменеджмент в купе с плохим интерфейсом превращается в ад.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>765d2bba-9889-11eb-82ed-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:rating>
        <review:title>Слишком сыро</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/7659fc92-93fa-11e8-bc70-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/7659fc92-93fa-11e8-bc70-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2008-11-08T14:57:49</review:date>
        <review:description>It doesn&apos;t matter what you&apos;ve played before, play Freespace 2. This game redefined the genre. The graphics are still strong, there&apos;s a bunch of mods, the story is great, the combat is varied and the differences in scale between small fighter ships and capital ships is incredible.

I can go on at great length and break things down but it all comes down to this: BUY THE GAME.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>7659fc92-93fa-11e8-bc70-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>One of the best space sims around</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/7678d096-906f-11e9-8300-00163e4e60cc -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/7678d096-906f-11e9-8300-00163e4e60cc">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-06-16T22:46:41</review:date>
        <review:description>Un petit jeu indépendant qui ne paie pas de mine mais qui se révèle étonnamment addictif.  

Aux commandes de votre ordinateur, vous devez espionner différents lieux avec des caméras. Si certains ne présentent aucun intérêt, hormi d&apos;afficher des petits easter eggs, d&apos;autres vous montrent des scènes sur lesquelles vous pouvez agir de manière plus ou moins directe. 

Pour cela, vous devez noter des mots (prédéfinis) dans les différents dialogues de ces scènes, puis faire des recherches sur le browser fictif du jeu pour trouver de nouvelles informations. Par exemple, rechercher le nom d&apos;une chanson d&apos;un artiste que vous voyez répéter vous donnera son nom. Puis en fouillant un peu plus vous pourrez trouver son numéro de téléphone et son adresse, afin de le contacter etc...

En dehors de cette phase caméra, il y a une phase de gestion de ressources assez stressantes. Pour accéder à de nouvelles caméras, il faut les acheter. Il faut aussi avoir de quoi payer son loyer tous les 3 jours sous peine de risquer l&apos;expulsion. Il faut aussi faire des courses ou se faire livrer des plats, aller travailler pour gagner un peu d&apos;argent et bien sûr penser à dormir un peu. Cette gestion de ressource est pour moi un peu trop sévère, heureusement un mode &quot;light&quot; est proposé par les développeurs qui permet de se concentrer sur les caméras, la partie gestion étant beaucoup plus facile à gérer.

Point noir pour moi, le jeu n&apos;est pas disponible en français, même si l&apos;anglais utilisé ici n&apos;est pas bien compliqué à comprendre, pour un jeu narratif comme celui-là je peux comprendre que ça puisse rebuter les allergiques à la langue de Shakespeare.

Au final, un bon petit jeu qui m&apos;a bien occupé, le concept est franchement chouette et on prend plaisir à regarder ces petits diorama et d&apos;essayer d&apos;aider (ou pas) les acteurs de ces scènes. Dommage que le jeu ne soit pas disponible en français et qu&apos;il soit un peu court, j&apos;en reprendrai bien un morceau !</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>7678d096-906f-11e9-8300-00163e4e60cc</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Petit indé rafraîchissant</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/7681257e-93fa-11e8-bfd2-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/7681257e-93fa-11e8-bfd2-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2008-11-08T17:04:10</review:date>
        <review:description>IMHO, needs the fan generated higher resolution graphics and extras to do it justice. Just Google and you&apos;d find an installer that grabs the lot and installs it all automatically and correctly.

Enjoy

DrTeeth</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">15</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>7681257e-93fa-11e8-bfd2-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:rating>
        <review:title>Okay...but</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">8</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/77d19bee-93fe-11e8-80f4-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/77d19bee-93fe-11e8-80f4-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2009-08-26T20:01:42</review:date>
        <review:description>This is quite simply a brilliant game and one of, if not the best, space combat simulations ever made. A cool story coupled with great gameplay and awesome amounts of fun. 

The ships handle pretty damn well, obviously not Newtonian but more in the vein of the classic X-Wing/TIE Fighter, Wing Commander vein yet feels somehow more appropriate. The scale of battles can be quite rather huge with giant capital ships duking it out and you in a smaller fighter or bomber in the midst of some pretty epic battles and this really immerses you in the game and it&apos;s universe.

It has all the classic tenets of the genre, a lot of targeting controls, power management, weapon grouping controls, communications and the like, and a fair few hefty buttons. It did take me a few trial and error runs to find the perfect setup up my ancient, but still great, Saitek X35/36 Throttle and Stick but once I got that nailed down I had everything at my finger tips and rarely needed the keyboard, which is always nice.

The game itself can be pretty damn tough and I had to retry some of the missions a fair few times before I nailed them. Tough but fair, makes a change from all the damn easy games of today.

As others have no doubt mentioned there&apos;s still large modding scene for this game. The Source Code Project makes all of this possible and then the Upgrade Project which improves the visual quality a lot amongst other things, and dozens of other mods including full conversions and massive new campaign arcs.

In conclusion, if you&apos;re a fan of the genre and do not own this game then get out there and bloody buy it!</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>77d19bee-93fe-11e8-80f4-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Brilliance!</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/77d90d02-93fe-11e8-8f54-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/77d90d02-93fe-11e8-8f54-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2010-04-30T09:08:47</review:date>
        <review:description>I recently pried myself from FreeSpace 2 and gave 1 a shot and I&apos;m glad I did. An amazing game which still stands on it own merits despite the sequel, a great story line and some pretty awesome missions.

The addon missions are a bit meh but playing through the excellent main campaign is pretty much mandatory if you want to get more enjoyment out of FS2 and it&apos;s well worth your time and money.

5/5!</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>77d90d02-93fe-11e8-8f54-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Simply brilliant</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/771f8572-416a-11ec-8407-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/771f8572-416a-11ec-8407-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-11-09T16:36:46</review:date>
        <review:description>Very interesting idea, but so bad realization. Okey, you find a guy who died because of &quot;thing&quot;. You are opening menu to choose his death, but you can&apos;t choose anything but his name (because you met him for the first time, or, i don&apos;t no. So you need to go through all this memory, which you can&apos;t exit before some time, then you should see the next memory, cause there was a corpse in previous... After this 10 incredible minutes you finally returned to &quot;real world&quot; and want to choose the first guy&apos;s death, but there are so many corpses on the flour after all of this memories, so you need to go through memories to find which was the first.... So annoying. </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">23</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>771f8572-416a-11ec-8407-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>Annoying inception</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


