    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/8aaa02ac-bace-11eb-83e1-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/8aaa02ac-bace-11eb-83e1-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-05-22T10:23:01</review:date>
        <review:description>The game crashed the first time as soon as the word START was typed, had to ALT + F4 out of it because it draws focus.
Second time I launched it, crashed even before you were able to type START, and absolutely REFUSED to close. Completely locked up my PC. Couldn&apos;t ALT + F4 out of it, couldn&apos;t bring up task manager because the game brings itself to the foreground.

Im sure the full game doesn&apos;t have issues like this, but I will not be buying it based on my experience here. There are some major issues to iron out in this demo.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>8aaa02ac-bace-11eb-83e1-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:rating>
        <review:title>Absolutely unplayable. Locked up my PC</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/8aae9f92-b298-11e8-9686-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/8aae9f92-b298-11e8-9686-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2018-01-01T15:49:45</review:date>
        <review:description>Once I met it when I was 7, on an old PC running Windows 98,which someone elder gave it to me, didnt have any interesting things but this one. This was my first FPS game. I only know how to click the mouse-buttons at that time. Very funny memories.

Surprised to see it on GOG. Once again, everything is back.

 It runs smooth on Windows 10 (ver 15063.786). Same sentences. Same Fun!</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>8aae9f92-b298-11e8-9686-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Childhood&apos;s Back!</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/8aaf7916-b779-11ea-bb57-fa163e62c76a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/8aaf7916-b779-11ea-bb57-fa163e62c76a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-06-26T09:52:03</review:date>
        <review:description>Its starts off easy but gets realy challenging. The game forces you to make critical decisions that shape your future battles and decisions. The campain is very well made. My only compaint is that thier isnt enough factions. and only one campain. I realy hope they release more as dlc.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>8aaf7916-b779-11ea-bb57-fa163e62c76a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Fantastic game!</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/8ae87b2e-5d29-11ec-bc7a-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/8ae87b2e-5d29-11ec-bc7a-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-12-15T00:02:34</review:date>
        <review:description>i know that EVERYONE seems to love this game but to be honest it just doesn&apos;t DO IT for me.
the first game didn&apos;t do much for me either, don&apos;t get me wrong...i enjoyed playing it but it never
really satisfied that space dog fighter in me, and the 2nd freespace game doesn&apos;t either.
the first game let you choose between running the game in software OR hardware mode, this
time around it&apos;s 3D HARDWARE mode ONLY, also i was able to easily control my ship with my mouse
in the first game, not so with freespace2 , you really can only play this with a joystick!
i connected my laptop to my TV VIA HDMI and was disappointed that i could NOT run the game at my
TV&apos;S native resolution( so no fullscreen on your TV ). the first one had that FRED editor thing but BALLS if i could ever figure it out? this time around they have it again, haven&apos;t messed with it yet but i expect it won&apos;t be any easier to use than the first freespace, also i never really liked the large motherships in the first game and sadly they are not much better looking this time around, too bad they didn&apos;t hire some japanese modelers to give us some really kewl looking motherships
hey this game doesn&apos;t suck or anything...it&apos;s just an OK game, but if they ever make a third installment then it will be time to hire some NEW TALENT because the guys and gals who are making these games just aren&apos;t giving us their best.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">8</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>8ae87b2e-5d29-11ec-bc7a-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>has not grown on me yet.</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/8b13bc18-17fb-11eb-9f73-fa163e7e880a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/8b13bc18-17fb-11eb-9f73-fa163e7e880a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-10-27T04:24:30</review:date>
        <review:description>Pumpkin Jack feels like a throwback to early 3D action platformers from the PS1 and PS2.  The game may be linear but due to the simple, addictive gamplay accompanied by great graphics (especially with RTX) and the fun writing/characters,  I can say with confidence that Pumpkin Jack is definitely worth the price!  Especially during the Halloween seaon!</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>8b13bc18-17fb-11eb-9f73-fa163e7e880a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Im happy I gave this game a chance!</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/8b230146-fe34-11e9-9f1e-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/8b230146-fe34-11e9-9f1e-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-11-03T14:22:03</review:date>
        <review:description>Un grand OUI pour ce jeu de Lucas Pope qui m&apos;a fait passer une dizaine d&apos;heures passionnante !

Avec son look old school, &quot;Return of the Obra Dinn&quot; vous fera penser à vos vieux jeux du temps de l&apos;Amstrad CPC ou du Commodore 64. Du moins sur les captures d&apos;écran, car en jeu, vous vous déplacerez en 3D dans cet environnement &quot;filaire&quot; et les dialogues seront doublés en anglais.

Mais que ces graphismes plaisent ou au contraire rebutent, il ne faut pas s&apos;arrêter à cette enveloppe. Obra Dinn est un véritable jeu d&apos;enquête qui vous obligera à réfléchir par vous même, prendre des notes, et poser des hypothèses afin de comprendre l&apos;histoire. Et ce, à l&apos;instar de ces jeux cultes que sont &quot;Maupiti Island&quot;, &quot;Croisière pour un Cadavre&quot; ou encore &quot;The Last Express&quot;. En (beaucoup) plus facile cependant.

La mécanique laisse grande part à la réflexion, mais le jeu vous fournit un journal qui se remplira automatiquement. Très pratique, mais il est dommage qu&apos;il ne permette pas d&apos;écrire ses propres notes sur les fiches des personnages.

Si le scénario très &quot;Lovecrat&quot; est intéressant, il n&apos;est cependant pas exceptionnel et la fin m&apos;a d&apos;ailleurs un peu déçu. Je m&apos;attendais à des révélations tonitruantes, mais rien d&apos;inattendu. Cependant, le plaisir de l&apos;enquête n&apos;est pas atténué pour autant.

Une très belle</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>8b230146-fe34-11e9-9f1e-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Un véritable jeu d&apos;enquête</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


