        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:rating>
        <review:title>Forgettable</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">74</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/81ccc686-a97a-11e9-81c8-3abd2cfe2ff8 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/81ccc686-a97a-11e9-81c8-3abd2cfe2ff8">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-07-18T16:38:44</review:date>
        <review:description>Стар я наверное стал, редко какая игра, даже очень хорошая, может по настоящему удивить. MDK смогла. По нынешним меркам она довольно проста, если не сказать примитивна (беги да стреляй, иногда прыгай по платформам, что может быть проще?), графически устарела (но тогда, в &apos;97, вполне могла произвести впечатление не хуже чем Crysis десять лет спустя), сюжета почти и нет (по сути только текстовые брифинги)... Но всё гениальное просто. Бегать по просторным уровням и отстреливать волны супостатов увлекательно, главное не останавливаться, иначе убьют быстро. Дизайн уровней просто невероятный, качество скачет от &quot;потрясающе&quot; до &quot;безумие какое-то&quot;; каждый уровень по своему хорош и эффектен. И конечно же, саундтрек. Музыка Томми Талларико это нечто, обожаю его работы ещё со времён Sega Mega Drive (Earthworm Jim 1-2, Cool Spot, Aladdin - музыка к этим культовым хитам его заслуга), и в MDK мастер не ударил в грязь лицом. Какие-то треки динамичные, какие-то пугающие, а какие-то... Безумные. Как и сама игра и творчество студии Shiny в частности. А какая тут концовка... Осмелюсь предположить, что ради неё всё и затевалось, взрыв мозга обеспечен. Очень штучная вещь, эта MDK. Проста геймплейно, но увлекает, а потрясающая атмосфера созданная благодаря исключительному таланту художников и композитора обволакивает. За фулл прайс не рекомендую, а вот со скидкой приобрести MDK определённо стоит. В топ любимых игр может и не попадёт, но запомнится надолго это точно. Ах да, тут же ещё есть отсылочка на Червяка Джима... И коровы!</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>81ccc686-a97a-11e9-81c8-3abd2cfe2ff8</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Атмосферно, дерзко и сюрреалистично</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/81d9b39a-e6aa-11eb-8d49-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/81d9b39a-e6aa-11eb-8d49-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-07-17T05:55:56</review:date>
        <review:description>I played Ski Resort Tycoon as a little kid and this game immediately reminded me of it. 

The demo appears to be pretty old (out of date). It&apos;s not very long and a lot clunky. It was still fun enough to consider buying the full game, which I did. The developer has released a lot of updates since the demo was posted and the game has a lot more content. I&apos;m looking forward to the continued development of this game!</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>81d9b39a-e6aa-11eb-8d49-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Fun demo, a little out of date.</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/81e8b988-32bc-11ea-a7a7-00163e4e60cc -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/81e8b988-32bc-11ea-a7a7-00163e4e60cc">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-01-09T10:46:20</review:date>
        <review:description>Simply a janky game, from the animations to the story. Emotional beats fall flat, implications for the relatively coherent part of the story are overdone due to the lack of dialogue, animations go from one key pose to another in a very artificial way. 

I understand this isn&apos;t trying to be a conventional game experience, but it fails at what it tries to be as well in my eyes, they could not sell the humanity of the characters without dialogue and with such abstract character models, the frequent &quot;trippy&quot; parts felt dull, the downtime between interactions was simply confusing, as I threw my mouse across the environment looking for an interactable or for the next section to start. The nonsensical parts of the story are unprecendented and more confusing than anything else.

Abstract art can be less demanding from the creator in a variety of ways but demands excellent ideas behind it to support any impact it can make, put simply, this game combines the style of Picasso with the artistic depth of Suess. Occasionally visually appealling, but eccentric for the sake of being so.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>81e8b988-32bc-11ea-a7a7-00163e4e60cc</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:rating>
        <review:title>Un-Recommendable Considering Ending</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">11</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/8130cf7e-94c2-11e8-a1e8-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/8130cf7e-94c2-11e8-a1e8-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2012-07-21T22:09:59</review:date>
        <review:description>I don´t know many about this game and I play it first time,but I am rather positive then negative about this game after first played game. Most of this I really like-and like Baldur´s Gate series,Icewind series,Throne of Darkness and maybe some other which I don´t mentioned it has one super great advantge against all today classic hardcore RPG-I can enjoy it in co-operation with another player (try it today, no problem and it rock!)-whole story and game from begining to the credits. What today hardcore RPG like this (from old school) I can enjoy this way? I miss these type of isometric hardcore RPG which have both solo and co-op capability. But that you think I am just focus solely on one feature-
So I recomend this RPG for people who love classic 2D isometric RPG, which are quite hard, but still fair. It has quite interesting system of skills (specially magic skills) and have also system of perks which you can find in Fallout. In my opinion it is very interesting mix of first two Fallout games and Baldur´s Gate series (and maybe from some other RPGs from that era). For me, story isn´t so bad and after 8 hours and 32 minute I can say this RPG is just amazing. Story, some funny/interesting moments in game and interesting system of skills (some of them) and maybe for me very important capability to play solo or in four people (just classic system of co-op for many other RPG from that era which I sorely miss today and two last resorts which left are just Action RPG or MMORPG).  
Only one thing which you can consider is you can (maybe) easy forget which location you already visit-if you have weaker memory, where you should go to progress in quest and maybe little dumb AI (but this are maybe problems which are quite common for most of hardcore RPGs from this era)</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>8130cf7e-94c2-11e8-a1e8-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Quite interesting and quite fun RPG</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/8150b73a-b34f-11ec-85af-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/8150b73a-b34f-11ec-85af-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-04-03T16:10:59</review:date>
        <review:description>If I was to sum this up in a minimal fashion it&apos;s &quot;Papers Please With Plants&quot; but that do the game a disservice. It&apos;s a particularly unique and neat title unable to be categories. It requires attention to detail and patience to play effectively.  Totally zen.
It&apos;s not a particuarly LONG game, but well worth the entrance fee.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>8150b73a-b34f-11ec-85af-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Particularly pleasant</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/8163c54e-8569-11e9-abd2-00163e4e60cc -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/8163c54e-8569-11e9-abd2-00163e4e60cc">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-06-02T22:06:20</review:date>
        <review:description>I must say this game is a disappointment. The graphics and sounds are excellent. However, that&apos;s about it. I am a big fan of Darkest Dungeon and that game took quite a few patches to get good too, BUT, the mechanics are there already and just need polish. This game don&apos;t even seem to have the mechanics in place or require some drastic rewiring to get it. 

Let&apos;s start with the polish part. You cannot access your inventory or menus in town map. Yup, you have to enter an area before you can open your inventory or look at your character sheets. Also, when hiring you cannot look up the details of the hires. So if a brand new character show up, only way you can look into the character&apos;s skills and statistics is to dismiss an existing character in your part, who is gone forever then, and hire the new one. 

But what really kills my enthusiasm for the game is lack of character progression. Both the MC and hires only have 1 normal attack and 1 limit breakish skills. That is it, the other 2 slots are defend and pass. Seriously, instead of adding a second skill, the game wasted a slot to have BOTH defend and pass. Also, only the MC level up, everyone else stays the same. So yeah, really regret buying this game.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">9</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>8163c54e-8569-11e9-abd2-00163e4e60cc</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>Not a lot under the hood</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">69</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/8163c61e-58d9-11e9-b35d-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/8163c61e-58d9-11e9-b35d-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-04-07T05:04:41</review:date>
        <review:description>Very nice aestetic with a switchable palette to emulate many diffrent popular late 80&apos;s computers; a little hard on the eyes at first, but you get used to it after about half an hour. Identifying the Chinese Topmen is the most frustrating part of the game, but you can get them all eventually.
(Copyed over from my Steam Review)</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>8163c61e-58d9-11e9-b35d-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Would recommend checking this out!</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/817125ea-c8f2-11ea-9eee-fa163e62c76a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/817125ea-c8f2-11ea-9eee-fa163e62c76a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-07-18T15:30:46</review:date>
        <review:description>Dieses Spiel von 1999 (!) sieht selbst heute noch fantastisch aus, insbesondere mit den modernen Grafikmods (Freespace 2 SCP) die man im Internet findet. Die Steuerung der Raumschiffe ist fantastisch, die Missionen sind sehr spannend und erzählen eine gute Geschichte. Die Effekte, Explosionen usw. waren zur damaligen Zeit atemberaubend. In keinem anderen Spiel gibt es so riesige Großkampfschiffe, die sich mit ihren großen Kanonen beschießen, während man selbst als kleiner Jäger oder Bomber dazwischen hindurchfliegt - enorm episch!

Außerdem gibt es einen guten Editor, mit dem man selbst eigene Missionen erstellen kann, und man findet massenhaft von der Community generierte Kampagnen und Missionen zum Download, z.B. Blue Planet.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>817125ea-c8f2-11ea-9eee-fa163e62c76a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Das beste Einzelspieler-Weltraumspiel</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


