    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/828deb28-e042-11e9-90aa-d2856434588f -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/828deb28-e042-11e9-90aa-d2856434588f">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-09-26T09:46:27</review:date>
        <review:description>I still remember feeling dubious about buying this back in (99?) 2000, thinking &quot;well, this won&apos;t be as good as Privateer or the Wing Commander series, or X-Wing, but it looks like it should be something...&quot;

Absolutely blown away by this game.  Here we are 20 years later and I&apos;m buying a Saitek just so I can play this game again.

I remember the thrill of flying and blasting fighters while in the midst of huge capital ship battles where their batteries literally lit up space around you (great sound and effects) making you feel the passage of those weapons.

If you&apos;ve ever liked a space flight combat sim - you&apos;ll LOVE this game.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>828deb28-e042-11e9-90aa-d2856434588f</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Simple - greatest starfighter game EVER</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">8</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/8294a54a-97fb-11eb-ba11-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/8294a54a-97fb-11eb-ba11-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-04-08T02:46:44</review:date>
        <review:description>Ein klassisches Rollenspiel aus Deutschland und basierend auf dem DSA-Regelwerk. Die Atmospähre ist fantastisch, das Charaktersystem ist tief und zugleich zugänglich, die Geschichte ist sehr gut und das Spiel hat auch richtig viel Inhalt - enorm viele handgestaltete Nebenquests und interessante Charaktere. Die taktischen Kämpfe machen auch viel Spaß. Einziger Wermutstropfen ist, dass nicht alle Dialoge vertont sind, sondern nur manche. </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>8294a54a-97fb-11eb-ba11-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Das beste deutsche Rollenspiel</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">7</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/83bbce00-3fde-11eb-a546-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/83bbce00-3fde-11eb-a546-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-12-16T22:37:29</review:date>
        <review:description>I have been playing computer games for 40 years now, and this is a truly unique and gripping experience.  I can only hope that my memory eventually fades so I can experience that game again.</review:description>
