    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/83dc9696-93fe-11e8-b166-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/83dc9696-93fe-11e8-b166-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2009-07-27T18:54:34</review:date>
        <review:description>The still latest space sim shooter with the epic feel you would expect from anything space related. It&apos;s not really that long but the joy of dogfighting guarantees high replay value. 

In short - get it.
If this already isn&apos;t the reason you are buying Freespace 2 on GOG, search the web for mods, they are plentiful and vastly improve the look and feel of the game by upping the graphics high enough to make running Freespace 2 a hard job for your PC.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>83dc9696-93fe-11e8-b166-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Classic</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/830dbd5a-b1e3-11e8-b250-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/830dbd5a-b1e3-11e8-b250-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2016-10-02T09:47:19</review:date>
        <review:description>Got into a shootout. 
Won with only 1% health left. 
Went searching for a medkit.
Got bitten by a rat and died.
Now there&apos;s a fist hole in my monitor.

10/10 Would play again!</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>830dbd5a-b1e3-11e8-b250-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Rats are deadly!</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/8302de88-526f-11eb-b575-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/8302de88-526f-11eb-b575-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-01-09T13:40:45</review:date>
        <review:description>This is more like an iteractive movie. All you do is walk and click on some part of the screen. The game isn&apos;t about the gameplay, but about the story. No single line of text or dialogue, just great music and staging. You are an FBI agent trying to solve a case in a small town, That&apos;s all i&apos;m going to say.

The graphic part is quite simple, but the light add something special. As for the end, i didn&apos;t understand it, and i guess it&apos;s intentionnal. I like this kind of story where, you have to think of it after playing, where you question yourself. But i acknowledge it&apos;s not for every one.

So if you don&apos;t like that kind of gameplay don&apos;t buy it. If you like mystery, investigation and atypical storytelling this might be the game for you.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>8302de88-526f-11eb-b575-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Intriguing game but not for all</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/83340408-aaa9-11eb-b383-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/83340408-aaa9-11eb-b383-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-05-01T21:17:39</review:date>
        <review:description>First free game on GOG that I didnt claim. 
Played it on a friends computer first to give it a fair eval. 
Its what you&apos;d expect, given the title. 
Communist propaganda masquerading as social justice.
Repetitive scenarios, cringy villains (although cops on segways was kinda funny). 
The central theme is to destroy businesses
An Antifa wet dream.
</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">70</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>83340408-aaa9-11eb-b383-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:rating>
        <review:title>Redistribute to your recycle bin</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">61</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/84c4473a-94b1-11e8-8ce1-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/84c4473a-94b1-11e8-8ce1-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2012-04-14T04:50:19</review:date>
        <review:description>This is quite possibly the best space sim ever made and terribly overlooked. Everything from the first game is still here and improved upon with a better story too.

The dog fighting is brilliant, played well with a mouse but best use a joystick, and the space battles are just epic, seeing two 5KM long ships (and they really are 5KM long) dueling each other with massive beam cannons is a sight to behold, no game has matched it and probably never will.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>84c4473a-94b1-11e8-8ce1-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Legendary!</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


