    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/84f995c6-f38a-11eb-8769-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/84f995c6-f38a-11eb-8769-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-08-02T15:09:42</review:date>
        <review:description>I haven&apos;t beat Unbound yet, but I&apos;m having a blast so far! It&apos;s like Metroid but with platforming puzzles instead of shooting. The gameplay is accessible but also challenging, the story is cute.

Lots of &quot;a-ha&quot; moments when I figured out how to progress or get secrets.

Definitely recommend Unbound to anyone who likes platforming puzzles.</review:description>
