    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/9cd1789a-b902-11e9-8f63-3680111ee808 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/9cd1789a-b902-11e9-8f63-3680111ee808">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-08-07T11:00:48</review:date>
        <review:description>​Until release My Time At Portia worked just fine, never were there any game crashing bugs. But with release they changed the minimum pc specs and made it impossible to play with older graphics cards. All the support has to say is &quot;just buy a new one, we won&apos;t look into the issue until then&quot;. I contacted pathea and they didn&apos;t even answer.


I&apos;m with this game since the Demo, i backed it on Kickstarter, i tested it since then and reported all the few bugs i encountered. And now i&apos;m not able to play the finished game. For Patheas sake do i need a non-limited steam account for a review there.

I have no idea if the GOG-version would work, but as they don&apos;t seem to fix anything here, i strongly doubt it.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">7</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>9cd1789a-b902-11e9-8f63-3680111ee808</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:rating>
        <review:title>Worked fine until release</review:title>
