    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/9d4fcb3c-45a6-11eb-aeb7-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/9d4fcb3c-45a6-11eb-aeb7-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-12-24T07:12:27</review:date>
        <review:description>I have been on GOG for a long time and this game does not deserve to be here. From the very start this game doesn&apos;t even run properly, you will find people in the help forums trying to help GOG users out since the version on this site is so bad (800x600 graphics locked in for most people).  

The actual game play is extremely underwhelming starting with the fact that the basic game mechanics aren&apos;t explained and once you do learn them you&apos;ll find that you&apos;re often in a situation where you save, jump around like a moron and hope you are lucky enough to continue. Oftentimes you aren&apos;t that lucky and then you&apos;ll be forced to re-load and try the spot you were in again.

Not what I&apos;m used to on this site and hopefully a title which will be either fixed or removed.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>9d4fcb3c-45a6-11eb-aeb7-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:rating>
        <review:title>Not worth more than $3</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


