    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/905a7d5a-73d4-11e9-877e-00163e4e60cc -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/905a7d5a-73d4-11e9-877e-00163e4e60cc">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-05-11T13:07:20</review:date>
        <review:description>I just cannot figure out how to play this game. For the longest time it showed me a screen telling me to &quot;press A&quot; and I couldn’t get past it either using the keyboard or my gamepad.

Then now it tells me to &quot;press X&quot;, which works when I press X on my keyboard, but I want to play with a gamepad.

My dualshock 4 is not recognized by the game whether I use ds4drv or not.

Games should have proper input support out of the box for at least the most common input controllers (and not just the xbox360 gamepad). I already spend my week debugging things, I want games to just work, thank you.

Also the developer does not read the GOG forum for the game... (sure, the GOG forums are shit and have no notifications, but if it’s your job you should check them regularly anyway…)</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>905a7d5a-73d4-11e9-877e-00163e4e60cc</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:rating>
        <review:title>Terrible input support</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/906934ee-5e75-11ea-ab9e-fa163e62c76a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/906934ee-5e75-11ea-ab9e-fa163e62c76a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-03-05T02:09:21</review:date>
        <review:description>Gameplay is good.  Not great, just good.  It gets the job done.  I personally love the graphics choice for this game, though I can see how others would not be a big fan of it.  But this is not why it&apos;s getting 5 stars.  It is getting 5 stars because it was such an amazing journey, with so many twists and extremely meta/WTF moments.  

Several points during my playthrough, I would shout at my screen &quot;WHAT&quot;  at what I was seeing, what had just happened to the main character or NPC, and especially at the super spoiler moments that will not be mentioned here.

This game for me was absolutely worth every penny.  I&apos;ve never played anything like it before, and with the way the game ended, I was very satisfied, left wondering what will happen next, and desperately hoping that question will be answered some day.  

If you get this game, get it for the crazy amazing story, and enjoy the ride.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>906934ee-5e75-11ea-ab9e-fa163e62c76a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Play for story, not gameplay</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


