    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/917342a8-430c-11ec-9c17-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/917342a8-430c-11ec-9c17-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-11-11T18:29:40</review:date>
        <review:description>The title pretty much says it all, the movement is stiff and the actual fighting demons is less of a challenge than fighting with the game to do what i want it to do. The story is something you could completely choose to ignore, and the acting is just absolutely awful, there were assets reused for random enemies that were used for one of the main characters which makes no sense in terms of plot or mechanics. Overall awful game, I&apos;m sorry but I cannot recommend it nor do I have any suggestions to improve something that is just fundamentally flawed
</review:description>
