        <review:title>Не стоит она того</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">8</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/96ee386c-21d6-11eb-a579-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/96ee386c-21d6-11eb-a579-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-11-08T17:25:10</review:date>
        <review:description>I LOVE the characters, the world, the story, the voice acting the animation, the music, the art style...it&apos;s all fantastic!

But this game is not without it&apos;s issues which to be fair I probably wouldn&apos;t notice or care about if I didn&apos;t love the rest of it so much.
The Detective mini-game doesn&apos;t make a lot of sense. Lines of questioning seem almost random and although there&apos;s a big to-do about different characters having weaknesses or you&apos;re told to press certain issues I didn&apos;t see a big correlation between these suggestions and success. 
Some scenes have mismatched dialogue and voice acting. Not a big issue, just one I noticed.
One scene talking to Natasha had no dialogue at all: just text. I think that was an oversight. 

Besides these little tiny problems I had no technical issues and I&apos;m enjoying my time!
I just want to remind the developers maybe to take another look at their work. It&apos;s too good in so many ways to have these little problems mar it. 
</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>96ee386c-21d6-11eb-a579-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Fair Rating: Great Concept, a Bit Rough </review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">32</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/9621a4ae-dccc-11ea-b152-fa163e93294d -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/9621a4ae-dccc-11ea-b152-fa163e93294d">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-08-12T21:49:43</review:date>
        <review:description>Naprawdę rzadko mi się zdarza nie kończyć gier. W tym przypadku po kilkunastu godzinach nie mam ochoty na dalszą rozgrywkę. Gra próbuje być czymś pomiędzy klasycznym rpg, a hack&apos;n&apos;slashem, przez co w ani jednym, ani drugim gatunku nie jest dobra. Szkoda, bo początek był naprawdę niezły... 2.5/5</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>9621a4ae-dccc-11ea-b152-fa163e93294d</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>Średniak</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/964e61ba-3bf9-11eb-b14f-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/964e61ba-3bf9-11eb-b14f-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-12-11T23:41:11</review:date>
        <review:description>Plenty of shortcomings in UI/UX, foreign policy is overly simplistic and basic. Battles are not bad. Internal politics on the other hand is nicely done!

+ I like how the control+interventionism+militarism level defines the type of government countries have.

- A very big issue is that 90% of the time not much is happening outside of clicking on new projects and waiting for projects to finish and also declining all request from your factions. This would be bearable if there would be a really high speed setting (like in Paradox games).</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>964e61ba-3bf9-11eb-b14f-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:rating>
        <review:title>Nice internal politics, but otherwise lacking</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/9641682a-df81-11ec-b6e1-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/9641682a-df81-11ec-b6e1-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2022-05-29T22:00:20</review:date>
        <review:description>Sehr entspanntes Mystery-Rätsel mit interessanten Charakteren und einer kurzen, aber spannenden Story. Kein Wettlauf gegen die Zeit, man bekommt ausreichend Tipps, also nicht allzu schwer. Nichts für Spieler, die auf schwere Rätsel stehen.

Entscheidungen im Spiel beeinflussen das Ende - bist du das Gute oder das Böse?
Der erste Durchlauf dauert ca. 5h, aber wegen der variierenden Enden kann man es durchaus mehrmals spielen.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>9641682a-df81-11ec-b6e1-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Kaufempfehlung für entspanntes Rätseln</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


