    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/97ee52de-2fd8-11e9-8452-00163e4e60cc -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/97ee52de-2fd8-11e9-8452-00163e4e60cc">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-02-13T23:44:51</review:date>
        <review:description>I have honestly seen mobile phone games from 10 years ago look and play better than this thing. There is a very fine line between &quot;retro inspired game&quot; and &quot;Slap a retro sticker on the game to excuse the lazily cobbled together mess we created&quot;.

If you really want to relive the nostalgia of 1980&apos;s driving games, instead of buying this pile of absolute trash, you should petition GOG to release a proper retro driving game like &quot;Horizon Chase Turbo&quot; here. </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">70</review:downvotes>
