    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/98113836-c3ca-11e9-bf8c-2a88eff2d357 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/98113836-c3ca-11e9-bf8c-2a88eff2d357">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-08-21T04:17:31</review:date>
        <review:description>Чего не хватает людям так это хорошей эстетики, которой в игре товарный вагон.
Атмосфера - 10 из 10 
Саунд - 10 из 10
Сюжет и сценарий - 10 из 10
Гамуплей - 6.5 из 10. Это всё ещё симулятор ходьбы с наворотами, а прохождение истории за одного только Бураха занимаете около 60 часов, а там скоро еще две сюжетные линии будет. Такой гамуплей изрядно подзадолбает, но прикол в том, что все ваши страдания от унылого гамуплея вознаграждаются отменным всем остальным, а еще авторы специально так задумали. Терпи казуал. Есть читы хдд
Техническая часть - 7.5 из 10 - таки на топовой машине лахает, но не критично. Комон ребят этож юнити...

Итог: эстетический оргазм. 
 </review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>98113836-c3ca-11e9-bf8c-2a88eff2d357</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Шедевр</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">20</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/98120546-d457-11eb-86b7-fa163ec1b1bd -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/98120546-d457-11eb-86b7-fa163ec1b1bd">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-06-23T22:17:04</review:date>
        <review:description>The first part of the Bridge Constructor (BC) series of currently 6 games and 3 DLCs is
a physics puzzle at heart: Build bridges and test them with vehicles of different weight.
It is a casual game (maybe also party game if the group is so inclined).
One does not need to know a lot about physics but can experiment to find a solution
by try and error (or think a lot to succeed with the 1st construction - even estimating using
force vectors to see how gravitational force is supported by the construction ;).
As a hint, stressed parts turn a different color (red by default).
The game is nice to play in short sessions. For testing under GNU/Linux with Logitech
Gamepad F310 we wanted to play a little - and spent more than 7 hours without really noticing
as time goes by - it was that fascinating!
The goal is not to build the most stable bridge - for each construction you have a limited budget
and several different types of parts/material to use - so realistic. It is sufficient if both cars/trucks
or trains can cross the bridge - even if the bridge topples immediately after!
BC1 comes with the Slopes DLC already built-in, so the basic game has double substance -
plus the Trains DLC for extra purchasing (which also has better graphics).
The entire BC series comes as pure 64 bit using Unity 2019.x.y and F310 is supported by
this game (but maybe one may prefer using mouse) and by #5 (&apos;Portal&apos;) + #6 (&apos;The Walking Dead&apos;) -
but not by #4 (&apos;Stunts&apos;); see technical details about the entire series in my forum post:
* https://www.gog.com/forum/bridge_constructor_series/linuxversion_funktioniert_nicht/post5
So it deserves 4 stars - the graphics are closer to FullHD quality for the base game - so lacks
plenty of details ... also the music could be better (both are OK!) and one may wish for more
variety of parts/materials to solve the puzzles - but there are also other sequels which may fill
that niche.
This game can be recommended for all ages - just have fun!</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>98120546-d457-11eb-86b7-fa163ec1b1bd</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>BC1: Fun Casual Physics Puzzler</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/98221754-945b-11e8-acba-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/98221754-945b-11e8-acba-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2011-03-14T10:44:05</review:date>
        <review:description>Freespace is a game that has top notch re-playability, excellent story line, awesome dog fighting, and great multiplayer(vs. and co-op). This game stands up to the space games of today, with large scale battles and completely open environment. Having the original game, I have put hours upon hours into it, I&apos;m very happy that this game was dusted off, and put into GOG. I recommend this game, one of my favorites growing up, and still is, awesome price, awesome game... Definitely  a 5 star rating...</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>98221754-945b-11e8-acba-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Still an excellent game...</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/98746c66-1a24-11ea-851a-00163e4e60cc -->

