    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/987571f0-8ee1-11eb-af31-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/987571f0-8ee1-11eb-af31-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-03-27T11:48:34</review:date>
        <review:description>Momodora was my first metroidvania game.  I liked everything about this game. I played on normal difficulty, but got some problems with some bosses, maybe because I&apos;m too old for such games :) But practice makes everything perfect, so I managed to beat the game in 7 hours.

Pros: 
- art style looks fancy
- pretty animations
- price is good, especially on discounts
- neat controls

Cons (comparing to steam verion):
- no achievements
- no cloud saves

So if you like short metroidvania with nice animations - it is a best bet, especially on discounts.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>987571f0-8ee1-11eb-af31-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>A good game</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/989b99ae-0c70-11ec-8e4e-fa163e99870e -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/989b99ae-0c70-11ec-8e4e-fa163e99870e">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-09-03T07:37:07</review:date>
        <review:description>An interesting art style and decent music are about all this game has going for it. Unbalanced audio, so-so voice acting, weird scaling of various art assets.

The game does have a hint system which I always appreciate in a point-and-click game. I used it once and managed to figure out the puzzle, but the hint I was given was still not very intuitive.

The demo took me a total of 25 minutes to complete and did not in any way entice me to revisit the game upon its full release.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>989b99ae-0c70-11ec-8e4e-fa163e99870e</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>Whateverland is just whatever</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/989824dc-946d-11e8-b0f8-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/989824dc-946d-11e8-b0f8-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2011-06-21T06:51:31</review:date>
        <review:description>Freespace 2 offers the best space-based storyline ever created, fast-paced action and, even now, beautiful graphics. 

A must-have for absolutely all people who enjoy a good story and like computer games.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>989824dc-946d-11e8-b0f8-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>Best space-sim ever</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/99a6f70c-703b-11eb-8e27-fa163e9aa6fa -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/99a6f70c-703b-11eb-8e27-fa163e9aa6fa">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2021-02-16T11:44:44</review:date>
        <review:description>If you want a good horror game, you can get by with most resident evil entries or dead space as well as other well known titles like these. For my money however, The Evil Within 2 is better than all of these and my favourite, for its fair and well organised horror gameplay, but also its compelling and interesting story and aesthetic. The horror setting forces you to put yourself in Sebastian&apos;s shoes, interestingly making the player that much more compelled by Sebastians&apos;s primal drive to save his daughter.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">0</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>99a6f70c-703b-11eb-8e27-fa163e9aa6fa</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:rating>
        <review:title>More than just a great horror game</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/9905b594-9443-11e8-9736-00163e97122a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/9905b594-9443-11e8-9736-00163e97122a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2010-06-07T18:15:52</review:date>
        <review:description>I downloaded it...played it for an hour.  Found a walkthrough on the internet to try and make sense of it. Dealt with the crappiest graphics, buggiest code, artifacts etc. And then uninstalled it. There&apos;s some great games on this site and some great games by Shiny Entertainment, but this is not one of them. DO NOT BUY THIS...It sucks as much now as it did back in the day, just read some old reviews on IGN or somewhere.  I was curious, now disappointed. Download Sacrifice, Citizen Kabuto, MDK, MDK 2. There all way better.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">9</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>9905b594-9443-11e8-9736-00163e97122a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:rating>
        <review:title>Worst Game Ever</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/990724f2-da37-11e9-b118-eee04beaf2cd -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/990724f2-da37-11e9-b118-eee04beaf2cd">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-09-18T17:13:13</review:date>
        <review:description>The primary issue with the entire game are the controls. The game was developed with controllers in mind only. A developer mentioned on another forum they hadn&apos;t even tried the mouse and keyboard but it &quot;should work&quot;. They do.. but not too terribly well. Switching to a controller the controls and movement are still very &quot;stiff&quot; overall.

The overall progression of the game is very awkward, you end up walking (sometimes without the option of running) from point a to point b, just walking, unable to do attacks or anything. You then end up at an encounter or boss that you get to fight a bit, and it&apos;s back to walking and pressing &quot;e&quot;. The main protagonist is unlikable and has very cringe worthy one liners, in addition the voice acting is extremely amateur sounding.

It&apos;s unfortunate since the trailers make the game look so pretty, like it&apos;s an alternative to DmC however I implore you to watch some game play videos before jumping into the purchase.

If physical was still king you&apos;d find this at your local Walmart or staples in their tiny jewel case selection for $5.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">11</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>990724f2-da37-11e9-b118-eee04beaf2cd</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</review:rating>
        <review:title>Unpolished and stiff</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">69</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/995ca39c-b640-11ea-bb46-fa163e93294d -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/995ca39c-b640-11ea-bb46-fa163e93294d">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-06-24T20:31:55</review:date>
        <review:description>I wanted to like this game, and I do, but the no-save mid run just killed it for me.  No saves during expeditions are just too much of a grind and a block of time I don&apos;t always have.  That&apos;s not &apos;git-gud&apos; difficulty, because this ame is not complex or hardcore, just poor quality of life planning.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>995ca39c-b640-11ea-bb46-fa163e93294d</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</review:rating>
        <review:title>Poor save system</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">12</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/9959d8ce-949e-11ea-b015-fa163e62c76a -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl/review/9959d8ce-949e-11ea-b015-fa163e62c76a">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/naymoll/ontologies/2022/3/games.owl#Review"/>
        <review:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-05-13T01:19:08</review:date>
        <review:description>Came for the art, stayed to read all the fuming reviews from coddled children upset at politics.</review:description>
        <review:downvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">45</review:downvotes>
        <review:id>9959d8ce-949e-11ea-b015-fa163e62c76a</review:id>
        <review:rating rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</review:rating>
        <review:title>Nice art, good music, neat game</review:title>
        <review:upvotes rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">32</review:upvotes>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


